window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"13 animated films, level Spirits 1":"13 部動畫影片，烈酒 1 程度","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Spirits 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過烈酒 1 考試的學習路線，只需要回答 5 個簡短的問題。","Spirits 1 exam":"烈酒 1 考試","All of Spirits 1":"烈酒 1 全部內容","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Spirits 1 syllabus.":"課程、字卡與錯題：只涵蓋烈酒 1 的考試範圍。","Spirits 1 games":"烈酒 1 遊戲","Short games on Spirits 1 questions and terms.":"以烈酒 1 題目與術語設計的小遊戲。","Four steps and two stills":"四個步驟與兩種蒸餾器","Flavour, sweetness and colour":"風味、甜度與顏色","American and other whiskies":"美國及其他威士忌","Caribbean rum":"加勒比海蘭姆酒","Aromatised wines":"加味葡萄酒","Tasting a spirit":"品飲烈酒","A balanced cocktail":"平衡的調酒","How a spirit is made":"烈酒如何製成","The main spirit families":"主要的烈酒家族","Taste and mix":"品飲與調製","Which definition best describes a spirit?":"下列哪一項最能說明烈酒的定義？","An alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation":"經蒸餾提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料","An alcoholic drink made stronger by fermentation":"經發酵提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料","An alcoholic drink that is always aged in oak":"一定在橡木桶中陳年的酒精飲料","An alcoholic drink that always has sugar added":"一定有添加糖的酒精飲料","Distillation is what raises the alcohol level and turns a fermented liquid into a spirit.":"蒸餾提高了酒精濃度，把發酵後的液體變成烈酒。","Fermentation creates the alcohol but stops at around 8–10%: on its own it gives a drink like wine or beer, not a spirit. Many spirits, vodka for example, never see oak, and most receive no sugar. Only distillation is shared by every spirit.":"發酵會產生酒精，但大約在 8–10% 就停止：單靠發酵只能得到像葡萄酒或啤酒的飲料，而不是烈酒。許多烈酒（例如伏特加）從未接觸橡木桶，大多數也沒有加糖。只有蒸餾是所有烈酒的共同點。","In which order do the four steps of spirit production happen?":"烈酒生產的四個步驟依什麼順序進行？","Fermentation, raw material, distillation, post-distillation":"發酵、原料、蒸餾、蒸餾後處理","Raw material, post-distillation, fermentation, distillation":"原料、蒸餾後處理、發酵、蒸餾","First a sugary liquid is made, then fermented, then distilled, and finally finished.":"先製作含糖液體，再發酵、蒸餾，最後進行收尾處理。","Distillation needs a liquid that already contains alcohol, so it cannot come before fermentation. Fermentation, in turn, needs sugar, which comes from the processed raw material. Ageing, sweetening or dilution only happen once the spirit has left the still.":"蒸餾需要已經含有酒精的液體，所以不可能在發酵之前。而發酵需要糖，糖來自經過處理的原料。陳年、加甜或稀釋都只會在烈酒離開蒸餾器之後進行。","What is the main aim of processing the raw material?":"處理原料的主要目的是什麼？","To create a sugary liquid that can ferment":"製作出可以發酵的含糖液體","To create an already alcoholic liquid for distilling":"製作出已含酒精、可直接蒸餾的液體","To remove all the plant's aromas":"去除植物的所有香氣","Without a sugary liquid, yeast has nothing to turn into alcohol.":"沒有含糖液體，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化成酒精。","Alcohol only appears with fermentation, the next step. The raw material's aromas are not removed: on the contrary, each plant leaves its mark on the spirit. Colour, when there is any, is decided much later, after distillation.":"酒精要到下一步的發酵才會出現。原料的香氣不會被去除；相反地，每種植物都會在烈酒中留下印記。至於顏色（如果有的話），要到蒸餾之後很久才決定。","Which statement about the raw materials for spirits is correct?":"關於烈酒原料，下列哪一項正確？","They must be of plant origin":"必須是植物來源","They must always be cereals":"必須一律是穀物","They must already contain ready sugar":"必須本身就含有現成的糖","They must grow in a hot climate":"必須生長在炎熱氣候","In theory any plant can be used, but it has to be a plant.":"理論上任何植物都可以使用，但必須是植物。","Grapes, sugar cane, agave and potatoes show that cereals are not the only option. Some plants, cereals among them, contain no sugar and must be processed to create it, so ready-made sugar is not a requirement. A hot climate suits sugar cane, not every raw material.":"葡萄、甘蔗、龍舌蘭和馬鈴薯證明了穀物並非唯一選擇。有些植物（包括穀物）不含糖，必須經過處理才能產生糖，所以不一定需要現成的糖。炎熱氣候適合甘蔗，但並非所有原料都如此。","A distiller is using a raw material that contains no sugar. What must happen?":"蒸餾師使用的原料不含糖，必須怎麼做？","Process it to create sugar before fermentation":"在發酵前先處理原料以產生糖","Distil it directly without fermenting it":"不經發酵直接蒸餾","Add extra yeast, which replaces the sugar":"多加酵母來取代糖","Age it in oak so it develops sugar":"放進橡木桶陳年，讓它產生糖","Fermentation needs sugar, so it has to be created from the raw material itself.":"發酵需要糖，所以必須從原料本身製造出糖。","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to concentrate, so distilling straight away would make no sense. Yeast does not replace sugar: it eats it. Oak comes after distillation and creates no sugar to ferment.":"沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以濃縮，直接蒸餾毫無意義。酵母無法取代糖：酵母是吃糖的。橡木桶是在蒸餾之後才使用，也不會產生可發酵的糖。","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into…":"發酵時，酵母會把糖轉化為…","ethanol and carbon dioxide":"乙醇和二氧化碳","ethanol and pure water":"乙醇和純水","carbon dioxide and caramel":"二氧化碳和焦糖","starch and oxygen":"澱粉和氧氣","Yeast produces the alcohol that is wanted, ethanol, and a waste gas, carbon dioxide.":"酵母會產生需要的酒精（乙醇），以及一種副產物氣體：二氧化碳。","Water is already in the sugary liquid; yeast does not create it. Caramel is a colouring that may be added at the very end. Starch is what some cereals contain before it is turned into sugar: a starting point, not a product.":"水本來就存在於含糖液體中，不是酵母產生的。焦糖是最後階段才可能添加的著色劑。澱粉是某些穀物在轉化為糖之前所含的物質：它是起點，而不是產物。","What strength does a freshly fermented liquid usually have?":"剛發酵完成的液體，酒精濃度通常是多少？","Between 8% and 10% abv":"8% 至 10% abv","Between 25% and 30% abv":"25% 至 30% abv","About 40% abv":"大約 40% abv","Between 1% and 2% abv":"1% 至 2% abv","Fermentation gives a weak liquid of around 8–10%, which distillation will then make stronger.":"發酵得到的是大約 8–10% 的低濃度液體，之後再由蒸餾提高濃度。","About 25% is typical after the first pass through a pot still, not after fermentation. 40% is the most common bottling strength, reached by diluting the spirit. 1–2% would be far too low: yeast produces much more alcohol than that.":"大約 25% 是第一次通過壺式蒸餾器後的典型濃度，而不是發酵後。40% 是最常見的裝瓶濃度，要靠加水稀釋才能達到。1–2% 太低了：酵母產生的酒精遠多於此。","Apart from alcohol, what does fermentation add to the future spirit?":"除了酒精，發酵還為未來的烈酒帶來什麼？","New aromas, especially fruity ones":"新的香氣，尤其是果香","Vanilla and coconut aromas":"香草和椰子香氣","Sweetness that stays in the spirit":"會留在烈酒中的甜味","Besides alcohol, yeast creates aromas, fruity ones in particular.":"除了酒精，酵母還會產生香氣，尤其是果香。","Vanilla and coconut are typical oak aromas, so they come from ageing. A golden colour also comes from oak or caramel. Yeast eats the sugar, and in any case every newly made spirit is dry: sweetness can only be added later.":"香草和椰子是典型的橡木香氣，所以來自陳年。金黃色同樣來自橡木桶或焦糖色。酵母會把糖吃掉，而且所有剛製成的烈酒都是不甜的：甜味只能之後再添加。","To concentrate the ethanol in the fermented liquid":"濃縮發酵液中的乙醇","To turn sugar into alcohol":"把糖轉化為酒精","To add colour and woody aromas":"增添顏色和木頭香氣","To lower the strength so it is drinkable":"降低酒精濃度，讓它適合飲用","Distillation separates and concentrates the alcohol that fermentation has already created.":"蒸餾會分離並濃縮發酵時已經產生的酒精。","Turning sugar into alcohol is yeast's job, during fermentation. Colour and woody aromas come from oak, after distillation. Lowering the strength is the role of dilution with water before bottling: the exact opposite of distillation.":"把糖轉化為酒精是酵母在發酵時的工作。顏色和木頭香氣來自蒸餾後的橡木桶。降低濃度是裝瓶前加水稀釋的作用：正好與蒸餾相反。","Why does heating a fermented liquid give vapours that are richer in alcohol?":"為什麼加熱發酵液會得到酒精含量較高的蒸氣？","Because ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water":"因為乙醇的沸點比水低","Because water boils at a lower temperature than ethanol":"因為水的沸點比乙醇低","Because heat turns the remaining sugar into alcohol":"因為加熱會把剩下的糖轉化為酒精","Because the condenser adds alcohol to the vapours":"因為冷凝器會在蒸氣中加入酒精","Because it boils first, ethanol makes up a bigger share of the vapours than water does.":"乙醇先沸騰，所以在蒸氣中所佔的比例比水高。","If water boiled first, the vapours would be more watery, not more alcoholic. Heat creates no new alcohol: alcohol only comes from yeast. The condenser simply cools the vapours so they turn back into liquid.":"如果水先沸騰，蒸氣會含更多水，而不是更多酒精。加熱不會產生新的酒精：酒精只來自酵母。冷凝器只是把蒸氣冷卻，讓它變回液體。","A label reads 40% abv. What does this mean?":"酒標上寫著 40% abv，這是什麼意思？","That 40% of the liquid is alcohol":"液體的 40% 是酒精","That 40% of the liquid is sugar":"液體的 40% 是糖","That the spirit has been aged for 40 months":"這款烈酒陳年了 40 個月","That 40% of the liquid is water":"液體的 40% 是水","The abbreviation gives the percentage of alcohol in the volume of liquid.":"這個縮寫表示酒精在液體體積中所佔的百分比。","The figure measures alcohol, not sugar or age. If 40% is alcohol, the rest, around 60%, is mostly water, so the last option gets the numbers the wrong way round.":"這個數字衡量的是酒精，不是糖分或年份。如果 40% 是酒精，其餘大約 60% 主要是水，所以最後一個選項把數字弄反了。","How is distillation strength linked to aroma intensity?":"蒸餾濃度和香氣強度有什麼關係？","The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas":"濃度越低，香氣越濃郁","The higher the strength, the more intense the aromas":"濃度越高，香氣越濃郁","Strength has no effect on aromas":"濃度對香氣沒有影響","Only the bottling strength affects the aromas":"只有裝瓶濃度會影響香氣","Distilling to a low strength keeps more aromas; distilling to a high strength strips them away.":"蒸餾到較低濃度能保留更多香氣；蒸餾到較高濃度則會去除香氣。","The link is inverse: a spirit at 96% abv is so low in aroma that it is called neutral, so distillation strength clearly matters. Dilution before bottling uses pure water and adds no aroma: the style is set earlier, in the still.":"兩者成反比：96% abv 的烈酒香氣極少，所以被稱為中性烈酒，可見蒸餾濃度確實有影響。裝瓶前的稀釋用的是純水，不會增添香氣：風格在更早的蒸餾器階段就已決定。","What is a spirit distilled to 96% abv, with almost no aroma, called?":"蒸餾到 96% abv、幾乎沒有香氣的烈酒叫做什麼？","Flavoured":"調味","Aged":"陳年","At that strength so little aroma remains that the spirit is called neutral.":"在這個濃度下剩下的香氣極少，所以這種烈酒被稱為中性烈酒。","A flavoured spirit has had flavours added, and a liqueur has been sweetened as well: both happen after distillation. Aged means time in oak, which adds aromas rather than removing them.":"調味烈酒是添加了風味，利口酒則還經過加甜：兩者都在蒸餾後進行。陳年是指在橡木桶中度過的時間，會增添香氣而不是去除香氣。","Within what range does the strength of a newly made spirit vary?":"剛製成的烈酒，酒精濃度大約在什麼範圍內？","From about 60% to 96% abv":"大約 60% 至 96% abv","From about 40% to 60% abv":"大約 40% 至 60% abv","From about 8% to 40% abv":"大約 8% 至 40% abv","From about 90% to 100% abv":"大約 90% 至 100% abv","Newly made spirits run from about 60%, the most aromatic, up to 96%, the neutral ones.":"剛製成的烈酒從大約 60%（香氣最豐富）到 96%（中性烈酒）都有。","40% is the usual bottling strength after dilution, not the strength leaving the still. 8–10% is the fermented liquid, before distillation. 96% is the ceiling: 100% is not reached, and many aromatic spirits come off the still well below 90%.":"40% 是稀釋後常見的裝瓶濃度，而不是離開蒸餾器時的濃度。8–10% 是蒸餾前的發酵液。96% 是上限：100% 是達不到的，而且許多香氣豐富的烈酒離開蒸餾器時遠低於 90%。","Which statement about the pot still is correct?":"關於壺式蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","It must be emptied and cleaned after each distillation":"每次蒸餾後都必須清空並清洗","It can run continuously without ever stopping":"可以連續運作、從不停機","It easily produces neutral spirits at 96% abv":"很容易產出 96% abv 的中性烈酒","It is a vertical structure divided into many sections":"是分成許多層的直立式結構","A pot still works in batches: once a batch is finished, it is emptied and cleaned.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次方式運作：一批完成後就要清空並清洗。","Continuous running, neutral strengths and a tall structure divided into sections all describe the column still. However many times it is used, a pot still never reaches a very high-strength neutral spirit.":"連續運作、達到中性濃度、分成多層的高聳結構，這些都是在描述柱式蒸餾器。無論使用多少次，壺式蒸餾器都無法得到極高濃度的中性烈酒。","In double pot still distillation, which sequence of strengths is most realistic?":"在壺式蒸餾器的二次蒸餾中，哪一組濃度變化最符合實際？","About 10% → about 25% → about 75%":"約 10% → 約 25% → 約 75%","About 10% → about 40% → about 96%":"約 10% → 約 40% → 約 96%","About 25% → about 50% → about 75%":"約 25% → 約 50% → 約 75%","About 2% → about 10% → about 40%":"約 2% → 約 10% → 約 40%","It starts from a fermented liquid of about 10%, rises to about 25%, then to about 75%.":"從約 10% 的發酵液開始，先升到約 25%，再升到約 75%。","A pot still cannot reach 96%: that strength is typical of the tallest column stills. The starting liquid is not 25%, since fermentation stops around 8–10%. And finishing at 40% matches bottling strength, not a newly made spirit.":"壺式蒸餾器達不到 96%：這是最高的柱式蒸餾器才有的濃度。起始液體也不會是 25%，因為發酵大約在 8–10% 就停止了。而最後停在 40% 對應的是裝瓶濃度，不是剛製成的烈酒。","In a pot still, which part turns the vapours back into liquid?":"在壺式蒸餾器中，哪個部分把蒸氣變回液體？","The still head":"蒸餾器頂部（鵝頸）","In the condenser, the vapours pass through a cooled coil and become liquid again.":"在冷凝器中，蒸氣通過冷卻的盤管，再度變成液體。","The pot holds the liquid and the heat source boils it: both create the vapours rather than cooling them. The still head simply carries the rising vapours towards the condenser.":"蒸餾鍋裝著液體，熱源讓液體沸騰：兩者都是產生蒸氣，而不是冷卻蒸氣。蒸餾器頂部只是把上升的蒸氣導向冷凝器。","Which two needs led to the invention of the column still?":"發明柱式蒸餾器是為了滿足哪兩項需求？","Running continuously and reaching very high strengths":"連續運作，並達到極高的濃度","Working in batches and getting more aroma":"批次運作，並得到更多香氣","Ageing faster and colouring the spirit":"加快陳年，並為烈酒上色","Fermenting and distilling in the same vessel":"在同一個容器中發酵與蒸餾","The pot still stops after every batch and cannot reach high strengths: the column solves both limits.":"壺式蒸餾器每批都要停機，也無法達到高濃度：柱式蒸餾器同時解決了這兩個限制。","Working in batches is exactly the pot still's limitation, and a tall column gives less aroma, not more. The column has nothing to do with ageing or colour, which come later. Fermentation remains a separate step before distillation.":"批次運作正是壺式蒸餾器的限制，而高聳的蒸餾柱帶來的香氣更少，而不是更多。蒸餾柱和陳年或顏色無關，那些都在之後才發生。發酵仍是蒸餾之前的獨立步驟。","In a column still, where is the liquid with the highest alcohol level?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，哪裡的液體酒精濃度最高？","On the top section":"最上層","On the bottom section":"最下層","Halfway up the column":"蒸餾柱的中段","It is the same on every section":"每一層都一樣","The higher the vapour rises, the richer in alcohol it gets: the top section is the strongest.":"蒸氣上升得越高，酒精含量就越高：最上層的濃度最高。","The bottom section, where hot vapour enters, holds the weakest liquid. Strength is neither uniform nor highest in the middle: it rises step by step, which is why the spirit leaves from the top.":"熱蒸氣進入的最下層，液體濃度最低。濃度既不是處處相同，也不是中段最高：而是逐層上升，所以烈酒從頂部流出。","A distiller wants continuous production but a spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, similar to a pot still spirit. What should be chosen?":"蒸餾師想要連續生產，但希望烈酒的香氣中等或濃郁，類似壺式蒸餾器的烈酒。應該選擇什麼？","A short column with few sections":"層數少的矮蒸餾柱","A very tall column with many sections":"層數很多的高蒸餾柱","A pot still used three times":"使用三次的壺式蒸餾器","A tall column followed by dilution with water":"高蒸餾柱再加水稀釋","A short column runs continuously but stops at a lower strength, keeping aromas.":"矮蒸餾柱可連續運作，但停在較低的濃度，因而保留香氣。","A very tall column reaches high strengths and gives light or neutral spirits. A pot still works in batches, so it does not meet the need for continuous production. Diluting with water lowers the strength but brings back no aroma: the water is pure and adds no flavour.":"很高的蒸餾柱能達到高濃度，得到清淡或中性的烈酒。壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，無法滿足連續生產的需求。加水稀釋會降低濃度，但不會找回香氣：水是純的，不帶任何風味。","A producer needs a spirit at 95% abv. Which equipment is required?":"生產者需要 95% abv 的烈酒，必須使用什麼設備？","A very tall column still":"很高的柱式蒸餾器","A pot still and double distillation":"壺式蒸餾器加二次蒸餾","A long fermentation with lots of yeast":"使用大量酵母長時間發酵","Only the tallest columns, with the most sections, reach 95–96% abv.":"只有層數最多的最高蒸餾柱才能達到 95–96% abv。","Double pot still distillation stops at around 75%, and no number of passes will produce a neutral spirit. A short column gives lower-strength, more aromatic spirits. Fermentation, however long, only reaches around 8–10%.":"壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾大約停在 75%，蒸餾再多次也得不到中性烈酒。矮蒸餾柱得到的是濃度較低、香氣較豐富的烈酒。發酵不論多久，都只能達到大約 8–10%。","Why do most pot still distillers distil twice?":"為什麼大多數使用壺式蒸餾器的蒸餾師要蒸餾兩次？","Because a single pass is not enough to make a spirit":"因為只蒸餾一次不足以製成烈酒","Because the second pass makes the spirit neutral":"因為第二次蒸餾會讓烈酒變成中性","Because the first pass only cleans the still":"因為第一次蒸餾只是在清洗蒸餾器","Because the second pass adds sugar and colour":"因為第二次蒸餾會加入糖和顏色","From the fermented liquid, one pass only reaches about 25%: a second is needed to make a spirit.":"從發酵液開始，蒸餾一次只能達到約 25%：必須再蒸餾一次才能製成烈酒。","Even after two passes the spirit stays around 75% and full of character: it does not become neutral. Cleaning happens between batches, not through a distillation. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: sugar and colour can only be added afterwards.":"即使蒸餾兩次，烈酒的濃度仍在約 75%，而且充滿個性：不會變成中性。清洗是在批次之間進行，而不是靠蒸餾。而且所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是無色、不甜的：糖和顏色只能之後再添加。","What is a newly made spirit like as it leaves the still?":"剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒是什麼樣子？","Colourless and dry":"無色、不甜","Golden and dry":"金黃色、不甜","Colourless and slightly sweet":"無色、微甜","Amber and sweet":"琥珀色、甜","Every spirit is born clear and sugar-free; colour and sweetness only come later.":"所有烈酒誕生時都是清澈無糖的；顏色和甜味都是之後才出現。","A golden or amber colour comes from oak or caramel, so from the post-distillation stage. Sugar does not travel with the vapours through the still, which is why any sweetness must be added afterwards.":"金黃色或琥珀色來自橡木桶或焦糖色，也就是蒸餾後處理階段。糖不會隨著蒸氣通過蒸餾器，所以任何甜味都必須之後再添加。","What is the main aim of the post-distillation stage?":"蒸餾後處理階段的主要目的是什麼？","Adjusting colour, aroma, sweetness and strength to suit the style":"依照風格調整顏色、香氣、甜度與濃度","Turning the remaining alcohol into sugar":"把剩下的酒精轉化為糖","Raising the strength up to 96%":"把濃度提高到 96%","Restarting fermentation":"重新開始發酵","After the still, colour, aroma, sweetness and strength are adjusted for the spirit being made.":"離開蒸餾器之後，會依照要製作的烈酒調整顏色、香氣、甜度與濃度。","Alcohol does not turn back into sugar: sweetness, if wanted, is added. After distillation the strength usually goes down through dilution rather than up. And fermentation belongs to an earlier step, before the still.":"酒精不會變回糖：如果需要甜味，就要另外添加。蒸餾後的濃度通常是透過稀釋往下降，而不是往上升。發酵則屬於更早、蒸餾之前的步驟。","Where does an unaged spirit rest for a short time?":"未陳年的烈酒會在哪裡短暫靜置？","In stainless steel tanks":"不鏽鋼桶槽","In new oak barrels":"新的橡木桶","In used oak barrels":"用過的橡木桶","In the pot of the still":"蒸餾器的蒸餾鍋","Stainless steel adds no colour or aroma, so the spirit stays as it was.":"不鏽鋼不會增添顏色或香氣，所以烈酒會保持原樣。","Any oak barrel, new or used, adds colour and aroma: that is exactly what ageing means. The pot of the still is for distilling, not for storing the finished spirit.":"任何橡木桶，不論新舊，都會增添顏色和香氣：這正是陳年的意義。蒸餾鍋是用來蒸餾的，不是用來存放成品烈酒的。","In what order does a spirit's colour change as it ages in oak?":"烈酒在橡木桶中陳年時，顏色依什麼順序變化？","Lemon → gold → amber → brown":"檸檬黃 → 金黃 → 琥珀 → 棕色","Gold → lemon → brown → amber":"金黃 → 檸檬黃 → 棕色 → 琥珀","Amber → gold → lemon → brown":"琥珀 → 金黃 → 檸檬黃 → 棕色","Lemon → amber → brown → gold":"檸檬黃 → 琥珀 → 棕色 → 金黃","Colour darkens gradually from lemon to gold to amber, and only rarely to brown.":"顏色會從檸檬黃逐漸加深到金黃、琥珀，只有少數會變成棕色。","The other sequences jumble the order: oak always darkens a spirit, so it never goes back from amber to lemon or from brown to gold. Brown is the end point and is seen only very rarely.":"其他順序都打亂了：橡木桶總是讓烈酒顏色變深，所以不會從琥珀退回檸檬黃，也不會從棕色變回金黃。棕色是終點，而且非常少見。","Which barrel gives the most aroma to a spirit?":"哪一種桶能為烈酒帶來最多香氣？","A new oak barrel that has never been used":"從未使用過的新橡木桶","A barrel already used twice":"已經用過兩次的桶","A barrel used many times":"用過很多次的桶","A stainless steel tank":"不鏽鋼桶槽","A new barrel still has all of its aromas to give.":"新桶仍保有全部可釋出的香氣。","Each time a barrel is used it gives less aroma, so a barrel used twice or many times always gives less than a new one. Stainless steel gives nothing at all: that is precisely why it is used to keep a spirit unchanged.":"桶子每使用一次，釋出的香氣就會減少，所以用過兩次或很多次的桶，香氣總是比新桶少。不鏽鋼則完全不會帶來香氣：這正是用它來讓烈酒保持不變的原因。","Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut":"香草、肉桂、丁香、椰子","Cut grass, olive, pepper":"割下的青草、橄欖、胡椒","Apple, lemon, white flowers":"蘋果、檸檬、白花","Juniper, coriander, citrus peel":"杜松子、芫荽籽、柑橘皮","Vanilla, warm spices and coconut are oak's classic signature.":"香草、溫暖的香料和椰子是橡木桶的經典標誌。","Grass, olive and pepper point to a raw material such as agave. Apple and flowers suggest fruit and fermentation, not wood. Juniper and coriander are plants added to flavour a spirit such as gin.":"青草、橄欖和胡椒指向龍舌蘭這類原料。蘋果和花香暗示水果和發酵，而不是木頭。杜松子和芫荽籽是用來為琴酒這類烈酒調味的植物。","Why does a spirit become more concentrated during long ageing?":"為什麼烈酒在長時間陳年後會變得更濃縮？","Because water and ethanol evaporate through the barrel":"因為水和乙醇會透過橡木桶蒸發","Because the oak adds sugar to the spirit":"因為橡木桶會在烈酒中加入糖","Because the alcohol level rises every year":"因為酒精濃度每年都會上升","Because fermentation restarts in the barrel":"因為發酵會在桶中重新開始","As water and ethanol evaporate, the remaining aromas become concentrated.":"水和乙醇蒸發後，剩下的香氣就變得更濃縮。","Oak gives colour and aroma, not sugar: sweetness is added separately. The point is not a rising strength, since ethanol evaporates too. And there is no sugar left in the barrel to ferment.":"橡木桶帶來的是顏色和香氣，不是糖：甜味是另外添加的。重點也不在濃度上升，因為乙醇同樣會蒸發。而且桶中已經沒有糖可以發酵。","A spirit has spent several decades in barrel. Which aromas are most likely?":"一款烈酒在桶中度過了數十年，最可能出現哪些香氣？","Fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish":"水果蛋糕、果乾、皮革、木頭亮光蠟","Fresh grass, green apple, white flowers":"新鮮青草、青蘋果、白花","No aroma at all: the spirit becomes neutral":"完全沒有香氣：烈酒變成中性","Only light vanilla, as after a few months":"只有淡淡的香草，就像陳年幾個月之後","Very long ageing brings complex aromas of dried fruit, leather and polish.":"非常長的陳年會帶來果乾、皮革和亮光蠟等複雜香氣。","Fresh grass and green apple suggest a young spirit. Oak adds aromas rather than removing them, so the spirit does not become neutral. A light vanilla note is typical of short ageing, whereas decades bring concentration and new layers.":"新鮮青草和青蘋果暗示年輕的烈酒。橡木桶會增添香氣而不是去除香氣，所以烈酒不會變成中性。淡淡的香草是短期陳年的典型特徵，而數十年的陳年則帶來濃縮感和新的層次。","What are the two main aims of blending oak-aged spirits?":"調和經橡木桶陳年的烈酒，兩個主要目的是什麼？","Sweetness and colour":"甜度和顏色","Higher strength and less aroma":"提高濃度並減少香氣","Faster ageing and fewer barrels":"加快陳年並減少用桶","Blending keeps every bottle tasting the same and builds depth.":"調和能讓每一瓶的風味保持一致，並增加深度。","Sweetness and colour are adjusted with sugar and caramel, separate steps from blending. Mixing barrels neither raises the strength nor strips aroma. Blending does not shorten ageing; in fact it needs many different barrels.":"甜度和顏色是用糖和焦糖色調整的，是與調和不同的步驟。混合不同的桶既不會提高濃度，也不會去除香氣。調和不會縮短陳年時間；事實上，調和需要許多不同的桶。","Why does a blender add small amounts of caramel colouring?":"為什麼調和師要加入少量焦糖色？","To give every batch the same colour":"讓每一批的顏色都一樣","To make the spirit sweeter":"讓烈酒更甜","To add vanilla aromas":"增添香草香氣","Barrels give different shades; caramel evens out the colour from batch to batch.":"不同的桶會帶來不同的色調；焦糖色能讓每批的顏色保持一致。","Caramel colouring is not sweet and, used properly, adds no aroma: vanilla comes from oak. It contains no alcohol, so it cannot raise the strength. It is there purely for appearance.":"焦糖色不甜，正確使用時也不會增添香氣：香草來自橡木桶。它不含酒精，所以無法提高濃度。它純粹是為了外觀。","A customer says: 'This spirit is dark, so it must have been aged for a long time.' What is the best reply?":"一位顧客說：「這款烈酒顏色很深，一定陳年很久了。」最好的回答是什麼？","Not necessarily: the colour can come almost entirely from caramel":"不一定：顏色可能幾乎完全來自焦糖色","Yes, only oak can colour a spirit":"沒錯，只有橡木桶能讓烈酒上色","Yes, because a dark colour always means a new barrel":"沒錯，因為深色一定代表新桶","No, because aged spirits are always pale":"不對，因為陳年烈酒一定顏色很淺","Some spirits get all or nearly all their colour from caramel, so colour does not prove age.":"有些烈酒的顏色全部或幾乎全部來自焦糖色，所以顏色無法證明年份。","Oak is not the only source of colour: there is caramel and other colourings. A new barrel does give more colour, but dark colour can have other causes. And aged spirits are not always pale: oak tends to darken them over time.":"橡木桶不是顏色的唯一來源：還有焦糖色和其他著色劑。新桶確實會帶來更多顏色，但深色也可能有其他原因。而且陳年烈酒不一定顏色淺：橡木桶通常會隨著時間讓顏色變深。","Where does the sweetness you taste in a spirit come from?":"你在烈酒中嚐到的甜味來自哪裡？","From sugar added after distillation":"來自蒸餾後添加的糖","From the raw material's sugar passing through the still":"來自通過蒸餾器的原料糖分","From caramel colouring":"來自焦糖色","From the water used for dilution":"來自稀釋用的水","Every spirit leaves the still dry, so sweetness has to be added later, usually as sugar.":"所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的，所以甜味必須之後再添加，通常是糖。","The raw material's sugar is eaten by yeast and does not travel with the vapours anyway. Caramel colouring is not sweet. Dilution water is pure and brings neither flavour nor sugar.":"原料的糖會被酵母吃掉，而且本來就不會隨著蒸氣移動。焦糖色不甜。稀釋用的水是純水，既不帶風味也不帶糖。","A whiskey with no added sugar has intense vanilla and fruit aromas. How should its palate be described?":"一款沒有加糖的威士忌，有濃郁的香草和水果香氣。它的口感應該怎麼描述？","Dry, because sweet refers only to the taste of sugar":"不甜，因為「甜」只指糖的味道","Sweet, because vanilla and fruit are sweet aromas":"甜，因為香草和水果是甜美的香氣","Sweet, because oak adds sugar":"甜，因為橡木桶會加入糖","Neutral, because it has no sugar":"中性，因為它沒有糖","With no added sugar the spirit is dry, even if the nose smells sweet.":"沒有加糖的烈酒就是不甜的，即使聞起來很甜美。","Calling vanilla and fruit aromas sweet causes confusion: sweetness is a taste, tied to sugar. Oak adds no sugar. Neutral, on the other hand, describes a spirit with almost no aroma, the opposite of this whiskey.":"把香草和水果香氣說成「甜」會造成混淆：甜度是一種味道，與糖有關。橡木桶不會加入糖。而「中性」是描述幾乎沒有香氣的烈酒，正好與這款威士忌相反。","Why are most spirits diluted to 40% abv before bottling?":"為什麼大多數烈酒在裝瓶前會稀釋到 40% abv？","To make them drinkable: too much alcohol numbs the palate":"讓它適合飲用：酒精太多會麻痺味覺","To add aromas through the water":"透過水增添香氣","To make them sweeter":"讓它更甜","To give them a paler, even colour":"讓顏色更淺、更均勻","At very high strength it is impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit.":"濃度非常高時，根本無法品嚐或享受烈酒。","The water is completely pure and adds no aroma or sugar. Colour is managed with oak or caramel, not water. Dilution only lowers the strength.":"水是完全的純水，不會增添香氣或糖。顏色是靠橡木桶或焦糖色控制，而不是水。稀釋只會降低濃度。","Which of these steps adds no aroma to the spirit?":"下列哪個步驟不會為烈酒增添香氣？","Dilution with pure water":"用純水稀釋","Ageing in a new barrel":"在新桶中陳年","Macerating herbs and spices":"浸漬香草和香料","Fermentation with yeast":"用酵母發酵","Pure water only lowers the strength and brings no flavour.":"純水只會降低濃度，不帶任何風味。","A new barrel is the richest source of oak aroma. Maceration exists precisely to draw flavour out of plants. And fermentation creates fruity aromas as well as alcohol.":"新桶是橡木香氣最豐富的來源。浸漬的目的正是從植物中萃取風味。而發酵除了產生酒精，也會產生果香。","What are the three most common ways to give a spirit flavours other than oak?":"除了橡木桶之外，為烈酒增添風味最常見的三種方法是什麼？","Redistillation, maceration, adding flavourings":"再蒸餾、浸漬、添加調味料","Fermentation, blending, dilution":"發酵、調和、稀釋","Caramel, sugar, water":"焦糖色、糖、水","New barrel, used barrel, stainless steel":"新桶、舊桶、不鏽鋼","The spirit is redistilled with plants, steeped with them, or given ready-made flavourings.":"烈酒會與植物一起再蒸餾、用植物浸泡，或加入現成的調味料。","Blending and dilution add no new flavours, and fermentation comes before the still. Caramel and water bring no aroma, while sugar brings sweetness. Barrels give exactly the oak flavours being excluded, and steel gives none.":"調和與稀釋不會增添新的風味，發酵則在蒸餾之前。焦糖色和水不帶香氣，糖則帶來甜味。橡木桶帶來的正是題目排除的橡木風味，不鏽鋼則什麼都不帶來。","Which flavouring technique also gives the spirit colour?":"哪一種調味技術也會為烈酒帶來顏色？","Dilution":"稀釋","Column distillation":"柱式蒸餾","When plants steep in the spirit, both flavour and colour pass into it.":"植物浸泡在烈酒中時，風味和顏色都會進入烈酒。","Redistilling with plants gives a flavoured but colourless liquid, because colour does not travel with the vapours. Dilution uses pure water. A column still is for distilling, not flavouring.":"與植物一起再蒸餾會得到有風味但無色的液體，因為顏色不會隨著蒸氣移動。稀釋使用的是純水。柱式蒸餾器是用來蒸餾的，不是用來調味的。","Which statement about post-distillation choices is correct?":"關於蒸餾後處理的選擇，下列哪一項正確？","Scotch must be oak-aged, while Tequila may be aged or not":"Scotch 必須在橡木桶中陳年，Tequila 則可陳年也可不陳年","Tequila must be oak-aged, while Scotch may be aged or not":"Tequila 必須在橡木桶中陳年，Scotch 則可陳年也可不陳年","Producers are always free: the law never steps in":"生產者永遠可以自由選擇：法律從不介入","Every spirit must spend at least a year in oak":"所有烈酒都必須在橡木桶中至少陳年一年","Local laws limit the options: Scotch must be aged, Tequila can be young or aged.":"當地法律會限制選擇：Scotch 必須陳年，Tequila 可以年輕也可以陳年。","The second option swaps the two cases. The law often steps in, so producers are not always free. And many spirits, vodka for one, never see oak: no rule imposes a year on all of them.":"第二個選項把兩者對調了。法律經常介入，所以生產者並非永遠能自由選擇。而許多烈酒（例如伏特加）從未接觸橡木桶：沒有任何規定要求所有烈酒陳年一年。","What is a grape brandy such as Cognac?":"Cognac 這類葡萄白蘭地是什麼？","A distilled wine":"蒸餾過的葡萄酒","Grape juice distilled without fermentation":"未經發酵直接蒸餾的葡萄汁","A wine strengthened with neutral spirit":"加入中性烈酒強化的葡萄酒","A grain spirit flavoured with grapes":"以葡萄調味的穀物烈酒","Grape juice is fermented into wine, and that wine is distilled.":"葡萄汁先發酵成葡萄酒，再將這款葡萄酒蒸餾。","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil, so the juice must first become wine. Adding spirit to a wine is not distilling it. And Cognac is made from grapes, not flavoured grain spirit.":"沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾，所以葡萄汁必須先變成葡萄酒。在葡萄酒中加入烈酒並不是蒸餾。而且 Cognac 是用葡萄製成，不是調味的穀物烈酒。","Where must the grapes for Cognac come from?":"Cognac 的葡萄必須來自哪裡？","From an area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux":"法國西南部、Bordeaux 以北的一個產區","From any vineyard in France":"法國任何一座葡萄園","From an area of south-east France, near the Mediterranean":"法國東南部、靠近地中海的一個產區","From any country, as long as it is distilled in France":"任何國家，只要在法國蒸餾即可","Cognac requires grapes from a specific area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux.":"Cognac 規定葡萄必須來自法國西南部、Bordeaux 以北的特定產區。","It is not enough for the grapes to be French: they must come from that defined area. South-east France is a different region. And the place of distillation alone does not count: the grapes themselves must be grown in the area.":"光是法國葡萄還不夠：必須來自這個劃定的產區。法國東南部是另一個地區。而且只看蒸餾地點也不算數：葡萄本身必須種植在該產區內。","Which aromas do the grapes bring to Cognac?":"葡萄為 Cognac 帶來哪些香氣？","Vanilla and toast":"香草和烘烤","Herbal and peppery":"草本和胡椒","Cereal and smoke":"穀物和煙燻","Grapes, the raw material, give Cognac its fruity and floral notes.":"葡萄這項原料為 Cognac 帶來果香和花香。","Vanilla and toast are there, but they come from oak, not grapes. Herbal and peppery notes are typical of agave. Cereal and smoke suggest a malt whisky, not a wine spirit.":"香草和烘烤確實存在，但來自橡木桶，而不是葡萄。草本和胡椒是龍舌蘭的典型特徵。穀物和煙燻則暗示麥芽威士忌，而不是葡萄酒蒸餾的烈酒。","What happens to the freshly pressed juice destined for Cognac?":"用來製作 Cognac 的新鮮壓榨葡萄汁會怎麼處理？","It is fermented straight away into wine":"立刻發酵成葡萄酒","It is distilled at once, before fermenting":"在發酵前立即蒸餾","It is cooked to create sugar":"加熱烹煮以產生糖","It is aged in oak for two years":"在橡木桶中陳年兩年","Grape juice is already full of sugar, so it is fermented into wine right away.":"葡萄汁本身已含有大量的糖，所以會立刻發酵成葡萄酒。","Distilling before fermentation would leave no alcohol to concentrate. Cooking to create sugar is for raw materials like agave, not grapes. The two years in oak apply to the spirit after distillation, not to the juice.":"在發酵前蒸餾，就沒有酒精可以濃縮。烹煮產生糖是龍舌蘭這類原料的做法，不是葡萄。兩年的橡木桶陳年是針對蒸餾後的烈酒，而不是葡萄汁。","How must Cognac be distilled by law?":"依法規，Cognac 必須如何蒸餾？","Twice in a pot still":"在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","Once in a tall column still":"在高柱式蒸餾器中蒸餾一次","Only once in a pot still":"在壺式蒸餾器中只蒸餾一次","Continuously, up to 96% abv":"連續蒸餾到 96% abv","The law requires double distillation in a pot still.":"法規要求以壺式蒸餾器進行二次蒸餾。","A column and continuous distillation to 96% would give a light or neutral spirit, far from the Cognac style. A single pass through a pot still is not enough to make a spirit from wine.":"使用蒸餾柱連續蒸餾到 96%，會得到清淡或中性的烈酒，與 Cognac 的風格相去甚遠。而只通過壺式蒸餾器一次，不足以把葡萄酒製成烈酒。","Why is a pot still used for Cognac?":"為什麼 Cognac 使用壺式蒸餾器？","It gives a low-strength spirit full of flavour and character":"能得到濃度較低、風味豐富且有個性的烈酒","It gives a neutral spirit that is easy to flavour":"能得到容易調味的中性烈酒","It runs continuously and is very fast":"能連續運作，速度很快","It adds colour and sweetness by itself":"本身就能增添顏色和甜味","The low strength keeps the grape aromas and gives a characterful spirit.":"較低的濃度保留了葡萄的香氣，得到有個性的烈酒。","A pot still cannot make a neutral spirit: that is the job of the tallest columns. It works in batches, so it is slow rather than continuous. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: colour and sweetness come later.":"壺式蒸餾器無法製作中性烈酒：那是最高的蒸餾柱的工作。它以批次運作，所以速度慢，而不是連續的。而且所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是無色、不甜的：顏色和甜味之後才出現。","How are Cognac pot stills traditionally heated?":"Cognac 的壺式蒸餾器傳統上用什麼加熱？","With gas burners":"瓦斯爐火","With steam coils":"蒸汽盤管","With electric elements":"電熱元件","With heat from the sun":"太陽熱能","Cognac stills still use gas burners.":"Cognac 的蒸餾器至今仍使用瓦斯爐火。","Steam, through jackets or coils, heats many modern pot stills, which is exactly why it is the trap: Cognac is the exception. Electric elements and solar heat are not the traditional method.":"透過夾套或盤管的蒸汽是許多現代壺式蒸餾器的加熱方式，這正是陷阱所在：Cognac 是例外。電熱元件和太陽熱能都不是傳統做法。","What is the minimum time in oak before a spirit can be called Cognac?":"烈酒至少要在橡木桶中陳年多久，才能稱為 Cognac？","Four years":"四年","The law requires at least two years in oak barrels.":"法規要求在橡木桶中至少陳年兩年。","Six months is not enough. Four years is the minimum for VSOP and ten years for XO: these are higher ages tied to specific categories, not the threshold for using the name at all.":"六個月不夠。四年是 VSOP 的最低要求，十年是 XO 的最低要求：這些是特定等級的較高年份，而不是能使用這個名稱的門檻。","Which aromas does oak give a young Cognac?":"橡木桶為年輕的 Cognac 帶來哪些香氣？","Flowers and fresh fruit":"花香和新鮮水果","Grass and olive":"青草和橄欖","Time in barrel adds vanilla and toasty notes to Cognac.":"在桶中的時間為 Cognac 增添了香草和烘烤風味。","Flowers and fresh fruit come from the grapes, not the wood. Peat smoke is found in some malt whiskies. Grass and olive are typical agave notes.":"花香和新鮮水果來自葡萄，而不是木頭。泥煤煙燻出現在某些麥芽威士忌中。青草和橄欖是龍舌蘭的典型風味。","A very old Cognac shows fruit cake and leather aromas. Where do they come from?":"一款非常老的 Cognac 帶有水果蛋糕和皮革香氣，這些香氣來自哪裡？","From the fermentation of the juice":"來自葡萄汁的發酵","From double distillation":"來自二次蒸餾","Many years in oak concentrate the spirit and develop these complex aromas.":"在橡木桶中的多年時光讓烈酒濃縮，發展出這些複雜香氣。","Fermentation mainly creates fresh fruity aromas, not evolved notes like leather. Double distillation keeps the grape aromas but does not create the aromas of age. Caramel, used properly, adds no aroma.":"發酵主要產生新鮮的果香，而不是皮革這類演化後的風味。二次蒸餾保留了葡萄的香氣，但不會產生陳年的香氣。焦糖色正確使用時不會增添香氣。","Which statement about Cognac is correct?":"關於 Cognac，下列哪一項正確？","Nearly all Cognacs are blends":"幾乎所有 Cognac 都是調和的","Nearly all Cognacs come from a single barrel":"幾乎所有 Cognac 都來自單一酒桶","Cognac may never be blended":"Cognac 絕對不能調和","Cognac is only blended with vodka":"Cognac 只會與伏特加調和","Combining spirits of different ages adds complexity, and nearly all Cognacs are blends.":"結合不同年份的烈酒能增添複雜度，幾乎所有 Cognac 都是調和的。","Single-barrel Cognacs are the exception, not the rule. Blending is not forbidden; it is the norm. And Cognac spirits are blended with each other, not with other spirits such as vodka.":"單桶 Cognac 是例外，而不是常態。調和並未被禁止，反而是常態。而且 Cognac 的烈酒是彼此調和，而不是與伏特加等其他烈酒調和。","Which adjustments are common for Cognac before dilution and bottling?":"Cognac 在稀釋和裝瓶前，常見的調整有哪些？","A little caramel colouring and slight sweetening":"少量焦糖色和輕微加甜","Adding herbs by maceration":"以浸漬方式加入香草","A third distillation in a column":"用蒸餾柱進行第三次蒸餾","Charcoal filtering to remove the colour":"用木炭過濾去除顏色","Many producers use caramel to even out the colour and sweeten their Cognac slightly.":"許多生產者會用焦糖色統一顏色，並為 Cognac 稍微加甜。","Macerating herbs would turn Cognac into a flavoured spirit. Distillation happens only in pot stills, never columns. Stripping colour with charcoal would make no sense for a spirit valued precisely for the shade oak gives it.":"浸漬香草會讓 Cognac 變成調味烈酒。蒸餾只在壺式蒸餾器中進行，從不使用蒸餾柱。用木炭去除顏色毫無意義，因為這種烈酒受重視的正是橡木桶帶來的色澤。","What does the term VS guarantee on a Cognac?":"Cognac 上的 VS 保證什麼？","At least 2 years of ageing":"至少陳年 2 年","At least 4 years of ageing":"至少陳年 4 年","At least 10 years of ageing":"至少陳年 10 年","At least 6 months of ageing":"至少陳年 6 個月","VS matches the legal minimum: at least 2 years.":"VS 對應法定最低要求：至少 2 年。","4 years is the minimum for VSOP and 10 years for XO. Six months is below the legal minimum: a spirit that young cannot even be called Cognac.":"4 年是 VSOP 的最低要求，10 年是 XO 的最低要求。六個月低於法定最低要求：這麼年輕的烈酒甚至不能稱為 Cognac。","What minimum age does VSOP guarantee?":"VSOP 保證的最低年份是多少？","4 years":"4 年","6 years":"6 年","10 years":"10 年","VSOP guarantees the youngest spirit is at least 4 years old.":"VSOP 保證其中最年輕的烈酒至少 4 年。","2 years is VS and 10 years is XO. 6 years is not tied to any of the three terms: it sounds plausible but is made up.":"2 年是 VS，10 年是 XO。6 年與這三個術語都無關：聽起來合理，但是編造的。","A customer wants the Cognac with the longest minimum ageing. Which term should they look for?":"一位顧客想要最低陳年時間最長的 Cognac，應該找哪個術語？","XO, at least 10 years":"XO，至少 10 年","VSOP, at least 4 years":"VSOP，至少 4 年","VS, at least 2 years":"VS，至少 2 年","XO, at least 6 years":"XO，至少 6 年","Of the three terms, XO guarantees the highest minimum age: 10 years.":"在這三個術語中，XO 保證的最低年份最高：10 年。","VSOP and VS guarantee 4 and 2 years respectively, so less. The last option names the right term with the wrong age: the XO minimum is 10 years.":"VSOP 和 VS 分別保證 4 年和 2 年，所以比較少。最後一個選項術語正確但年份錯誤：XO 的最低要求是 10 年。","Which spirit does the age shown by VS, VSOP or XO refer to?":"VS、VSOP 或 XO 標示的年份，指的是哪一個烈酒？","The youngest spirit in the blend":"調和中最年輕的烈酒","The oldest spirit in the blend":"調和中最老的烈酒","The average age of the spirits":"所有烈酒的平均年份","The years spent in the bottle":"在瓶中度過的年數","The term guarantees a minimum age, which means the age of the youngest spirit.":"術語保證的是最低年份，也就是最年輕烈酒的年份。","If the oldest spirit counted, a single old drop could lift the category. An average would also let very young spirits hide in the blend. Time in bottle does not count: ageing happens in barrel.":"如果以最老的烈酒來算，一滴老酒就能提升整體的等級。用平均值也會讓很年輕的烈酒藏在調和裡。瓶中的時間不算：陳年是在桶中進行的。","A blend contains Cognacs aged 5, 8 and 15 years. What is the highest age term it can carry?":"一款調和包含陳年 5 年、8 年和 15 年的 Cognac，它能標示的最高年份術語是什麼？","VS only":"只能標 VS","No age term":"不能標示任何年份術語","The youngest spirit counts, 5 years: that beats VSOP's 4 years but not XO's 10.":"以最年輕的烈酒為準，也就是 5 年：超過 VSOP 的 4 年，但未達 XO 的 10 年。","XO would need even the youngest spirit to be at least 10, and here it is only 5. VS would be allowed, but it is not the highest possible term. The blend is well past the 2-year minimum, so it can carry a term.":"XO 要求連最年輕的烈酒都至少 10 年，而這裡只有 5 年。VS 是允許的，但不是能標示的最高術語。這款調和遠超過 2 年的最低要求，所以可以標示術語。","A wine spirit from the Cognac area, distilled by the rules, has spent 18 months in oak. Can it be sold as Cognac?":"一款來自 Cognac 產區、依規定蒸餾的葡萄酒烈酒，在橡木桶中陳年了 18 個月。它可以用 Cognac 的名義販售嗎？","No, it needs at least two years in oak":"不行，至少需要在橡木桶中陳年兩年","Yes, as a VS":"可以，標為 VS","Yes, as long as it was distilled twice":"可以，只要蒸餾過兩次","Yes, if caramel is added":"可以，只要加入焦糖色","With less than two years in oak, the name Cognac is not allowed.":"在橡木桶中不滿兩年，就不能使用 Cognac 這個名稱。","VS is the youngest term but still requires at least 2 years. Double distillation is compulsory but does not replace ageing. Caramel only changes the colour, not the age.":"VS 是最年輕的術語，但仍要求至少 2 年。二次蒸餾是強制規定，但不能取代陳年。焦糖色只會改變顏色，不會改變年份。","What makes a spirit a vodka?":"什麼條件讓一款烈酒成為伏特加？","Its distillation strength":"它的蒸餾濃度","The raw material used":"使用的原料","The country of production":"生產國家","The time spent in barrel":"在桶中的時間","Vodka is defined by its very high distillation strength.":"伏特加的定義是極高的蒸餾濃度。","The raw material can be anything and vodka can be made in any country, so neither plant nor place defines it. Vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged.":"原料可以是任何東西，伏特加也可以在任何國家生產，所以植物和地點都不是定義條件。伏特加不會進桶：它維持未陳年。","Which raw material can vodka be made from?":"伏特加可以用哪種原料製成？","Any plant-based raw material":"任何植物性原料","Potatoes only":"只能用馬鈴薯","Rye only":"只能用黑麥","Grapes only":"只能用葡萄","Vodka has no required raw material: any plant will do.":"伏特加沒有規定的原料：任何植物都可以。","Potatoes and rye are favoured for premium vodka, but they are not compulsory. Grapes are possible too, but they are not the only choice: no ingredient is required.":"高級伏特加偏好使用馬鈴薯和黑麥，但並非強制。葡萄也可以，但不是唯一的選擇：沒有任何必須使用的原料。","Where can vodka be made?":"伏特加可以在哪裡生產？","In any country in the world":"世界上任何國家","Only in Russia and Poland":"只能在俄羅斯和波蘭","Only in northern Europe":"只能在北歐","Only where potatoes are grown":"只能在種植馬鈴薯的地方","Vodka has no required area of origin.":"伏特加沒有規定的原產地。","Some countries have a long vodka tradition, but the law does not restrict production to them or to any region. And since the raw material is free, there is no need to grow potatoes to make it.":"有些國家有悠久的伏特加傳統，但法律並未把生產限制在這些國家或任何地區。而且原料可以自由選擇，所以不需要種植馬鈴薯也能生產。","Which raw materials are often linked with premium vodka?":"哪些原料常與高級伏特加聯想在一起？","Cereals such as barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes":"大麥、小麥和黑麥等穀物，以及馬鈴薯","Sugar cane and molasses":"甘蔗和糖蜜","Blue agave and corn":"藍色龍舌蘭和玉米","Grapes and apples":"葡萄和蘋果","Cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, plus potatoes are the classic premium vodka raw materials.":"穀物（尤其是大麥、小麥和黑麥）加上馬鈴薯，是高級伏特加的經典原料。","Sugar cane and molasses point to rum. Blue agave is Tequila's raw material. Grapes and apples can be used, but they are not the ones linked with premium vodka.":"甘蔗和糖蜜指向蘭姆酒。藍色龍舌蘭是 Tequila 的原料。葡萄和蘋果可以使用，但不是與高級伏特加聯想在一起的原料。","To what minimum strength must a neutral spirit be distilled?":"中性烈酒至少必須蒸餾到多少濃度？","95% or 96% abv, depending on national law":"95% 或 96% abv，視各國法律而定","40% abv, as in the bottle":"40% abv，和瓶中一樣","75% abv, as after double distillation":"75% abv，和二次蒸餾後一樣","60% abv in every country":"所有國家都是 60% abv","A neutral spirit must reach at least 95% or 96%, depending on local law.":"中性烈酒必須至少達到 95% 或 96%，視當地法律而定。","40% is the strength after dilution, not the distillation strength. Around 75% is typical of double pot still distillation, with plenty of aroma. 60% is the lowest strength for newly made spirits, the most aromatic ones: the opposite of neutral.":"40% 是稀釋後的濃度，不是蒸餾濃度。約 75% 是壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾的典型濃度，香氣豐富。60% 是剛製成烈酒的最低濃度，屬於香氣最豐富的烈酒：正好與中性相反。","Which type of still is essential for making vodka?":"製作伏特加不可或缺的是哪一種蒸餾器？","No still: fermentation is enough":"不需要蒸餾器：發酵就夠了","Only a column still can reach the 95–96% needed for a neutral spirit.":"只有柱式蒸餾器能達到中性烈酒所需的 95–96%。","Some producers use pot stills for part of the process, but on their own they cannot reach a neutral spirit. Fermentation stops at around 8–10%. A barrel is not a still, and vodka is not aged in oak.":"有些生產者會在部分流程中使用壺式蒸餾器，但光靠壺式蒸餾器無法得到中性烈酒。發酵大約在 8–10% 就停止。木桶不是蒸餾器，而且伏特加不在橡木桶中陳年。","Why is the spirit behind vodka called neutral?":"為什麼作為伏特加基底的烈酒被稱為中性？","Because at that strength it has almost no aroma":"因為在那個濃度下幾乎沒有香氣","Because it contains no alcohol":"因為它不含酒精","Because it has the same strength as water":"因為它的濃度和水一樣","Because it can be sold in any country":"因為它可以在任何國家販售","Distilled to 95–96%, the spirit loses almost all aroma and becomes neutral.":"蒸餾到 95–96% 時，烈酒幾乎失去所有香氣，成為中性。","Neutral refers to aroma, not alcohol: in fact it is one of the strongest spirits. It has nothing to do with water or where it can be sold; it describes an almost absent smell.":"「中性」指的是香氣，而不是酒精：事實上它是濃度最高的烈酒之一。這和水或能在哪裡販售都無關；它描述的是幾乎不存在的氣味。","What happens to vodka after distillation?":"伏特加在蒸餾後會怎麼處理？","It stays unaged and is diluted, usually to 40% abv":"維持未陳年，並稀釋，通常到 40% abv","It ages for at least two years in oak":"在橡木桶中至少陳年兩年","It is bottled at 96% abv without dilution":"以 96% abv 裝瓶，不經稀釋","It is always sweetened with sugar":"一定會加糖增甜","Vodka skips the barrel and is brought down to bottling strength with water.":"伏特加不進桶，並加水降到裝瓶濃度。","Two years in oak describes Cognac, not vodka. At 96% it would be undrinkable, as such strong alcohol numbs the palate. Sweetening is not part of vodka's basic recipe.":"在橡木桶中陳年兩年說的是 Cognac，不是伏特加。96% 的濃度根本無法飲用，因為這麼高的酒精會麻痺味覺。加甜也不屬於伏特加的基本做法。","Why is vodka so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails?":"為什麼伏特加在混合飲料和調酒中這麼受歡迎？","Because its neutrality makes it versatile":"因為它的中性讓它用途廣泛","Because it is sweeter than other spirits":"因為它比其他烈酒甜","Because it is lower in alcohol than other spirits":"因為它的酒精濃度比其他烈酒低","Because it has strong oak aromas":"因為它有濃郁的橡木香氣","With almost no aroma, vodka works with many ingredients without masking them.":"伏特加幾乎沒有香氣，能與許多材料搭配，而不會掩蓋它們。","Vodka is not sweet: like every spirit it leaves the still dry and is not normally sweetened. It is usually bottled at 40%, like many other spirits. And it is not aged in barrels, so it has no oak aromas.":"伏特加不甜：和所有烈酒一樣，它離開蒸餾器時是不甜的，通常也不會加甜。它通常以 40% 裝瓶，和許多其他烈酒一樣。而且它不在桶中陳年，所以沒有橡木香氣。","A vodka shows a faint hint of grain on the nose. How should it be classed?":"一款伏特加在香氣中帶有淡淡的穀物氣息，應該如何歸類？","Still neutral, but with a little character":"仍是中性，但帶有一點個性","No longer vodka, because it is not neutral":"不再是伏特加，因為它不是中性","A flavoured vodka":"調味伏特加","A young whisky":"年輕的威士忌","Faint raw-material notes are allowed: the vodka is still correctly called neutral.":"允許帶有淡淡的原料氣息：這款伏特加仍可正確地稱為中性。","Some vodkas keep a hint of character without ceasing to be vodka. A flavoured vodka has added flavourings, whereas here the grain note comes from the raw material. A whisky would be far more intense and aged in oak.":"有些伏特加保留了一點個性，但仍然是伏特加。調味伏特加是添加了調味料，而這裡的穀物氣息來自原料。威士忌的風味會濃郁得多，而且經過橡木桶陳年。","A bartender wants to make a fruit drink stronger without changing its taste. Which spirit fits best?":"調酒師想讓一杯水果飲料更有酒勁，但不改變它的味道。哪一種烈酒最合適？","An XO Cognac":"XO 等級的 Cognac","A peated malt whisky":"泥煤風格的麥芽威士忌","An aged Tequila":"陳年的 Tequila","Neutral vodka adds alcohol while adding almost no aroma.":"中性伏特加能增加酒精，卻幾乎不增添香氣。","An XO Cognac has intense dried fruit, leather and oak aromas. A peated whisky brings smoke. An aged Tequila combines agave and oak: all of them would change the drink's flavour.":"XO 等級的 Cognac 有濃郁的果乾、皮革和橡木香氣。泥煤威士忌帶來煙燻味。陳年 Tequila 結合了龍舌蘭和橡木：這些都會改變飲料的風味。","A producer has only pot stills and distils several times. Can this produce vodka's neutral spirit?":"一位生產者只有壺式蒸餾器，並蒸餾多次。這樣能得到伏特加的中性烈酒嗎？","No, 95–96% can only be reached with a column still":"不能，95–96% 只能用柱式蒸餾器達到","Yes, three distillations are enough":"可以，蒸餾三次就夠了","Yes, if water is added afterwards":"可以，只要之後加水","Yes, if potatoes are the raw material":"可以，只要原料是馬鈴薯","However many times it is used, a pot still cannot reach neutral-spirit strength.":"無論使用多少次，壺式蒸餾器都無法達到中性烈酒的濃度。","The number of passes is not enough: a column still is needed, possibly alongside pot stills for part of the process. Diluting lowers the strength rather than raising it. And the raw material does not change the still's limit.":"蒸餾次數不是關鍵：必須使用柱式蒸餾器，或許在部分流程中搭配壺式蒸餾器。稀釋是降低濃度，而不是提高。原料也不會改變蒸餾器的極限。","What raw material is whisky made from?":"威士忌是用什麼原料製成的？","Grains":"穀物","By definition, whisky is an oak-aged spirit made from grain.":"依照定義，威士忌是以穀物製成、經橡木桶陳年的烈酒。","Whisky can be pictured as distilled beer: it starts from grains such as barley, corn or rye. Grapes are the base of brandies like Cognac, and sugar cane is the base of rum. Potatoes can be used for vodka, but not for whisky.":"可以把威士忌想像成蒸餾過的啤酒：它從大麥、玉米或黑麥等穀物開始。葡萄是 Cognac 等白蘭地的基底，甘蔗是蘭姆酒的基底。馬鈴薯可以用來做伏特加，但不能做威士忌。","Why do grains need processing before fermentation?":"為什麼穀物在發酵前需要處理？","They hold starch, which must be turned into sugar":"穀物含有澱粉，必須轉化為糖","They hold too much sugar for the yeast":"穀物含糖太多，酵母無法負荷","They already hold alcohol, which must be removed":"穀物本身含有酒精，必須去除","They hold acids that stop the yeast working":"穀物含有會阻止酵母作用的酸","Yeast feed on sugar, but dry grains mostly contain starch.":"酵母以糖為食，但乾燥的穀物主要含有澱粉。","Grains are hard, dry and full of starch. Without converting it to sugar, the yeast would have nothing to turn into alcohol. The problem is not too much sugar, since sugar is actually missing, nor alcohol, which only appears during fermentation.":"穀物又硬又乾，充滿澱粉。如果不把澱粉轉化為糖，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化成酒精。問題不在糖太多，因為根本缺糖；也不在酒精，因為酒精要到發酵時才出現。","During malting, what does barley produce as it grows?":"發芽過程中，大麥在生長時會產生什麼？","Enzymes that can convert starch":"能轉化澱粉的酵素","Yeast that starts the fermentation":"啟動發酵的酵母","Small amounts of alcohol":"少量酒精","Natural smoky aromas":"天然的煙燻香氣","As it sprouts, the grain makes enzymes that later convert starch into sugar.":"穀物發芽時會產生酵素，之後這些酵素會把澱粉轉化為糖。","The enzymes really get to work once the crushed barley is mixed with water. Yeast, by contrast, is added later to the sugary liquid. Smoke does not come from sprouting: it only appears if peat is burned while the barley is heated.":"酵素真正發揮作用，是在碾碎的大麥與水混合之後。相反地，酵母是之後才加入含糖液體中的。煙燻味不是來自發芽：只有在烘乾大麥時燃燒泥煤才會出現。","With hot air":"用熱空氣","With ice-cold water":"用冰水","By adding yeast":"加入酵母","By charcoal filtering":"用木炭過濾","Heat dries the grain and halts sprouting, giving malted barley.":"熱氣把穀物烘乾並停止發芽，得到麥芽大麥。","This heating stage is exactly when some distilleries burn peat to add smoke. Water comes in later, when the crushed barley is mixed to release its sugar. Yeast and charcoal filtering belong to other stages of production altogether.":"正是在這個加熱階段，有些蒸餾廠會燃燒泥煤來增添煙燻味。水是之後才加入的，與碾碎的大麥混合以釋出糖分。酵母和木炭過濾則屬於完全不同的生產階段。","What is the minimum ageing for any Scotch whisky?":"所有 Scotch 威士忌的最低陳年要求是什麼？","Three years, in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭陳年三年","Two years, in any country":"在任何國家陳年兩年","Three years, anywhere in the UK":"在英國任何地方陳年三年","Ten years, in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭陳年十年","All Scotch is distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"所有 Scotch 都在蘇格蘭蒸餾，並在當地陳年至少三年。","Where the whisky ages matters as much as how long: maturing elsewhere in the UK is not enough. Two years is the minimum for Cognac, not Scotch. Ten years recalls the XO term for Cognac and is not a rule for Scotch.":"威士忌在哪裡陳年和陳年多久同樣重要：在英國其他地方熟成是不夠的。兩年是 Cognac 的最低要求，不是 Scotch。十年讓人聯想到 Cognac 的 XO 術語，並不是 Scotch 的規定。","Which combination defines a Single Malt Scotch whisky?":"哪一組條件定義了 Single Malt Scotch 威士忌？","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery":"100% 麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠","Malted barley and other grains, column still, one distillery":"麥芽大麥加其他穀物、柱式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠","100% malted barley, pot stills, several distilleries":"100% 麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、多家蒸餾廠","At least 51% barley, any still, one distillery":"至少 51% 大麥、任何蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠","A Single Malt uses only malted barley, pot stills and one distillery.":"Single Malt 只使用麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器，並來自單一蒸餾廠。","All three conditions must be true together. Other grains and a column still describe grain whisky. Malts from several distilleries would no longer be 'single'. The 51% threshold belongs to American rules such as those for Bourbon.":"三個條件必須同時成立。其他穀物和柱式蒸餾器描述的是穀物威士忌。來自多家蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌就不再是「single」。51% 的門檻屬於美國的規定，例如 Bourbon。","Where does the smoky flavour of some Single Malts come from?":"某些 Single Malt 的煙燻風味來自哪裡？","Peat burned while the malted barley is heated":"烘乾麥芽大麥時燃燒的泥煤","New barrels charred on the inside":"內部經過炙燒的新桶","Finished whisky exposed to smoke":"讓成品威士忌接觸煙燻","A charcoal filter after distillation":"蒸餾後的木炭過濾","Peat smoke flavours the grains during the final heating of malting.":"在製麥最後的烘乾階段，泥煤煙為穀物增添了風味。","The smoke enters the whisky before fermentation even begins, through the barley. New charred barrels are typical of Bourbon and give vanilla and coconut, not peat. The charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey removes impurities and adds no flavour.":"煙燻味在發酵開始之前就已透過大麥進入威士忌。內部炙燒的新桶是 Bourbon 的典型做法，帶來香草和椰子，而不是泥煤。Tennessee 威士忌的木炭過濾是去除雜質，不會增添風味。","Which statement about peaty Single Malts is true?":"關於泥煤風格的 Single Malt，下列哪一項正確？","Only a few exist, and some are very smoky":"數量不多，其中有些煙燻味非常濃","The law requires peat in every Single Malt":"法律規定每款 Single Malt 都要用泥煤","Almost every Single Malt is peaty":"幾乎所有 Single Malt 都有泥煤風味","Peat is added in the bottle as a flavouring":"泥煤是在瓶中添加的調味料","Only a minority of Single Malts are peaty, sometimes intensely.":"只有少數 Single Malt 帶有泥煤風味，有時非常濃烈。","Smoke is a famous trait but not the rule: most Single Malts show cereal, fruit, flowers and honey with no smoky notes. No law makes peat compulsory. And peat is not a flavouring added later; it is burned during malting.":"煙燻味是著名的特色，但不是常規：大多數 Single Malt 呈現穀物、水果、花香和蜂蜜，沒有煙燻氣息。沒有法律強制使用泥煤。而且泥煤不是之後添加的調味料，而是在製麥時燃燒的。","How is Scottish grain whisky best described?":"下列哪一項最能描述蘇格蘭穀物威士忌？","Column-distilled, light and smooth":"以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，清淡而柔順","Pot-distilled, intense and peaty":"以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾，濃郁且帶泥煤","Made only from malted barley, very aromatic":"只用麥芽大麥製成，香氣非常豐富","Unaged and bottled straight away":"未經陳年，直接裝瓶","Grain whisky comes off the column still with a light aroma and smooth texture.":"穀物威士忌離開柱式蒸餾器時，香氣清淡，口感柔順。","It is made from malted barley plus other grains, so not from malted barley alone like Single Malt. The intensity and character of pot stills belong to the malts. And because it is Scotch, it must age for at least three years, so it cannot be bottled straight away.":"它是用麥芽大麥加上其他穀物製成，而不像 Single Malt 只用麥芽大麥。壺式蒸餾器的濃郁與個性屬於麥芽威士忌。而且既然是 Scotch，就必須陳年至少三年，不能直接裝瓶。","What is a Blended Scotch whisky?":"什麼是 Blended Scotch 威士忌？","Malt and grain whiskies from different distilleries":"來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌與穀物威士忌","Several malts from the same distillery":"來自同一家蒸餾廠的多款麥芽威士忌","Grain whiskies only, of various ages":"只有不同年份的穀物威士忌","Scotch mixed with Irish whiskey":"Scotch 混合愛爾蘭威士忌","A blend combines both types of Scottish whisky from several distilleries.":"調和威士忌結合了來自多家蒸餾廠的兩種蘇格蘭威士忌。","Both parts are essential: malts bring character, grain whisky brings lightness and smoothness. Several malts from one distillery do not make a Blended Scotch. And to be Scotch, every part must be distilled and aged in Scotland, so Irish whiskey cannot be included.":"兩個部分都不可或缺：麥芽威士忌帶來個性，穀物威士忌帶來輕盈與柔順。同一家蒸餾廠的多款麥芽威士忌，並不構成 Blended Scotch。而且要成為 Scotch，每個部分都必須在蘇格蘭蒸餾和陳年，所以不能包含愛爾蘭威士忌。","A customer wants a smooth, easy-going Scotch with no smoke. What is usually the best suggestion?":"一位顧客想要一款柔順易飲、沒有煙燻味的 Scotch。通常最好的建議是什麼？","A Blended Scotch whisky":"Blended Scotch 威士忌","A heavily peated Single Malt":"泥煤味很重的 Single Malt","An old, intense Single Malt":"老而濃郁的 Single Malt","A pot-distilled whisky":"以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾的威士忌","Thanks to grain whisky, blends are usually smoother than Single Malts.":"因為有穀物威士忌，調和威士忌通常比 Single Malt 更柔順。","The light, smooth grain whisky softens the whole blend. A peaty malt brings exactly the smoke the customer wants to avoid. Old, intense malts, like pot-still spirits in general, aim for character and power rather than smoothness.":"清淡柔順的穀物威士忌讓整體調和變得柔和。泥煤麥芽威士忌帶來的正是顧客想避開的煙燻味。老而濃郁的麥芽威士忌，就像一般的壺式蒸餾烈酒，追求的是個性與力度，而不是柔順。","Making Blended Scotch":"製作 Blended Scotch","Being sold as Single Malt":"以 Single Malt 的名義販售","Giving smoke to peaty malts":"為泥煤麥芽威士忌增添煙燻味","Diluting Scotch before bottling":"在裝瓶前稀釋 Scotch","Rarely sold on its own, grain whisky is the light backbone of blends.":"穀物威士忌很少單獨販售，它是調和威士忌的清爽骨架。","It cannot be a Single Malt, because it contains other grains and is column-distilled. Smoke comes from peat, not from another whisky. Dilution before bottling is done with pure water, not with another spirit.":"它不可能是 Single Malt，因為它含有其他穀物，而且是用柱式蒸餾器蒸餾。煙燻味來自泥煤，而不是另一款威士忌。裝瓶前的稀釋是用純水，而不是另一種烈酒。","Which set of aromas is typical of an unpeated Single Malt?":"哪一組香氣是無泥煤 Single Malt 的典型特徵？","Cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, sweet spice":"穀物、水果、花香、蜂蜜、甜香料","Fresh grass, vegetal and cane notes":"新鮮青草、植物和甘蔗氣息","Juniper, citrus and roots":"杜松子、柑橘和根類","Almost no aroma, a neutral style":"幾乎沒有香氣，中性風格","Single Malt is expressive, with cereal, fruit, flower, honey and spice notes.":"Single Malt 香氣豐富，帶有穀物、水果、花香、蜂蜜和香料氣息。","With age in the barrel, fruit cake notes join them too. Grassy cane notes describe rum made from cane juice, and juniper is the signature of gin. A neutral style belongs to vodka, distilled to a very high strength.":"隨著在桶中陳年，還會出現水果蛋糕的氣息。草本的甘蔗氣息描述的是以甘蔗汁製成的蘭姆酒，杜松子則是琴酒的標誌。中性風格屬於蒸餾到極高濃度的伏特加。","A whisky is distilled in Scotland, then aged four years in England. Can it be called Scotch?":"一款威士忌在蘇格蘭蒸餾，然後在英格蘭陳年四年。它可以稱為 Scotch 嗎？","No: the ageing must also take place in Scotland":"不行：陳年也必須在蘇格蘭進行","Yes: only the place of distillation counts":"可以：只看蒸餾地點","Yes, as long as it is made from malted barley":"可以，只要是用麥芽大麥製成","No: Scotch must age for ten years":"不行：Scotch 必須陳年十年","Scotch must be both distilled and aged in Scotland, for at least three years.":"Scotch 必須在蘇格蘭蒸餾並陳年，至少三年。","Four years would be long enough, but the place is wrong. The grain used does not change this rule, which applies to every Scotch. The minimum is three years, not ten: the only problem here is geography.":"四年的時間夠長，但地點錯了。使用的穀物不會改變這項規定，它適用於所有 Scotch。最低要求是三年，不是十年：這裡唯一的問題是地點。","A label reads 'Single Malt Scotch Whisky'. What can you be sure of?":"酒標上寫著「Single Malt Scotch Whisky」。你可以確定什麼？","It comes from one distillery and only malted barley":"來自單一蒸餾廠，只使用麥芽大麥","It comes from a single barrel, with no blending":"來自單一酒桶，沒有經過調和","It has a smoky peat flavour":"帶有煙燻的泥煤風味","It has been aged at least ten years":"至少陳年十年","'Single' means one distillery; 'Malt' means only malted barley, pot-distilled.":"「Single」表示單一蒸餾廠；「Malt」表示只使用麥芽大麥，並以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。","A Single Malt can still be a blend of many barrels from the same distillery: 'single' does not mean one barrel. Only a few Single Malts are peaty, so smoke is not guaranteed. The minimum age is three years, as for every Scotch.":"Single Malt 仍可以是同一家蒸餾廠許多酒桶的調和：「single」並不代表單一酒桶。只有少數 Single Malt 帶有泥煤風味，所以不保證有煙燻味。最低年份是三年，和所有 Scotch 一樣。","Why do Blended Scotch producers combine whiskies from different barrels and distilleries?":"為什麼 Blended Scotch 的生產者要結合來自不同酒桶和蒸餾廠的威士忌？","To achieve consistency and complexity":"為了達到一致性和複雜度","To raise the final alcohol strength":"為了提高最終的酒精濃度","To make the whisky colourless":"為了讓威士忌變成無色","To shorten the required ageing time":"為了縮短規定的陳年時間","Blending keeps each batch like the last and adds depth.":"調和讓每一批都和上一批一樣，並增添深度。","Every barrel is unique, so blending is the way to a consistent taste, and combining different characters creates complexity. Strength is adjusted with water, not by blending. Blending does not remove colour, and the three-year minimum still applies to every component.":"每個酒桶都是獨一無二的，所以調和是讓風味保持一致的方法，而結合不同的個性則能創造複雜度。濃度是用水調整，而不是靠調和。調和不會去除顏色，而且三年的最低要求仍適用於每個組成部分。","Why is whisky often described as 'distilled beer'?":"為什麼威士忌常被形容為「蒸餾過的啤酒」？","Because a fermented grain liquid is distilled":"因為它是將發酵的穀物液體加以蒸餾","Because beer is added before bottling":"因為裝瓶前會加入啤酒","Because it ages in old beer barrels":"因為它在舊啤酒桶中陳年","Because it has the same strength as beer":"因為它的濃度和啤酒一樣","Like beer, whisky starts from fermented grain; that liquid is then distilled.":"和啤酒一樣，威士忌從發酵的穀物開始；接著再將這個液體蒸餾。","The image describes the process: sugar from grain, fermentation, distillation. No beer is added to finished whisky, and the phrase says nothing about barrels. After distilling and diluting, whisky is far stronger than any beer, usually 40% abv.":"這個比喻描述的是製程：從穀物取得糖、發酵、蒸餾。成品威士忌中不會加入啤酒，而且這個說法也與酒桶無關。經過蒸餾和稀釋後，威士忌的濃度遠高於任何啤酒，通常是 40% abv。","A blender adds a tiny amount of caramel to a batch of Scotch. What is the purpose?":"調和師在一批 Scotch 中加入極少量的焦糖色，目的是什麼？","To keep the colour the same from batch to batch":"讓每一批的顏色保持一致","To make the whisky slightly sweet":"讓威士忌稍微帶點甜味","To add a toffee aroma":"增添太妃糖香氣","To speed up ageing in the barrel":"加速在桶中的陳年","Caramel colour is used only to even out colour between batches.":"焦糖色只用來統一各批次之間的顏色。","Each barrel gives a slightly different colour, and caramel corrects those differences. Used correctly it is not sweet and adds no aroma, so it brings neither sugar nor toffee notes. It has no effect on maturation, which depends on wood and time.":"每個酒桶帶來的顏色都略有不同，焦糖色可以修正這些差異。正確使用時它不甜，也不會增添香氣，所以既不帶來糖，也不帶來太妃糖氣息。它對熟成沒有任何影響，熟成取決於木頭和時間。","Which grain must make up at least 51% of a Bourbon's recipe?":"Bourbon 的配方中，哪一種穀物必須佔至少 51%？","Bourbon is a corn-majority whiskey, at least 51%.":"Bourbon 是以玉米為主的威士忌，至少 51%。","Barley and rye often appear in the recipe, but only as secondary grains. If rye reaches 51%, the whiskey becomes a Rye. 100% malted barley is the rule for Scottish Single Malt.":"大麥和黑麥經常出現在配方中，但只是次要穀物。如果黑麥達到 51%，這款威士忌就成了 Rye。100% 麥芽大麥是蘇格蘭 Single Malt 的規定。","Where can Bourbon be made?":"Bourbon 可以在哪裡生產？","Only in Kentucky":"只能在肯塔基州","Only in Kentucky and Tennessee":"只能在肯塔基州和田納西州","Anywhere in North America":"北美洲任何地方","Bourbon can be made across the USA, though Kentucky leads production.":"Bourbon 可以在全美各地生產，不過肯塔基州的產量居首。","The link with Kentucky is strong because most Bourbon is made there, but it is not a requirement. It is Tennessee whiskey that is tied to one state. Outside the USA, in Canada for example, Bourbon cannot be made.":"Bourbon 與肯塔基州的連結很強，因為大多數 Bourbon 都在那裡生產，但這並不是規定。和單一州綁定的是 Tennessee 威士忌。在美國以外，例如加拿大，就不能生產 Bourbon。","What barrels must Bourbon be aged in?":"Bourbon 必須在什麼樣的桶中陳年？","Previously used oak":"用過的橡木桶","Former Cognac barrels":"曾裝過 Cognac 的桶","New uncharred oak":"未經炙燒的新橡木桶","The law requires new oak barrels charred on the inside.":"法律規定必須使用內部經過炙燒的新橡木桶。","Used barrels give less aroma each time they are used, so they are not allowed for Bourbon. Even a new barrel is not enough unless it is charred. This choice explains Bourbon's deep colour and strong vanilla and coconut notes.":"用過的桶每使用一次，釋出的香氣就會減少，所以 Bourbon 不允許使用。即使是新桶，沒有經過炙燒也不行。這項選擇說明了 Bourbon 為何有深邃的顏色，以及濃郁的香草和椰子氣息。","Which aromas are typical of a Bourbon?":"哪些香氣是 Bourbon 的典型特徵？","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit":"甜玉米、香草、椰子、水果","Peat smoke, cereal, honey":"泥煤煙燻、穀物、蜂蜜","Grass, vegetal, fresh cane":"青草、植物、新鮮甘蔗","Agave, pepper, olive":"龍舌蘭、胡椒、橄欖","Corn gives sweetcorn notes; new charred barrels give vanilla and coconut.":"玉米帶來甜玉米氣息；炙燒過的新桶帶來香草和椰子。","Peat smoke belongs to some Scottish Single Malts. Grassy cane notes are typical of rum made from cane juice. Agave, pepper and olive describe Tequila.":"泥煤煙燻屬於某些蘇格蘭 Single Malt。草本的甘蔗氣息是甘蔗汁蘭姆酒的典型特徵。龍舌蘭、胡椒和橄欖描述的是 Tequila。","How is Bourbon usually distilled?":"Bourbon 通常如何蒸餾？","In a column still, to a low strength":"以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度","In a column still, up to 96% abv":"以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到 96% abv","Twice in a pot still, by law":"依法以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾兩次","In a short column, then charcoal filtered":"以矮蒸餾柱蒸餾，再經木炭過濾","A column still is normal, but stopped at low strength to keep flavour.":"使用柱式蒸餾器是常態，但會停在較低濃度以保留風味。","At 96% abv you would get a neutral spirit like vodka's, and Bourbon would lose its pronounced character. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac. Maple charcoal filtering is the signature step of Tennessee whiskey.":"蒸餾到 96% abv 會得到像伏特加那樣的中性烈酒，Bourbon 就會失去鮮明的個性。強制以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾是 Cognac 的規定。楓木炭過濾則是 Tennessee 威士忌的招牌步驟。","A customer says Bourbon 'tastes sweet'. Which explanation is correct?":"一位顧客說 Bourbon「喝起來很甜」。哪一種解釋才正確？","It has no added sugar; vanilla and fruit aromas create that impression":"它沒有加糖；是香草和水果香氣造成了這種印象","Sugar is always added after ageing":"陳年後一定會加糖","Sugar from the corn survives distillation":"玉米的糖分在蒸餾後仍保留下來","New barrels release sugar into the whiskey":"新桶會把糖釋放到威士忌中","Bourbon is dry: the perceived 'sweetness' comes from aromas, not sugar.":"Bourbon 是不甜的：感受到的「甜」來自香氣，而不是糖。","Every spirit is dry when it comes off the still, and no sugar is added to Bourbon afterwards. Barrels give colour and aromas such as vanilla and coconut, which the nose links with desserts, but not sugar.":"所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的，之後 Bourbon 也不會加糖。酒桶帶來顏色和香草、椰子等香氣，鼻子會把這些香氣與甜點聯想在一起，但它們不是糖。","Compared with a used barrel, a new barrel gives a spirit...":"和用過的桶相比，新桶會為烈酒帶來…","more colour and more aroma":"更多顏色和更多香氣","less colour and less aroma":"更少顏色和更少香氣","more sugar and sweetness":"更多糖分和甜味","only colour, no aroma":"只有顏色，沒有香氣","A never-used barrel gives the most; each reuse weakens its effect.":"從未使用過的桶帶來的影響最大；每重複使用一次，效果就減弱一些。","That is why Bourbon, which must use new barrels, shows such clear oak colour and aromas. Barrels do not add sugar: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation. And a new barrel always brings aromas too, such as vanilla and coconut.":"這就是為什麼必須使用新桶的 Bourbon，會呈現如此鮮明的橡木色澤和香氣。酒桶不會加入糖：甜味只來自蒸餾後添加的糖。而新桶一定也會帶來香氣，例如香草和椰子。","What sets Tennessee whiskey apart from Bourbon in production?":"在生產上，Tennessee 威士忌與 Bourbon 有什麼不同？","Maple charcoal filtering before the barrel":"入桶前以楓木炭過濾","A recipe with at least 51% rye":"配方中黑麥至少 51%","Ageing in previously used barrels":"在用過的桶中陳年","Double distillation in a pot still":"以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾","The new spirit runs through maple charcoal before it goes into the barrel.":"剛蒸餾出的烈酒在入桶前會先通過楓木炭。","Otherwise Tennessee whiskey follows Bourbon's rules: mostly corn, low-strength column distillation, new charred barrels. 51% rye defines Rye whiskey. Used barrels and double pot distillation are not part of its rules.":"除此之外，Tennessee 威士忌遵循 Bourbon 的規定：以玉米為主、以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度、使用炙燒過的新桶。51% 黑麥是 Rye 威士忌的定義。用過的桶和壺式二次蒸餾都不在它的規定之中。","What does the maple charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey do?":"Tennessee 威士忌的楓木炭過濾有什麼作用？","Removes impurities and smooths it, adding no flavour":"去除雜質、讓口感柔順，不增添風味","Adds a light maple syrup flavour":"增添淡淡的楓糖漿風味","Adds smoky, peat-like notes":"增添類似泥煤的煙燻氣息","Removes all the colour from the barrel":"去除來自酒桶的所有顏色","The charcoal holds back some impurities and smooths, but adds no aroma.":"木炭會留住部分雜質並讓口感柔順，但不會增添香氣。","The word 'maple' is misleading: the charcoal passes on no syrup or smoke flavour. Also, the filtering happens before the barrel, on a spirit that is still colourless, so it cannot remove colour that is not there yet.":"「楓木」這個詞容易誤導：木炭不會帶來糖漿或煙燻風味。此外，過濾是在入桶之前，針對仍然無色的烈酒進行，所以不可能去除還不存在的顏色。","Where can Tennessee whiskey be made?":"Tennessee 威士忌可以在哪裡生產？","Only in the state of Tennessee":"只能在田納西州","In Tennessee or Kentucky":"田納西州或肯塔基州","Anywhere, if maple charcoal filtered":"任何地方，只要經過楓木炭過濾","The name is tied to the state: it can only be made in Tennessee.":"這個名稱與州綁定：只能在田納西州生產。","It is Bourbon that can be made anywhere in the USA. Kentucky is the heart of Bourbon, not of Tennessee whiskey. Charcoal filtering is necessary but not enough: without the right place, the name cannot be used.":"可以在美國任何地方生產的是 Bourbon。肯塔基州是 Bourbon 的核心產地，而不是 Tennessee 威士忌的。木炭過濾是必要條件，但還不夠：產地不對，就不能使用這個名稱。","What defines an American Rye whiskey?":"美國 Rye 威士忌的定義是什麼？","At least 51% rye; spicy, peppery aromas":"黑麥至少 51%；辛香、胡椒般的香氣","100% rye and smoky notes":"100% 黑麥，帶煙燻氣息","At least 51% corn; coconut notes":"玉米至少 51%；椰子氣息","At least 51% rye; grassy cane notes":"黑麥至少 51%；草本的甘蔗氣息","Rye has at least 51% rye grain, giving a spicy, peppery character.":"Rye 含有至少 51% 的黑麥，帶來辛香、胡椒般的個性。","The threshold is 51%, not 100%, and smoke has nothing to do with it. 51% corn defines Bourbon. Grassy cane notes belong to rum made from cane juice, not to a grain whiskey.":"門檻是 51%，不是 100%，而且與煙燻味無關。51% 玉米是 Bourbon 的定義。草本的甘蔗氣息屬於甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，而不是穀物威士忌。","A bartender wants an American whiskey with a spicy, peppery character. Which should they choose?":"調酒師想要一款帶辛香、胡椒般個性的美國威士忌，應該選擇哪一款？","Tennessee whiskey":"Tennessee 威士忌","A light Irish whiskey":"清淡的愛爾蘭威士忌","Rye grain, the main grain in Rye whiskey, gives spicy, peppery aromas.":"黑麥是 Rye 威士忌的主要穀物，帶來辛香、胡椒般的香氣。","Bourbon and Tennessee whiskey are mostly corn, so they lean towards sweetcorn, vanilla and coconut. A light, smooth Irish whiskey is not American and does not have this peppery profile.":"Bourbon 和 Tennessee 威士忌以玉米為主，所以偏向甜玉米、香草和椰子。清淡柔順的愛爾蘭威士忌不是美國威士忌，也沒有這種胡椒般的風味輪廓。","What is the only rule that separates American Rye whiskey from Bourbon?":"美國 Rye 威士忌與 Bourbon 唯一的區別規定是什麼？","The main grain in the recipe":"配方中的主要穀物","The type of still used":"使用的蒸餾器類型","The state where it is made":"生產的州","Rye is made exactly like Bourbon, but with rye instead of corn.":"Rye 的製作方式與 Bourbon 完全相同，只是用黑麥取代玉米。","Both use new charred oak barrels and usually low-strength column distillation. Neither is tied to one state; it is Tennessee whiskey that has a geographical limit. Only the grain that makes up 51% changes.":"兩者都使用炙燒過的新橡木桶，通常也都以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度。兩者都不與單一州綁定；有地理限制的是 Tennessee 威士忌。唯一改變的是佔 51% 的那種穀物。","By blending pot-still and column-still spirits":"調和壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒","Only from malted barley and peat":"只用麥芽大麥和泥煤","With 51% corn in new barrels":"51% 玉米加上新桶","Without any oak ageing":"完全不經橡木桶陳年","Most Irish whiskeys combine pot-still and column-still spirits.":"大多數愛爾蘭威士忌結合了壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒。","The typical result is a light, smooth whiskey. Peat belongs to some Scottish Single Malts, and 51% corn with new barrels to Bourbon. Like all whiskies, Irish whiskeys are aged in oak.":"典型的成果是清淡柔順的威士忌。泥煤屬於某些蘇格蘭 Single Malt，51% 玉米加新桶屬於 Bourbon。和所有威士忌一樣，愛爾蘭威士忌也在橡木桶中陳年。","What character does unmalted barley give some Irish pot-still whiskeys?":"未發芽的大麥為某些愛爾蘭壺式蒸餾威士忌帶來什麼個性？","Nutty notes and an oily texture":"堅果氣息和油潤質地","Smoky, medicinal notes":"煙燻、藥水般的氣息","Spicy, peppery notes":"辛香、胡椒般的氣息","Sweetcorn and coconut notes":"甜玉米和椰子氣息","Unmalted barley brings a nutty character and an oily texture.":"未發芽的大麥帶來堅果般的個性和油潤的質地。","It is an unusual ingredient, used only in some Irish whiskeys made in pot stills. Smoke comes from peat, pepper from rye, and sweetcorn and coconut from corn and new barrels as in Bourbon.":"這是一種不尋常的原料，只用於某些以壺式蒸餾器製作的愛爾蘭威士忌。煙燻來自泥煤，胡椒來自黑麥，甜玉米和椰子則來自玉米和新桶，就像 Bourbon。","What is the signature flavour of the best Canadian whiskies?":"最優秀的加拿大威士忌，招牌風味是什麼？","Spicy, peppery rye is the signature of the best Canadian whiskies.":"辛香、胡椒般的黑麥，是最優秀加拿大威士忌的招牌。","Canada uses many different grains, but rye gives the most recognisable character. Peat is typical of some Scottish malts. Corn dominates Bourbon, and unmalted barley is an Irish speciality.":"加拿大使用許多不同的穀物，但黑麥帶來最容易辨認的個性。泥煤是某些蘇格蘭麥芽威士忌的特徵。玉米主導 Bourbon，未發芽的大麥則是愛爾蘭的特色。","Which description fits a typical Canadian whisky?":"哪一項描述符合典型的加拿大威士忌？","Many grains; a blend of high- and low-strength spirits":"多種穀物；高濃度與低濃度烈酒的調和","Malted barley only, pot still, one distillery":"只用麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠","51% corn and maple charcoal filtering":"51% 玉米加上楓木炭過濾","Neutral spirit at 96%, unaged":"96% 的中性烈酒，未經陳年","Canada uses several grains and blends lighter and more flavourful spirits.":"加拿大使用多種穀物，並調和較清淡與風味較濃的烈酒。","Malted barley only from one distillery describes a Single Malt. Corn plus maple charcoal is the profile of Tennessee whiskey. An unaged neutral spirit is the base of vodka, while every whisky spends time in oak.":"只用麥芽大麥、來自單一蒸餾廠，描述的是 Single Malt。玉米加楓木炭是 Tennessee 威士忌的特徵。未陳年的中性烈酒是伏特加的基底，而所有威士忌都會在橡木桶中度過一段時間。","Which country was Japanese whisky production modelled on?":"日本威士忌的生產是以哪個國家為範本？","Canada":"加拿大","Japanese whisky follows the Scottish model, with malts and blends.":"日本威士忌依循蘇格蘭模式，有麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。","As in Scotland, Japan makes malt whiskies and blended whiskies. The USA has a different model based on corn or rye and new barrels. Ireland and Canada have their own traditions of blending different spirits.":"和蘇格蘭一樣，日本生產麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。美國的模式不同，以玉米或黑麥和新桶為基礎。愛爾蘭和加拿大則各有調和不同烈酒的傳統。","How is the traditional style of Japanese whisky described?":"日本威士忌的傳統風格如何描述？","Elegant and refined":"優雅而細緻","Very sweet from added sugar":"因加糖而非常甜","Peppery and rye-based":"胡椒般的辛香，以黑麥為基礎","Neutral, with almost no aroma":"中性，幾乎沒有香氣","Traditionally, Japanese whiskies are elegant and refined.":"傳統上，日本威士忌優雅而細緻。","Today many producers are also exploring new styles, but the classic hallmark remains elegance. Added sugar is not part of the typical profile. Rye is the signature of Canada and American Rye, and a neutral style describes vodka.":"如今許多生產者也在探索新風格，但經典的特徵仍是優雅。加糖不屬於典型的風味輪廓。黑麥是加拿大和美國 Rye 的招牌，中性風格則描述伏特加。","A Kentucky whiskey: 70% corn, low-strength column still, new charred oak, no charcoal filtering. What is it?":"一款肯塔基州的威士忌：70% 玉米、以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度、炙燒過的新橡木桶、沒有木炭過濾。它是什麼？","A Bourbon":"Bourbon","A Tennessee whiskey":"Tennessee 威士忌","A Rye whiskey":"Rye 威士忌","Mostly corn, new charred barrels, made in the USA: every Bourbon rule is met.":"以玉米為主、炙燒過的新桶、在美國生產：符合 Bourbon 的所有規定。","To be Tennessee whiskey it would need maple charcoal filtering and to be made in Tennessee; both are missing here. With 70% corn it cannot be a Rye, which needs 51% rye. And Kentucky is not in Canada.":"要成為 Tennessee 威士忌，必須經過楓木炭過濾並在田納西州生產；這裡兩者都缺。70% 玉米不可能是 Rye，Rye 需要 51% 黑麥。而且肯塔基州不在加拿大。","What is the raw material of rum?":"蘭姆酒的原料是什麼？","Rum comes from sugar cane, used as juice or as molasses.":"蘭姆酒來自甘蔗，使用甘蔗汁或糖蜜。","Grains are the base of whisky, blue agave of Tequila and grapes of brandies such as Cognac. Cane can be used fresh, by crushing out its juice, or in the form of molasses.":"穀物是威士忌的基底，藍色龍舌蘭是 Tequila 的基底，葡萄則是 Cognac 等白蘭地的基底。甘蔗可以新鮮使用（壓榨出甘蔗汁），也可以用糖蜜的形式。","Why is rum production centred on places like the Caribbean?":"為什麼蘭姆酒的生產集中在加勒比海這類地方？","Sugar cane grows in hot climates":"甘蔗生長在炎熱氣候","Column stills are only allowed there":"只有那裡允許使用柱式蒸餾器","The law bans rum outside the Caribbean":"法律禁止在加勒比海以外生產蘭姆酒","Heat speeds up ageing":"高溫能加速陳年","Rum is made where cane grows, which means hot countries.":"蘭姆酒在甘蔗生長的地方生產，也就是炎熱的國家。","The reason is agricultural: the raw material needs heat. No law reserves rum for the Caribbean, and column stills are used all over the world. The idea of faster ageing is not why rum is made in these areas.":"原因在農業：原料需要高溫。沒有法律把蘭姆酒保留給加勒比海，柱式蒸餾器也在世界各地使用。加速陳年的說法也不是蘭姆酒在這些地區生產的原因。","A black, sticky by-product of sugar-making":"製糖過程中產生的黑色黏稠副產品","The fresh juice of just-crushed cane":"剛壓碎的甘蔗的新鮮汁液","A cane wine that has already fermented":"已經發酵的甘蔗酒","The caramel colouring used in rums":"蘭姆酒使用的焦糖色","Molasses is left over when cane juice is turned into sugar.":"糖蜜是甘蔗汁製成糖之後剩下的東西。","It is black and sticky and must be mixed with water before fermentation. Fresh juice is the other raw material, used for rhum agricole. Molasses is not already fermented, and it should not be confused with caramel, which is only used to adjust colour.":"它黑色又黏稠，發酵前必須與水混合。新鮮甘蔗汁是另一種原料，用於 rhum agricole。糖蜜並不是已經發酵的，也不應與只用來調整顏色的焦糖色混淆。","What flavour do cane-juice rums often have?":"甘蔗汁蘭姆酒通常帶有什麼風味？","Very pronounced grassy, herbaceous":"非常明顯的青草、草本氣息","Caramel and brown sugar":"焦糖和紅糖","Juniper and citrus":"杜松子和柑橘","Fresh cane juice gives rum a grassy, herbaceous character.":"新鮮甘蔗汁為蘭姆酒帶來青草、草本的個性。","Caramel and brown sugar are the mark of molasses rums, the most common choice in the Caribbean. Peat smoke belongs to some Scotch whiskies, while juniper and citrus are typical of gin.":"焦糖和紅糖是糖蜜蘭姆酒的標誌，也是加勒比海最常見的選擇。泥煤煙燻屬於某些 Scotch 威士忌，杜松子和柑橘則是琴酒的典型特徵。","In the Caribbean, where must rhum agricole come from?":"在加勒比海，rhum agricole 必須來自哪裡？","Martinique or Guadeloupe":"馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普","Jamaica or Cuba":"牙買加或古巴","Puerto Rico or Jamaica":"波多黎各或牙買加","Any Caribbean island":"任何加勒比海島嶼","In the Caribbean, rhum agricole must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"在加勒比海，rhum agricole 必須來自馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普。","Rhum agricole is the best example of a cane-juice rum. Jamaica is known for very fruity rums, Cuba and Puerto Rico for light rums from tall columns. Simply being a Caribbean island is not enough to use this name.":"Rhum agricole 是甘蔗汁蘭姆酒最好的例子。牙買加以果香非常濃郁的蘭姆酒聞名，古巴和波多黎各則以高蒸餾柱製作的清淡蘭姆酒聞名。光是加勒比海島嶼，並不足以使用這個名稱。","Which raw material do most Caribbean distillers use?":"大多數加勒比海蒸餾師使用哪一種原料？","Refined white sugar":"精製白糖","Molasses is the choice of most Caribbean distillers.":"糖蜜是大多數加勒比海蒸餾師的選擇。","Fresh juice is used mainly for rhum agricole, a smaller share of production. Refined sugar is the main product of the industry that leaves molasses behind, not rum's raw material. Honey has nothing to do with rum.":"新鮮甘蔗汁主要用於 rhum agricole，在產量中佔比較小。精製糖是製糖業的主要產品，糖蜜是它留下的副產品，精製糖並不是蘭姆酒的原料。蜂蜜與蘭姆酒無關。","Which flavours are typical of a molasses rum?":"哪些風味是糖蜜蘭姆酒的典型特徵？","Fresh grass and vegetal notes":"新鮮青草和植物氣息","Sweetcorn and coconut":"甜玉米和椰子","Agave, olive and pepper":"龍舌蘭、橄欖和胡椒","Molasses brings caramel and brown sugar notes to rum.":"糖蜜為蘭姆酒帶來焦糖和紅糖氣息。","Grassy, vegetal notes are typical of fresh cane juice. Sweetcorn and coconut recall Bourbon, and agave, olive and pepper recall Tequila. Each raw material leaves its own set of aromas.":"青草、植物氣息是新鮮甘蔗汁的典型特徵。甜玉米和椰子讓人想到 Bourbon，龍舌蘭、橄欖和胡椒則讓人想到 Tequila。每種原料都會留下自己的一組香氣。","What must be done to molasses before it can ferment?":"糖蜜在發酵前必須怎麼處理？","Mix it with water":"與水混合","Let it sprout":"讓它發芽","Cook it in ovens":"放進窯爐烹煮","Filter it through charcoal":"用木炭過濾","Molasses is too thick: it must be mixed with water to ferment.":"糖蜜太濃稠：必須與水混合才能發酵。","Sprouting belongs to malting grain for whisky. Cooking in ovens is how sugar is created from agave cores for Tequila. Charcoal filtering comes after distillation, for example to remove colour from rum.":"發芽屬於威士忌穀物的製麥過程。放進窯爐烹煮是 Tequila 從龍舌蘭心產生糖的方式。木炭過濾是在蒸餾之後，例如用來去除蘭姆酒的顏色。","Which stage mainly creates the intense tropical fruit aromas of some rums?":"某些蘭姆酒濃郁的熱帶水果香氣，主要在哪個階段產生？","Oak ageing":"橡木桶陳年","Charcoal filtering":"木炭過濾","Dilution with water":"加水稀釋","During fermentation, yeast can create intense tropical fruit aromas.":"在發酵時，酵母可以產生濃郁的熱帶水果香氣。","Oak adds vanilla and sweet spice instead. Charcoal filtering removes colour; it does not add fruit. The water used for dilution is pure and brings no flavour.":"橡木桶帶來的是香草和甜香料。木炭過濾是去除顏色，不會增添果香。稀釋用的水是純水，不帶任何風味。","Which rum style are Jamaican distillers famous for?":"牙買加的蒸餾師以哪種風格的蘭姆酒聞名？","Intensely fruity rums":"果香濃郁的蘭姆酒","Light rums from tall columns":"以高蒸餾柱製作的清淡蘭姆酒","Grassy cane-juice rums":"草本風格的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒","Neutral rums at 96% abv":"96% abv 的中性蘭姆酒","In Jamaica, fermentation is used to create rums loaded with tropical fruit.":"在牙買加，發酵被用來創造充滿熱帶水果風味的蘭姆酒。","Light rums from tall columns are linked to Cuba and Puerto Rico. Grassy cane-juice rums are the rhum agricole of Martinique and Guadeloupe. A neutral rum at 96% would have almost no aroma, the opposite of the Jamaican style.":"以高蒸餾柱製作的清淡蘭姆酒與古巴和波多黎各有關。草本風格的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒是馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普的 rhum agricole。96% 的中性蘭姆酒幾乎沒有香氣，與牙買加風格正好相反。","How are the light-aroma rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico made?":"古巴和波多黎各香氣清淡的蘭姆酒是如何製作的？","In tall columns, to a high strength":"以高蒸餾柱蒸餾到高濃度","In pot stills, to a low strength":"以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾到低濃度","In short columns, like rhum agricole":"以矮蒸餾柱蒸餾，和 rhum agricole 一樣","With no distillation, only fermented":"不經蒸餾，只發酵","Tall columns and high strength give rums with a light aroma.":"高蒸餾柱和高濃度造就香氣清淡的蘭姆酒。","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains. Pot stills and short columns give flavourful, characterful spirits instead. Without distillation you would not have rum at all, just a low-strength fermented liquid.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下的香氣就越少。壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱得到的則是風味豐富、有個性的烈酒。沒有蒸餾就根本不是蘭姆酒，只是低濃度的發酵液。","A distillery wants a pronounced, characterful rum. Which still could it choose?":"一家蒸餾廠想要一款風味濃郁、有個性的蘭姆酒，可以選擇哪一種蒸餾器？","A pot still":"壺式蒸餾器","A tall column run to high strength":"蒸餾到高濃度的高蒸餾柱","A column still taken to 96% abv":"蒸餾到 96% abv 的柱式蒸餾器","None: charcoal filtering is enough":"都不需要：木炭過濾就夠了","A pot still gives a low-strength, pronounced, characterful spirit.":"壺式蒸餾器能得到濃度低、風味濃郁、有個性的烈酒。","A short column could also work, but among these options only the pot still points the right way. Tall columns and 96% abv lead to light or neutral spirits. Charcoal filtering does not create character; if anything, it removes colour.":"矮蒸餾柱也可以，但在這些選項中只有壺式蒸餾器指向正確方向。高蒸餾柱和 96% abv 會得到清淡或中性的烈酒。木炭過濾不會創造個性；它頂多去除顏色。","What type of still is typically used for rhum agricole?":"rhum agricole 通常使用哪一種蒸餾器？","A short column still":"矮柱式蒸餾器","A compulsory double pot still":"強制使用的壺式二次蒸餾","A pot still with a maple filter":"附楓木過濾器的壺式蒸餾器","Rhum agricole is distilled in short columns, which give a flavourful spirit.":"Rhum agricole 以矮蒸餾柱蒸餾，能得到風味豐富的烈酒。","A short column with few sections keeps plenty of intensity, similar to a pot still. Very tall columns are used for light rums. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac, and maple charcoal belongs to Tennessee whiskey.":"層數少的矮蒸餾柱能保留大量的濃郁度，類似壺式蒸餾器。很高的蒸餾柱用於清淡的蘭姆酒。強制以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾是 Cognac 的規定，楓木炭則屬於 Tennessee 威士忌。","In a country where rum must be oak-aged, how can a colourless rum be made?":"在規定蘭姆酒必須經橡木桶陳年的國家，要如何製作無色的蘭姆酒？","By charcoal filtering it after the barrel":"出桶後用木炭過濾","By adding caramel":"加入焦糖色","By diluting it with more water":"加更多水稀釋","Charcoal filtering removes the colour picked up from the wood.":"木炭過濾能去除從木頭吸收的顏色。","Caramel adds colour rather than removing it. Water lowers the strength but leaves the colour almost unchanged, and sugar changes sweetness, not shade. The other way to get a white rum, where the law allows, is not to age it and to keep it in steel.":"焦糖色是增添顏色，而不是去除顏色。水會降低濃度，但顏色幾乎不變；糖改變的是甜度，而不是色調。在法律允許的地方，另一種製作白色蘭姆酒的方法是不經陳年，並存放在不鏽鋼桶槽中。","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and columns. Why is that useful?":"許多加勒比海蒸餾廠同時擁有壺式蒸餾器和蒸餾柱，為什麼這很有用？","To have spirits of different intensities to blend":"能得到不同濃郁度的烈酒來調和","Because the law requires two distillations":"因為法律規定要蒸餾兩次","Because columns are used for ageing":"因為蒸餾柱用來陳年","Because the pot still is used to sweeten":"因為壺式蒸餾器用來加甜","Two kinds of still give light and pronounced spirits for building different styles.":"兩種蒸餾器能得到清淡與濃郁的烈酒，用來打造不同的風格。","With several types of spirit, blenders can create very different products, also combining different ages and distilleries. No general Caribbean rule requires two distillations. Columns are for distilling, not ageing, and sugar is added afterwards, not in the still.":"有了多種類型的烈酒，調和師能創造出非常不同的產品，還能結合不同年份和蒸餾廠的酒。加勒比海並沒有規定一律要蒸餾兩次。蒸餾柱是用來蒸餾的，不是用來陳年，而糖是之後才加入的，不是在蒸餾器中。","Which aromas does oak ageing add to a rum?":"橡木桶陳年為蘭姆酒增添哪些香氣？","Vanilla and sweet spice":"香草和甜香料","Intense tropical fruit":"濃郁的熱帶水果","Oak gives rum vanilla and sweet spice, as well as colour.":"橡木桶為蘭姆酒帶來香草和甜香料，以及顏色。","Grassy notes come from cane juice, the raw material. Intense tropical fruit is born in fermentation. Peat smoke is created while malting grain, so it has nothing to do with rum.":"青草氣息來自原料甘蔗汁。濃郁的熱帶水果誕生於發酵。泥煤煙燻是在穀物製麥時產生的，與蘭姆酒無關。","Which statement about adding sugar to rum is correct?":"關於在蘭姆酒中加糖，下列哪一項正確？","Common in Central and South America, banned in some countries":"在中南美洲很常見，在某些國家則被禁止","Required for every Caribbean rum":"所有加勒比海蘭姆酒都必須加糖","Banned everywhere in the world":"全世界都禁止","Happens on its own during ageing":"在陳年過程中自然發生","Some rums are sweetened: common in Central and South America, but not allowed everywhere.":"有些蘭姆酒會加甜：在中南美洲很常見，但並非到處都允許。","The rules change from country to country, so neither a requirement nor a ban applies everywhere. Every spirit is dry when it leaves the still: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation, not from the barrel.":"規定因國家而異，所以沒有放諸四海皆準的要求或禁令。所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的：甜味只來自蒸餾後添加的糖，而不是來自酒桶。","A rum has a deep amber colour. What can you conclude for certain?":"一款蘭姆酒呈現深琥珀色。你能確定什麼？","Nothing about age: the colour may come from caramel":"無法判斷年份：顏色可能來自焦糖色","That it was aged at least ten years":"它至少陳年了十年","That it was made from fresh cane juice":"它是用新鮮甘蔗汁製成的","Many rums get caramel, sometimes for almost all their colour, so shade proves nothing about age.":"許多蘭姆酒會加入焦糖色，有時幾乎所有顏色都來自焦糖色，所以色調無法證明年份。","This is why sorting rum by colour works badly. Colour also says nothing about the raw material or the type of still: those depend on the production stages, not on the shade in the glass.":"這就是為什麼依顏色分類蘭姆酒的效果很差。顏色也無法說明原料或蒸餾器類型：這些取決於生產階段，而不是杯中的色調。","Which plant is Tequila made from?":"Tequila 是用哪一種植物製成的？","By law, Tequila must be made from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico.":"依法規，Tequila 必須以原產於墨西哥的藍色龍舌蘭製成。","Blue agave is the only plant allowed and gives Tequila its herbaceous, peppery aromas. Sugar cane is the raw material of rum, corn is the main grain in Bourbon, and potato is one of the classic raw materials for vodka.":"藍色龍舌蘭是唯一允許的植物，為 Tequila 帶來草本和胡椒般的香氣。甘蔗是蘭姆酒的原料，玉米是 Bourbon 的主要穀物，馬鈴薯則是伏特加的經典原料之一。","Where can Tequila be made?":"Tequila 可以在哪裡生產？","Only in certain states of Mexico":"只能在墨西哥的特定州","In any state of Mexico":"墨西哥的任何一州","Anywhere in Central America":"中美洲任何地方","Wherever blue agave grows":"任何種植藍色龍舌蘭的地方","The law limits production to certain named Mexican states.":"法律將生產限制在墨西哥特定指名的州。","Being in Mexico is not enough: only certain states are allowed. Growing blue agave elsewhere does not earn the name Tequila, and Central America is outside the zone. This is a key difference from vodka, which can be made anywhere.":"光在墨西哥還不夠：只有特定的州才允許。在其他地方種植藍色龍舌蘭並不能使用 Tequila 這個名稱，而中美洲在產區之外。這是與可以在任何地方生產的伏特加的關鍵差異。","Why are agave cores cooked in ovens?":"為什麼要把龍舌蘭心放進窯爐烹煮？","To soften them and create sugars":"讓它變軟並產生糖","To give them a smoky aroma":"讓它帶有煙燻香氣","To remove their colour":"去除它的顏色","To kill the natural yeasts":"殺死天然酵母","Cooking softens the core and forms the sugars needed for fermentation.":"烹煮能讓龍舌蘭心變軟，並形成發酵所需的糖。","Like grains, freshly harvested agave has no sugar ready to use: without cooking there would be nothing to ferment. Smoke is not the goal (that is more the peat in some Scotch whiskies), colour is irrelevant, and yeast is needed right afterwards for fermentation.":"和穀物一樣，剛採收的龍舌蘭沒有現成可用的糖：不烹煮就沒有東西可以發酵。目標不是煙燻味（那比較像某些 Scotch 威士忌的泥煤），顏色也無關緊要，而酵母在烹煮之後立刻就需要用來發酵。","A Tequila label says ‘Silver’. What does that tell you?":"Tequila 酒標上寫著「Silver」。這告訴你什麼？","It is an unaged Tequila, the same as Blanco":"它是未陳年的 Tequila，和 Blanco 一樣","It has been aged for 2 to 12 months":"它陳年了 2 到 12 個月","It is made from 100% agave":"它是用 100% agave 製成的","It has been coloured with caramel":"它用焦糖色著色過","Silver is another name for Blanco: unaged Tequila.":"Silver 是 Blanco 的另一個名稱：未陳年的 Tequila。","Blanco and Silver name the same style, colourless with a pure agave profile. The 2–12 month period belongs to Reposado; ‘100% agave’ is a separate piece of information, and caramel is typical of Joven/Oro instead.":"Blanco 和 Silver 指的是同一種風格，無色，呈現純粹的龍舌蘭風味。2–12 個月屬於 Reposado；「100% agave」是另一項獨立資訊，而焦糖色則是 Joven／Oro 的典型做法。","What minimum share of the sugars in any Tequila must come from blue agave?":"任何 Tequila 的糖分中，至少要有多少比例來自藍色龍舌蘭？","At least 51% of the fermented sugars must come from blue agave.":"發酵的糖分中至少 51% 必須來自藍色龍舌蘭。","The producer may add other sugars, but agave must stay in the majority. 100% is not compulsory: it is the condition for writing ‘100% agave’ on the label. The 25% and 75% figures match no rule.":"生產者可以加入其他糖，但龍舌蘭必須佔多數。100% 並非強制：那是在酒標上標示「100% agave」的條件。25% 和 75% 這兩個數字不符合任何規定。","What does ‘100% agave’ on a Tequila label guarantee?":"Tequila 酒標上的「100% agave」保證什麼？","No sugar other than blue agave was used":"除了藍色龍舌蘭，沒有使用其他糖","Distillation in pot stills only":"只使用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾","A minimum period in oak":"在橡木桶中有最低陳年時間","No caramel or other additives":"沒有焦糖色或其他添加物","It means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid.":"表示製作含糖液體時只使用了藍色龍舌蘭。","The term is only about where the sugars came from. It says nothing about the type of still or about ageing: there are both unaged and aged ‘100% agave’ Tequilas. Nor does it promise no caramel, which may be used in aged versions.":"這個術語只關乎糖的來源。它與蒸餾器類型或陳年無關：「100% agave」的 Tequila 有未陳年的，也有陳年的。它也不保證沒有焦糖色，陳年款可能會使用焦糖色。","A customer wants the purest possible expression of agave. Which Tequila would you suggest?":"一位顧客想要最純粹的龍舌蘭風味。你會建議哪一款 Tequila？","A Blanco labelled 100% agave":"標示 100% agave 的 Blanco","An Añejo labelled 100% agave":"標示 100% agave 的 Añejo","A Joven/Oro":"Joven／Oro","A Reposado with no other label terms":"沒有其他酒標術語的 Reposado","Blanco sees no oak, and ‘100% agave’ rules out other sugars: agave has the stage to itself.":"Blanco 不接觸橡木桶，「100% agave」排除了其他糖：舞台完全留給龍舌蘭。","Two choices point the same way: no oak and only agave sugars. Añejo adds oak notes, Joven/Oro has caramel and additives that soften its texture, and a Reposado without ‘100% agave’ may contain other sugars on top of its time in oak.":"兩個選擇指向同一個方向：不經橡木桶，而且只有龍舌蘭的糖。Añejo 增添了橡木氣息，Joven／Oro 含有焦糖色和讓口感變柔和的添加物，而沒有「100% agave」的 Reposado 除了在橡木桶中的時間，還可能含有其他糖。","How are the best Tequilas distilled?":"最優秀的 Tequila 如何蒸餾？","Twice in pot stills, to a low strength":"以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾兩次，到較低濃度","Once in a tall column, to 96% abv":"以高蒸餾柱蒸餾一次，到 96% abv","Three times in columns, to a high strength":"以蒸餾柱蒸餾三次，到高濃度","Once in a pot still, then charcoal filtered":"以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾一次，再經木炭過濾","Double pot distillation to a low strength keeps the agave aromas.":"以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾到較低濃度，能保留龍舌蘭的香氣。","The lower the strength, the more aroma stays in the spirit. A tall column reaching 96% abv makes a neutral spirit, the opposite of what is wanted. Charcoal filtering is not part of the typical Tequila method; it belongs rather to Tennessee whiskey or some white rums.":"濃度越低，留在烈酒中的香氣就越多。達到 96% abv 的高蒸餾柱會製成中性烈酒，與想要的正好相反。木炭過濾不屬於 Tequila 的典型做法，而是屬於 Tennessee 威士忌或某些白色蘭姆酒。","Which aromas are typical of blue agave?":"哪些香氣是藍色龍舌蘭的典型特徵？","Herbaceous, earthy and peppery":"草本、泥土和胡椒","Cereal, honey and smoke":"穀物、蜂蜜和煙燻","Vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn":"香草、椰子和甜玉米","Blue agave brings herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy and peppery notes.":"藍色龍舌蘭帶來草本、植物、橄欖、泥土和胡椒氣息。","Every raw material leaves its signature. Cereal, honey and smoke point to a peated Scotch single malt, caramel and brown sugar to a molasses rum, and vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn to a Bourbon aged in new oak.":"每種原料都會留下自己的印記。穀物、蜂蜜和煙燻指向泥煤風格的 Scotch 單一麥芽威士忌，焦糖和紅糖指向糖蜜蘭姆酒，香草、椰子和甜玉米則指向在新橡木桶中陳年的 Bourbon。","How long is a Reposado Tequila aged in oak?":"Reposado Tequila 在橡木桶中陳年多久？","Between 2 and 12 months":"2 到 12 個月","At least 12 months":"至少 12 個月","At least 2 years":"至少 2 年","It is not aged at all":"完全不經陳年","Reposado rests in oak for 2 to 12 months.":"Reposado 在橡木桶中靜置 2 到 12 個月。","At least 12 months is the Añejo rule; no ageing applies to Blanco and Joven. At least 2 years recalls the Cognac minimum (VS), not a Tequila rule.":"至少 12 個月是 Añejo 的規定；Blanco 和 Joven 則不經陳年。至少 2 年讓人想到 Cognac 的最低要求（VS），並不是 Tequila 的規定。","Which Tequila style spends at least 12 months in oak?":"哪一種 Tequila 風格在橡木桶中至少陳年 12 個月？","Añejo is aged for at least 12 months and combines agave and oak.":"Añejo 至少陳年 12 個月，結合了龍舌蘭和橡木。","Reposado stops at between 2 and 12 months. Blanco and Joven are unaged: Joven may look mature because of its golden colour, but that colour comes from caramel, not from a barrel.":"Reposado 只陳年 2 到 12 個月。Blanco 和 Joven 未經陳年：Joven 可能因為金黃色而看起來像陳年過，但那個顏色來自焦糖色，而不是酒桶。","Where does the golden colour of a Joven (Oro) Tequila come from?":"Joven（Oro）Tequila 的金黃色來自哪裡？","Added caramel":"添加的焦糖色","A few months in oak":"在橡木桶中待了幾個月","A golden variety of agave":"金黃色品種的龍舌蘭","A longer cooking time":"較長的烹煮時間","Joven is unaged: it is coloured with caramel and softened with other additives.":"Joven 未經陳年：它用焦糖色著色，並用其他添加物讓口感變柔和。","It is a classic trap: the golden look suggests wood, but Joven never goes into a barrel. Tequila is made only from blue agave, not a ‘golden’ variety, and cooking creates sugars rather than colour; the spirit always leaves the still colourless.":"這是經典陷阱：金黃的外觀讓人聯想到木桶，但 Joven 從未進桶。Tequila 只用藍色龍舌蘭製成，沒有「金黃色」品種，而烹煮產生的是糖而不是顏色；烈酒離開蒸餾器時一定是無色的。","Which statement about Reposado Tequila is true?":"關於 Reposado Tequila，下列哪一項正確？","It is softer, but agave stays in the lead":"口感較柔和，但龍舌蘭仍居主導","Oak flavours dominate the agave":"橡木風味蓋過了龍舌蘭","It is always made from 100% agave":"一定是用 100% agave 製成","It spends at least two years in barrel":"在桶中至少陳年兩年","Its short time in oak softens it without erasing the agave.":"在橡木桶中的短暫時間讓它變得柔和，但沒有抹去龍舌蘭風味。","With 2–12 months in oak, the wood rarely takes over, so the agave stays pronounced; two years would be well beyond the limit. A Reposado can be ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’, like any other style.":"在橡木桶中 2–12 個月，木頭很少喧賓奪主，所以龍舌蘭風味依然鮮明；兩年則遠遠超出上限。Reposado 可以是「100% agave」，也可以只是「Tequila」，和其他風格一樣。","Why are aged Tequilas rarely matured for very long?":"為什麼陳年 Tequila 很少熟成很久？","To keep oak from masking the agave character":"避免橡木掩蓋龍舌蘭的個性","Because the law forbids more than a year in oak":"因為法律禁止在橡木桶中超過一年","Because agave ruins the barrels":"因為龍舌蘭會損壞酒桶","Because the Mexican climate evaporates it all":"因為墨西哥的氣候會讓酒全部蒸發","Producers want a balance between oak's vanilla and spice and the agave.":"生產者追求橡木的香草、香料與龍舌蘭之間的平衡。","It is a style choice, not a ban: Añejo, for example, has a 12-month minimum and no maximum. The other two answers have no basis: the aim is for oak to support the agave, not dominate it.":"這是風格上的選擇，不是禁令：例如 Añejo 有 12 個月的最低要求，但沒有上限。另外兩個答案毫無根據：目標是讓橡木襯托龍舌蘭，而不是壓過它。","Which statement about Tequila labels is true?":"關於 Tequila 酒標，下列哪一項正確？","Any style can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’":"任何風格都可以是「Tequila」或「100% agave」","Only Añejo can be ‘100% agave’":"只有 Añejo 可以是「100% agave」","Blanco must always be ‘100% agave’":"Blanco 一定要是「100% agave」","A ‘100% agave’ Tequila must be aged":"「100% agave」的 Tequila 必須經過陳年","Sugar source and ageing are two independent pieces of information.":"糖的來源和陳年是兩項彼此獨立的資訊。","Blanco, Joven, Reposado and Añejo can all be either ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’. The other answers wrongly tie the sugar term to one style or to ageing, which the law does not do.":"Blanco、Joven、Reposado 和 Añejo 都可以是「100% agave」或單純的「Tequila」。其他答案錯誤地把糖的術語與某一種風格或陳年綁在一起，法律並沒有這樣規定。","What is the correct order of the first steps in making Tequila?":"製作 Tequila 的前幾個步驟，正確順序是什麼？","Cut the leaves, cook, crush, ferment":"切除葉片、烹煮、壓碎、發酵","Crush, cook, cut the leaves, ferment":"壓碎、烹煮、切除葉片、發酵","Cut the leaves, ferment, cook, crush":"切除葉片、發酵、烹煮、壓碎","Cook, ferment, crush, cut the leaves":"烹煮、發酵、壓碎、切除葉片","The core is freed, cooked to create sugars, crushed to release juice, then fermented.":"先取出龍舌蘭心，烹煮以產生糖，壓碎以釋出汁液，然後發酵。","Logic helps: fermentation needs a sugary liquid, so the sugars must already exist (cooking) and be extracted (crushing). A raw core is too hard to crush usefully, and fermenting before cooking would leave no sugar to work on.":"用邏輯推理會有幫助：發酵需要含糖液體，所以糖必須已經存在（烹煮）並被萃取出來（壓碎）。生的龍舌蘭心太硬，很難有效壓碎，而在烹煮前發酵，就沒有糖可以作用。","What does a flavoured-spirit producer usually start from?":"調味烈酒的生產者通常從什麼開始？","A bought-in neutral spirit":"外購的中性烈酒","Fruit harvested and fermented on site":"在廠內採收並發酵的水果","An oak-aged brandy":"經橡木桶陳年的白蘭地","A mash of malted grain":"麥芽穀物的糖化醪","Most buy in the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka.":"大多數生產者外購的中性烈酒，和製作伏特加的是同一種。","These spirits do not need to start from a raw material: the work lies in the flavouring. Rum, whisky or brandy are only occasionally used as a base, and fermenting fruit or grain in-house is not the norm.":"這些烈酒不需要從原料開始：功夫在於調味。蘭姆酒、威士忌或白蘭地只偶爾被用作基底，而在廠內發酵水果或穀物並不是常態。","What do you get by redistilling neutral spirit with botanicals?":"把中性烈酒與植物性原料一起再蒸餾，會得到什麼？","A flavoured, colourless spirit":"有風味的無色烈酒","A flavoured, coloured spirit":"有風味的有色烈酒","A sweet, coloured spirit":"甜的有色烈酒","A spirit that is neutral again":"再次變成中性的烈酒","The vapour carries the botanicals' aromas but not their colour.":"蒸氣會帶走植物性原料的香氣，但不會帶走它們的顏色。","Everything that leaves a still is colourless and dry, so there is no colour and no sweetness. Colour comes from maceration, sweetness from added sugar. The aromas do come through, though, so the result is far from neutral.":"所有離開蒸餾器的東西都是無色、不甜的，所以沒有顏色也沒有甜味。顏色來自浸漬，甜味來自添加的糖。不過香氣確實會被帶過來，所以結果絕非中性。","What is maceration?":"什麼是浸漬？","Steeping botanicals in the spirit":"把植物性原料浸泡在烈酒中","Distilling the spirit with botanicals":"把烈酒與植物性原料一起蒸餾","Adding concentrated essences":"加入濃縮香精","Ageing the spirit in used barrels":"在用過的桶中陳年烈酒","In maceration the botanicals soak and release flavour and colour.":"浸漬時，植物性原料浸泡在酒中，釋出風味和顏色。","Distilling with botanicals is redistillation, and adding essences is the third method, bought-in flavourings. Time in barrel is ageing: it gives oak aromas, not those of fruit, herbs and spices.":"與植物性原料一起蒸餾是再蒸餾，加入香精則是第三種方法，也就是外購調味料。在桶中的時間是陳年：它帶來的是橡木香氣，而不是水果、香草和香料的香氣。","A producer wants to extract more flavour, faster, during maceration. What can they do?":"生產者想在浸漬時更快萃取出更多風味，可以怎麼做？","Gently heat the spirit":"溫和加熱烈酒","Chill the spirit":"冷卻烈酒","Add caramel":"加入焦糖色","Gentle heat speeds up flavour extraction.":"溫和加熱能加快風味的萃取。","As with tea, heat helps extraction and cold slows it. Caramel adds colour but no flavour, and charcoal filtering removes things (impurities or colour) rather than adding aroma.":"就像泡茶一樣，熱能幫助萃取，冷則會減緩萃取。焦糖色增添顏色但不增添風味，木炭過濾則是去除東西（雜質或顏色），而不是增添香氣。","Why do some producers use bought-in flavourings instead of botanicals?":"為什麼有些生產者使用外購調味料，而不用植物性原料？","Mostly for reasons of cost":"主要是出於成本考量","Because the law requires it for gin":"因為法律規定琴酒必須使用","To give the spirit colour":"為了給烈酒上色","Because they raise the strength":"因為它們能提高濃度","Concentrated bought-in flavourings are usually a cost-driven choice.":"使用外購的濃縮調味料，通常是出於成本考量的選擇。","The law does not make gin use them: in fact the best gins are redistilled with real botanicals. Flavourings are used in small doses for taste, not colour, and have nothing to do with strength.":"法律並沒有要求琴酒使用調味料：事實上，最優秀的琴酒是與真正的植物性原料一起再蒸餾的。調味料以小劑量使用，是為了味道而不是顏色，也與濃度無關。","What are ‘botanicals’?":"什麼是「植物性原料」（botanicals）？","Fruits, seeds, herbs and spices used for flavour":"用來增添風味的水果、種子、香草和香料","Highly concentrated artificial flavours":"高度濃縮的人工香料","The yeasts that start fermentation":"啟動發酵的酵母","The plants used to make barrels":"用來製作酒桶的植物","They are the natural ingredients that flavour flavoured spirits.":"它們是為調味烈酒增添風味的天然原料。","Artificial flavours are the alternative to botanicals, not the same thing. Yeast turns sugar into alcohol and barrel oak gives ageing aromas: neither fits the definition.":"人工香料是植物性原料的替代品，而不是同一種東西。酵母把糖轉化為酒精，桶用橡木則帶來陳年香氣：兩者都不符合這個定義。","Which flavour must lead in a gin?":"琴酒中必須以哪一種風味為主？","Coriander":"芫荽籽","Lemon peel":"檸檬皮","By definition, gin must have juniper as its main flavour.":"依照定義，琴酒必須以杜松子為主要風味。","Coriander and citrus peel are common gin botanicals, but they play supporting roles. Gentian is a classic bitter botanical, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines, not the heart of gin.":"芫荽籽和柑橘皮是常見的琴酒植物性原料，但扮演的是配角。龍膽是經典的苦味植物性原料，常見於苦味烈酒和加味葡萄酒，而不是琴酒的核心。","What does the term ‘London Dry Gin’ tell you?":"「London Dry Gin」這個術語告訴你什麼？","The flavours were added by redistillation":"風味是透過再蒸餾加入的","The gin was made in London":"這款琴酒是在倫敦製作的","The gin has been aged in oak":"這款琴酒經過橡木桶陳年","The gin contains no juniper":"這款琴酒不含杜松子","It is a method term: flavours added during redistillation.":"這是一個製法術語：風味在再蒸餾時加入。","The name is misleading, but it is not a place: it can be made anywhere. Typical gin is unaged, and a gin without leading juniper would not be gin at all.":"這個名稱容易誤導，但它不是地名：可以在任何地方製作。典型的琴酒不經陳年，而不以杜松子為主的琴酒根本就不是琴酒。","Which group lists typical gin botanicals besides juniper?":"除了杜松子，哪一組列出了典型的琴酒植物性原料？","Coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel":"芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根、柑橘皮","Gentian, quinine, wormwood, bitter orange":"龍膽、奎寧、苦艾、苦橙","Mint, lime, cane sugar, cream":"薄荷、萊姆、蔗糖、鮮奶油","Coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel are classic gin botanicals.":"芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根和柑橘皮是經典的琴酒植物性原料。","The second group is made of bitter botanicals, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines. Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves and coconut recall the aromas oak gives. The fourth group looks like cocktail ingredients or a cream liqueur.":"第二組是苦味植物性原料，常見於苦味烈酒和加味葡萄酒。香草、肉桂、丁香和椰子讓人想到橡木帶來的香氣。第四組看起來像調酒材料或奶酒。","What is a typical gin like?":"典型的琴酒是什麼樣子？","Colourless and unaged":"無色、未經陳年","Golden and oak-aged":"金黃色、經橡木桶陳年","Colourless and sweetened":"無色、經過加甜","Amber and coloured with caramel":"琥珀色、以焦糖色著色","Typical gin sees no oak and stays clear.":"典型的琴酒不接觸橡木桶，保持清澈。","A golden or amber colour would suggest oak or caramel, neither of which belongs to typical gin. A colourless but sweetened gin would be closer to a liqueur: sweetness is not a feature of gin.":"金黃色或琥珀色暗示橡木桶或焦糖色，兩者都不屬於典型的琴酒。無色但加甜的琴酒會比較接近利口酒：甜味不是琴酒的特徵。","How are flavoured vodkas usually made?":"調味伏特加通常如何製作？","Neutral vodka plus bought-in flavourings":"中性伏特加加上外購調味料","Long maceration in oak barrels":"在橡木桶中長時間浸漬","Distilling the fruit directly":"直接蒸餾水果","Adding sugar and caramel":"加入糖和焦糖色","Most add bought-in flavourings to neutral vodka; some redistil.":"大多數是在中性伏特加中加入外購調味料；有些則會再蒸餾。","The base is the same neutral vodka, not a fruit spirit. Oak plays no part, and sugar plus caramel would lead to a coloured liqueur, not a flavoured vodka.":"基底是同樣的中性伏特加，而不是水果烈酒。橡木桶完全不參與，而糖加上焦糖色會做出有顏色的利口酒，而不是調味伏特加。","What do all bitter spirits have in common?":"所有苦味烈酒的共同點是什麼？","At least one bitter botanical, such as gentian":"至少一種苦味植物性原料，例如龍膽","A minimum time in oak":"在橡木桶中的最低陳年時間","A dark rum base":"以深色蘭姆酒為基底","A legal minimum sugar level":"法定的最低含糖量","Gentian, quinine or bitter orange provide the bitterness.":"龍膽、奎寧或苦橙帶來苦味。","No oak or rum base is needed. The legal minimum sweetness is the rule for liqueurs, not for bitter spirits.":"不需要橡木桶或蘭姆酒基底。法定的最低甜度是利口酒的規定，而不是苦味烈酒的。","When tasting a bitter spirit, where is the bitterness detected?":"品飲苦味烈酒時，在哪裡察覺苦味？","Only on the nose":"只在香氣中","On both nose and palate":"香氣和口中都有","Already from the colour":"從顏色就能看出","Bitterness is a taste: it is felt in the mouth, not smelled.":"苦味是一種味道：要在口中感受，而不是用鼻子聞。","On the nose you pick up the aromas of the botanicals, bitter or not, but not the bitterness itself. Colour reveals nothing about taste: a bitter spirit can be coloured like any other.":"在香氣中你會聞到植物性原料的香氣，不論苦不苦，但聞不到苦味本身。顏色無法透露味道：苦味烈酒可以和其他烈酒一樣有顏色。","A bartender wants to add complexity to a drink with just a few drops. What do they reach for?":"調酒師只想用幾滴就為飲品增添複雜度，會拿什麼？","A spiced rum":"香料蘭姆酒","A London Dry Gin":"London Dry Gin","Cocktail bitters are so concentrated that a few dashes are enough.":"調酒用苦精非常濃縮，幾滴就夠了。","Cream liqueur, spiced rum and gin are used in normal measures and can be drunk on their own. Cocktail bitters are never drunk neat: they are there only to add depth to a drink.":"奶酒、香料蘭姆酒和琴酒都以一般份量使用，也可以單獨飲用。調酒用苦精從不單喝：它們只用來為飲品增添深度。","When were bitter spirits traditionally drunk?":"傳統上，苦味烈酒在什麼時候飲用？","At the start or end of a meal":"在用餐開始或結束時","Only with breakfast":"只在早餐時","Only as a cooking ingredient":"只作為烹飪材料","Only diluted in hot water":"只用熱水稀釋後飲用","Traditionally they opened or closed a meal; today they are mostly used in cocktails.":"傳統上它們用來開啟或結束一餐；如今則主要用於調酒。","Their classic place was around a meal, as an aperitif or digestif. The other answers describe invented habits: today their main use is in mixing.":"它們的經典位置在用餐前後，作為餐前酒或餐後酒。其他答案描述的是虛構的習慣：如今它們主要用於調酒。","Which statement about spiced rum is true?":"關於香料蘭姆酒，下列哪一項正確？","It often starts from a light, unaged rum":"通常以清淡、未陳年的蘭姆酒為基底","It must always start from an aged rum":"一定要以陳年蘭姆酒為基底","It may only be flavoured with botanicals":"只能用植物性原料調味","Its colour always comes from oak":"它的顏色一定來自橡木桶","Many spiced rums use a light unaged rum, flavoured and coloured with caramel.":"許多香料蘭姆酒使用清淡的未陳年蘭姆酒，經調味並以焦糖色著色。","Only a handful of spiced rums start from an oak-aged rum. Both botanicals and other flavourings are used, and the colour often comes from caramel: an amber look does not prove long ageing.":"只有少數香料蘭姆酒以橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒為基底。植物性原料和其他調味料都會使用，而顏色常常來自焦糖色：琥珀色的外觀不能證明陳年很久。","What sets a liqueur apart from a plain flavoured spirit?":"利口酒與單純的調味烈酒有什麼不同？","It has also been sweetened":"它還經過了加甜","It has been aged in oak":"它經過橡木桶陳年","It always contains cream":"它一定含有鮮奶油","It has a higher strength":"它的濃度比較高","Liqueur = flavoured spirit plus sugar.":"利口酒 = 調味烈酒加上糖。","Ageing is not part of the definition. Cream appears only in some liqueurs, not all. And no rule demands a higher strength: what matters is the sweetness.":"陳年不屬於定義的一部分。鮮奶油只出現在某些利口酒中，不是全部。也沒有規定要求更高的濃度：重點在甜度。","What does the law say about sugar in liqueurs?":"關於利口酒中的糖，法律怎麼規定？","There must be a minimum level of sweetness":"必須達到最低甜度","Sugar is not allowed":"不允許加糖","Sugar is optional":"加糖可有可無","Sugar may only come from fruit":"糖只能來自水果","To be called a liqueur, a spirit must reach a minimum sweetness.":"要稱為利口酒，烈酒必須達到最低甜度。","Sugar is not just allowed but required, so it cannot be banned or optional. It is added after flavouring and does not have to come from fruit.":"糖不只是允許，而是必須的，所以不可能被禁止或可有可無。糖是在調味之後加入的，也不一定要來自水果。","Which ingredient, unusual for a spirit, is found in some liqueurs?":"某些利口酒中含有哪一種對烈酒來說不尋常的原料？","Some liqueurs contain cream, a notable ingredient in this category.":"有些利口酒含有鮮奶油，這是這個類別中一個值得注意的原料。","Yeast is for fermentation, before distillation, and is not added to a liqueur. Wine as a base belongs to aromatised wines, a different category. Sea water plays no part.":"酵母用於蒸餾前的發酵，不會加進利口酒。以葡萄酒為基底屬於加味葡萄酒，是另一個類別。海水則毫無關係。","Why do many liqueurs use artificial colourings?":"為什麼許多利口酒使用人工色素？","Natural colour fades quickly":"天然顏色很快就會褪色","They make the liqueur sweeter":"它們能讓利口酒更甜","The law bans natural colours":"法律禁止使用天然色素","They add fruity aromas":"它們能增添果香","Artificial colours keep the colour stable and offer more shades.":"人工色素讓顏色保持穩定，並提供更多色調。","Natural colour from maceration is allowed, but it loses its brightness: so more stable colourings are preferred, which also allow very vivid shades. Colourings add neither sweetness nor aroma; those come from sugar and flavouring.":"來自浸漬的天然顏色是允許的，但會失去鮮豔度：所以生產者偏好較穩定的色素，這些色素還能呈現非常鮮豔的色調。色素既不增添甜味也不增添香氣；那些來自糖和調味。","What is an aromatised wine?":"什麼是加味葡萄酒？","A wine with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit":"加入調味料、糖和少量烈酒的葡萄酒","A wine spirit aged in oak":"經橡木桶陳年的葡萄酒烈酒","A liqueur based on neutral spirit":"以中性烈酒為基底的利口酒","A wine left to oxidise in barrel":"在桶中氧化的葡萄酒","It is wine-based, not a spirit, with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit added.":"它以葡萄酒為基底，而不是烈酒，並加入了調味料、糖和少量烈酒。","An aged wine spirit is a brandy, such as Cognac. A liqueur starts from a spirit, not a wine. Oxidation in barrel is not part of the definition: what counts is the flavourings, always including something bitter.":"陳年的葡萄酒烈酒是白蘭地，例如 Cognac。利口酒以烈酒為起點，而不是葡萄酒。在桶中氧化不屬於定義：重要的是調味料，而且一定包含某種苦味。","Which list gives the four components of every aromatised wine?":"哪一組列出了所有加味葡萄酒的四個組成部分？","Wine, flavourings incl. a bitter, sugar, spirit":"葡萄酒、含苦味的調味料、糖、烈酒","Wine, flavourings, caramel, soda water":"葡萄酒、調味料、焦糖色、蘇打水","Spirit, sugar, cream, colourings":"烈酒、糖、鮮奶油、色素","Wine, fruit juice, sugar, yeast":"葡萄酒、果汁、糖、酵母","Base wine, flavourings (always with something bitter), sugar and a little spirit.":"基酒、調味料（一定包含某種苦味）、糖和少量烈酒。","Caramel is only optional and soda water does not belong. Spirit, cream and colourings describe a cream liqueur instead. Juice and yeast are not part of the recipe, and that list leaves out the spirit, which is required.":"焦糖色只是可選的，蘇打水則不屬於配方。烈酒、鮮奶油和色素描述的是奶酒。果汁和酵母不在配方中，而且那組遺漏了必需的烈酒。","Why is a little spirit added to an aromatised wine?":"為什麼要在加味葡萄酒中加入少量烈酒？","To raise the alcohol and make it keep longer":"提高酒精濃度，並讓它保存更久","The spirit raises alcohol and extends shelf life, even once opened.":"烈酒能提高酒精濃度並延長保存期限，即使開瓶後也一樣。","A neutral spirit is nearly always used, so it brings no colour or oak notes. Spirits are dry: sweetness comes from the wine or added sugar, and any colour from caramel.":"幾乎總是使用中性烈酒，所以不會帶來顏色或橡木氣息。烈酒是不甜的：甜味來自葡萄酒或添加的糖，顏色則來自焦糖色。","Which type of spirit is nearly always used in aromatised wines?":"加味葡萄酒幾乎都使用哪一種烈酒？","A neutral spirit":"中性烈酒","An aged brandy":"陳年白蘭地","A peated whisky":"泥煤威士忌","Neutral spirit raises the strength without clashing with the chosen flavours.":"中性烈酒能提高濃度，又不會與選用的風味衝突。","A characterful spirit would bring its own aromas, such as oak, peat or molasses, competing with the recipe. Here the spirit's role is technical, not aromatic.":"有個性的烈酒會帶來自己的香氣，例如橡木、泥煤或糖蜜，與配方互相競爭。在這裡，烈酒扮演的是技術性角色，而不是香氣角色。","Which group lists bitter botanicals used in aromatised wines?":"哪一組列出了加味葡萄酒使用的苦味植物性原料？","Wormwood, gentian, quinine":"苦艾、龍膽、奎寧","Juniper, coriander, angelica":"杜松子、芫荽籽、歐白芷根","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon":"香草、椰子、肉桂","Mint, lime, ginger":"薄荷、萊姆、薑","Every recipe includes a bitter, such as wormwood, gentian or quinine.":"每個配方都包含一種苦味原料，例如苦艾、龍膽或奎寧。","Juniper, coriander and angelica are gin classics, and they are not bitter. Vanilla, coconut and cinnamon recall oak aromas. Mint, lime and ginger suggest a long drink, not an aromatised wine recipe.":"杜松子、芫荽籽和歐白芷根是琴酒的經典原料，而且不苦。香草、椰子和肉桂讓人想到橡木香氣。薄荷、萊姆和薑則像是長飲，而不是加味葡萄酒的配方。","Which botanical must vermouth be flavoured with?":"香艾酒必須以哪一種植物性原料調味？","Bitter orange":"苦橙","Wormwood is required in vermouth.":"香艾酒必須使用苦艾。","Juniper is gin's signature. Bitter orange and quinine are bitter botanicals that may appear in aromatised wines and bitter spirits, but the vermouth rule is specifically about wormwood.":"杜松子是琴酒的標誌。苦橙和奎寧是可能出現在加味葡萄酒和苦味烈酒中的苦味原料，但香艾酒的規定特別指的是苦艾。","A red vermouth is made from white wine. Where does its colour usually come from?":"一款紅香艾酒是用白葡萄酒製成的，它的顏色通常來自哪裡？","Black grape skins":"黑葡萄的果皮","Long ageing in oak":"在橡木桶中長時間陳年","Macerated juniper":"浸漬的杜松子","With a white base, the red colour usually comes from caramel.":"以白葡萄酒為基底時，紅色通常來自焦糖色。","If the base is white, black grape skins play no part. Long oak ageing is not part of the recipe, and juniper is a gin botanical that does not turn things red. Caramel can also add a light caramel aroma.":"如果基底是白葡萄酒，黑葡萄的果皮就沒有作用。長時間橡木桶陳年不屬於配方，而杜松子是琴酒的原料，不會讓酒變紅。焦糖色還能增添淡淡的焦糖香氣。","A customer orders a ‘dry’ vermouth thinking it has no sugar. What is the correct reply?":"一位顧客點了「dry」（不甜）香艾酒，以為裡面沒有糖。正確的回答是什麼？","It nearly always contains added sugar":"它幾乎都含有添加的糖","By law it contains no sugar at all":"依法規它完全不含糖","It is sweeter than a red vermouth":"它比紅香艾酒更甜","It is made without wine":"它不是用葡萄酒製成的","Even ‘dry’ vermouths nearly always have some added sugar.":"即使是「dry」香艾酒，幾乎都加了一些糖。","Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry, and no rule bans sugar in ‘dry’. It is red vermouth that is usually heavily sweetened. And every vermouth starts from a white wine.":"幾乎沒有加味葡萄酒是完全不甜的，也沒有規定禁止「dry」款加糖。通常大量加甜的是紅香艾酒。而所有香艾酒都以白葡萄酒為起點。","Which areas are best known for aromatised wines?":"哪些地區最以加味葡萄酒聞名？","South-east France and north-west Italy":"法國東南部和義大利西北部","Northern France and southern Italy":"法國北部和義大利南部","Scotland and Ireland":"蘇格蘭和愛爾蘭","Mexico and the Caribbean":"墨西哥和加勒比海","They are made everywhere, but the famous areas are south-east France and north-west Italy.":"加味葡萄酒到處都有生產，但著名的產區是法國東南部和義大利西北部。","The second answer flips the directions. Scotland and Ireland point to whisky, Mexico and the Caribbean to Tequila and rum: those are spirits, while this is about wine-based products.":"第二個答案把方位弄反了。蘇格蘭和愛爾蘭指向威士忌，墨西哥和加勒比海指向 Tequila 和蘭姆酒：那些都是烈酒，而這題問的是以葡萄酒為基底的產品。","Why are aromatised wines so useful in cocktails?":"為什麼加味葡萄酒在調酒中這麼有用？","They bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity at once":"它們同時帶來甜味、苦味和酸度","They are the strongest spirit in the drink":"它們是飲品中最烈的酒","They add colour without changing the taste":"它們能增添顏色而不改變味道","They replace ice for dilution":"它們能取代冰塊來稀釋","One ingredient adds sweetness, bitterness and acidity to the drink.":"一種材料就能為飲品增添甜味、苦味和酸度。","They are wines with a little spirit, so far weaker than the base spirit, which is usually 40% abv or more. They clearly change the taste, and dilution is still the job of ice and non-alcoholic ingredients.":"它們是加了少量烈酒的葡萄酒，所以比通常 40% abv 以上的基酒弱得多。它們會明顯改變味道，而稀釋仍然是冰塊和無酒精材料的工作。","Why is water added to the sample when tasting a spirit?":"品飲烈酒時，為什麼要在樣品中加水？","Because at 40% abv it is hard to judge accurately":"因為在 40% abv 時很難準確判斷","Because water changes the colour and makes it easier to read":"因為水會改變顏色，讓顏色更容易判讀","Because water adds sugar and softens the sip":"因為水會加入糖分，讓口感更柔和","Because the spirit has never been diluted before":"因為這款烈酒之前從未稀釋過","The strength of the alcohol hides many aromas; diluting reveals them.":"酒精的強度會掩蓋許多香氣；稀釋能讓它們顯現出來。","A bottled spirit has already been diluted by the producer, but at around 40% abv it is still very strong: the alcohol stings the nose and masks the details. Adding water makes it easier to judge. Water adds no sugar and is not used to assess colour, which is looked at before diluting.":"裝瓶的烈酒已經由生產者稀釋過，但在大約 40% abv 時仍然非常烈：酒精會刺鼻，並掩蓋細節。加水能讓判斷更容易。水不會加入糖分，也不是用來評估顏色的，顏色要在稀釋前觀察。","How much spirit is usually poured as a tasting sample?":"品飲時，通常倒多少烈酒作為樣品？","About 15 cL":"大約 15 cL","About 0.1 cL":"大約 0.1 cL","A sample of about 1.5 cL is enough to look, smell and taste.":"大約 1.5 cL 的樣品就足以觀察、聞香和品嚐。","1.5 cL is roughly a tablespoon: enough for every step, small enough not to tire your senses. 5 cL is already a drinking measure and 15 cL a full glass, while 0.1 cL would be just a few drops, too little to work with.":"1.5 cL 大約是一湯匙：足以完成每個步驟，又少到不會讓感官疲乏。5 cL 已經是一份飲用的量，15 cL 是滿滿一杯，而 0.1 cL 只有幾滴，少到無法操作。","Which glass shape is best for tasting a spirit?":"哪一種杯形最適合品飲烈酒？","A wide bowl that narrows towards the top":"杯肚寬、往杯口收窄的杯子","A short, straight, wide-open tumbler":"矮而直、杯口大開的平底杯","A flat, wide saucer like a sparkling-wine coupe":"像氣泡酒淺碟杯那樣扁平寬口的杯子","A tall, narrow glass with a flared rim":"高而窄、杯緣外翻的杯子","The wide bowl releases the aromas and the narrow top concentrates them.":"寬杯肚讓香氣釋放，窄杯口則把香氣集中。","A tulip-shaped glass is designed to gather the scents. In very open glasses, such as a flat coupe or a tumbler, the aromas escape at once. A flared rim has the same effect: it widens the opening instead of narrowing it.":"鬱金香形的杯子就是為了聚集香氣而設計的。在非常開口的杯子裡，例如扁平的淺碟杯或平底杯，香氣會立刻散逸。外翻的杯緣也有同樣的效果：它讓開口變寬，而不是收窄。","What is a white surface used for during a tasting?":"品飲時，白色表面有什麼用途？","To judge the colour of the spirit better":"更準確地判斷烈酒的顏色","To work out how long the finish is":"判斷餘韻有多長","To reduce the smells in the room":"減少室內的氣味","To keep the sample at the right temperature":"讓樣品維持在適當溫度","A white background lets you see the colour without distractions.":"白色背景讓你能不受干擾地看清顏色。","Holding the glass against white paper or a white tablecloth, in good natural light, lets you read the colour reliably. The surface has no effect on smells, temperature or finish: those depend on the room, the sample and the palate.":"在良好的自然光下，把酒杯放在白紙或白色桌布前，就能可靠地判讀顏色。表面對氣味、溫度或餘韻沒有影響：那些取決於房間、樣品和味覺。","Just before a tasting, which of these habits is best avoided?":"品飲前，下列哪一個習慣最好避免？","Brushing your teeth or drinking coffee":"刷牙或喝咖啡","Drinking a glass of still water":"喝一杯白開水","Sitting near a bright window":"坐在明亮的窗戶旁","Putting a white sheet on the table":"在桌上放一張白紙","Toothpaste and coffee leave lingering flavours that distort the tasting.":"牙膏和咖啡會留下殘餘味道，干擾品飲。","Your palate should be clean and neutral, with no lingering flavours. The other three habits actually help: water keeps you hydrated, while natural light and white paper help you see the colour properly.":"你的味覺應該乾淨中性，沒有殘留的味道。另外三個習慣反而有幫助：喝水能保持水分，自然光和白紙則能幫你正確看清顏色。","What is the correct order of steps when tasting a spirit?":"品飲烈酒時，步驟的正確順序是什麼？","Eyes and nose, water, nose again, palate, spit":"看與聞、加水、再聞、品嚐、吐出","Water, eyes and nose, palate, nose again, spit":"加水、看與聞、品嚐、再聞、吐出","Palate, eyes and nose, water, palate again, spit":"品嚐、看與聞、加水、再品嚐、吐出","Eyes and nose, palate, spit, water, nose again":"看與聞、品嚐、吐出、加水、再聞","Look and smell neat, dilute, smell again, then taste and spit.":"先觀察並聞未稀釋的烈酒，稀釋後再聞一次，然後品嚐並吐出。","The first look and sniff are on the neat spirit, to get a starting impression. Water comes next, so you can compare the nose before and after dilution. Tasting comes last, on the diluted sample, which is easier to judge; tasting before the water or smelling after spitting breaks this logic.":"第一次觀察和聞香是針對未稀釋的烈酒，以取得初步印象。接著才加水，讓你能比較稀釋前後的香氣。品嚐放在最後，針對稀釋過、比較容易判斷的樣品；在加水前品嚐，或吐出後才聞香，都會打亂這個邏輯。","After adding water and smelling again, new aromas appear. Why does this happen?":"加水後再聞一次，出現了新的香氣。為什麼會這樣？","The alcohol, now weaker, no longer masks some aromas":"酒精變弱了，不再掩蓋某些香氣","The water itself brings fruit and floral aromas":"水本身帶來水果和花香","The sample has warmed up and started to age":"樣品變暖並開始陳年","The glass has released aromas from the previous sample":"酒杯釋放出前一個樣品的香氣","With less alcoholic strength, hidden aromas become noticeable.":"酒精濃度降低後，隱藏的香氣就變得明顯。","Diluting with an equal amount of water halves the strength of the sample: the sting of the alcohol fades and lets hidden details come through. Water has no aroma of its own, and a few minutes in a glass do not age a spirit. A dirty glass would be a preparation mistake, not the normal effect of dilution.":"加入等量的水會讓樣品的濃度減半：酒精的刺激感減弱，隱藏的細節就能顯現出來。水本身沒有香氣，烈酒在杯中待幾分鐘也不會陳年。不乾淨的酒杯是準備上的錯誤，而不是稀釋的正常效果。","A vodka has almost no smell at all. Which nose intensity do you record?":"一款伏特加幾乎完全沒有氣味。你要記錄哪一個香氣強度？","Simple":"簡單","'Neutral' is the lowest intensity level, for an almost absent nose.":"「中性」是最低的強度等級，用於幾乎沒有香氣的情況。","Nose intensity runs from neutral to light, medium and pronounced. 'Light' means there is some aroma, however delicate. 'Short' describes the finish and 'simple' refers to complexity: real terms, but used in a different part of the note.":"香氣強度從中性、清淡、中等到濃郁。「清淡」表示有一些香氣，即使很細緻。「短」描述的是餘韻，「簡單」則是指複雜度：它們都是正式術語，但用在品飲筆記的其他部分。","In an aged brandy you notice vanilla and sweet spice. Where do these aromas most likely come from?":"在一款陳年白蘭地中，你注意到香草和甜香料。這些香氣最可能來自哪裡？","From the oak and maturation":"來自橡木桶和熟成","From the grapes used as raw material":"來自作為原料的葡萄","From the water added in the glass":"來自杯中加入的水","Vanilla and spice are typical aromas given by oak during maturation.":"香草和香料是橡木桶在熟成期間帶來的典型香氣。","Aromas are grouped by source: raw material, processing, and oak and maturation. Grapes tend to give fruity notes, not vanilla. Water has no smell, and sugar, if present, shows up as sweetness on the palate rather than as a spicy aroma.":"香氣依來源分類：原料、加工，以及橡木桶和熟成。葡萄往往帶來果香，而不是香草。水沒有氣味，而糖（如果有的話）會在口中以甜味呈現，而不是辛香的香氣。","In a tasting note, what does the 'finish' describe?":"在品飲筆記中，「餘韻」描述的是什麼？","How long the flavours linger after spitting":"吐出後風味停留多久","The colour of the liquid at the bottom of the glass":"杯底液體的顏色","The last aroma noticed before adding water":"加水前注意到的最後一個香氣","The alcoholic strength shown on the label":"酒標上標示的酒精濃度","The finish measures how long flavours persist: short, medium or long.":"餘韻衡量風味持續多久：短、中等或長。","The finish is the last observation on the palate: after spitting, you note how long the flavours last. A long finish is often a sign of quality. Colour belongs to appearance, aromas to the nose, and alcoholic strength is label information, not a tasting observation.":"餘韻是口中最後的觀察：吐出後，記錄風味持續多久。長餘韻通常是品質的指標。顏色屬於外觀，香氣屬於嗅覺，酒精濃度則是酒標資訊，而不是品飲觀察。","In a cocktail, what makes up the 'strong' element?":"在調酒中，構成「強」元素的是什麼？","The base spirit":"基酒","The citrus juice":"柑橘汁","The sugar syrup":"糖漿","The ice used for chilling":"用來冰鎮的冰塊","The base spirit is the strong element and the heart of the flavour.":"基酒是強元素，也是風味的核心。","The strong element brings the alcohol and the main character of the drink. Citrus gives acidity, syrup gives sweetness and ice gives dilution, which belongs to the weak side: they are counterweights, not the base.":"強元素帶來酒精和飲品的主要個性。柑橘帶來酸度，糖漿帶來甜味，冰塊則帶來稀釋，屬於弱的一方：它們是平衡的砝碼，而不是基底。","What is the typical strength of a cocktail's base spirit?":"調酒基酒的典型濃度是多少？","Usually 40% abv or higher":"通常 40% abv 或更高","Usually between 12 and 15% abv":"通常 12% 至 15% abv","Usually around 20% abv":"通常約 20% abv","Usually above 90% abv":"通常高於 90% abv","A cocktail's strong base is generally a spirit at 40% abv or more.":"調酒的強基底一般是 40% abv 以上的烈酒。","Strengths of 12–15% abv are typical of wine, and around 20% you find lighter products such as some aromatised wines. Above 90% abv you are looking at neutral spirit for production, not a spirit ready for mixing.":"12–15% abv 是葡萄酒的典型濃度，約 20% 則是較清淡的產品，例如某些加味葡萄酒。高於 90% abv 的是生產用的中性烈酒，而不是可以直接調酒的烈酒。","In a short drink stirred with ice and served with nothing added, where does the 'weak' element come from?":"在一杯加冰攪拌、不添加其他東西的短飲中，「弱」元素來自哪裡？","From water as the ice melts during stirring":"來自攪拌時冰塊融化的水","From the bitters added by the dash":"來自以滴數加入的苦精","From the base spirit":"來自基酒","From the citrus peel used as a garnish":"來自作為裝飾的柑橘皮","Stirring with ice adds meltwater and softens the alcohol.":"加冰攪拌會加入融水，讓酒精變得柔和。","In short drinks, dilution comes almost entirely from ice during mixing, by stirring or shaking. Bitters are a bitter accent, the spirit is the strong part and a citrus peel adds scent, but none of them really lengthens the drink.":"在短飲中，稀釋幾乎完全來自調製時的冰塊，不論是攪拌還是搖盪。苦精是苦味點綴，烈酒是強的部分，柑橘皮增添香氣，但它們都不會真正讓飲品變長。","What is the ingredient called that brings a bitter and/or sour note to balance sweetness?":"為飲品帶來苦味和／或酸味、以平衡甜味的材料叫做什麼？","The modifier":"修飾材料（modifier）","The garnish":"裝飾物","The sweetener":"甜味劑","The modifier 'seasons' the drink with bitterness and/or sourness.":"修飾材料用苦味和／或酸味為飲品「調味」。","A cocktail is often sweetened first and then balanced by a modifier, such as citrus juice or bitters. A garnish is mainly decorative or aromatic, the base spirit is the strong part, and the sweetener is exactly what the modifier has to offset.":"調酒通常先加甜，再以修飾材料（例如柑橘汁或苦精）取得平衡。裝飾物主要是裝飾或增添香氣，基酒是強的部分，而甜味劑正是修飾材料要抵銷的對象。","What is simple syrup?":"什麼是簡易糖漿？","Sugar dissolved in water":"溶於水中的糖","Sweetened lemon juice":"加了糖的檸檬汁","An orange liqueur":"柳橙利口酒","Vermouth reduced over heat":"加熱濃縮的香艾酒","Simple syrup is just sugar and water, an unflavoured sweetener.":"簡易糖漿就是糖和水，一種沒有調味的甜味劑。","Dissolving sugar in water makes it easy to mix into a cold cocktail. Lemon juice is a sour ingredient, orange liqueur is a flavoured, alcoholic sweetener and vermouth is an aromatised wine: none of them is 'simple'.":"把糖溶解在水中，就很容易混入冰涼的調酒裡。檸檬汁是酸味材料，柳橙利口酒是有風味又含酒精的甜味劑，香艾酒則是加味葡萄酒：它們都不「簡易」。","A bartender tastes a cocktail and finds it cloying and too sweet. Which fix makes most sense?":"調酒師試喝一杯調酒，覺得太膩、太甜。哪一種修正最合理？","Add a little citrus juice or a dash of bitters":"加入一點柑橘汁或幾滴苦精","Add a spoonful of simple syrup":"加入一匙簡易糖漿","Swap the spirit for a liqueur":"把烈酒換成利口酒","Serve it warmer, without ice":"不加冰，以較溫的溫度供應","Sourness or bitterness balances too much sweetness.":"酸味或苦味能平衡過多的甜味。","On the sweet-versus-bitter-and-sour scale, you offset too much sugar by adding weight to the other side. More syrup or a liqueur would add even more sweetness. Removing the ice reduces dilution and does nothing about the sweetness.":"在「甜」對「苦與酸」的天平上，要抵銷過多的糖，就要在另一邊加重量。更多糖漿或利口酒只會讓它更甜。拿掉冰塊會減少稀釋，對甜度毫無幫助。","Which ingredient can bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity to a cocktail on its own?":"哪一種材料能單獨為調酒帶來甜味、苦味和酸度？","An aromatised wine such as vermouth":"加味葡萄酒，例如香艾酒","Club soda":"蘇打水","A neutral spirit such as vodka":"中性烈酒，例如伏特加","Aromatised wines combine sweet, bitter and sour in one ingredient.":"加味葡萄酒在一種材料中結合了甜、苦和酸。","Vermouth starts from wine, so it has acidity, it contains bitter botanicals and almost always some sugar: that is why it is so useful in cocktails. Syrup gives only sweetness, club soda only dilution and vodka mainly alcoholic strength.":"香艾酒以葡萄酒為起點，所以有酸度；它含有苦味植物性原料，而且幾乎總是含有一些糖：這就是它在調酒中如此有用的原因。糖漿只帶來甜味，蘇打水只帶來稀釋，伏特加則主要帶來酒精濃度。","Which two cocktail families are short drinks?":"哪兩個調酒家族屬於短飲？","Spirit-forward and short sours":"烈酒主導型和短酸酒","Highballs and long sours":"高球和長酸酒","Highballs and spirit-forward":"高球和烈酒主導型","Short sours and long sours":"短酸酒和長酸酒","Spirit-forward drinks and short sours are the two short groups.":"烈酒主導型飲品和短酸酒是兩個短飲類別。","Short drinks have few ingredients and are diluted only by ice, as with a Manhattan or a Daiquiri. Highballs and long sours are long drinks, lengthened with sodas or juices. The mixed options pair a short group with a long one.":"短飲的材料不多，只靠冰塊稀釋，例如 Manhattan 或 Daiquiri。高球和長酸酒是長飲，以汽水或果汁延長。混合的選項把一個短飲類別和一個長飲類別配在一起。","In long drinks, where does most of the 'weak' element usually come from?":"在長飲中，「弱」元素大多來自哪裡？","From sodas, juices or dairy":"來自汽水、果汁或乳製品","From a second spirit added to the base":"來自加進基酒的第二種烈酒","From a few dashes of bitters":"來自幾滴苦精","From a sweet liqueur":"來自甜利口酒","Non-alcoholic mixers such as sodas and juices lengthen the drink.":"汽水和果汁等無酒精調和飲料能延長飲品。","What sets a long drink apart is its bigger volume, achieved with non-alcoholic ingredients: tonic, club soda, juice, milk or cream. A second spirit would raise the strength instead of lowering it, bitters are used by the dash and a liqueur mainly adds sugar and alcohol.":"長飲的特點在於較大的份量，是用無酒精材料達成的：通寧水、蘇打水、果汁、牛奶或鮮奶油。第二種烈酒會提高濃度而不是降低，苦精是以滴數使用，利口酒則主要增添糖和酒精。","An Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey is an example of what?":"用蘭姆酒取代威士忌製作的 Old Fashioned，是哪一種例子？","A variation made by changing the strong element":"改變強元素而產生的變化版","A variation made by changing the modifier":"改變修飾材料而產生的變化版","A way of turning it into a long drink":"把它變成長飲的方法","A way of making it a short sour":"把它變成短酸酒的方法","The base spirit, the strong element, is replaced.":"強元素，也就是基酒，被替換了。","Knowing the four points of balance lets you change a recipe in a targeted way. Swapping whiskey for rum leaves the sugar and bitters, the sweet part and the modifier, unchanged. The volume stays the same, so it does not become a long drink, and with no citrus it is not a sour.":"了解平衡的四個要點，就能有針對性地調整酒譜。把威士忌換成蘭姆酒，糖和苦精（甜的部分和修飾材料）保持不變。份量也沒變，所以不會成為長飲；沒有柑橘，也不是酸酒。","What is the base spirit of a Negroni?":"Negroni 的基酒是什麼？","The Negroni is built on gin.":"Negroni 以琴酒為基底。","The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari in a spirit-forward drink. Vodka lacks gin's botanical character, rum is the base of the Daiquiri and Mojito, and Bourbon appears in drinks such as the Old Fashioned or Whiskey Sour.":"Negroni 結合琴酒、甜紅香艾酒和 Campari，是一款烈酒主導型飲品。伏特加缺乏琴酒的植物性個性，蘭姆酒是 Daiquiri 和 Mojito 的基底，Bourbon 則出現在 Old Fashioned 或 Whiskey Sour 等飲品中。","In a Negroni, which ingredient mainly provides the bitter note?":"在 Negroni 中，主要由哪一種材料提供苦味？","Campari":"Campari","Sweet red vermouth":"甜紅香艾酒","Gin":"琴酒","A sugar cube":"方糖","Campari, a red bitter spirit, is the Negroni's bitter element.":"紅色苦味烈酒 Campari 是 Negroni 的苦味元素。","Each Negroni ingredient has a role: gin is the strong part, sweet red vermouth brings sweetness and Campari the bitterness. The sugar cube belongs to the Old Fashioned, not the Negroni.":"Negroni 的每種材料都有角色：琴酒是強的部分，甜紅香艾酒帶來甜味，Campari 則帶來苦味。方糖屬於 Old Fashioned，而不是 Negroni。","The Old Fashioned and the Manhattan both use whiskey and Angostura bitters. What makes the Manhattan different?":"Old Fashioned 和 Manhattan 都使用威士忌和 Angostura 苦精。Manhattan 有什麼不同？","Sweet red vermouth instead of sugar":"用甜紅香艾酒取代糖","Lemon juice instead of bitters":"用檸檬汁取代苦精","Club soda that makes it a long drink":"加入蘇打水，變成長飲","Cream that makes it smooth":"加入鮮奶油，讓它更滑順","In the Manhattan, sweetness comes from sweet red vermouth, which is more complex than sugar.":"在 Manhattan 中，甜味來自甜紅香艾酒，比糖更有層次。","Both drinks share the whiskey base and Angostura bitters; the Manhattan replaces the sugar cube with vermouth, which also brings bitter and sour nuances. It remains a short spirit-forward drink: no citrus, soda or cream, which belong to sours, long drinks and the Alexander family respectively.":"兩款飲品都以威士忌為基底並使用 Angostura 苦精；Manhattan 用香艾酒取代方糖，香艾酒也帶來苦味和酸味的細微層次。它仍然是一款短的烈酒主導型飲品：沒有柑橘、汽水或鮮奶油，這些分別屬於酸酒、長飲和 Alexander 家族。","Which combination provides the bitter note in a Sazerac?":"在 Sazerac 中，哪一組材料提供苦味？","Peychaud's bitters and absinthe":"Peychaud's 苦精和苦艾酒","Angostura bitters and dry vermouth":"Angostura 苦精和不甜香艾酒","Campari and sweet red vermouth":"Campari 和甜紅香艾酒","Grapefruit juice and ginger ale":"葡萄柚汁和薑汁汽水","The Sazerac stands out for Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe.":"Sazerac 的特色在於 Peychaud's 苦精和一點苦艾酒。","The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye, sugar and, as its bitter element, Peychaud's bitters with absinthe. Angostura and dry vermouth appear in other classics (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari and sweet vermouth are the Negroni and Americano pair, and grapefruit and ginger ale are highball mixers.":"Sazerac 使用 Cognac 或黑麥威士忌、糖，苦味元素則是 Peychaud's 苦精加苦艾酒。Angostura 和不甜香艾酒出現在其他經典調酒中（Old Fashioned、Manhattan、Martini），Campari 和甜香艾酒是 Negroni 和 Americano 的組合，葡萄柚和薑汁汽水則是高球的調和飲料。","A customer wants a simple drink of Scotch whisky sweetened with a liqueur. Which classic do you suggest?":"一位顧客想要一款以利口酒加甜的簡單 Scotch 威士忌飲品。你會建議哪一款經典調酒？","The Rusty Nail is Scotch whisky with Drambuie, a liqueur.":"Rusty Nail 是 Scotch 威士忌加上利口酒 Drambuie。","It is the simplest example of a spirit-forward drink made of spirit plus liqueur. The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye with sugar, bitters and absinthe; the Sidecar is a Cognac sour with lemon; the Horse's Neck is a Cognac highball with ginger ale.":"它是「烈酒加利口酒」這種烈酒主導型飲品最簡單的例子。Sazerac 使用 Cognac 或黑麥威士忌加糖、苦精和苦艾酒；Sidecar 是加檸檬的 Cognac 酸酒；Horse's Neck 則是加薑汁汽水的 Cognac 高球。","What are the ingredients of a classic Martini?":"經典 Martini 的材料是什麼？","Gin and dry vermouth":"琴酒和不甜香艾酒","Gin and sweet red vermouth":"琴酒和甜紅香艾酒","Vodka and lemon juice":"伏特加和檸檬汁","Gin, Campari and club soda":"琴酒、Campari 和蘇打水","The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth.":"Martini 把琴酒和不甜香艾酒搭配在一起。","In the Martini, dry vermouth does two jobs at once: it brings a hint of sweetness (even 'dry' vermouth has a little sugar) and a bitter note. Sweet vermouth goes into the Manhattan and Negroni; vodka and lemon suggest a sour, and Campari with soda points to the highball family.":"在 Martini 中，不甜香艾酒一次扮演兩個角色：帶來一絲甜味（即使是「dry」香艾酒也有一點糖）和苦味。甜香艾酒用於 Manhattan 和 Negroni；伏特加和檸檬暗示酸酒，Campari 加蘇打水則指向高球家族。","What do you get by adding cream to a spirit-forward cocktail?":"在烈酒主導型調酒中加入鮮奶油，會得到什麼？","The Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander":"Alexander 家族，例如 Brandy Alexander","The Collins family, such as the Tom Collins":"Collins 家族，例如 Tom Collins","The Sling family, such as the Singapore Sling":"Sling 家族，例如 Singapore Sling","The sour family, such as the Pisco Sour":"酸酒家族，例如 Pisco Sour","Cream turns the drink into an Alexander.":"鮮奶油讓飲品變成 Alexander。","Alexanders are a twist on spirit-forward drinks in which cream makes everything rounder and velvety. Collinses and Slings are long sours topped with soda, and the Pisco Sour is a short sour whose smoothness comes from egg white, not cream.":"Alexander 是烈酒主導型飲品的變化版，鮮奶油讓整體變得圓潤絲滑。Collins 和 Sling 是補滿蘇打水的長酸酒，而 Pisco Sour 是短酸酒，它的滑順來自蛋白，而不是鮮奶油。","Built in the glass or stirred, with ice to chill and dilute":"直接在杯中調製或攪拌，用冰塊冰鎮並稀釋","Shaken with egg white to create a foam":"與蛋白一起搖盪以產生泡沫","Topped with plenty of club soda in a tall glass":"在高杯中補滿大量蘇打水","Served warm, with no ice or dilution":"溫熱供應，不加冰也不稀釋","They are built or stirred; the ice chills and dilutes.":"它們以直調或攪拌製作；冰塊負責冰鎮和稀釋。","Stirring keeps the drink clear and dense, ideal for showcasing the spirit. Shaking with egg white is typical of short sours, and soda in a tall glass of long drinks. Without ice you would lose the very weak element that makes such a strong drink pleasant to sip.":"攪拌能讓飲品保持清澈、濃稠，最適合展現烈酒。與蛋白一起搖盪是短酸酒的典型做法，高杯加蘇打水則是長飲的做法。沒有冰塊，就會失去讓這麼烈的飲品變得適口的弱元素。","What are the three elements of a classic short sour?":"經典短酸酒的三個元素是什麼？","Spirit, citrus juice, simple syrup":"烈酒、柑橘汁、簡易糖漿","Spirit, vermouth, bitters":"烈酒、香艾酒、苦精","Spirit, cream, liqueur":"烈酒、鮮奶油、利口酒","Spirit, tonic, ice":"烈酒、通寧水、冰塊","The short sour balances strong, sour and sweet: spirit, citrus, syrup.":"短酸酒平衡了強、酸、甜：烈酒、柑橘、糖漿。","The basic formula uses an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup and a citrus fruit such as lime or lemon. Spirit, vermouth and bitters describe a spirit-forward drink; cream and liqueur lead to the Alexander family; tonic gives a highball.":"基本公式使用簡易糖漿這類無調味甜味劑，以及萊姆或檸檬這類柑橘。烈酒、香艾酒和苦精描述的是烈酒主導型飲品；鮮奶油和利口酒通往 Alexander 家族；通寧水則會變成高球。","Which recipe is a Daiquiri?":"哪一個酒譜是 Daiquiri？","Rum, lime, simple syrup":"蘭姆酒、萊姆、簡易糖漿","Tequila, lime, triple sec":"Tequila、萊姆、triple sec","Rum, lime, sugar, mint":"蘭姆酒、萊姆、糖、薄荷","The Daiquiri is the classic rum-based short sour.":"Daiquiri 是以蘭姆酒為基底的經典短酸酒。","The Daiquiri follows the pure sour pattern: rum, lime and syrup, shaken. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre, a highball; tequila, lime and triple sec is the Margarita; add mint and a long format and you reach the Mojito.":"Daiquiri 遵循最純粹的酸酒模式：蘭姆酒、萊姆和糖漿，搖盪而成。蘭姆酒、可樂和萊姆是 Cuba Libre，一款高球；Tequila、萊姆和 triple sec 是 Margarita；加入薄荷並做成長飲，就成了 Mojito。","In which cocktail is egg white considered essential?":"在哪一款調酒中，蛋白被視為不可或缺？","The Pisco Sour always calls for an egg white.":"Pisco Sour 一定要加蛋白。","In the Pisco Sour, egg white creates a foam head and a silky texture and is an integral part of the recipe. It is optional in the Whiskey Sour and included in the Clover Club, while the Daiquiri, Sidecar and Margarita are normally made without it.":"在 Pisco Sour 中，蛋白會形成泡沫層和絲滑的質地，是酒譜不可或缺的一部分。在 Whiskey Sour 中是可選的，Clover Club 中則有使用，而 Daiquiri、Sidecar 和 Margarita 通常不加蛋白。","Which recipe is a Sidecar?":"哪一個酒譜是 Sidecar？","Cognac, lemon, triple sec":"Cognac、檸檬、triple sec","Cognac, ginger ale, bitters":"Cognac、薑汁汽水、苦精","Cognac, lemon, syrup, Champagne":"Cognac、檸檬、糖漿、Champagne","Cognac, sugar, Peychaud's, absinthe":"Cognac、糖、Peychaud's、苦艾酒","The Sidecar is a Cognac sour sweetened with triple sec.":"Sidecar 是以 triple sec 加甜的 Cognac 酸酒。","The Sidecar is a sour variation in which triple sec, an orange liqueur, takes the place of syrup. Every option contains Cognac, but Cognac, ginger ale and bitters is the Horse's Neck; with Champagne it is the French 75; with Peychaud's and absinthe, the Sazerac.":"Sidecar 是酸酒的變化版，用柳橙利口酒 triple sec 取代糖漿。每個選項都有 Cognac，但 Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精是 Horse's Neck；加 Champagne 是 French 75；加 Peychaud's 和苦艾酒則是 Sazerac。","In a Margarita, which ingredient provides the sweetness?":"在 Margarita 中，哪一種材料提供甜味？","Triple sec":"Triple sec","The salt rim":"杯口的鹽邊","Triple sec, an orange liqueur, is the Margarita's sweetener.":"柳橙利口酒 triple sec 是 Margarita 的甜味劑。","The Margarita is tequila, lime and triple sec: the lime is the sour part, not the sweet one. The salt rim is optional and lifts the flavours. Grapefruit soda belongs to the Paloma, another tequila drink, but a long one.":"Margarita 是 Tequila、萊姆和 triple sec：萊姆是酸的部分，而不是甜的。鹽邊是可選的，能提升風味。葡萄柚汽水屬於 Paloma，另一款 Tequila 飲品，但它是長飲。","Which short sour uses gin, lemon and raspberry syrup?":"哪一款短酸酒使用琴酒、檸檬和覆盆子糖漿？","The Clover Club is the gin variation with raspberry syrup.":"Clover Club 是加覆盆子糖漿的琴酒變化版。","The Clover Club is a short sour with a flavoured sweetener, plus egg white and optionally a little vermouth. The other three contain gin but are long sours: the Tom Collins with simple syrup and soda, the Singapore Sling with liqueurs and soda, and the French 75 with Champagne.":"Clover Club 是使用有風味甜味劑的短酸酒，另加蛋白，並可選擇加一點香艾酒。另外三款含琴酒，但都是長酸酒：Tom Collins 加簡易糖漿和蘇打水，Singapore Sling 加利口酒和蘇打水，French 75 則加 Champagne。","The Whiskey Sour and the Pisco Sour are both classic sours. How do their citrus juices differ?":"Whiskey Sour 和 Pisco Sour 都是經典酸酒。它們的柑橘汁有什麼不同？","The Whiskey Sour uses lemon, the Pisco Sour lime":"Whiskey Sour 用檸檬，Pisco Sour 用萊姆","The Whiskey Sour uses lime, the Pisco Sour lemon":"Whiskey Sour 用萊姆，Pisco Sour 用檸檬","Both use grapefruit juice":"兩者都用葡萄柚汁","Both use orange juice":"兩者都用柳橙汁","Lemon for the Whiskey Sour, lime for the Pisco Sour.":"Whiskey Sour 用檸檬，Pisco Sour 用萊姆。","Of the three classic sours, only the Whiskey Sour uses lemon; the Pisco Sour and Daiquiri use lime. A memory tip: whiskey, like the Cognac in a Sidecar, goes with lemon. Grapefruit appears in the Greyhound and the Paloma, not in these sours.":"在三款經典酸酒中，只有 Whiskey Sour 使用檸檬；Pisco Sour 和 Daiquiri 使用萊姆。記憶小訣竅：威士忌就像 Sidecar 裡的 Cognac，搭配檸檬。葡萄柚出現在 Greyhound 和 Paloma 中，而不是這些酸酒。","What is a Greyhound?":"什麼是 Greyhound？","Vodka and grapefruit juice":"伏特加和葡萄柚汁","Rum and cola with lime":"蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆","Gin and tonic water":"琴酒和通寧水","Tequila and grapefruit soda":"Tequila 和葡萄柚汽水","The Greyhound is a highball of vodka and grapefruit juice.":"Greyhound 是伏特加加葡萄柚汁的高球。","It is one of the highballs with its own name, as simple as the rest of the family. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre; gin and tonic has no special name; tequila and grapefruit soda with lime is the Paloma, which is a long sour.":"它是有自己名字的高球之一，和這個家族的其他成員一樣簡單。蘭姆酒、可樂和萊姆是 Cuba Libre；琴通寧沒有特別的名字；Tequila 加葡萄柚汽水和萊姆是 Paloma，屬於長酸酒。","A customer asks for a Cognac highball with ginger ale and a few dashes of bitters. What do you make?":"一位顧客點一杯加薑汁汽水和幾滴苦精的 Cognac 高球。你要調什麼？","A Horse's Neck":"Horse's Neck","A Sidecar":"Sidecar","A French 75":"French 75","An Americano":"Americano","The Horse's Neck is Cognac, ginger ale and bitters.":"Horse's Neck 是 Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精。","It is an example of a highball that adds bitters to the spirit and mixer. The Sidecar and French 75 contain Cognac but are sours, with lemon; the Americano is a highball with no Cognac, made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda.":"它是在烈酒和調和飲料之外再加入苦精的高球範例。Sidecar 和 French 75 含有 Cognac，但它們是加檸檬的酸酒；Americano 是不含 Cognac 的高球，以 Campari、甜香艾酒和蘇打水製成。","Why is the Americano said to have a 'split base'?":"為什麼說 Americano 有「分拆基底」？","Its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet vermouth together":"它的酒精部分是 Campari 和甜香艾酒兩者合起來","It is served half in a short glass and half in a tall one":"它一半裝在矮杯、一半裝在高杯中供應","It uses two different gins":"它使用兩種不同的琴酒","It mixes lemon juice and lime juice":"它混合了檸檬汁和萊姆汁","Campari and sweet red vermouth share the role of the strong element.":"Campari 和甜紅香艾酒共同分擔強元素的角色。","Instead of a single spirit, the Americano uses two alcoholic ingredients that together form the base, then lengthened with club soda. It contains no gin and no citrus: think of a Negroni without the gin, made long with soda.":"Americano 不用單一烈酒，而是用兩種酒精材料共同構成基底，再以蘇打水延長。它不含琴酒也不含柑橘：可以想成是去掉琴酒、加蘇打水做成長飲的 Negroni。","How is a short sour turned into a Tom Collins?":"如何把短酸酒變成 Tom Collins？","By using gin and topping with club soda":"使用琴酒並補滿蘇打水","By using rum and adding mint leaves":"使用蘭姆酒並加入薄荷葉","By using Cognac and topping with Champagne":"使用 Cognac 並補滿 Champagne","By using tequila and grapefruit soda":"使用 Tequila 和葡萄柚汽水","The Tom Collins is a gin sour lengthened with club soda.":"Tom Collins 是以蘇打水延長的琴酒酸酒。","Gin, lemon and simple syrup make a sour; topped with soda over ice it becomes a Collins, the simplest long sour. Rum and mint lead to the Mojito, Cognac and Champagne to the French 75, and tequila with grapefruit soda to the Paloma.":"琴酒、檸檬和簡易糖漿構成一款酸酒；加冰後補滿蘇打水，就成了 Collins，最簡單的長酸酒。蘭姆酒和薄荷通往 Mojito，Cognac 和 Champagne 通往 French 75，Tequila 加葡萄柚汽水則是 Paloma。","What is a French 75 topped with?":"French 75 最後補上的是什麼？","The French 75 is a sparkling sour topped with Champagne.":"French 75 是補上 Champagne 的氣泡酸酒。","The base is Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup; Champagne replaces the soda and makes it a sparkling sour. Tonic is typical of highballs such as the gin and tonic, ginger ale of the Horse's Neck and cola of the Cuba Libre.":"基底是 Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬和簡易糖漿；Champagne 取代蘇打水，讓它成為氣泡酸酒。通寧水是琴通寧等高球的典型材料，薑汁汽水屬於 Horse's Neck，可樂則屬於 Cuba Libre。","In a Paloma, what provides both sweetness and bubbles?":"在 Paloma 中，什麼同時提供甜味和氣泡？","A Mexican-style grapefruit soda":"墨西哥風格的葡萄柚汽水","Ginger ale":"薑汁汽水","Grapefruit soda both sweetens and lengthens the Paloma.":"葡萄柚汽水同時為 Paloma 加甜並延長。","The Paloma is tequila and lime topped with grapefruit soda; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water can be used. Triple sec sweetens the Margarita, Champagne tops the French 75 and ginger ale goes into the Horse's Neck.":"Paloma 是 Tequila 和萊姆，再補滿葡萄柚汽水；也可以改用葡萄柚汁和蘇打水。Triple sec 為 Margarita 加甜，Champagne 補在 French 75 上，薑汁汽水則用於 Horse's Neck。","Which extra ingredient sets the Mojito apart from a plain rum sour?":"哪一種額外材料讓 Mojito 有別於單純的蘭姆酸酒？","Mint leaves":"薄荷葉","Mint, with the lime, makes the Mojito fresh and fragrant.":"薄荷搭配萊姆，讓 Mojito 清新芬芳。","The Mojito is rum, lime and sugar or syrup, enriched with mint: a long sour with one simple extra ingredient. Egg white is typical of the Pisco Sour, salt of the Margarita and cream of the Alexander family.":"Mojito 是蘭姆酒、萊姆和糖或糖漿，再加上薄荷：一款只多了一種簡單材料的長酸酒。蛋白是 Pisco Sour 的典型材料，鹽是 Margarita 的，鮮奶油則屬於 Alexander 家族。","Four steps behind every spirit":"每款烈酒背後的四個步驟","Put as simply as possible, a spirit is an alcoholic drink that distillation has made stronger. But distillation never works alone: behind every bottle, whether vodka or Cognac, there are always four steps. The raw material is prepared, it is fermented, it is distilled, and finally the producer decides what to do with the spirit fresh from the still. Knowing these four steps unlocks almost every spirit on the shelf.":"說得越簡單越好：烈酒就是經由蒸餾提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料。但蒸餾從不單獨運作：每一瓶酒背後，不論是伏特加還是 Cognac，總是有四個步驟。先準備原料，接著發酵，然後蒸餾，最後由生產者決定如何處理剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒。掌握這四個步驟，就能理解酒架上幾乎所有的烈酒。","The first step has a single goal: to obtain a sugary liquid, because without sugar there is no fermentation. The raw material must come from a plant. Some plants, such as sugar cane or grapes, already hold sugar that is easy to extract. Others, such as cereals, contain none and must be processed to create it. Either way, the starting plant leaves its signature: every raw material gives the spirit its own set of aromas.":"第一步只有一個目標：取得含糖液體，因為沒有糖就沒有發酵。原料必須來自植物。有些植物，例如甘蔗或葡萄，本身就含有容易萃取的糖。其他植物，例如穀物，不含糖，必須經過處理才能產生糖。不論哪一種，起始的植物都會留下印記：每種原料都會為烈酒帶來自己的一組香氣。","After fermentation and distillation comes the fourth step, often overlooked but decisive. A newly made spirit is colourless and dry, so the producer can leave it that way, put it into oak barrels, add flavours, sugar or colour, and finally dilute it with water. A handy image: the first three steps build the house, the fourth furnishes it. Two spirits that start out identical can leave this stage tasting very different.":"發酵和蒸餾之後是第四步，經常被忽略，卻有決定性的影響。剛製成的烈酒無色、不甜，所以生產者可以讓它保持原樣、放進橡木桶、加入風味、糖或顏色，最後再加水稀釋。一個好記的比喻：前三步是蓋房子，第四步是佈置房子。兩款一開始完全相同的烈酒，經過這個階段後，味道可能截然不同。","Spirit = an alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation.":"烈酒 = 經由蒸餾提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料。","Four steps: raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation.":"四個步驟：原料、發酵、蒸餾、蒸餾後處理。","The raw material is always a plant and is used to make a sugary liquid.":"原料一定是植物，用來製作含糖液體。","Each raw material brings its own aromas.":"每種原料都帶來自己的香氣。","Fermentation makes alcohol, distillation concentrates it":"發酵產生酒精，蒸餾將它濃縮","Yeasts are tiny living organisms added to the sugary liquid. They feed on the sugar and leave two things behind: ethanol, the alcohol the distiller wants, and carbon dioxide, a waste gas. At the end, the fermented liquid usually sits between 8% and 10% abv, roughly the strength of a strong beer. Yeasts also create new aromas, especially fruity ones, so fermentation adds flavour as well as alcohol.":"酵母是加入含糖液體中的微小生物。它們以糖為食，並留下兩樣東西：乙醇，也就是蒸餾師想要的酒精；以及二氧化碳，一種副產物氣體。發酵結束時，發酵液的濃度通常在 8% 到 10% abv 之間，大約是烈性啤酒的濃度。酵母也會產生新的香氣，尤其是果香，所以發酵除了酒精，也增添了風味。","Distillation relies on one simple fact: ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water. When the fermented liquid is heated to boiling, the vapours rising from it are richer in alcohol than the liquid left behind. Collected and cooled, those vapours turn back into a liquid that is stronger than the one we started with. This is the step where a spirit is truly born.":"蒸餾依據的是一個簡單的事實：乙醇的沸點比水低。把發酵液加熱到沸騰時，升起的蒸氣所含的酒精比留下的液體更多。將這些蒸氣收集並冷卻後，就會變回比原本更烈的液體。烈酒真正誕生，就是在這一步。","The strength reached during distillation matters a lot. A newly made spirit can range from about 60% up to 96% abv. The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas; the higher the strength, the less aroma survives. At 96% abv a spirit has so little smell that it is called neutral. Picture a radio: the louder the alcohol, the fainter the music of the aromas.":"蒸餾時達到的濃度非常重要。剛製成的烈酒可以從大約 60% 到 96% abv。濃度越低，香氣越濃郁；濃度越高，留下的香氣越少。在 96% abv 時，烈酒的氣味極少，被稱為中性。想像一台收音機：酒精的音量越大，香氣的音樂就越微弱。","Yeast + sugar → ethanol + carbon dioxide.":"酵母 + 糖 → 乙醇 + 二氧化碳。","Fermented liquid is usually 8–10% abv; yeast adds fruity aromas.":"發酵液通常為 8–10% abv；酵母帶來果香。","Distillation concentrates ethanol because it boils before water.":"蒸餾能濃縮乙醇，因為乙醇比水先沸騰。","Low strength = more aroma; high strength = less aroma; 96% = neutral.":"低濃度 = 香氣較多；高濃度 = 香氣較少；96% = 中性。","Whatever its shape, a pot still always has three parts: a pot sitting on a heat source, a cooled condenser and a pipe linking the two. The liquid boils in the pot, the vapours climb the still head and pass into the condenser, where a coiled tube bathed in cold water turns them back into liquid. Many modern pot stills are heated with steam; those used for Cognac still rely on gas burners.":"不論外形如何，壺式蒸餾器一定有三個部分：放在熱源上的蒸餾鍋、冷卻的冷凝器，以及連接兩者的管子。液體在蒸餾鍋中沸騰，蒸氣沿著蒸餾器頂部上升並進入冷凝器，泡在冷水中的盤管會把蒸氣變回液體。許多現代壺式蒸餾器以蒸汽加熱；Cognac 使用的蒸餾器則仍然使用瓦斯爐火。","A pot still works in batches, much like a washing machine: load it, run the cycle, empty it and clean it before the next round. It cannot run non-stop. What is more, a single pass cannot turn the fermented liquid into a spirit. That is why most distillers run it twice: from about 10% abv to about 25%, then to about 75%. This is known as double pot still distillation.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，就像洗衣機一樣：裝入、運轉一個循環、清空，然後在下一輪之前清洗。它無法不停運轉。此外，蒸餾一次無法把發酵液變成烈酒。這就是為什麼大多數蒸餾師要蒸餾兩次：從約 10% abv 到約 25%，再到約 75%。這稱為壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾。","The result is a spirit of relatively low strength, with medium to pronounced aroma intensity and plenty of character and complexity. That is why this still is chosen whenever a flavour-packed spirit is the goal. The price is labour: each batch takes time and care, and no matter how many times the spirit is redistilled, a pot still will never reach a very high-strength neutral spirit.":"成果是濃度相對較低的烈酒，香氣強度中等至濃郁，充滿個性和複雜度。這就是為什麼想要風味飽滿的烈酒時，會選擇這種蒸餾器。代價是人力：每一批都需要時間和照顧，而且不論烈酒再蒸餾多少次，壺式蒸餾器都無法達到極高濃度的中性烈酒。","Three parts: pot with heat source, condenser, linking pipe.":"三個部分：附熱源的蒸餾鍋、冷凝器、連接管。","Batch process: emptied and cleaned after every distillation.":"批次運作：每次蒸餾後都要清空並清洗。","Usually two distillations: ~10% → ~25% → ~75% abv.":"通常蒸餾兩次：~10% → ~25% → ~75% abv。","Low strength, medium to pronounced aromas, lots of character; never neutral.":"低濃度，香氣中等至濃郁，個性十足；絕不會是中性。","Over time, distillers wanted a still that could run without stopping and reach very high strengths, which the pot still cannot do. The answer was the column: a vertical structure divided into many sections. Hot vapour enters at the bottom and rises, while liquid runs down. It is like stacking many distillations on top of one another, all happening at the same time.":"隨著時間過去，蒸餾師想要一種能不停運轉、並達到極高濃度的蒸餾器，這是壺式蒸餾器做不到的。答案就是蒸餾柱：一種分成許多層的直立式結構。熱蒸氣從底部進入並上升，液體則往下流。這就像把許多次蒸餾疊在一起，全部同時進行。","The higher the vapour climbs in the column, the higher its alcohol level: the bottom section holds the weakest liquid, the top section the strongest, and that is where the spirit leaves the still. Because the distillations happen simultaneously and the column never needs emptying, production is continuous and fast. Think of an escalator that never stops, compared with the stop-start lift of the pot still.":"蒸氣在蒸餾柱中爬得越高，酒精含量就越高：最下層的液體最弱，最上層的最強，烈酒也從那裡離開蒸餾器。因為多次蒸餾同時進行，而且蒸餾柱從不需要清空，所以生產是連續且快速的。可以想成一座永不停止的手扶梯，對比壺式蒸餾器走走停停的電梯。","Not all columns are alike. A short column with few sections gives a lower-strength spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, close to a pot still spirit. A tall column with many sections reaches high strengths and gives a light spirit. The very tallest reach 95% or 96% abv, producing a neutral spirit with almost no smell, the base of most vodkas.":"蒸餾柱並非都一樣。層數少的矮蒸餾柱得到的是濃度較低、香氣中等或濃郁的烈酒，接近壺式蒸餾器的烈酒。層數多的高蒸餾柱能達到高濃度，得到清淡的烈酒。最高的蒸餾柱能達到 95% 或 96% abv，產出幾乎沒有氣味的中性烈酒，也就是大多數伏特加的基底。","A column still runs continuously: many stacked, simultaneous distillations.":"柱式蒸餾器連續運作：許多層疊、同時進行的蒸餾。","The highest strength is at the top of the column.":"最高濃度在蒸餾柱的頂部。","Short column = flavourful spirit, similar to a pot still.":"矮蒸餾柱 = 風味豐富的烈酒，類似壺式蒸餾器。","Tall column = light spirit; tallest = neutral at 95–96%.":"高蒸餾柱 = 清淡的烈酒；最高的 = 95–96% 的中性烈酒。","Where flavour comes from":"風味從哪裡來","A spirit's flavour is built step by step. The raw material lays the foundation: grapes bring fruity and floral notes, agave brings herbal and peppery ones. Fermentation adds further aromas, mostly fruity. Then distillation decides how much of all this survives: at a low strength the aromas stay intense, at a very high strength they almost vanish. Each step works like a filter letting more or less character through.":"烈酒的風味是一步一步建立起來的。原料打下基礎：葡萄帶來果香和花香，龍舌蘭帶來草本和胡椒氣息。發酵再增添其他香氣，主要是果香。接著由蒸餾決定這一切能留下多少：濃度低時香氣保持濃郁，濃度極高時香氣幾乎消失。每一步都像一道濾網，讓或多或少的個性通過。","What leaves the still is always colourless and dry, meaning it has no sugar. From here the producer takes one of three routes, often set by law as well. The spirit can stay unaged, kept briefly in stainless steel tanks so its colour and aromas stay as they were. It can be aged in oak barrels, usually for years. Or it can be flavoured with something other than wood, as happens with gin.":"離開蒸餾器的烈酒一定是無色、不甜的，也就是不含糖。從這裡開始，生產者會走上三條路之一，而這通常也由法律決定。烈酒可以不經陳年，只在不鏽鋼桶槽中短暫存放，讓顏色和香氣維持原樣。可以在橡木桶中陳年，通常長達數年。也可以用木頭以外的東西調味，例如琴酒。","The law often makes the choice for the producer. Scotch whisky, for instance, must spend time in oak, while a Tequila may be aged or not. So it always pays to ask: is this spirit unaged, oak-aged or flavoured? The answer already explains a great deal about its colour and its aromas, before it is even tasted.":"法律經常替生產者做了選擇。例如 Scotch 威士忌必須在橡木桶中度過一段時間，而 Tequila 則可陳年也可不陳年。所以每次都值得問一句：這款烈酒是未陳年、橡木桶陳年，還是調味的？還沒品嚐，答案就已經說明了它的顏色和香氣的許多事。","Flavour comes from raw material, fermentation and distillation strength.":"風味來自原料、發酵和蒸餾濃度。","Every newly made spirit is colourless and dry.":"每一款剛製成的烈酒都是無色、不甜的。","Three routes: unaged, oak-aged, flavoured.":"三條路：未陳年、橡木桶陳年、調味。","The law often dictates the route.":"法律經常決定要走哪一條路。","Unaged or oak-aged":"未陳年或橡木桶陳年","An unaged spirit rests briefly in stainless steel, a material that gives nothing away: it stays clear and keeps the aromas born in the still. Oak, on the other hand, does real work. A barrel adds colour in a sequence that goes from lemon to gold, then amber and, very rarely, brown. The newer the barrel and the longer the spirit stays in it, the deeper the colour.":"未陳年的烈酒在不鏽鋼中短暫靜置，這種材質不會釋出任何東西：烈酒保持清澈，並保留在蒸餾器中誕生的香氣。相反地，橡木桶會真正發揮作用。酒桶會依序增添顏色：從檸檬黃到金黃，再到琥珀色，極少數會變成棕色。桶越新、烈酒在桶中待得越久，顏色就越深。","Oak also brings aromas: vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut. A new barrel that has never been used gives a lot of them. A previously used barrel, called an old barrel, gives less, and a little less again with every reuse, just like a tea bag steeped several times. So the producer chooses between new barrels for a strong oak imprint and used barrels for a gentler touch.":"橡木桶也會帶來香氣：香草、肉桂、丁香、椰子。從未使用過的新桶會帶來大量香氣。用過的桶（稱為舊桶）帶來的較少，而且每重複使用一次就再少一點，就像泡過好幾次的茶包。所以生產者會在新桶（強烈的橡木印記）和舊桶（較溫和的影響）之間做選擇。","Time matters too. During ageing, water and ethanol slowly evaporate through the wood, so what remains becomes more concentrated. After many years, sometimes decades, new aromas appear and add depth: fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish. That is why a long-aged spirit feels layered, with shades of flavour revealing themselves one after another.":"時間也很重要。陳年期間，水和乙醇會慢慢透過木頭蒸發，剩下的部分就變得更濃縮。經過許多年，有時是數十年，會出現新的香氣並增添深度：水果蛋糕、果乾、皮革、木頭亮光蠟。這就是為什麼長期陳年的烈酒感覺層次豐富，風味的細微變化一層接著一層展現。","Unaged: a short rest in stainless steel, no colour or aroma added.":"未陳年：在不鏽鋼中短暫靜置，不增添顏色或香氣。","Oak colours: lemon → gold → amber → (rarely) brown.":"橡木桶的顏色：檸檬黃 → 金黃 → 琥珀 →（少見）棕色。","New barrel = more aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut); used barrel = less.":"新桶 = 香氣較多（香草、香料、椰子）；舊桶 = 較少。","Over time: evaporation, concentration, dried fruit, leather, polish aromas.":"隨著時間：蒸發、濃縮、果乾、皮革、亮光蠟香氣。","Blending, flavouring and dilution":"調和、調味與稀釋","Every barrel is its own little world: two barrels filled with the same spirit on the same day will never turn out exactly alike. The blender combines the contents of many barrels with two aims. The first is consistency: anyone buying the same bottle again expects the same taste. The second is complexity: bringing together spirits with different characters is the easiest way to create depth.":"每個酒桶都是一個獨特的小世界：同一天裝入同一種烈酒的兩個桶，結果永遠不會完全相同。調和師把許多酒桶的內容物結合在一起，有兩個目的。第一是一致性：再次購買同一瓶酒的人，期待喝到相同的味道。第二是複雜度：把不同個性的烈酒結合在一起，是創造深度最簡單的方法。","When flavours other than wood are wanted, three main techniques are used. The spirit can be redistilled together with herbs, seeds or spices, giving a flavoured but colourless liquid. The same plants can be left to soak in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, so their flavours and colour seep out slowly. Or ready-made flavourings, natural or artificial, can simply be added.":"想要木頭以外的風味時，主要有三種技術。烈酒可以與香草、種子或香料一起再蒸餾，得到有風味但無色的液體。也可以把同樣的植物浸泡在烈酒中，就像冷泡花草茶，讓風味和顏色慢慢滲出。或者直接加入天然或人工的現成調味料。","The last move before bottling is almost always dilution. Completely pure water is added and the vast majority of spirits come down to 40% abv. The reason is practical: alcohol that is too strong numbs the palate, making it impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit. The water brings no aroma; it simply lowers the strength, like opening a window in an overheated room.":"裝瓶前的最後一步幾乎都是稀釋。加入完全純淨的水，絕大多數烈酒會降到 40% abv。原因很實際：太烈的酒精會麻痺味覺，讓人無法品嚐或享受烈酒。水不會帶來香氣，只是降低濃度，就像在過熱的房間裡打開一扇窗。","Blending aims for consistency and complexity.":"調和追求一致性和複雜度。","Three ways to flavour: redistillation, maceration, added flavourings.":"三種調味方法：再蒸餾、浸漬、添加調味料。","Maceration also adds colour; redistillation gives a colourless liquid.":"浸漬也會增添顏色；再蒸餾則得到無色的液體。","Dilution with pure water, usually to 40% abv, makes the spirit drinkable.":"用純水稀釋，通常到 40% abv，讓烈酒適合飲用。","Since every spirit leaves the still dry, any sweetness you notice in the mouth was added afterwards, usually simply as sugar. Watch the wording: here, sweet refers only to the taste of sugar. A whiskey with vanilla and fruity aromas may seem sweet on the nose, but with no added sugar it is still dry. A sweet-smelling nose and a sweet palate are not the same thing.":"既然每款烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的，你在口中察覺到的任何甜味都是之後才添加的，通常就是糖。注意用詞：在這裡，「甜」只指糖的味道。一款帶有香草和果香的威士忌聞起來可能很甜美，但沒有加糖，它仍然是不甜的。聞起來甜美的香氣和口中的甜味不是同一回事。","Colour can come from several sources. Oak is the most natural one. Then there is caramel colouring: barrels give different shades, so the blender uses tiny amounts to keep every batch the same colour. Used properly, caramel is not sweet and adds no aroma. Other spirits, including many liqueurs, receive natural or artificial colourings, sometimes in very bright shades.":"顏色可能有幾種來源。橡木桶是最天然的一種。另外還有焦糖色：不同的桶會帶來不同的色調，所以調和師會用極少量的焦糖色讓每一批的顏色保持一致。正確使用時，焦糖色不甜，也不會增添香氣。其他烈酒，包括許多利口酒，則會加入天然或人工色素，有時是非常鮮豔的色調。","This gives a useful tasting lesson: colour is no proof of age. Some spirits get all or nearly all of their colour from caramel, so an unaged spirit can be deeply coloured. An amber glass suggests long years in barrel, but only the label or knowledge of the style can confirm it.":"這帶來一個有用的品飲觀念：顏色不能證明年份。有些烈酒的顏色全部或幾乎全部來自焦糖色，所以未陳年的烈酒也可能顏色很深。琥珀色的酒液暗示在桶中多年，但只有酒標或對風格的了解才能證實。","Sweetness is always added after distillation, usually as sugar.":"甜味一定是在蒸餾後添加的，通常是糖。","Sweet = taste of sugar, not a sweet-smelling aroma.":"甜 = 糖的味道，而不是聞起來甜美的香氣。","Colour sources: oak, caramel, natural or artificial colourings.":"顏色來源：橡木桶、焦糖色、天然或人工色素。","Colour does not prove age: an unaged spirit can be dark.":"顏色不能證明年份：未陳年的烈酒也可能顏色很深。","From grapes to wine":"從葡萄到葡萄酒","A grape brandy is simply wine that has been distilled, and Cognac is the most famous of them all. It comes from south-west France, from a clearly defined area north of the town of Bordeaux. Only grapes grown there can become Cognac: as with many products tied to a place, the name is a precise address rather than a recipe that can be copied elsewhere.":"葡萄白蘭地就是經過蒸餾的葡萄酒，而 Cognac 是其中最有名的。它來自法國西南部，Bordeaux 市以北一個明確劃定的產區。只有在那裡種植的葡萄才能成為 Cognac：就像許多與產地綁定的產品，這個名稱是一個精確的地址，而不是可以在別處複製的配方。","The grapes from this area give Cognac its basic aromas, fruity and floral. After harvest they are pressed to release their juice, which is full of sugar and so needs no complicated processing: it is fermented straight away. The result is a wine, and it is this wine, not the grapes, that goes into the still. Before it is a spirit, then, Cognac is a wine.":"這個產區的葡萄為 Cognac 帶來基本的香氣：果香和花香。採收後，葡萄被壓榨以釋出汁液，汁液富含糖分，所以不需要複雜的處理：立刻就能發酵。結果就是葡萄酒，而進入蒸餾器的正是這款葡萄酒，而不是葡萄。所以，在成為烈酒之前，Cognac 是一款葡萄酒。","Cognac follows the four steps of every spirit closely: processing the grapes, fermenting them into wine, distilling, and a final stage in barrel. One image helps: a bunch of Cognac grapes travels the same road as a bunch of wine grapes, but halfway along, instead of ending up in the glass, it takes the turning towards the still.":"Cognac 緊密地遵循每款烈酒的四個步驟：處理葡萄、發酵成葡萄酒、蒸餾，以及最後在桶中的階段。一個比喻很有幫助：一串 Cognac 葡萄走的路和一串釀酒葡萄相同，但走到一半時，它沒有進到酒杯裡，而是轉向了蒸餾器。","Grape brandy = distilled wine; Cognac is the best known.":"葡萄白蘭地 = 蒸餾過的葡萄酒；Cognac 最為知名。","A defined area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux.":"法國西南部、Bordeaux 以北的劃定產區。","The grapes give fruity and floral aromas.":"葡萄帶來果香和花香。","Grapes pressed, juice fermented straight away into wine.":"葡萄經壓榨，汁液立刻發酵成葡萄酒。","Twice through the pot still":"兩次通過壺式蒸餾器","For Cognac the law leaves no choice: the wine must be distilled twice in a pot still. No column allowed. It is slow, batch-by-batch work, because after every distillation the still has to be emptied and cleaned. Traditional Cognac stills are heated with gas burners, and the condenser is a coil sitting in cold water that is constantly refreshed.":"對 Cognac 來說，法律沒有留下選擇：葡萄酒必須在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次。不允許使用蒸餾柱。這是緩慢、逐批進行的工作，因為每次蒸餾後都必須清空並清洗蒸餾器。傳統的 Cognac 蒸餾器以瓦斯爐火加熱，冷凝器則是一段浸在持續更換的冷水中的盤管。","Why go to so much trouble? Because a pot still gives a spirit of relatively low strength that keeps plenty of flavour and character, exactly what a Cognac needs. A tall column would give a lighter, less expressive spirit and lose much of the grapes' fruity and floral aromas. You could say that double distillation protects the soul of the wine instead of wiping it out.":"為什麼要這麼費工？因為壺式蒸餾器能得到濃度相對較低、保留大量風味和個性的烈酒，這正是 Cognac 所需要的。高蒸餾柱會得到更清淡、表現力較弱的烈酒，失去葡萄許多的果香和花香。可以說，二次蒸餾保護了葡萄酒的靈魂，而不是抹去它。","By law: double distillation in a pot still.":"依法規：以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾。","Slow, labour-intensive batch work.":"緩慢、耗費人力的批次作業。","Traditional stills heated with gas burners.":"傳統蒸餾器以瓦斯爐火加熱。","Low strength = lots of flavour and character.":"低濃度 = 大量風味和個性。","Oak, blending and age terms":"橡木桶、調和與年份術語","Fresh from the still, the future Cognac cannot yet use the name: the law requires at least two years in oak barrels. The wood gives it colour and aromas of vanilla and toast. The finest Cognacs stay in barrel far longer, becoming concentrated and developing notes of fruit cake, leather and wood polish, the mark of a long, slow maturation.":"剛離開蒸餾器時，未來的 Cognac 還不能使用這個名稱：法律要求在橡木桶中至少陳年兩年。木頭為它帶來顏色，以及香草和烘烤的香氣。最優秀的 Cognac 會在桶中待得更久，變得濃縮，並發展出水果蛋糕、皮革和木頭亮光蠟的氣息，這是長時間緩慢熟成的印記。","Nearly all Cognacs are blends of spirits of different ages: younger ones bring freshness, older ones depth, and together they create complexity. Before dilution and bottling it is common to add a little caramel colouring, to keep the shade consistent, and a touch of sweetening. So a Cognac can feel slightly rounded on the palate even though it left the still dry.":"幾乎所有 Cognac 都是不同年份烈酒的調和：年輕的帶來清新感，老的帶來深度，結合在一起則創造出複雜度。在稀釋和裝瓶前，常見的做法是加入少量焦糖色以保持色調一致，並稍微加甜。所以即使 Cognac 離開蒸餾器時是不甜的，在口中仍可能感覺略為圓潤。","Three label terms show the age, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. VS guarantees at least 2 years, VSOP at least 4 years, XO at least 10 years. Picture a staircase with three steps: 2, 4 and 10. If a blend contains a 5-year-old and a 20-year-old spirit, it is the 5 that counts.":"三個酒標術語標示年份，而且一律指調和中最年輕的烈酒。VS 保證至少 2 年，VSOP 至少 4 年，XO 至少 10 年。想像一座三階的樓梯：2、4、10。如果一款調和包含 5 年和 20 年的烈酒，以 5 年為準。","At least 2 years in oak by law; vanilla and toast.":"依法規在橡木桶中至少 2 年；香草和烘烤。","Long ageing: fruit cake, leather, wood polish.":"長期陳年：水果蛋糕、皮革、木頭亮光蠟。","Almost always blends; often caramel and a little sugar.":"幾乎都是調和的；常加焦糖色和少量的糖。","VS 2+ years, VSOP 4+ years, XO 10+ years: age of the youngest spirit.":"VS 2 年以上、VSOP 4 年以上、XO 10 年以上：以最年輕烈酒的年份為準。","Any raw material, anywhere":"任何原料，任何地方","Vodka is the freest spirit of all. It can be made in any country in the world and from any plant-based raw material. There is no compulsory area of origin, as with Cognac, and no required ingredient, as agave is for Tequila. What makes a spirit a vodka is neither the place nor the plant: it is the strength it is distilled to.":"伏特加是所有烈酒中最自由的。它可以在世界上任何國家生產，使用任何植物性原料。它不像 Cognac 有規定的原產地，也不像 Tequila 必須使用龍舌蘭。讓一款烈酒成為伏特加的，既不是產地也不是植物，而是它被蒸餾到的濃度。","Although the choice is open, some raw materials are linked with premium-quality vodka: cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes. After processing to make a sugary liquid, it is fermented just like any other spirit. So the first two steps are the classic ones; vodka's real distinguishing feature arrives with the third.":"雖然選擇是開放的，但有些原料與高品質伏特加聯想在一起：穀物，尤其是大麥、小麥和黑麥，以及馬鈴薯。經過處理製成含糖液體後，就和其他烈酒一樣進行發酵。所以前兩步是經典做法；伏特加真正的特點出現在第三步。","Vodka can be made anywhere, from any raw material.":"伏特加可以在任何地方、用任何原料製作。","It is defined by distillation strength, not place or plant.":"它由蒸餾濃度定義，而不是產地或植物。","Premium vodka: cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes.":"高級伏特加：穀物（大麥、小麥、黑麥）和馬鈴薯。","A neutral spirit, then diluted":"中性烈酒，再加以稀釋","Vodka is a diluted neutral spirit. To count as neutral, the spirit must reach at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on the law of the producing country. Such a high strength can only be achieved with a column still, although some producers use pot stills for part of the process. At that alcohol level almost no aroma remains, hence the name neutral.":"伏特加是稀釋過的中性烈酒。要算是中性，烈酒必須至少達到 95% 或 96% abv，視生產國的法律而定。這麼高的濃度只能用柱式蒸餾器達到，不過有些生產者會在部分流程中使用壺式蒸餾器。在這個酒精濃度下幾乎沒有香氣留下，因此稱為中性。","After distillation, vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water to bottling strength, typically 40% abv. Think of it as a blank canvas: the producer's whole effort goes into taking away rather than adding, so that what reaches the glass is a clean spirit with almost no smell.":"蒸餾後，伏特加不會進桶：它保持未陳年、清澈透明。接著用純水稀釋到裝瓶濃度，通常是 40% abv。可以把它想成一張空白畫布：生產者所有的努力都在於去除而不是增添，讓倒進杯中的是一款幾乎沒有氣味的潔淨烈酒。","Neutral spirit: at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on national law.":"中性烈酒：至少 95% 或 96% abv，視各國法律而定。","A column still is needed; pot stills only for part of the process.":"必須使用柱式蒸餾器；壺式蒸餾器只用於部分流程。","Unaged, usually diluted to 40% abv.":"未陳年，通常稀釋到 40% abv。","Neutral or with a little character":"中性，或帶一點個性","Most vodka aims for the most complete neutrality possible. That very lack of aroma is what makes it so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails: it blends into juices, sodas and liqueurs without imposing its own taste, adding alcohol while leaving the spotlight to the other ingredients. A bartender who wants to strengthen a drink without changing its flavour reaches for it first.":"大多數伏特加追求盡可能完全的中性。正是這種缺乏香氣的特質，讓它在混合飲料和調酒中如此受歡迎：它能融入果汁、汽水和利口酒，不會強加自己的味道，在增加酒精的同時把焦點留給其他材料。想加強一杯飲品又不改變風味的調酒師，第一個就會拿它。","Some vodkas, however, keep a hint of character. On the nose and palate there are faint touches of the raw material, such as a note of grain or potato. They remain very delicate, nowhere near the intensity of a whisky or a brandy, and are still correctly described as neutral. It is like the difference between mineral water and distilled water: subtle, but noticeable.":"不過，有些伏特加保留了一點個性。在香氣和口中有淡淡的原料氣息，例如穀物或馬鈴薯的氣息。這些氣息非常細緻，遠不及威士忌或白蘭地的濃郁，仍可正確地描述為中性。這就像礦泉水和蒸餾水之間的差別：細微，但察覺得到。","Most vodka is as neutral as possible.":"大多數伏特加盡可能中性。","Neutrality makes it versatile in mixed drinks and cocktails.":"中性讓它在混合飲料和調酒中用途廣泛。","Some show faint raw-material notes but are still neutral.":"有些帶有淡淡的原料氣息，但仍是中性。","From grain to sugar: malting":"從穀物到糖：製麥","Whisky always starts with grain, and you can picture it as beer that has been through a still. There is one obstacle, though: a barley grain is dry, hard and packed with starch rather than sugar. Yeast cannot do anything with starch, so it has to be turned into sugar before any fermentation can happen. The classic method lets the barley do almost all of that work itself.":"威士忌一定從穀物開始，你可以把它想像成經過蒸餾器的啤酒。不過有一個障礙：大麥粒又乾又硬，充滿的是澱粉而不是糖。酵母對澱粉無能為力，所以必須先把澱粉轉化為糖，才能發酵。經典做法是讓大麥自己完成幾乎所有的工作。","The first step is malting. The barley is allowed to start growing, and as it grows the grain makes enzymes, tiny chemical tools that can change starch. At the right moment hot air is blown through to stop the growth, and from then on it is called malted barley. The grain now carries everything it needs, but the sugar has not been released yet.":"第一步是製麥。讓大麥開始生長，穀粒在生長時會產生酵素，這是能改變澱粉的微小化學工具。在適當的時刻吹入熱空氣以停止生長，從此就稱為麥芽大麥。現在穀粒已具備一切所需，但糖還沒有被釋放出來。","Next the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, and other crushed grains can be added too. Everything is mixed with water, and in this bath the barley's enzymes get to work, converting the starch into sugar. The result is a sweet liquid ready for the yeast. From here the path is the one every spirit follows: fermentation, distillation, then what happens after the still.":"接著把麥芽大麥碾成粗粉，也可以加入其他碾碎的穀物。全部與水混合，大麥的酵素就在這個水浴中開始工作，把澱粉轉化為糖。結果是一種等著酵母的甜液體。從這裡開始，走的就是每款烈酒都走的路：發酵、蒸餾，然後是蒸餾後的處理。","Each grain leaves its own signature in the glass. Barley brings cereal notes, corn recalls sweetcorn and rye adds a spicy, peppery edge. All whiskies then spend time in oak barrels, are blended and, where the law allows, have their colour adjusted with caramel. Most are bottled at 40% abv.":"每種穀物都會在杯中留下自己的印記。大麥帶來穀物氣息，玉米讓人想到甜玉米，黑麥則增添辛香、胡椒般的鋒芒。所有威士忌接著都會在橡木桶中度過一段時間、經過調和，並在法律允許時以焦糖色調整顏色。大多數以 40% abv 裝瓶。","Whisky is made only from grain: think of it as distilled beer.":"威士忌只用穀物製作：把它想成蒸餾過的啤酒。","Grains hold starch, not sugar, so it must be converted before fermentation.":"穀物含有澱粉而不是糖，所以發酵前必須轉化。","Malting: barley sprouts, makes enzymes, then hot air stops the growth.":"製麥：大麥發芽、產生酵素，然後用熱空氣停止生長。","Crushed malt + water: the enzymes turn starch into sugar.":"碾碎的麥芽 + 水：酵素把澱粉轉化為糖。","The rules every Scotch follows":"每款 Scotch 都遵循的規定","Scotch is the name for whisky from Scotland, and it is more than a loose geographical label. To carry the name, a whisky must be distilled in Scotland and then aged in Scotland for at least three years. Both conditions matter: a Scottish spirit sent to mature across the border loses the right to the name, even if everything else about it is identical.":"Scotch 是蘇格蘭威士忌的名稱，而且不只是一個寬鬆的地理標籤。要使用這個名稱，威士忌必須在蘇格蘭蒸餾，然後在蘇格蘭陳年至少三年。兩個條件都很重要：一款蘇格蘭烈酒如果送到邊界另一邊熟成，即使其他一切都相同，也會失去使用這個名稱的權利。","Time in oak is therefore compulsory, and it leaves its mark. The barrels give colour and aromas, and over the years the spirit becomes more concentrated as a little water and alcohol escape through the wood. Older whiskies can show notes of fruit cake and sweet spice. After maturation the whisky is blended, its colour adjusted if needed, and it is diluted.":"因此在橡木桶中陳年是強制的，而且會留下印記。酒桶帶來顏色和香氣，隨著歲月推移，少量的水和酒精透過木頭散逸，烈酒變得更濃縮。較老的威士忌可能呈現水果蛋糕和甜香料的氣息。熟成後，威士忌會經過調和，必要時調整顏色，然後稀釋。","Scotch splits into two big families worth knowing well: Single Malt and Blended. The difference is not about prestige or age but about three simple questions: which grains it is made from, what kind of still it was distilled in, and how many distilleries it comes from. Answer those three and you can place any bottle of Scotch.":"Scotch 分成兩個值得熟悉的大家族：Single Malt 和 Blended。差別不在名氣或年份，而在三個簡單的問題：用哪些穀物製成、用哪一種蒸餾器蒸餾、來自幾家蒸餾廠。回答這三個問題，你就能為任何一瓶 Scotch 定位。","Scotch: distilled and aged in Scotland.":"Scotch：在蘇格蘭蒸餾並陳年。","Minimum ageing: three years, always in Scotland.":"最低陳年：三年，一定在蘇格蘭。","Two main families: Single Malt and Blended Scotch.":"兩大家族：Single Malt 和 Blended Scotch。","What separates them: grains, type of still, number of distilleries.":"區分它們的是：穀物、蒸餾器類型、蒸餾廠數量。","Single Malt and peat smoke":"Single Malt 與泥煤煙燻","A Single Malt Scotch meets three requirements. It is made only from malted barley, with no other grains. It is distilled in pot stills, the kind that work one batch at a time. And it comes from a single distillery. That is what 'single' refers to: one place of production, not one barrel.":"Single Malt Scotch 符合三項要求。只用麥芽大麥製成，沒有其他穀物。以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾，也就是一次處理一批的那種。而且來自單一蒸餾廠。這就是「single」的意思：單一生產地點，而不是單一酒桶。","Pot stills produce a spirit of fairly low strength that is full of character. That is why Single Malts are expressive whiskies: on the nose and palate you find cereal, fruit, flowers and honey and, with time in the barrel, fruit cake and sweet spice. Two Single Malts from different distilleries can taste very different from each other.":"壺式蒸餾器產出的烈酒濃度較低，充滿個性。這就是為什麼 Single Malt 是表現力豐富的威士忌：在香氣和口中，你會發現穀物、水果、花香和蜂蜜，在桶中陳年後還有水果蛋糕和甜香料。來自不同蒸餾廠的兩款 Single Malt，味道可能大不相同。","Some Single Malts carry one extra aroma: smoke. It comes from peat, a natural fuel that is burned when the barley is heated at the end of malting. The smoke wraps around the grains and flavours them, and that flavour travels all the way to the glass. These whiskies are a minority, though: only a few Single Malts are peaty, some of them very strongly.":"有些 Single Malt 多了一種香氣：煙燻。它來自泥煤，一種在製麥最後烘乾大麥時燃燒的天然燃料。煙霧包覆穀粒並為它們增添風味，這種風味會一路來到杯中。不過這類威士忌是少數：只有少數 Single Malt 帶有泥煤風味，其中有些非常濃烈。","Single Malt: 100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery.":"Single Malt：100% 麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠。","Typical aromas: cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, fruit cake, sweet spice.":"典型香氣：穀物、水果、花香、蜂蜜、水果蛋糕、甜香料。","Smoke comes from peat burned while the malted barley is heated.":"煙燻味來自烘乾麥芽大麥時燃燒的泥煤。","Only a few Single Malts are peaty.":"只有少數 Single Malt 帶有泥煤風味。","Blended Scotch and grain whisky":"Blended Scotch 與穀物威士忌","Alongside malt there is a second kind of Scottish whisky: grain whisky. It is made from malted barley together with other grains and distilled in a column still rather than a pot still. The result is a spirit with a light aroma and a smooth texture. It rarely reaches the shelf on its own, because its real job lies elsewhere.":"除了麥芽威士忌，還有第二種蘇格蘭威士忌：穀物威士忌。它用麥芽大麥加上其他穀物製成，以柱式蒸餾器而不是壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。結果是一款香氣清淡、口感柔順的烈酒。它很少單獨上架，因為它真正的工作在別處。","That job is Blended Scotch, the most widespread category. A blend brings together malt whiskies and grain whiskies from different distilleries. Think of an orchestra: the malts, intense and characterful, are the soloists, while the light, smooth grain whisky is the section that holds everything together. Whiskies of different ages also go into the mix to add variety.":"這份工作就是 Blended Scotch，最普遍的類別。調和威士忌把來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌結合在一起。想像一支管弦樂團：濃郁、有個性的麥芽威士忌是獨奏者，而清淡柔順的穀物威士忌則是把一切串連起來的聲部。不同年份的威士忌也會加入調和，增添變化。","Why blend? For two reasons. The first is consistency: every barrel is slightly different, and people expect a bottle to taste the same as last time. The second is complexity: combining spirits with different characters is the easiest way to build depth. A tiny amount of caramel then helps keep the colour identical from one batch to the next.":"為什麼要調和？有兩個原因。第一是一致性：每個酒桶都略有不同，而人們期待一瓶酒的味道和上次一樣。第二是複雜度：結合不同個性的烈酒，是建立深度最簡單的方法。極少量的焦糖色則有助於讓每一批的顏色完全相同。","Blends vary a great deal. Some have medium intensity and a simple style, ideal for mixing; others are pronounced and complex. Thanks to the grain whisky they are usually smoother than Single Malts. So there is no reason to see them as second-rate: they are the work of a real craft, the craft of blending.":"調和威士忌的差異很大。有些強度中等、風格簡單，非常適合調酒；有些則濃郁而複雜。因為有穀物威士忌，它們通常比 Single Malt 更柔順。所以沒有理由把它們看作次等：它們是一門真正技藝的成果，也就是調和的技藝。","Grain whisky: malted barley + other grains, column still, light and smooth.":"穀物威士忌：麥芽大麥 + 其他穀物、柱式蒸餾器、清淡柔順。","Blended Scotch: malt + grain whiskies from different distilleries.":"Blended Scotch：來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽 + 穀物威士忌。","Blending gives consistency and complexity.":"調和帶來一致性和複雜度。","Usually smoother than Single Malts; from simple to complex.":"通常比 Single Malt 柔順；從簡單到複雜都有。","Bourbon: corn and new barrels":"Bourbon：玉米與新桶","Bourbon is the best-known American whiskey. Many people link it to Kentucky, and that is indeed the state that makes the most, but the law allows it to be made anywhere in the United States. Its style comes down to three clear choices: the grain recipe, the way it is distilled and the type of barrel.":"Bourbon 是最知名的美國威士忌。許多人把它與肯塔基州聯想在一起，那確實是產量最多的州，但法律允許它在美國任何地方生產。它的風格取決於三個明確的選擇：穀物配方、蒸餾方式和酒桶類型。","First choice: at least 51% of the grain must be corn, usually topped up with barley and rye. Corn brings sweetcorn notes. Second choice: it is normally distilled in a column still, but only to a low strength, so the spirit keeps plenty of character. A column still does not have to make a light spirit; it all depends on how high the strength goes.":"第一個選擇：至少 51% 的穀物必須是玉米，通常再補上大麥和黑麥。玉米帶來甜玉米氣息。第二個選擇：通常以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，但只蒸餾到較低濃度，讓烈酒保留大量個性。柱式蒸餾器不一定會做出清淡的烈酒；一切取決於濃度拉到多高。","Third choice: the barrels must be new oak, charred on the inside. A barrel that has never been used gives the most colour and aroma, and the charring adds even more intensity. The result is a pronounced, complex whiskey with notes of sweetcorn, cereal, fruit, vanilla and coconut.":"第三個選擇：酒桶必須是新的橡木桶，內部經過炙燒。從未使用過的桶帶來最多的顏色和香氣，炙燒則增添更多濃郁度。結果是一款濃郁、複雜的威士忌，帶有甜玉米、穀物、水果、香草和椰子氣息。","A common trap: people often call Bourbon 'sweet'. In fact it has no added sugar and is dry. The impression of sweetness comes from the vanilla, fruit and coconut aromas, which the nose links with desserts. In tasting language, 'sweet' refers only to the taste of sugar, felt on the palate.":"一個常見陷阱：人們常說 Bourbon「很甜」。事實上它沒有加糖，是不甜的。甜的印象來自香草、水果和椰子香氣，鼻子會把這些香氣與甜點聯想在一起。在品飲用語中，「甜」只指在口中感受到的糖的味道。","Bourbon: at least 51% corn; made anywhere in the USA, mostly Kentucky.":"Bourbon：至少 51% 玉米；可在美國任何地方生產，大多在肯塔基州。","Usually column-distilled to a low strength.":"通常以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度。","New charred oak barrels: lots of colour and aroma.":"炙燒過的新橡木桶：大量顏色和香氣。","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit; no added sugar, so it is dry.":"甜玉米、香草、椰子、水果；沒有加糖，所以是不甜的。","Tennessee whiskey: through the charcoal":"Tennessee 威士忌：通過木炭","Tennessee whiskey is a close relative of Bourbon. It is made the same way, with the same majority of corn, the same distillation and the same new charred barrels. There are two differences. The first is geography: unlike Bourbon, it can only be made in the state of Tennessee. The second is one extra step that happens before the barrel.":"Tennessee 威士忌是 Bourbon 的近親。它的製作方式相同，同樣以玉米為主、同樣的蒸餾方式、同樣使用炙燒過的新桶。差別有兩個。第一是地理：與 Bourbon 不同，它只能在田納西州生產。第二是在入桶前多了一個步驟。","As soon as it leaves the still, the new spirit is passed through a bed of maple charcoal. It is not a very fine filter, but it holds back some impurities. The effect is a whiskey with a smoother character. This step adds no flavour at all: no maple, no smoke. It takes something away rather than putting anything in.":"新烈酒一離開蒸餾器，就會通過一層楓木炭。這不是非常精細的過濾，但能留住部分雜質。效果是讓威士忌的個性更柔順。這個步驟完全不增添風味：沒有楓糖，也沒有煙燻。它是拿走東西，而不是加入東西。","One image makes it easy to remember: Tennessee whiskey is a Bourbon that takes a shower before going into the barrel. Watch the order of the steps: the filtering is done on the new, colourless spirit, not on whiskey that has already aged. After that, the path is the same as Bourbon's, with new charred barrels giving colour and aroma.":"一個比喻讓它很好記：Tennessee 威士忌是在進桶前先沖了個澡的 Bourbon。注意步驟的順序：過濾是針對無色的新烈酒進行，而不是已經陳年的威士忌。之後的路就和 Bourbon 一樣，由炙燒過的新桶帶來顏色和香氣。","Made only in the state of Tennessee.":"只在田納西州生產。","Same recipe and barrels as Bourbon.":"配方和酒桶與 Bourbon 相同。","Extra step: maple charcoal filtering before the barrel.":"額外步驟：入桶前以楓木炭過濾。","Removes impurities, adds smoothness, adds no flavour.":"去除雜質、增添柔順感，不增添風味。","Rye whiskey: the spicy grain":"Rye 威士忌：辛香的穀物","American Rye whiskey is Bourbon's spicy twin. The rules are the same in every way except one: the main grain. Instead of corn, at least 51% of the recipe must be rye. So you still find low-strength column distillation and ageing in new charred oak barrels.":"美國 Rye 威士忌是 Bourbon 的辛香雙胞胎。規定在各方面都相同，只有一項例外：主要穀物。配方中至少 51% 必須是黑麥，而不是玉米。所以同樣是以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度，並在炙燒過的新橡木桶中陳年。","That change of grain is enough to change the character. Rye brings spicy, peppery aromas that show clearly on both nose and palate. Where Bourbon recalls sweetcorn and coconut, Rye has a livelier, sharper profile. The vanilla notes from the new barrel are still there, but they sit behind the spice.":"光是換了穀物，就足以改變個性。黑麥帶來辛香、胡椒般的香氣，在香氣和口中都很明顯。Bourbon 讓人想到甜玉米和椰子，Rye 的風味輪廓則更活潑、更鮮明。新桶帶來的香草氣息仍然存在，但退居在香料之後。","A simple way to fix the three American whiskeys is to look at the grain and the filter. Mostly corn: Bourbon. Mostly corn, plus maple charcoal, made only in Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Mostly rye: Rye. Anyone looking for an American whiskey with a peppery kick, for example in a cocktail, should think of Rye.":"要記住這三款美國威士忌，一個簡單的方法是看穀物和過濾。以玉米為主：Bourbon。以玉米為主，加上楓木炭，只在田納西州生產：Tennessee 威士忌。以黑麥為主：Rye。想找一款帶胡椒勁道的美國威士忌（例如用在調酒中）的人，應該想到 Rye。","Rye: at least 51% rye.":"Rye：至少 51% 黑麥。","Otherwise made like Bourbon: column still and new charred barrels.":"其他做法與 Bourbon 相同：柱式蒸餾器和炙燒過的新桶。","Spicy, peppery aromas.":"辛香、胡椒般的香氣。","Ireland, Canada and Japan":"愛爾蘭、加拿大與日本","In Ireland, most whiskeys are made by combining pot-still and column-still spirits. The typical style is light and smooth, easy to drink. There are also Irish whiskeys made only in pot stills, and some use an unusual ingredient: unmalted barley. This gives an oily texture and a nutty character.":"在愛爾蘭，大多數威士忌是結合壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒製成的。典型風格清淡柔順，容易入口。也有只用壺式蒸餾器製作的愛爾蘭威士忌，其中有些使用一種不尋常的原料：未發芽的大麥。它帶來油潤的質地和堅果般的個性。","Canada uses many different grains and usually blends high-strength spirits, which are lighter, with low-strength spirits, which have more flavour. The result is balanced, versatile whiskies. In the best Canadian whiskies, though, there is one common thread: rye. It is the signature flavour, spicy and peppery.":"加拿大使用許多不同的穀物，通常把較清淡的高濃度烈酒與風味較多的低濃度烈酒調和在一起。結果是均衡、用途廣泛的威士忌。不過，在最優秀的加拿大威士忌中有一條共同的主線：黑麥。它是招牌風味，辛香而帶胡椒味。","Japan built its whisky industry using Scotland as the model. That is why you find both malt and blended whiskies there, just as with Scotch. The traditional style is elegant and refined, precise in its details. In recent years, though, many Japanese producers have been exploring new styles and flavours, and the category keeps evolving.":"日本以蘇格蘭為範本建立了威士忌產業。這就是為什麼那裡和 Scotch 一樣，同時有麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。傳統風格優雅而細緻，講究細節。不過近年來，許多日本生產者一直在探索新的風格和風味，這個類別也持續在演變。","Ireland: mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth.":"愛爾蘭：大多是壺式 + 柱式的調和，清淡柔順。","Unmalted barley: nutty notes and an oily texture.":"未發芽的大麥：堅果氣息和油潤質地。","Canada: many grains, high + low strength blends; rye is the signature.":"加拿大：多種穀物，高 + 低濃度調和；黑麥是招牌。","Japan: Scottish model, elegant malts and blends.":"日本：蘇格蘭模式，優雅的麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。","Cane juice or molasses":"甘蔗汁或糖蜜","Rum is made from sugar cane, a plant that loves heat. That is why production is centred on hot countries, and its historic heartland is the Caribbean. The region is a patchwork of small countries, though, each with its own traditions and rules. Sorting rum by colour or by the language spoken works poorly; it is far more useful to follow the four stages of production.":"蘭姆酒用甘蔗製成，這是一種喜愛高溫的植物。這就是為什麼生產集中在炎熱的國家，而它歷史上的核心地帶是加勒比海。不過這個地區由許多小國拼湊而成，各有自己的傳統和規定。依顏色或使用的語言來分類蘭姆酒效果不佳；依循生產的四個階段要有用得多。","The first choice is the raw material. Freshly cut cane can be crushed and its sweet juice fermented straight away. Rums made from cane juice often have a very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour, like freshly mown grass. The best examples are rhum agricole, which in the Caribbean must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"第一個選擇是原料。新鮮砍下的甘蔗可以壓碎，甜甜的汁液立刻發酵。以甘蔗汁製成的蘭姆酒，通常帶有非常明顯的青草、草本風味，就像剛割下的青草。最好的例子是 rhum agricole，在加勒比海必須來自馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普。","Most Caribbean distillers, however, use molasses. It is a black, sticky substance, the by-product of the industry that turns cane juice into sugar. It has to be mixed with water before fermentation can start. Molasses rums have flavours of caramel and brown sugar, a rounder profile than the grassy freshness of cane juice.":"不過，大多數加勒比海蒸餾師使用糖蜜。它是一種黑色黏稠的物質，是把甘蔗汁製成糖的產業留下的副產品。發酵開始前必須先與水混合。糖蜜蘭姆酒帶有焦糖和紅糖風味，風味輪廓比甘蔗汁的草本清新更圓潤。","Rum is made from sugar cane, which grows in hot climates.":"蘭姆酒用甘蔗製成，甘蔗生長在炎熱氣候。","Understand it through the four stages, not colour or language.":"用四個階段來理解它，而不是顏色或語言。","Cane juice: grassy; rhum agricole from Martinique and Guadeloupe.":"甘蔗汁：青草氣息；rhum agricole 來自馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普。","Molasses (the most common choice): caramel and brown sugar.":"糖蜜（最常見的選擇）：焦糖和紅糖。","Fermentation and tropical fruit":"發酵與熱帶水果","In every spirit, fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, but it also does something else: it creates aromas. Yeast in particular produces fruity scents. In rum this work can take centre stage. By managing fermentation in a certain way, distillers get tropical fruit aromas, such as banana or pineapple, which can become very pronounced.":"在每款烈酒中，發酵都會把糖轉化為酒精，但它還做了另一件事：產生香氣。尤其是酵母會產生果香。在蘭姆酒中，這項工作可能成為主角。透過特定方式管理發酵，蒸餾師能得到香蕉或鳳梨這類熱帶水果香氣，而且可能非常明顯。","Pushing the flavour created during fermentation as far as it will go produces intensely fruity rums, almost explosive on the nose. Jamaican distillers are famous for exactly this style. When you meet a rum with a very concentrated tropical fruit aroma, the likely cause is a fermentation managed with that aim, not an added flavouring.":"把發酵時產生的風味推到極限，就能製作出果香極為濃郁、香氣幾乎爆發的蘭姆酒。牙買加的蒸餾師正是以這種風格聞名。當你遇到熱帶水果香氣非常集中的蘭姆酒，可能的原因是以此為目標管理的發酵，而不是添加的調味料。","This stage shows clearly why the four steps help more than colour. Two rums that are both colourless can be worlds apart: one light and discreet, the other loaded with tropical fruit. Asking what it was made from, how it was fermented and distilled and what happened afterwards tells you far more about the glass than its shade does.":"這個階段清楚說明了為什麼四個步驟比顏色更有幫助。兩款同樣無色的蘭姆酒可能天差地遠：一款清淡低調，另一款充滿熱帶水果。問它是用什麼製成的、如何發酵和蒸餾、之後發生了什麼，比它的色調更能告訴你杯中的內容。","Fermentation creates alcohol and fruity aromas too.":"發酵除了產生酒精，也產生果香。","In rum it can give very pronounced tropical fruit aromas.":"在蘭姆酒中，它可以帶來非常明顯的熱帶水果香氣。","Jamaica is known for this intensely fruity style.":"牙買加以這種果香濃郁的風格聞名。","Pot or column: intensity to order":"壺式或柱式：濃郁度依需求調整","In the Caribbean nearly every distiller can choose their still, and that choice decides how intense the rum will be. For a pronounced spirit full of character, a pot still is an option. Another is a short column with few sections, which also gives a flavourful spirit; this is how rhum agricole is made.":"在加勒比海，幾乎每位蒸餾師都能選擇自己的蒸餾器，而這個選擇決定了蘭姆酒的濃郁程度。想要風味濃郁、充滿個性的烈酒，可以選擇壺式蒸餾器。另一個選擇是層數少的矮蒸餾柱，同樣能得到風味豐富的烈酒；rhum agricole 就是這樣製作的。","At the opposite end are rums with a light aroma. They are made in tall column stills with many sections and distilled to a high strength. The higher the strength, the less aroma remains in the spirit. Examples of this style come from Cuba and Puerto Rico: delicate rums that work very well in cocktails.":"另一個極端是香氣清淡的蘭姆酒。它們以層數很多的高柱式蒸餾器製作，並蒸餾到高濃度。濃度越高，留在烈酒中的香氣就越少。這種風格的例子來自古巴和波多黎各：細緻的蘭姆酒，非常適合用於調酒。","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and column stills and make several spirits of different intensities. It is like a painter's palette: one light spirit, one pronounced, one fruity. Later, at the blending stage, this variety lets them compose rums in very different styles from the same distillery.":"許多加勒比海蒸餾廠同時擁有壺式蒸餾器和柱式蒸餾器，製作出多種不同濃郁度的烈酒。這就像畫家的調色盤：一款清淡、一款濃郁、一款果香。之後在調和階段，這些多樣性讓同一家蒸餾廠能調配出風格迥異的蘭姆酒。","Pot still: pronounced, characterful rum.":"壺式蒸餾器：濃郁、有個性的蘭姆酒。","Short column: also flavourful; used for rhum agricole.":"矮蒸餾柱：同樣風味豐富；用於 rhum agricole。","Tall column, high strength: light rums (Cuba, Puerto Rico).":"高蒸餾柱、高濃度：清淡的蘭姆酒（古巴、波多黎各）。","Many distilleries own both types of still.":"許多蒸餾廠同時擁有兩種蒸餾器。","After the still: oak, filters, sugar and colour":"蒸餾之後：橡木桶、過濾、糖與顏色","A rum can be aged or not. Time in oak adds vanilla and sweet spice aromas, as well as colour. In some Caribbean countries a period in the barrel is a legal requirement. Unaged rum, by contrast, rests in steel tanks: it stays colourless and keeps the aromas of the freshly distilled spirit.":"蘭姆酒可以陳年，也可以不陳年。在橡木桶中的時間會增添香草和甜香料香氣，以及顏色。在某些加勒比海國家，在桶中陳年一段時間是法定要求。相反地，未陳年的蘭姆酒在鋼製桶槽中靜置：它保持無色，並保留剛蒸餾出的烈酒的香氣。","What if a country requires oak but the producer wants a white rum? The answer is charcoal filtering, which removes the colour taken from the wood. The result is a colourless rum that has actually spent time in oak. This is one reason why colour alone cannot tell you how a rum was made.":"如果一個國家要求橡木桶陳年，但生產者想要白色蘭姆酒呢？答案是木炭過濾，它能去除從木頭吸收的顏色。結果就是一款確實在橡木桶中待過、卻無色的蘭姆酒。這也是為什麼光看顏色無法告訴你一款蘭姆酒是如何製作的原因之一。","Then comes blending. Blenders can combine pot-still and column-still spirits, of different ages and even from different distilleries, to build the style of each product. Finally, some rums are sweetened: this is common in Central and South America, while some countries forbid it. Many rums also receive caramel for colour, sometimes almost all of their colour.":"接著是調和。調和師可以結合壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒，不同年份，甚至來自不同的蒸餾廠，以建立每款產品的風格。最後，有些蘭姆酒會加甜：這在中南美洲很常見，而有些國家則禁止。許多蘭姆酒也會加入焦糖色來上色，有時幾乎所有顏色都來自焦糖色。","The last step, as for nearly every spirit, is dilution with pure water down to bottling strength. The result is a hugely varied family, from light, discreet white rum to dark, intense, spicy rum. To find your way, simply walk back through the four stages: raw material, fermentation, distillation and what happens afterwards.":"和幾乎所有烈酒一樣，最後一步是用純水稀釋到裝瓶濃度。結果是一個極為多樣的家族，從清淡低調的白色蘭姆酒，到深色、濃郁、帶辛香的蘭姆酒。要找到方向，只要沿著四個階段往回走：原料、發酵、蒸餾，以及之後發生的事。","Oak gives vanilla, sweet spice and colour; required in some countries.":"橡木桶帶來香草、甜香料和顏色；在某些國家是強制的。","White rum: steel tanks (unaged) or charcoal filtering (aged).":"白色蘭姆酒：鋼製桶槽（未陳年）或木炭過濾（陳年）。","Blending of different styles, ages and distilleries.":"調和不同風格、年份和蒸餾廠的烈酒。","Sugar: common in Central and South America, banned in some countries; caramel is common.":"糖：在中南美洲很常見，在某些國家被禁止；焦糖色很常見。","From blue agave to sweet juice":"從藍色龍舌蘭到甜汁液","Tequila is a Mexican spirit with a very clear identity: it can only be made in certain Mexican states named by law, and only from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico. It is not a cactus, even if it looks a bit like one: long, spiky leaves fan out around a large, hard core. That core is the part the distiller actually wants.":"Tequila 是一種身分非常明確的墨西哥烈酒：它只能在法律指名的特定墨西哥州生產，而且只能用藍色龍舌蘭製作，這是一種原產於墨西哥的植物。它不是仙人掌，即使看起來有點像：長而帶刺的葉片圍繞著一個又大又硬的核心呈扇形展開。這個核心才是蒸餾師真正想要的部分。","At harvest the leaves are cut away, leaving only the core. As with grains, a freshly harvested agave core has no sugar ready to ferment: it has to be processed first. The cores are cooked slowly in ovens until they turn soft and sugars form inside them. Think of a hard potato that you can mash with a fork once it has been cooked: the idea is much the same.":"採收時會切除葉片，只留下核心。和穀物一樣，剛採收的龍舌蘭心沒有現成可發酵的糖：必須先經過處理。龍舌蘭心放在窯爐中慢慢烹煮，直到變軟，內部形成糖分。想想一顆堅硬的馬鈴薯，煮熟後就能用叉子壓成泥：道理大致相同。","Once cooked, the cores are crushed and give up a sweet juice. That juice carries the very recognisable aromas of blue agave: herbaceous and vegetal notes, hints of olive and earth, and a touch of pepper. These aromas are what set Tequila so clearly apart from rum or whisky, and the producer will try to protect them through the following steps.":"烹煮後，龍舌蘭心被壓碎，釋出甜甜的汁液。這些汁液帶有藍色龍舌蘭非常容易辨認的香氣：草本和植物氣息、一絲橄欖和泥土，以及一點胡椒。這些香氣讓 Tequila 與蘭姆酒或威士忌截然不同，生產者會在接下來的步驟中努力保護它們。","Blue agave only, made only in certain Mexican states.":"只用藍色龍舌蘭，只在墨西哥特定州生產。","The core is used; the leaves are cut away.":"使用的是龍舌蘭心；葉片會被切除。","Oven cooking softens the core and creates sugars; then it is crushed.":"窯爐烹煮讓龍舌蘭心變軟並產生糖，然後壓碎。","Agave aromas: herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy, peppery.":"龍舌蘭香氣：草本、植物、橄欖、泥土、胡椒。","Tequila or Tequila 100% agave?":"Tequila 還是 Tequila 100% agave？","The agave juice is mixed with water to make a sugary liquid ready for fermentation. At this point the producer has a choice: other sugars, not from agave, may be added too. The law sets a clear floor, though: at least 51% of the sugars fermented must come from blue agave. In other words, more than half must always be agave.":"龍舌蘭汁與水混合，製成準備發酵的含糖液體。此時生產者有一個選擇：也可以加入不是來自龍舌蘭的其他糖。不過法律設下了明確的底線：發酵的糖中至少 51% 必須來自藍色龍舌蘭。換句話說，一定要有超過一半是龍舌蘭。","When a label says ‘100% agave’, it means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid, with no other sugars at all. The result tends to show a more pronounced agave character. Every other Tequila, the ones that use the option of adding other sugars, is simply labelled ‘Tequila’, with nothing more.":"當酒標寫著「100% agave」，表示製作含糖液體時只使用了藍色龍舌蘭，完全沒有其他糖。成品往往呈現更鮮明的龍舌蘭個性。其他所有 Tequila，也就是選擇加入其他糖的那些，酒標上就只寫「Tequila」，不會有其他說明。","Be careful not to mix this up with ageing: it is only about where the sugars came from. An unaged Tequila can be ‘100% agave’ or not, and the same is true of an oak-aged one. So, in front of a shelf, it pays to read two separate pieces of information: how much agave went in, and how long the spirit has rested.":"小心別把這個和陳年搞混：它只關乎糖的來源。未陳年的 Tequila 可以是「100% agave」，也可以不是，經橡木桶陳年的也一樣。所以站在酒架前時，值得讀兩項不同的資訊：用了多少龍舌蘭，以及烈酒靜置了多久。","Agave juice is mixed with water before fermentation.":"發酵前，龍舌蘭汁與水混合。","At least 51% of the sugars must come from blue agave.":"至少 51% 的糖必須來自藍色龍舌蘭。","‘100% agave’ = no other sugars, more pronounced agave character.":"「100% agave」= 沒有其他糖，龍舌蘭個性更鮮明。","Any style, aged or unaged, can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’.":"任何風格，不論陳年與否，都可以是「Tequila」或「100% agave」。","Distilling to keep the agave":"為保留龍舌蘭而蒸餾","After fermentation comes distillation. Tequila can be made in column stills, but the best ones take another route: they are distilled twice in pot stills and stopped at a notably low strength. Remember the general rule: the lower the distillation strength, the more of the raw material's aromas stay in the spirit.":"發酵之後是蒸餾。Tequila 可以用柱式蒸餾器製作，但最優秀的 Tequila 走另一條路：它們在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，並停在明顯較低的濃度。記住一般原則：蒸餾濃度越低，留在烈酒中的原料香氣就越多。","The result is a spirit with real personality, putting the herbaceous, peppery notes of blue agave front and centre, easy to spot from the first sip. It is the exact opposite of a neutral spirit such as vodka, which is pushed through a column to very high strength precisely to strip out almost all aroma.":"結果是一款真正有個性的烈酒，把藍色龍舌蘭的草本、胡椒氣息擺在最前面，第一口就很容易辨認。它正好與伏特加這類中性烈酒相反，伏特加被送進蒸餾柱蒸餾到極高濃度，正是為了去除幾乎所有的香氣。","A simple way to lock the idea in: pot still, double distillation and low strength mean ‘more agave in the glass’. If a question asks how the most expressive Tequilas are made, the answer lies here, not with tall columns and high strengths. Columns are still allowed, but they generally give Tequilas with less pronounced character.":"一個鞏固觀念的簡單方法：壺式蒸餾器、二次蒸餾、低濃度，代表「杯中有更多龍舌蘭」。如果題目問最有表現力的 Tequila 是如何製作的，答案就在這裡，而不是高蒸餾柱和高濃度。蒸餾柱仍然是允許的，但一般得到的 Tequila 個性較不鮮明。","Columns are allowed, but the best Tequilas are double distilled in pot stills.":"允許使用蒸餾柱，但最優秀的 Tequila 是在壺式蒸餾器中二次蒸餾。","Low distillation strength = more agave aroma.":"低蒸餾濃度 = 更多龍舌蘭香氣。","Result: a characterful, herbaceous, peppery spirit.":"結果：有個性、帶草本與胡椒氣息的烈酒。","After distillation the producer decides whether to age the Tequila or leave it as it is. There are two unaged versions. Blanco, also called Silver, is colourless and prized for showing agave at its purest. Joven, also called Oro or Gold, has an attractive golden colour but has never seen a barrel: the colour comes from caramel, and other additives soften its texture.":"蒸餾後，生產者決定要讓 Tequila 陳年，還是保持原樣。有兩種未陳年的版本。Blanco，也稱為 Silver，無色，因為展現最純粹的龍舌蘭而備受推崇。Joven，也稱為 Oro 或 Gold，有迷人的金黃色，但從未進過酒桶：顏色來自焦糖色，其他添加物則讓口感變得柔和。","There are also two oak-aged versions. Reposado (‘rested’) spends between 2 and 12 months in oak: it comes out softer, but the wood rarely shows strongly and the agave aromas stay pronounced. Añejo (‘aged’) spends at least 12 months in barrel and combines agave aromas with oak notes such as vanilla and spice.":"也有兩種經橡木桶陳年的版本。Reposado（「靜置過的」）在橡木桶中待 2 到 12 個月：口感變得較柔和，但木頭的味道很少明顯，龍舌蘭香氣仍然鮮明。Añejo（「陳年的」）在桶中至少待 12 個月，結合了龍舌蘭香氣和香草、香料等橡木氣息。","Why do aged Tequilas spend fairly little time in barrel? Because the producer is looking for balance: some vanilla and spice, without burying the agave character that makes Tequila unique. Aged versions are then blended and may receive caramel to even out the colour, before being diluted with water and bottled.":"為什麼陳年 Tequila 在桶中的時間相對較短？因為生產者追求平衡：帶一些香草和香料，又不掩蓋讓 Tequila 獨一無二的龍舌蘭個性。陳年版本接著會經過調和，可能加入焦糖色讓顏色均勻，然後加水稀釋並裝瓶。","Blanco/Silver: unaged, agave at its purest.":"Blanco／Silver：未陳年，最純粹的龍舌蘭。","Joven/Oro/Gold: unaged, coloured with caramel.":"Joven／Oro／Gold：未陳年，以焦糖色上色。","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak, softer, agave still in the lead.":"Reposado：在橡木桶中 2–12 個月，較柔和，龍舌蘭仍居主導。","Añejo: at least 12 months in oak, agave plus oak.":"Añejo：在橡木桶中至少 12 個月，龍舌蘭加上橡木。","Three ways to flavour a spirit":"為烈酒調味的三種方法","With flavoured spirits the starting point is different: the producer usually grows and ferments nothing, but buys in a ready-made spirit. In the vast majority of cases it is the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka once diluted with water. Now and then the base is a rum, whisky or brandy instead. The real work starts afterwards: adding flavours other than those from oak.":"調味烈酒的起點不同：生產者通常什麼都不種植、也不發酵，而是外購現成的烈酒。在絕大多數情況下，那就是加水稀釋後成為伏特加的同一種中性烈酒。偶爾基底會改用蘭姆酒、威士忌或白蘭地。真正的工作在之後才開始：加入橡木以外的風味。","The best products use natural ingredients such as fruits, seeds, herbs and spices, known as botanicals. The first method is redistillation: diluted neutral spirit and botanicals go into a pot still together and are distilled. What comes out is fragrant and colourless. The second is maceration: the botanicals steep in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, giving up flavour and colour too.":"最好的產品使用水果、種子、香草和香料等天然原料，稱為植物性原料（botanicals）。第一種方法是再蒸餾：稀釋過的中性烈酒和植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾。流出的液體芳香而無色。第二種是浸漬：植物性原料浸泡在烈酒中，就像冷泡花草茶，同時釋出風味和顏色。","Maceration can last a few days or several months: the longer it goes on, the more flavour is drawn out, and gentle heating speeds things up. The third method is the simplest: adding bought-in flavourings, natural or artificial, which are very concentrated and used in small amounts. It is usually chosen for cost reasons, instead of real botanicals.":"浸漬可以持續幾天到幾個月：時間越長，萃取出的風味越多，溫和加熱則能加快速度。第三種方法最簡單：加入外購的天然或人工調味料，這些調味料非常濃縮，只需少量使用。通常是出於成本考量，用它來取代真正的植物性原料。","Typical base: bought-in neutral spirit (sometimes rum, whisky or brandy).":"典型基底：外購的中性烈酒（有時是蘭姆酒、威士忌或白蘭地）。","Botanicals = fruits, seeds, herbs and spices.":"植物性原料 = 水果、種子、香草和香料。","Redistillation: flavoured and colourless. Maceration: flavoured and coloured.":"再蒸餾：有風味、無色。浸漬：有風味、有顏色。","Bought-in flavourings: concentrated, used in small doses, often to save cost.":"外購調味料：濃縮、少量使用，常為了節省成本。","Flavoured vodka and gin":"調味伏特加與琴酒","Flavoured vodka is the most intuitive case: a neutral base given one clear flavour. The options are endless: vanilla, fruits such as apple or lemon, even spices like pepper. Most producers simply add bought-in flavourings to their neutral vodka, although some use redistillation. The result is easy to spot on the nose: one flavour, clean and direct.":"調味伏特加是最直觀的例子：一個中性基底，加上一種明確的風味。選擇無窮無盡：香草、蘋果或檸檬等水果，甚至胡椒這類香料。大多數生產者只是在中性伏特加中加入外購調味料，不過也有些使用再蒸餾。結果在香氣上很容易辨認：一種風味，乾淨而直接。","Gin is a flavoured spirit with one essential rule: juniper must be the leading flavour, with its resinous, piney notes. Alongside juniper you often find coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel. The base is usually neutral spirit, although other distilled spirits are allowed in the USA. A typical gin is colourless and unaged.":"琴酒是一種有一條基本規定的調味烈酒：杜松子必須是主導風味，帶有樹脂和松木般的氣息。除了杜松子，常見的還有芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根和柑橘皮。基底通常是中性烈酒，不過在美國也允許使用其他蒸餾烈酒。典型的琴酒無色、未經陳年。","The best gins are usually redistilled with their botanicals, although some very delicate flavours are added afterwards. Other producers simply add bought-in flavourings. On a label, ‘London Dry Gin’ means the flavours were added during redistillation. Despite the name, it is not a place: a London Dry Gin can be made anywhere in the world.":"最優秀的琴酒通常是與植物性原料一起再蒸餾，不過有些非常細緻的風味是之後才加入的。其他生產者則直接加入外購調味料。在酒標上，「London Dry Gin」表示風味是在再蒸餾時加入的。儘管名稱如此，它並不是地名：London Dry Gin 可以在世界任何地方製作。","Flavoured vodka: neutral base + usually bought-in flavourings (sometimes redistillation).":"調味伏特加：中性基底 + 通常是外購調味料（有時以再蒸餾製作）。","Gin: juniper must lead.":"琴酒：杜松子必須居主導。","Other classic botanicals: coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel.":"其他經典植物性原料：芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根、柑橘皮。","London Dry = flavours added by redistillation; can be made anywhere.":"London Dry = 以再蒸餾加入風味；可在任何地方製作。","Bitter spirits, cocktail bitters and spiced rum":"苦味烈酒、調酒用苦精與香料蘭姆酒","Bitter spirits contain at least one bitter botanical, such as gentian, quinine or bitter orange. A curious detail: bitterness only shows up in the mouth, because the nose cannot detect it. The aromas come from the bitter botanicals but also from many other ingredients. These spirits were traditionally drunk before or after a meal; today they end up mostly in cocktails.":"苦味烈酒至少含有一種苦味植物性原料，例如龍膽、奎寧或苦橙。一個有趣的細節：苦味只在口中出現，因為鼻子無法察覺苦味。香氣來自苦味植物性原料，也來自許多其他材料。這些烈酒傳統上在餐前或餐後飲用；如今大多用在調酒中。","Cocktail bitters are something else: highly concentrated, intensely bitter spirits that nobody drinks on their own. They are used by the drop, a few dashes in a cocktail, to add complexity, rather like salt and pepper in cooking. A small bottle lasts a long time behind the bar precisely because so little is needed.":"調酒用苦精則是另一回事：高度濃縮、極苦的烈酒，沒有人會單獨飲用。它們以滴數使用，在調酒中加幾滴來增添複雜度，有點像烹飪中的鹽和胡椒。正因為用量很少，一小瓶在吧台後可以用很久。","Spiced rum, finally, is a very varied family, both in its base rum and in the flavourings added. Many start from a light, unaged rum that is flavoured and coloured with caramel; only a handful use an oak-aged rum. Both real botanicals and other flavourings are used. So be careful: an amber colour does not necessarily mean years in a barrel.":"最後，香料蘭姆酒是一個非常多樣的家族，不論是基底蘭姆酒還是加入的調味料都是如此。許多以清淡的未陳年蘭姆酒為起點，經過調味並以焦糖色上色；只有少數使用橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒。真正的植物性原料和其他調味料都會使用。所以要小心：琥珀色不一定代表在桶中多年。","Bitter spirits: at least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange).":"苦味烈酒：至少一種苦味植物性原料（龍膽、奎寧、苦橙）。","Bitterness is felt only on the palate, not the nose.":"苦味只在口中感受得到，鼻子聞不到。","Cocktail bitters: very concentrated, never drunk alone, used in dashes.":"調酒用苦精：非常濃縮，從不單喝，以滴數使用。","Spiced rum: often light unaged rum + flavourings + caramel.":"香料蘭姆酒：常是清淡的未陳年蘭姆酒 + 調味料 + 焦糖色。","Liqueurs: flavoured and sweet":"利口酒：有風味又甜","A liqueur is a flavoured spirit that has also been sweetened. That is the key difference from a gin or a flavoured vodka, which stay dry. Sugar goes in after the flavouring, and the law sets a minimum level of sweetness: without reaching it, a product cannot be called a liqueur.":"利口酒是經過調味、又加了甜的烈酒。這是它與琴酒或調味伏特加的關鍵差別，後兩者仍然是不甜的。糖是在調味之後加入的，法律規定了最低甜度：未達到這個甜度，產品就不能稱為利口酒。","Most liqueurs are made from neutral spirit, but some start from more characterful spirits such as brandy, rum or whisky. Beyond that, freedom is almost complete: any flavour and any method of adding it. Think citrus or coffee, herbs or hazelnuts. Some liqueurs even contain a surprising ingredient: cream, which gives them a soft, velvety texture.":"大多數利口酒以中性烈酒製成，但有些以更有個性的烈酒為起點，例如白蘭地、蘭姆酒或威士忌。除此之外，幾乎完全自由：任何風味、任何添加方式都可以。想想柑橘或咖啡、香草或榛果。有些利口酒甚至含有一種令人意外的原料：鮮奶油，為它們帶來柔軟絲滑的質地。","Many liqueurs are coloured as well. Natural colour from maceration is attractive but tends to fade quickly, so artificial colourings, which are more stable, are widely used. They also offer a much wider range of shades, which is why shelves show liqueurs in bright green, electric blue or vivid red.":"許多利口酒也會上色。來自浸漬的天然顏色很迷人，但往往很快褪色，所以廣泛使用較穩定的人工色素。它們也提供更廣泛的色調範圍，這就是為什麼酒架上會出現鮮綠、電光藍或鮮紅色的利口酒。","Liqueur = flavoured spirit + sugar.":"利口酒 = 調味烈酒 + 糖。","The law requires a minimum sweetness.":"法律規定最低甜度。","Neutral or characterful base; any flavour, even cream.":"中性或有個性的基底；任何風味，甚至鮮奶油。","Artificial colours: stable colour and brighter shades.":"人工色素：顏色穩定、色調更鮮豔。","The four building blocks of an aromatised wine":"加味葡萄酒的四個基本組成","Aromatised wines are not spirits, yet every bar has them because they are so useful in cocktails: a single ingredient brings sweetness, bitterness and acidity. The category is varied, but the basic recipe never changes. There are four components: a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar and a little spirit. Caramel is sometimes added too.":"加味葡萄酒不是烈酒，但每個酒吧都有，因為它們在調酒中非常有用：一種材料就能帶來甜味、苦味和酸度。這個類別很多樣，但基本配方從不改變。有四個組成部分：基酒、一定包含某種苦味的調味料、糖，以及少量烈酒。有時也會加入焦糖色。","The base wine is nearly always white, often fairly neutral, so it works as a blank canvas for the added flavours; some producers prefer aromatic wines and balance them with their recipe, and some use red or rosé wine. Flavourings go straight into the wine or are added as flavoured spirits. Recipes vary a lot, but all of them include bitter botanicals such as wormwood, gentian or quinine.":"基酒幾乎都是白葡萄酒，通常相當中性，所以能作為添加風味的空白畫布；有些生產者偏好芳香型葡萄酒，再用配方加以平衡，也有些使用紅葡萄酒或粉紅酒。調味料直接加入葡萄酒中，或以調味烈酒的形式加入。配方差異很大，但都包含苦艾、龍膽或奎寧等苦味植物性原料。","The spirit, nearly always neutral, is added in a small amount to raise the alcohol and give the product a longer life, especially once the bottle is open. Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry: sweetness can come from the wine itself or from added sugar. Caramel is optional and used for colour; in red products made from white wine it can also add caramel notes.":"烈酒幾乎都是中性的，少量加入以提高酒精濃度，讓產品保存更久，尤其是開瓶之後。幾乎沒有加味葡萄酒是完全不甜的：甜味可能來自葡萄酒本身，也可能來自添加的糖。焦糖色是可選的，用來上色；在以白葡萄酒製成的紅色產品中，它也能增添焦糖氣息。","Four components: base wine, flavourings with something bitter, sugar, spirit.":"四個組成部分：基酒、帶苦味的調味料、糖、烈酒。","Base wine usually white and fairly neutral.":"基酒通常是白葡萄酒，相當中性。","The spirit (usually neutral) raises alcohol and extends shelf life.":"烈酒（通常是中性的）提高酒精濃度並延長保存期限。","Almost never fully dry; caramel optional for colour.":"幾乎從不完全不甜；焦糖色可選，用於上色。","Aromatised wines can be made anywhere in the world, but two areas are especially famous: south-east France and north-west Italy. In both countries the most widely made type is vermouth. Two rules define it: it is made from a white wine base, and it must be flavoured with wormwood, a botanical with a strongly bitter taste.":"加味葡萄酒可以在世界任何地方製作，但有兩個地區特別有名：法國東南部和義大利西北部。在這兩個國家，最普遍的類型是香艾酒。兩條規定定義了它：以白葡萄酒為基酒，而且必須用苦艾調味，這是一種苦味強烈的植物性原料。","Watch the labels: a vermouth marked ‘dry’ nearly always contains added sugar, just less of it. Red vermouths, on the other hand, are usually heavily sweetened. And their colour? Since the base is a white wine, the red shade usually comes from caramel, which can also add a light caramel aroma.":"注意酒標：標示「dry」的香艾酒幾乎都含有添加的糖，只是比較少。相反地，紅香艾酒通常大量加甜。那它們的顏色呢？既然基酒是白葡萄酒，紅色通常來自焦糖色，焦糖色還能增添淡淡的焦糖香氣。","Behind the bar, vermouth is a real all-rounder. A dry vermouth can add dryness and perfume to a gin-based drink, while a red one, sweet with a bitter edge, rounds out a whiskey cocktail. Either way it does the same job: balancing sweetness, bitterness and acidity in one pour. That is why it pays to know its style and sweetness before reaching for the bottle.":"在吧台後，香艾酒是真正的全能選手。不甜香艾酒能為以琴酒為基底的飲品增添乾爽感和香氣，而甜中帶苦的紅香艾酒則能讓威士忌調酒更圓潤。不論哪一種，它的工作都一樣：一次倒入就平衡了甜、苦和酸。這就是為什麼在拿起酒瓶之前，值得先了解它的風格和甜度。","Best-known areas: south-east France and north-west Italy.":"最知名的產區：法國東南部和義大利西北部。","Vermouth = white wine base + wormwood, by rule.":"香艾酒 = 白葡萄酒基底 + 苦艾，依規定。","Even ‘dry’ nearly always has sugar; red is very sweet.":"即使是「dry」也幾乎都有糖；紅香艾酒非常甜。","Red vermouth usually gets its colour from caramel.":"紅香艾酒的顏色通常來自焦糖色。","Setting the scene and choosing the glass":"布置環境與選擇酒杯","Tasting a spirit means looking at it closely, and doing that well needs a method you repeat the same way every time. If every sample is treated identically, the notes you write today can be compared with the ones you write next month. Before pouring anything, though, it pays to prepare the setting: a good tasting depends as much on what surrounds the glass as on the liquid inside it.":"品飲烈酒就是仔細地觀察它，而要做好這件事，需要一套每次都以相同方式重複的方法。如果每個樣品都以相同方式對待，你今天寫下的筆記就能和下個月寫的相互比較。不過在倒酒之前，值得先準備好環境：一場好的品飲，取決於酒杯周圍的一切，不亞於杯中的液體。","The room should be free of distracting smells: no strong perfume, cooking or scented candles. You need good natural light and a white surface, such as a sheet of paper or a tablecloth, to hold the glass against so the colour can be judged without misleading reflections. The taster matters too: a clean palate with no lingering toothpaste or coffee, and a well-hydrated body.":"房間裡不應有干擾的氣味：沒有濃烈的香水、烹飪味或香氛蠟燭。你需要良好的自然光和白色表面，例如一張紙或桌布，把酒杯放在前面，這樣判斷顏色時就不會受到誤導性的反光影響。品飲者本身也很重要：味覺要乾淨，沒有殘留的牙膏或咖啡味，身體也要補充足夠的水分。","Then comes the glass. The ideal shape has a wide bowl that narrows towards the rim, a little like a tulip. The wide part gives the aromas room to rise, while the narrower opening gathers them and channels them straight to your nose. In a straight, open tumbler, by contrast, the scents drift away and the spirit seems less expressive than it really is.":"接著是酒杯。理想的杯形有寬大的杯肚，往杯口逐漸收窄，有點像鬱金香。寬的部分讓香氣有空間上升，較窄的開口則把香氣聚集起來，直接導向你的鼻子。相反地，在直筒開口的平底杯中，香氣會飄散，烈酒顯得比實際上更沒有表現力。","A consistent method makes your notes comparable over time.":"一致的方法讓你的筆記能隨著時間相互比較。","No stray smells, natural light and a white surface for colour.":"沒有雜味、有自然光，還有用來看顏色的白色表面。","A clean palate (no toothpaste or coffee) and good hydration.":"乾淨的味覺（沒有牙膏或咖啡味）和充足的水分。","A wide bowl narrowing at the top concentrates the aromas.":"寬杯肚、往上收窄的杯子能集中香氣。","The method step by step":"逐步說明品飲方法","Even though the distiller has already diluted it before bottling, a spirit is still a very strong drink. At 40% abv the alcohol stings the nose and warms the mouth, hiding many details. That is why you work with a small sample of about 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon. It gives you everything you need without tiring your senses.":"即使蒸餾師在裝瓶前已經稀釋過，烈酒仍然是非常烈的飲料。在 40% abv 時，酒精會刺鼻並讓口中發熱，掩蓋許多細節。這就是為什麼要使用大約 1.5 cL 的小樣品，大約一湯匙。它能提供你所需的一切，又不會讓感官疲乏。","The route is simple. First you look at the sample and smell it neat. Then you add the same amount of water, another 1.5 cL, which halves its strength. You smell again: aromas the alcohol was hiding often appear, like opening a window in a crowded room. Only then do you move on to tasting.":"流程很簡單。首先觀察樣品，並聞未稀釋的酒。然後加入等量的水，也就是另外 1.5 cL，讓濃度減半。再聞一次：被酒精掩蓋的香氣往往會出現，就像在擁擠的房間裡打開一扇窗。之後才進入品嚐。","In the mouth, you roll the liquid around for a few seconds, look for the flavours and then spit it out. Spitting is not rude: it lets you taste several samples while staying clear-headed and judge the last one as carefully as the first. In short: small sample, eyes and nose, equal water, nose again, palate, spit.":"在口中，讓液體轉動幾秒鐘，尋找風味，然後吐出。吐出並不失禮：它讓你能品嚐多個樣品並保持頭腦清醒，對最後一個樣品的判斷也能和第一個一樣仔細。簡單來說：小樣品、看與聞、加等量的水、再聞、品嚐、吐出。","Small sample: about 1.5 cL.":"小樣品：大約 1.5 cL。","Look and smell before adding any water.":"加水之前先觀察並聞香。","Add an equal amount of water, then smell again.":"加入等量的水，然後再聞一次。","Taste, then spit.":"品嚐，然後吐出。","What to write down":"要記錄什麼","Your notes follow the order of the tasting: eyes, nose, palate. For appearance, colour is all you need. Many unaged spirits are colourless, while those that have spent time in wood range from lemon to gold, amber and brown. Some flavoured products, especially liqueurs, can be vivid: pink, red, green, blue, even black. Colour is a first clue, not proof.":"筆記依照品飲的順序：眼睛、鼻子、口腔。外觀方面，只需要記錄顏色。許多未陳年的烈酒是無色的，而在木桶中待過的則從檸檬黃到金黃、琥珀和棕色都有。有些調味產品，尤其是利口酒，顏色可能很鮮豔：粉紅、紅、綠、藍，甚至黑色。顏色是第一條線索，而不是證據。","On the nose, you first judge intensity: a spirit can be neutral, with almost no smell like many vodkas, or light, medium or pronounced. Then you describe the aromas grouped by where they come from: the raw material, such as fruit or grain; the way it was made; and the oak and maturation, such as vanilla, spice or toasty notes. Asking 'where does this smell come from?' helps you sort your thoughts.":"在香氣方面，首先判斷強度：烈酒可以是中性的，像許多伏特加一樣幾乎沒有氣味，也可以是清淡、中等或濃郁。然後依來源分組描述香氣：原料，例如水果或穀物；製作方式；以及橡木桶和熟成，例如香草、香料或烘烤氣息。問自己「這個氣味從哪裡來？」能幫你整理思緒。","On the palate you find the same groups of flavours, plus two useful observations: how much sugar you can sense and what the texture is like, thin or richer. After spitting, you measure the finish, meaning how long the flavours linger: short, medium or long. Finally, you judge complexity, from neutral to simple, up to very complex when there are many flavours that keep changing.":"在口中，你會找到同樣的風味分組，再加上兩項有用的觀察：能感受到多少糖，以及質地如何，是稀薄還是較豐厚。吐出後，衡量餘韻，也就是風味停留多久：短、中等或長。最後判斷複雜度，從中性到簡單，一直到風味眾多且不斷變化時的非常複雜。","Appearance: colour, from colourless to brown, or vivid shades in flavoured products.":"外觀：顏色，從無色到棕色，或調味產品的鮮豔色調。","Nose: intensity (neutral, light, medium, pronounced) and aromas by source.":"香氣：強度（中性、清淡、中等、濃郁）和依來源分類的香氣。","Aroma sources: raw material, processing, oak and maturation.":"香氣來源：原料、加工、橡木桶和熟成。","Palate: flavours, sugar, texture; then finish (short, medium, long) and complexity.":"口中：風味、糖分、質地；接著是餘韻（短、中等、長）和複雜度。","Good ingredients and the right tools help, but what turns a decent cocktail into a memorable one is balance. Picture two sets of scales. The first weighs the strong part against the weak part; the second weighs sweet against bitter and sour. Together they give four points of balance, and every classic cocktail is built from exactly these four elements.":"好的材料和合適的工具有幫助，但讓一杯不錯的調酒變得令人難忘的，是平衡。想像兩座天平。第一座秤的是強的部分對弱的部分；第二座秤的是甜對苦和酸。兩者加起來就是平衡的四個要點，每一款經典調酒都正是由這四個元素構成的。","The strong part is the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more. It is the heart of the flavour: rum in a Daiquiri, gin in a Martini. Change the spirit and you change the drink. Even switching to another product from the same category alters the result, and replacing the base entirely creates a variation, such as an Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey.":"強的部分是基酒，通常是 40% abv 以上。它是風味的核心：Daiquiri 中的蘭姆酒、Martini 中的琴酒。換了烈酒，飲品也就變了。即使改用同一類別的另一款產品也會改變結果，而完全替換基酒則會產生變化版，例如用蘭姆酒取代威士忌製作的 Old Fashioned。","The weak part softens the power of the alcohol. One source is always there: ice, which melts a little as you stir or shake and adds water. Others are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, cream or milk, sodas, club soda and tonic. Think of a gin and tonic: the gin is the strong part, and the tonic and ice balance it.":"弱的部分讓酒精的力度變得柔和。有一個來源一定存在：冰塊，攪拌或搖盪時會融化一些並加入水分。其他來源是可選的，而且不含酒精：果汁、鮮奶油或牛奶、汽水、蘇打水和通寧水。想想琴通寧：琴酒是強的部分，通寧水和冰塊則平衡它。","Two scales: strong vs weak, and sweet vs bitter and/or sour.":"兩座天平：強對弱，以及甜對苦和／或酸。","Strong = the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more.":"強 = 基酒，通常 40% abv 以上。","Weak = dilution from ice, plus juices, dairy, sodas or tonic.":"弱 = 冰塊帶來的稀釋，加上果汁、乳製品、汽水或通寧水。","Swapping the base spirit creates a variation of the drink.":"替換基酒會產生飲品的變化版。","Sweet versus bitter and sour":"甜對苦與酸","Many cocktails are first sweetened and then 'seasoned' with another ingredient, called a modifier, which brings a bitter note, a sour note or both. Sweetness can come in several forms: sugar, simple syrup (sugar dissolved in water) or a liqueur. Sweetness rounds things off and binds them together, but on its own it tires the palate: a cocktail that is too sweet tastes cloying and heavy.":"許多調酒先加甜，再用另一種材料「調味」，這種材料稱為修飾材料（modifier），它帶來苦味、酸味或兩者兼具。甜味可以有幾種形式：糖、簡易糖漿（溶於水中的糖）或利口酒。甜味讓味道圓潤、把各種元素結合在一起，但單獨存在時會讓味覺疲乏：太甜的調酒喝起來膩口又沉重。","The counterweight is acidity or bitterness. Sourness comes mainly from citrus: a little lime or lemon juice makes the sip lively. Bitterness comes most obviously from cocktail bitters, used by the dash, but also from bitter spirits. It is just like cooking: a pinch of salt or a squeeze of lemon lifts a dish that seemed flat.":"平衡的砝碼是酸度或苦味。酸味主要來自柑橘：一點萊姆或檸檬汁就能讓每一口變得活潑。苦味最明顯的來源是以滴數使用的調酒用苦精，但也來自苦味烈酒。這就像烹飪一樣：一撮鹽或擠一點檸檬汁，就能讓一道平淡的菜變得生動。","A single ingredient can play several roles. Aromatised wines such as vermouth bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity all at once; a liqueur brings both alcohol and sweetness. The goal is a cohesive whole in which no part dominates the others: if the drink tastes only of sugar, lemon or alcohol, it is not balanced yet.":"一種材料可以扮演多個角色。香艾酒等加味葡萄酒同時帶來甜味、苦味和酸度；利口酒則同時帶來酒精和甜味。目標是一個融為一體、沒有任何部分壓過其他部分的整體：如果飲品喝起來只有糖、檸檬或酒精的味道，那就還沒有平衡。","Sweetness comes from sugar, simple syrup or liqueurs.":"甜味來自糖、簡易糖漿或利口酒。","Too sweet = cloying.":"太甜 = 膩口。","The modifier brings sour (citrus) and/or bitter (bitters).":"修飾材料帶來酸（柑橘）和／或苦（苦精）。","Aromatised wines can add sweet, bitter and sour at once.":"加味葡萄酒能同時增添甜、苦和酸。","Short drinks and long drinks":"短飲與長飲","Hundreds of cocktails can look like a maze, but one first split is enough to find your way: short drinks and long drinks. Short drinks have few ingredients and a small volume. Their weak part comes almost entirely from the water released by ice while stirring or shaking; they are then served in a small glass, concentrated and intense.":"數百款調酒看起來可能像一座迷宮，但只要先做一個區分就能找到方向：短飲和長飲。短飲的材料不多，份量也小。它們弱的部分幾乎完全來自攪拌或搖盪時冰塊釋出的水；接著倒入小杯中，濃縮而強烈。","Short drinks include two families: spirit-forward cocktails, where the spirit leads, such as the Manhattan, and short sours, which combine spirit, citrus and sweetness, such as the Daiquiri. Long drinks have a larger volume: their weak part comes from sodas, juices, dairy or other non-alcoholic drinks. This is where highballs and long sours belong.":"短飲包括兩個家族：以烈酒為主角的烈酒主導型調酒，例如 Manhattan；以及結合烈酒、柑橘和甜味的短酸酒，例如 Daiquiri。長飲的份量較大：它們弱的部分來自汽水、果汁、乳製品或其他無酒精飲料。高球和長酸酒就屬於這一類。","An example shows the link. A short gin sour, shaken and served in a small glass, becomes a long drink if you pour it over ice and top it with club soda. The core ingredients stay the same; what changes is the amount of the weak part, and with it the strength, the volume and the moment you might drink it.":"一個例子能說明兩者的關聯。一杯搖盪後倒入小杯的短琴酒酸酒，如果倒在冰塊上並補滿蘇打水，就變成長飲。核心材料保持不變；改變的是弱的部分的份量，連帶改變了濃度、份量，以及適合飲用的時機。","Short drinks: few ingredients, diluted only by ice during mixing.":"短飲：材料少，只靠調製時的冰塊稀釋。","Short families: spirit-forward and short sours.":"短飲家族：烈酒主導型和短酸酒。","Long drinks: bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy.":"長飲：份量較大，以汽水、果汁或乳製品延長。","Long families: highballs and long sours.":"長飲家族：高球和長酸酒。","These are the strongest cocktails, the ones that put the spirit on show. In their simplest form they combine a spirit with sugar and bitters, or a spirit with a liqueur; in more elaborate versions, sweetness and bitterness come from mixes of sugar, aromatised wines and bitters. They are built in the glass or stirred, and the ice both chills and dilutes.":"這些是最烈的調酒，也就是讓烈酒成為焦點的那些。最簡單的形式是烈酒加糖和苦精，或烈酒加利口酒；較講究的版本中，甜味和苦味來自糖、加味葡萄酒和苦精的組合。它們以直調或攪拌製作，冰塊同時負責冰鎮和稀釋。","The Old Fashioned is the template: American whiskey, a sugar cube and Angostura bitters. The Manhattan uses rye or Bourbon with the same bitters, but swaps the sugar for sweet red vermouth, which makes it more complex. The Sazerac starts from Cognac or rye, with sugar, Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe. The Rusty Nail is the simplest: Scotch whisky and Drambuie, a liqueur.":"Old Fashioned 是範本：美國威士忌、一顆方糖和 Angostura 苦精。Manhattan 使用黑麥威士忌或 Bourbon 和同樣的苦精，但把糖換成甜紅香艾酒，讓它更有層次。Sazerac 以 Cognac 或黑麥威士忌為起點，加上糖、Peychaud's 苦精和一點苦艾酒。Rusty Nail 最簡單：Scotch 威士忌和利口酒 Drambuie。","Gin gives two great classics. The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth, which on its own provides both the sweet and the bitter note. The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari, a red bitter spirit: three ingredients, three clear roles. Finally, adding cream to this kind of drink creates the Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander.":"琴酒造就了兩款偉大的經典調酒。Martini 把琴酒與不甜香艾酒搭配在一起，香艾酒單獨就提供了甜味和苦味。Negroni 結合琴酒、甜紅香艾酒和紅色苦味烈酒 Campari：三種材料，三個明確的角色。最後，在這類飲品中加入鮮奶油，就產生了 Alexander 家族，例如 Brandy Alexander。","Spirit-forward: the strongest drinks, built or stirred.":"烈酒主導型：最烈的飲品，以直調或攪拌製作。","Old Fashioned and Manhattan: whiskey and Angostura; the Manhattan adds sweet vermouth.":"Old Fashioned 和 Manhattan：威士忌和 Angostura；Manhattan 加了甜香艾酒。","Sazerac: Cognac or rye, Peychaud's and absinthe; Rusty Nail: Scotch and Drambuie.":"Sazerac：Cognac 或黑麥威士忌、Peychaud's 和苦艾酒；Rusty Nail：Scotch 和 Drambuie。","Martini: gin and dry vermouth; Negroni: gin, sweet vermouth, Campari. With cream: Alexander.":"Martini：琴酒和不甜香艾酒；Negroni：琴酒、甜香艾酒、Campari。加鮮奶油：Alexander。","Short sours":"短酸酒","The short sour rests on a trio: strong, sour, sweet. The basic recipe is a spirit, a citrus juice and an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup. These drinks are shaken: the shaker chills, mixes, dilutes a little and gives a light, airy, almost frothy texture. It is the family behind a huge number of successful cocktails.":"短酸酒建立在三重奏上：強、酸、甜。基本酒譜是一種烈酒、一種柑橘汁，以及簡易糖漿這類無調味甜味劑。這些飲品以搖盪製作：雪克杯能冰鎮、混合、稍微稀釋，並帶來輕盈、充滿空氣、幾乎起泡的質地。這個家族造就了為數眾多的成功調酒。","Three classics show the pure pattern. The Daiquiri: rum, lime and simple syrup. The Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye, lemon and syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. The Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and syrup, plus one egg white and a dash of bitters. Here the egg white is essential: it creates a foam head and a silky texture. Many bars now use aquafaba, the water chickpeas are cooked in, as a vegan alternative.":"三款經典調酒展現了純粹的模式。Daiquiri：蘭姆酒、萊姆和簡易糖漿。Whiskey Sour：Bourbon 或黑麥威士忌、檸檬和糖漿，可選擇加蛋白和苦精。Pisco Sour：Pisco、萊姆和糖漿，再加一顆蛋白和幾滴苦精。在這裡蛋白不可或缺：它形成泡沫層和絲滑的質地。如今許多酒吧使用鷹嘴豆水（aquafaba，煮鷹嘴豆的水）作為純素替代品。","Variations change the sweetener, the sour ingredient or both. In the Sidecar, Cognac meets lemon and triple sec, an orange liqueur that replaces the syrup. The Margarita uses tequila, lime and triple sec, with an optional salt rim. The Clover Club brings together gin, lemon and raspberry syrup, with egg white and optionally a little vermouth: the same pattern, a completely different colour.":"變化版會改變甜味劑、酸味材料，或兩者都改。在 Sidecar 中，Cognac 遇上檸檬和 triple sec，這種柳橙利口酒取代了糖漿。Margarita 使用 Tequila、萊姆和 triple sec，可選擇加鹽邊。Clover Club 結合了琴酒、檸檬和覆盆子糖漿，加上蛋白，並可選擇加一點香艾酒：同樣的模式，完全不同的顏色。","Short sour = spirit + citrus + sweetener, shaken.":"短酸酒 = 烈酒 + 柑橘 + 甜味劑，搖盪而成。","Daiquiri: rum and lime; Whiskey Sour: whiskey and lemon; Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and egg white.":"Daiquiri：蘭姆酒和萊姆；Whiskey Sour：威士忌和檸檬；Pisco Sour：Pisco、萊姆和蛋白。","Egg white: foam and a silky texture; vegan alternative: aquafaba.":"蛋白：泡沫和絲滑質地；純素替代品：鷹嘴豆水（aquafaba）。","Variations: Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (gin, raspberry).":"變化版：Sidecar（Cognac）、Margarita（Tequila）、Clover Club（琴酒、覆盆子）。","Highballs":"高球","The highball is the simplest of all mixed drinks: a spirit and a non-alcoholic mixer, served long over cubed ice. Gin and tonic, vodka and tonic, whisky and soda are examples almost everyone knows without realising they form a family. The rule is clear: little work, plenty of volume, and the weak part handed over to the mixer.":"高球是所有混合飲料中最簡單的：一種烈酒加一種無酒精調和飲料，加入方塊冰做成長飲。琴通寧、伏特加通寧、威士忌蘇打，幾乎人人都知道這些例子，卻沒發現它們屬於同一個家族。規則很明確：工夫少、份量多，弱的部分交給調和飲料。","Some highballs have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice: the slightly bitter, sour juice acts as the modifier. These are summer-afternoon drinks, easy to make at home with ingredients found anywhere, yet built on the same logic of balance as more complex cocktails.":"有些高球有自己的名字。Cuba Libre 是蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆。Greyhound 是伏特加和葡萄柚汁：微苦帶酸的果汁扮演修飾材料的角色。這些是夏日午後的飲品，用隨處可得的材料就能在家輕鬆調製，卻和更複雜的調酒建立在同樣的平衡邏輯上。","Other highballs add a detail. The Horse's Neck combines Cognac, ginger ale and bitters: a highball with a bitter accent on top of spirit and mixer. The Americano has a split base: its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet red vermouth together, topped with club soda. Lighter than a Negroni, it is almost a lengthened version of it without the gin.":"其他高球會多加一個細節。Horse's Neck 結合了 Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精：在烈酒和調和飲料之上再加一點苦味點綴的高球。Americano 有分拆基底：它的酒精部分是 Campari 和甜紅香艾酒兩者合起來，再補滿蘇打水。它比 Negroni 清淡，幾乎就是去掉琴酒、延長版的 Negroni。","Highball: spirit + non-alcoholic mixer, served long over ice.":"高球：烈酒 + 無酒精調和飲料，加冰做成長飲。","Cuba Libre: rum, cola and lime. Greyhound: vodka and grapefruit juice.":"Cuba Libre：蘭姆酒、可樂和萊姆。Greyhound：伏特加和葡萄柚汁。","Horse's Neck: Cognac, ginger ale and bitters.":"Horse's Neck：Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精。","Americano: split base of Campari and sweet vermouth, plus club soda.":"Americano：Campari 和甜香艾酒的分拆基底，加上蘇打水。","Long sours":"長酸酒","The long sour covers several sub-families: Collinses, Slings and sparkling sours. In its simplest form it is a short sour made long with club soda. The Tom Collins is the perfect example: gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, poured over ice and topped with soda. It is refreshing and thirst-quenching, and shows clearly how one recipe can change its outfit.":"長酸酒涵蓋幾個子家族：Collins、Sling 和氣泡酸酒。最簡單的形式就是用蘇打水延長的短酸酒。Tom Collins 是完美的例子：琴酒、檸檬汁和簡易糖漿，倒在冰塊上並補滿蘇打水。它清爽解渴，清楚展現了一個酒譜如何換上新裝。","Instead of club soda you can use a flavoured soda or Champagne. The Paloma combines tequila and lime with a Mexican-style grapefruit soda, which brings sweetness and bubbles at once; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water are used. The French 75 starts from Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup, and is topped with Champagne: an elegant sparkling sour.":"除了蘇打水，也可以使用有風味的汽水或 Champagne。Paloma 結合 Tequila 和萊姆，以及墨西哥風格的葡萄柚汽水，同時帶來甜味和氣泡；也可以改用葡萄柚汁和蘇打水。French 75 以 Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬和簡易糖漿為起點，再補上 Champagne：一款優雅的氣泡酸酒。","Some long sours are enriched with extra ingredients. The Mojito stays simple: rum, lime and sugar or syrup, with mint leaves that make it fresh and fragrant. The Singapore Sling is more complex: gin and lime, sweetened with a cherry liqueur and a herbal liqueur, with a dash of Angostura bitters and a final top of club soda.":"有些長酸酒會加入額外的材料。Mojito 保持簡單：蘭姆酒、萊姆和糖或糖漿，加上讓它清新芬芳的薄荷葉。Singapore Sling 則較複雜：琴酒和萊姆，以櫻桃利口酒和草本利口酒加甜，再加幾滴 Angostura 苦精，最後補滿蘇打水。","Long sour = a lengthened short sour; sub-families: Collins, Sling, sparkling sour.":"長酸酒 = 延長的短酸酒；子家族：Collins、Sling、氣泡酸酒。","Tom Collins: gin, lemon, syrup, club soda.":"Tom Collins：琴酒、檸檬、糖漿、蘇打水。","Paloma: tequila, lime, grapefruit soda. French 75: Cognac or gin, lemon, syrup, Champagne.":"Paloma：Tequila、萊姆、葡萄柚汽水。French 75：Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬、糖漿、Champagne。","Mojito: rum, lime, sugar and mint. Singapore Sling: gin, lime, liqueurs, bitters, soda.":"Mojito：蘭姆酒、萊姆、糖和薄荷。Singapore Sling：琴酒、萊姆、利口酒、苦精、蘇打水。","Spirit":"烈酒","An alcoholic drink whose strength has been raised by distillation.":"經由蒸餾提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料。","The four steps":"四個步驟","Raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation.":"原料、發酵、蒸餾、蒸餾後處理。","Alcohol by volume: 40% abv means 40% of the liquid is alcohol.":"酒精濃度（alcohol by volume）：40% abv 表示液體的 40% 是酒精。","What does yeast do?":"酵母做什麼？","Eats sugar, making ethanol, carbon dioxide and fruity aromas.":"吃掉糖，產生乙醇、二氧化碳和果香。","Strength after fermentation":"發酵後的濃度","Usually 8–10% abv.":"通常 8–10% abv。","Distillation strength and aroma":"蒸餾濃度與香氣","Lower strength = more aroma; higher strength = less; 96% = neutral.":"濃度越低 = 香氣越多；濃度越高 = 越少；96% = 中性。","Batch process, usually twice; low strength, lots of character.":"批次運作，通常蒸餾兩次；濃度低，個性十足。","Column still":"柱式蒸餾器","Continuous; short = flavourful, tall = light, tallest = neutral at 95–96%.":"連續運作；矮 = 風味豐富，高 = 清淡，最高 = 95–96% 的中性烈酒。","Always colourless and dry, with no sugar.":"一定是無色、不甜的，不含糖。","New oak barrel":"新橡木桶","Never used: gives the most colour and aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut).":"從未使用過：帶來最多顏色和香氣（香草、香料、椰子）。","Old oak barrel":"舊橡木桶","Already used: gives less aroma, and less again with each reuse.":"已經用過：帶來的香氣較少，每重複使用一次就再少一些。","Combining barrels for bottle-to-bottle consistency and for complexity.":"結合不同酒桶，讓每瓶酒保持一致並增添複雜度。","Caramel colouring":"焦糖色","Evens out batch colour; used properly, not sweet and adds no aroma.":"統一各批次的顏色；正確使用時不甜，也不增添香氣。","Where does sweetness come from?":"甜味從哪裡來？","Always added after distillation, usually as sugar.":"一定是在蒸餾後添加，通常是糖。","Final step: pure water, usually down to 40% abv; adds no flavour.":"最後一步：純水，通常降到 40% abv；不增添風味。","Grape brandy":"葡萄白蘭地","Distilled wine; Cognac is the most famous example.":"蒸餾過的葡萄酒；Cognac 是最著名的例子。","Where does Cognac come from?":"Cognac 來自哪裡？","Cognac distillation":"Cognac 的蒸餾","By law: twice in a pot still.":"依法規：在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次。","Cognac minimum ageing":"Cognac 的最低陳年","At least 2 years in oak; gives vanilla and toast.":"在橡木桶中至少 2 年；帶來香草和烘烤風味。","Youngest spirit: at least 2 years old.":"最年輕的烈酒：至少 2 年。","Youngest spirit: at least 4 years old.":"最年輕的烈酒：至少 4 年。","Youngest spirit: at least 10 years old.":"最年輕的烈酒：至少 10 年。","What defines vodka?":"什麼定義了伏特加？","Distillation strength; raw material and place are open.":"蒸餾濃度；原料和產地都不受限。","At least 95% or 96% abv, column-distilled; almost no aroma.":"至少 95% 或 96% abv，以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾；幾乎沒有香氣。","Premium vodka raw materials":"高級伏特加的原料","Cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes.":"穀物（大麥、小麥、黑麥）和馬鈴薯。","Vodka after distillation":"蒸餾後的伏特加","Unaged; usually diluted to 40% abv.":"未陳年；通常稀釋到 40% abv。","Vodka with some character":"帶點個性的伏特加","Faint raw-material notes, yet still neutral.":"帶淡淡的原料氣息，但仍是中性。","Barley sprouts and makes enzymes; hot air then stops the growth.":"大麥發芽並產生酵素；接著用熱空氣停止生長。","What do barley enzymes do?":"大麥的酵素做什麼？","In water, they turn the grain's starch into sugar yeast can ferment.":"在水中把穀物的澱粉轉化為酵母能發酵的糖。","Scotch: the basic rule":"Scotch：基本規定","Distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"在蘇格蘭蒸餾，並在當地陳年至少三年。","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery.":"100% 麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠。","Fuel burned while heating malted barley; gives smoke to a few Single Malts.":"烘乾麥芽大麥時燃燒的燃料；為少數 Single Malt 帶來煙燻味。","Grain whisky":"穀物威士忌","Malted barley plus other grains, column-distilled: light, smooth, rarely sold alone.":"麥芽大麥加其他穀物，以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾：清淡、柔順，很少單獨販售。","Malt plus grain whiskies from different distilleries; usually smoother.":"來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌加穀物威士忌；通常較柔順。","Bourbon: grain rule":"Bourbon：穀物規定","At least 51% corn, usually with some barley and rye.":"至少 51% 玉米，通常加一些大麥和黑麥。","Bourbon: barrels":"Bourbon：酒桶","New charred oak: vanilla, coconut and deep colour.":"炙燒過的新橡木桶：香草、椰子和深邃的顏色。","Where is Bourbon made?":"Bourbon 在哪裡生產？","Anywhere in the USA; Kentucky is the leading state.":"美國任何地方；肯塔基州是主要產地。","Like Bourbon, but made only in Tennessee and maple-charcoal filtered before the barrel.":"和 Bourbon 一樣，但只在田納西州生產，並在入桶前以楓木炭過濾。","American Rye whiskey":"美國 Rye 威士忌","Made like Bourbon but with at least 51% rye: spicy and peppery.":"製法和 Bourbon 相同，但至少 51% 黑麥：辛香、帶胡椒味。","Mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth; sometimes unmalted barley.":"大多是壺式 + 柱式的調和，清淡柔順；有時使用未發芽的大麥。","Canadian whisky":"加拿大威士忌","Many grains, high- and low-strength blend; rye is the signature.":"多種穀物，高濃度與低濃度烈酒的調和；黑麥是招牌。","Scottish model: malts and blends, traditionally elegant and refined.":"蘇格蘭模式：麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌，傳統上優雅而細緻。","Black, sticky sugar by-product; mixed with water; gives caramel and brown sugar.":"黑色黏稠的製糖副產品；與水混合；帶來焦糖和紅糖風味。","Cane-juice rum":"甘蔗汁蘭姆酒","Fresh juice fermented at once: very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour.":"新鮮汁液立刻發酵：非常明顯的青草、草本風味。","Cane juice, short column; in the Caribbean, only Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"甘蔗汁、矮蒸餾柱；在加勒比海，只限馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普。","Jamaican rum":"牙買加蘭姆酒","Known for intense tropical fruit aromas created during fermentation.":"以發酵時產生的濃郁熱帶水果香氣聞名。","Light rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico":"古巴和波多黎各的清淡蘭姆酒","Tall columns, high strength: light aroma.":"高蒸餾柱、高濃度：香氣清淡。","Charcoal filtering in rum":"蘭姆酒的木炭過濾","Removes oak colour, giving a white rum even after ageing.":"去除橡木桶的顏色，即使陳年過也能得到白色蘭姆酒。","Sweetened rum":"加甜的蘭姆酒","Common in Central and South America; not allowed in some countries.":"在中南美洲很常見；在某些國家不被允許。","Blue agave core":"藍色龍舌蘭心","Leaves cut off; cooked in ovens to create sugars, then crushed.":"切除葉片；在窯爐中烹煮以產生糖，然後壓碎。","Tequila vs Tequila 100% agave":"Tequila 與 Tequila 100% agave","At least 51% agave sugars, or agave sugars only.":"至少 51% 的龍舌蘭糖分，或只用龍舌蘭糖分。","Twice in pot stills to a low strength: lots of agave character.":"在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，到較低濃度：龍舌蘭個性十足。","Unaged and colourless: agave at its purest.":"未陳年、無色：最純粹的龍舌蘭。","Unaged; colour from caramel, texture softened by additives.":"未陳年；顏色來自焦糖色，口感以添加物變柔和。","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak. Añejo: at least 12 months.":"Reposado：在橡木桶中 2–12 個月。Añejo：至少 12 個月。","Botanicals":"植物性原料","Natural flavouring ingredients: fruits, seeds, herbs and spices.":"天然調味原料：水果、種子、香草和香料。","Neutral spirit and botanicals distilled together in a pot still: flavoured, colourless.":"中性烈酒與植物性原料一起在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾：有風味、無色。","Botanicals steeped for days or months; give flavour and colour. Heat speeds it up.":"植物性原料浸泡數天或數月；帶來風味和顏色。加熱能加快速度。","Flavoured spirit led by juniper; usually colourless and unaged.":"以杜松子為主導的調味烈酒；通常無色、未陳年。","Flavours added by redistillation. Can be made anywhere, not just London.":"風味以再蒸餾加入。可以在任何地方製作，不限倫敦。","Bitter spirit":"苦味烈酒","At least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange); bitterness felt only on the palate.":"至少一種苦味植物性原料（龍膽、奎寧、苦橙）；苦味只在口中感受得到。","Very concentrated and very bitter; never drunk alone, a few drops add complexity.":"非常濃縮、非常苦；從不單喝，幾滴就能增添複雜度。","Flavoured, sweetened spirit with a legal minimum sweetness; often coloured.":"經調味並加甜的烈酒，有法定最低甜度；常經過上色。","Aromatised wine":"加味葡萄酒","Base wine + flavourings with a bitter + sugar + a little spirit.":"基酒 + 帶苦味的調味料 + 糖 + 少量烈酒。","Why add spirit?":"為什麼要加烈酒？","To raise alcohol and extend shelf life, even after opening.":"提高酒精濃度並延長保存期限，即使開瓶後也一樣。","White wine base flavoured with wormwood; France and Italy.":"以苦艾調味的白葡萄酒基底；法國和義大利。","‘Dry’ vermouth":"「Dry」香艾酒","Nearly always has added sugar, just less than red.":"幾乎都有添加的糖，只是比紅香艾酒少。","Red vermouth colour":"紅香艾酒的顏色","Usually from caramel, as the base is a white wine.":"通常來自焦糖色，因為基酒是白葡萄酒。","Sample size for tasting a spirit":"品飲烈酒的樣品份量","About 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon.":"大約 1.5 cL，大約一湯匙。","How much water to add?":"要加多少水？","The same amount as the sample, after the first look and sniff.":"與樣品等量，在第一次觀察和聞香之後加入。","Ideal tasting glass":"理想的品飲杯","Wide bowl narrowing at the top, to concentrate the aromas.":"寬杯肚、往上收窄，用來集中香氣。","Nose intensity levels":"香氣強度等級","Neutral, light, medium, pronounced.":"中性、清淡、中等、濃郁。","Two palate observations besides flavours":"風味之外的兩項口中觀察","Sugar level and the texture of the liquid.":"含糖量和液體的質地。","The four points of balance":"平衡的四個要點","Strong, weak, sweet, bitter and/or sour.":"強、弱、甜、苦和／或酸。","Sugar dissolved in water: an unflavoured sweetener.":"溶於水中的糖：一種無調味的甜味劑。","Modifier":"修飾材料","Ingredient that balances sweetness with bitter and/or sour, like citrus or bitters.":"以苦和／或酸平衡甜味的材料，例如柑橘或苦精。","Short drink":"短飲","Few ingredients, diluted by ice when stirred or shaken.":"材料少，攪拌或搖盪時由冰塊稀釋。","Long drink":"長飲","Bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy.":"份量較大，以汽水、果汁或乳製品延長。","Whiskey (usually Bourbon), sugar cube, Angostura bitters.":"威士忌（通常是 Bourbon）、方糖、Angostura 苦精。","Rye or Bourbon, sweet red vermouth, Angostura bitters.":"黑麥威士忌或 Bourbon、甜紅香艾酒、Angostura 苦精。","Example of the Alexander family: a spirit-forward drink with cream added.":"Alexander 家族的例子：加了鮮奶油的烈酒主導型飲品。","Bourbon or rye, lemon, simple syrup; optional egg white and bitters.":"Bourbon 或黑麥威士忌、檸檬、簡易糖漿；可選擇加蛋白和苦精。","Chickpea cooking water: a vegan alternative to egg white for foam.":"煮鷹嘴豆的水：取代蛋白製造泡沫的純素選擇。","The simplest mixed drink: spirit and mixer, served long over cubed ice.":"最簡單的混合飲料：烈酒加調和飲料，加入方塊冰做成長飲。","Highball of rum and cola with lime.":"蘭姆酒加可樂和萊姆的高球。","Cognac or gin, lemon, simple syrup, topped with Champagne.":"Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬、簡易糖漿，再補上 Champagne。","Gin, lime, cherry and herbal liqueurs, Angostura bitters, club soda.":"琴酒、萊姆、櫻桃和草本利口酒、Angostura 苦精、蘇打水。","Long sour sub-families":"長酸酒的子家族","Collins, Sling and sparkling sour.":"Collins、Sling 和氣泡酸酒。","Spirit families":"烈酒家族","Flavoured spirits and aromatised wines":"調味烈酒與加味葡萄酒","Tasting and cocktails":"品飲與調酒","The four steps of every spirit":"每款烈酒的四個步驟","Every spirit, from vodka to Cognac, follows the same four steps. First a plant raw material is turned into a sugary liquid. Then yeast ferments it into alcohol. Distillation makes that alcohol stronger. Finally the producer decides what to do with the new spirit: age it, flavour it, sweeten it, colour it and dilute it.":"每款烈酒，從伏特加到 Cognac，都遵循同樣的四個步驟。首先把植物原料變成含糖液體。接著由酵母將它發酵成酒精。蒸餾讓酒精變得更濃。最後由生產者決定如何處理新烈酒：陳年、調味、加甜、上色和稀釋。","After the still":"蒸餾之後","A sugary liquid from a plant":"來自植物的含糖液體","Fermentation needs sugar, so step one is to get a sugary liquid from a plant. Grapes and sugar cane already contain sugar that is easy to extract. Cereals contain none: they must be processed to create it. Whatever the plant, it leaves its signature, because each raw material brings its own aromas to the spirit.":"發酵需要糖，所以第一步是從植物取得含糖液體。葡萄和甘蔗本身就含有容易萃取的糖。穀物則不含糖：必須經過處理才能產生糖。不論是哪種植物，都會留下印記，因為每種原料都為烈酒帶來自己的香氣。","sugar ready":"現成的糖","starch: must convert":"澱粉：必須轉化","sugary liquid":"含糖液體","Fermentation makes the alcohol":"發酵產生酒精","Yeasts are tiny living organisms. They feed on the sugar and leave behind ethanol, the alcohol the distiller wants, and carbon dioxide, a gas that escapes. The fermented liquid usually reaches 8 to 10% abv, about the strength of a strong beer. Yeasts also create new aromas, especially fruity ones.":"酵母是微小的生物。它們以糖為食，留下乙醇（蒸餾師想要的酒精）和二氧化碳（一種會散逸的氣體）。發酵液通常達到 8% 到 10% abv，大約是烈性啤酒的濃度。酵母也會產生新的香氣，尤其是果香。","yeast + sugar":"酵母 + 糖","ethanol + CO₂":"乙醇 + CO₂","+ fruity aromas":"+ 果香","Ethanol boils before water":"乙醇比水先沸騰","Distillation relies on one simple fact: ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water. Heat the fermented liquid and the vapour rising from it is richer in alcohol than the liquid left behind. Collect that vapour and cool it, and it turns back into a liquid stronger than the one you started with.":"蒸餾依據的是一個簡單的事實：乙醇的沸點比水低。加熱發酵液，升起的蒸氣所含的酒精比留下的液體更多。收集這些蒸氣並冷卻，它就會變回比原本更烈的液體。","ethanol: boils first":"乙醇：先沸騰","water: boils later":"水：後沸騰","cooled vapour":"冷卻的蒸氣","stronger":"更烈","Low strength, more aroma":"低濃度，更多香氣","Fresh from the still, a spirit can range from about 60% to 96% abv, and that strength shapes its flavour. The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas. The higher it goes, the less aroma survives. At 96% there is almost nothing left to smell: the spirit is called neutral.":"剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒，濃度可以從大約 60% 到 96% abv，而這個濃度會塑造它的風味。濃度越低，香氣越濃郁。濃度越高，留下的香氣越少。到了 96%，幾乎沒有東西可以聞了：這種烈酒被稱為中性。","intense aromas":"濃郁的香氣","high strength":"高濃度","A pot still always has three parts: a pot on a heat source, a condenser, and a pipe linking the two. The liquid boils in the pot, the vapour climbs the still head and passes into the condenser, where a coiled tube in cold water turns it back into liquid. Many are steam-heated today; Cognac stills use gas burners.":"壺式蒸餾器一定有三個部分：放在熱源上的蒸餾鍋、冷凝器，以及連接兩者的管子。液體在蒸餾鍋中沸騰，蒸氣沿著蒸餾器頂部上升並進入冷凝器，泡在冷水中的盤管會把蒸氣變回液體。如今許多蒸餾器以蒸汽加熱；Cognac 的蒸餾器則使用瓦斯爐火。","pot + heat":"蒸餾鍋 + 熱源","linking pipe":"連接管","condenser":"冷凝器","In batches, and twice":"批次運作，而且兩次","A pot still works in batches, like a washing machine: fill it, run the cycle, then empty and clean it before the next load. One pass is not enough, so most distillers run it twice: from about 10% abv to about 25%, then to about 75%. The result has medium to pronounced aromas and lots of character, but is never neutral.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，就像洗衣機：裝滿、運轉一個循環，然後在下一批之前清空並清洗。蒸餾一次不夠，所以大多數蒸餾師會蒸餾兩次：從約 10% abv 到約 25%，再到約 75%。成果的香氣中等至濃郁，個性十足，但絕不會是中性。","one batch at a time":"一次一批","fermented":"發酵液","1st distillation":"第一次蒸餾","2nd distillation":"第二次蒸餾","never neutral":"絕不中性","The column still was designed to run without stopping and to reach high strengths. It is a vertical structure divided into many sections. Hot vapour rises while liquid flows down: it is like many distillations stacked on top of one another, all happening at once. The strongest spirit is at the top, and that is where it leaves the still.":"柱式蒸餾器的設計目的是不停運轉，並達到高濃度。它是分成許多層的直立式結構。熱蒸氣上升，液體往下流：就像許多次蒸餾疊在一起，全部同時進行。最烈的烈酒在頂部，也從那裡離開蒸餾器。","steam":"蒸汽","vapour rises":"蒸氣上升","liquid flows down":"液體下流","strongest at the top":"頂部最烈","continuous":"連續運作","Short or tall column":"矮蒸餾柱或高蒸餾柱","Not all columns are alike. A short column with few sections gives a lower-strength spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, close to a pot still spirit. A tall column with many sections gives a light spirit, and the very tallest reach 95 to 96% abv: a neutral spirit with almost no smell, the base of most vodkas.":"蒸餾柱並非都一樣。層數少的矮蒸餾柱得到的是濃度較低、香氣中等或濃郁的烈酒，接近壺式蒸餾器的烈酒。層數多的高蒸餾柱得到清淡的烈酒，而最高的能達到 95% 到 96% abv：幾乎沒有氣味的中性烈酒，也就是大多數伏特加的基底。","flavourful":"風味豐富","tall column":"高蒸餾柱","light → neutral":"清淡 → 中性","A spirit's flavour is built step by step. The raw material lays the foundation: grapes bring fruity and floral notes, agave herbal and peppery ones. Fermentation adds more aromas, mostly fruity. Distillation then decides how much survives: at a low strength the aromas stay intense, at a very high strength they almost vanish.":"烈酒的風味是一步一步建立起來的。原料打下基礎：葡萄帶來果香和花香，龍舌蘭帶來草本和胡椒氣息。發酵增添更多香氣，主要是果香。接著由蒸餾決定能留下多少：濃度低時香氣保持濃郁，濃度極高時香氣幾乎消失。","Distillation strength":"蒸餾濃度","fruity · herbal":"果香 · 草本","+ fruity":"+ 果香","low = intense":"低 = 濃郁","Colourless, dry, and three routes":"無色、不甜，以及三條路","Whatever its origin, a spirit leaves the still colourless and dry, meaning with no sugar. The producer then takes one of three routes, often set by law: keep it unaged, briefly in stainless steel; age it in oak barrels, usually for years; or flavour it with something other than wood, as happens with gin.":"不論來源為何，烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是無色、不甜的，也就是不含糖。生產者接著會走上三條路之一，這通常由法律決定：保持未陳年，在不鏽鋼中短暫存放；在橡木桶中陳年，通常長達數年；或用木頭以外的東西調味，例如琴酒。","oak-aged":"橡木桶陳年","flavoured":"調味","often set by law":"常由法律決定","Steel or oak: colour":"不鏽鋼或橡木桶：顏色","Stainless steel gives nothing away: an unaged spirit stays clear and keeps the aromas born in the still. Oak does real work. It adds colour in a sequence that runs from lemon to gold, then amber and, very rarely, brown. The newer the barrel and the longer the stay, the deeper the colour.":"不鏽鋼不會釋出任何東西：未陳年的烈酒保持清澈，並保留在蒸餾器中誕生的香氣。橡木桶則會真正發揮作用。它依序增添顏色：從檸檬黃到金黃，再到琥珀色，極少數會變成棕色。桶越新、待得越久，顏色就越深。","adds nothing":"什麼都不增添","adds colour":"增添顏色","New barrel, used barrel":"新桶，舊桶","Oak also brings aromas: vanilla, cinnamon, cloves and coconut. A new barrel, never used before, gives a lot of them. A used barrel gives less, and a little less again with every refill, just like a tea bag steeped several times. New barrels mean a strong oak imprint; used ones a gentler touch.":"橡木桶也會帶來香氣：香草、肉桂、丁香和椰子。從未使用過的新桶會帶來大量香氣。用過的桶帶來的較少，每重新裝填一次就再少一點，就像泡過好幾次的茶包。新桶代表強烈的橡木印記；舊桶則是較溫和的影響。","new barrel":"新桶","cinnamon":"肉桂","used barrel":"舊桶","Time concentrates":"時間帶來濃縮","Time matters too. Through the wood, water and ethanol slowly evaporate, so what remains becomes more concentrated. After many years, sometimes decades, new aromas appear: fruit cake, dried fruit, leather and wood polish. That is why a long-aged spirit feels layered, revealing one shade of flavour after another.":"時間也很重要。水和乙醇會透過木頭慢慢蒸發，剩下的部分就變得更濃縮。經過許多年，有時是數十年，會出現新的香氣：水果蛋糕、果乾、皮革和木頭亮光蠟。這就是為什麼長期陳年的烈酒感覺層次豐富，風味的細微變化一層接著一層展現。","evaporation":"蒸發","years":"年","fruit cake":"水果蛋糕","wood polish":"木頭亮光蠟","Blending: consistency and complexity":"調和：一致性與複雜度","Every barrel is its own little world: two barrels filled on the same day never turn out exactly alike. So the blender combines many barrels, with two aims. Consistency: the same bottle should taste the same every time. Complexity: bringing together spirits with different characters is the easiest way to create depth.":"每個酒桶都是一個獨特的小世界：同一天裝填的兩個桶，結果永遠不會完全相同。所以調和師會結合許多酒桶，有兩個目的。一致性：同一瓶酒每次喝起來都應該一樣。複雜度：把不同個性的烈酒結合在一起，是創造深度最簡單的方法。","consistency":"一致性","complexity":"複雜度","Three ways to add flavour":"增添風味的三種方法","Flavours other than wood can be added in three ways. The spirit can be redistilled with herbs, seeds or spices: it comes out flavoured but colourless. The plants can soak in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, so flavour and colour seep out slowly. Or ready-made flavourings, natural or artificial, are simply added.":"木頭以外的風味可以用三種方式加入。烈酒可以與香草、種子或香料一起再蒸餾：得到有風味但無色的液體。植物可以浸泡在烈酒中，就像冷泡花草茶，讓風味和顏色慢慢滲出。或者直接加入天然或人工的現成調味料。","redistillation":"再蒸餾","added flavourings":"添加調味料","The last move before bottling is almost always dilution. Completely pure water is added, and most spirits come down to 40% abv. The reason is practical: alcohol that is too strong numbs the palate, so the spirit cannot be tasted or enjoyed. The water adds no aroma; it simply lowers the strength.":"裝瓶前的最後一步幾乎都是稀釋。加入完全純淨的水，大多數烈酒會降到 40% abv。原因很實際：太烈的酒精會麻痺味覺，讓人無法品嚐或享受烈酒。水不會增添香氣，只是降低濃度。","before":"之前","pure water":"純水","bottled":"裝瓶","Sweetness is added":"甜味是添加的","Every spirit leaves the still dry, so any sweetness you taste was added afterwards, usually as sugar. Careful with the word: sweet refers only to the taste of sugar. A whiskey with vanilla and fruity aromas may smell sweet, but with no added sugar it is still dry on the palate.":"每款烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的，所以你嚐到的任何甜味都是之後添加的，通常是糖。小心這個詞：「甜」只指糖的味道。一款帶有香草和果香的威士忌聞起來可能很甜美，但沒有加糖，在口中仍然是不甜的。","added sugar":"添加的糖","smells of vanilla":"聞起來有香草味","but tastes dry":"但喝起來不甜","Colour does not prove age":"顏色不能證明年份","Colour has several sources. Oak is the most natural. Caramel is used in tiny amounts to keep every batch the same shade; used properly it adds no sweetness or aroma. Many liqueurs get natural or artificial colourings, sometimes very bright. So colour is no proof of age: an unaged spirit can be deeply coloured.":"顏色有幾種來源。橡木桶是最天然的。焦糖色以極少量使用，讓每一批的色調保持一致；正確使用時不會增添甜味或香氣。許多利口酒會加入天然或人工色素，有時非常鮮豔。所以顏色不能證明年份：未陳年的烈酒也可能顏色很深。","colourings":"色素","years in oak":"在橡木桶中的年數","A grape brandy with an address":"有地址的葡萄白蘭地","A grape brandy is simply distilled wine, and Cognac is the most famous of them all. It comes from a clearly defined area of south-west France, north of the town of Bordeaux. Only grapes grown there can become Cognac: the name is a precise address, not a recipe that can be copied elsewhere.":"葡萄白蘭地就是蒸餾過的葡萄酒，而 Cognac 是其中最有名的。它來自法國西南部、Bordeaux 市以北一個明確劃定的產區。只有在那裡種植的葡萄才能成為 Cognac：這個名稱是一個精確的地址，而不是可以在別處複製的配方。","south-west":"西南部","north of Bordeaux":"Bordeaux 以北","First of all, a wine":"首先，它是一款葡萄酒","The grapes from this area give Cognac its basic aromas, fruity and floral. After harvest they are pressed, and the sugary juice needs no complicated processing: it is fermented straight away. The result is a wine, and it is this wine, not the grapes, that goes into the still. Before it is a spirit, Cognac is a wine.":"這個產區的葡萄為 Cognac 帶來基本的香氣：果香和花香。採收後葡萄被壓榨，含糖的汁液不需要複雜的處理：立刻就能發酵。結果就是葡萄酒，而進入蒸餾器的正是這款葡萄酒，而不是葡萄。在成為烈酒之前，Cognac 是一款葡萄酒。","fruity, floral":"果香、花香","fermented at once":"立刻發酵","For Cognac the law leaves no choice: the wine must be distilled twice in a pot still, with no column allowed. It is slow, batch-by-batch work, because the still must be emptied and cleaned after every run. Traditional Cognac stills are heated with gas burners, and the condenser coil sits in constantly refreshed cold water.":"對 Cognac 來說，法律沒有留下選擇：葡萄酒必須在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，不允許使用蒸餾柱。這是緩慢、逐批進行的工作，因為每次蒸餾後都必須清空並清洗蒸餾器。傳統的 Cognac 蒸餾器以瓦斯爐火加熱，冷凝盤管則浸在持續更換的冷水中。","gas burners":"瓦斯爐火","by law":"依法規","Why a pot still":"為什麼用壺式蒸餾器","Why go to so much trouble? Because a pot still gives a spirit of relatively low strength that keeps plenty of flavour and character, exactly what Cognac needs. A tall column would make a lighter, less expressive spirit and lose much of the fruity and floral aromas of the grapes. Double distillation protects the soul of the wine.":"為什麼要這麼費工？因為壺式蒸餾器能得到濃度相對較低、保留大量風味和個性的烈酒，這正是 Cognac 所需要的。高蒸餾柱會做出更清淡、表現力較弱的烈酒，失去葡萄許多的果香和花香。二次蒸餾保護了葡萄酒的靈魂。","At least two years in oak":"在橡木桶中至少兩年","Fresh from the still, the future Cognac cannot use the name yet: the law requires at least two years in oak barrels. The wood gives colour and aromas of vanilla and toast. The finest Cognacs stay far longer, becoming concentrated and developing notes of fruit cake, leather and wood polish.":"剛離開蒸餾器時，未來的 Cognac 還不能使用這個名稱：法律要求在橡木桶中至少陳年兩年。木頭帶來顏色，以及香草和烘烤的香氣。最優秀的 Cognac 會待得更久，變得濃縮，並發展出水果蛋糕、皮革和木頭亮光蠟的氣息。","2+ years":"2 年以上","vanilla, toast":"香草、烘烤","long ageing":"長期陳年","Blending, caramel, a little sugar":"調和、焦糖色、少量的糖","Nearly all Cognacs are blends of spirits of different ages: younger ones bring freshness, older ones depth, and together they build complexity. Before dilution and bottling it is common to add a little caramel, to keep the colour consistent, and a touch of sweetening. So a Cognac can feel slightly rounded, even though it left the still dry.":"幾乎所有 Cognac 都是不同年份烈酒的調和：年輕的帶來清新感，老的帶來深度，結合在一起則建立複雜度。在稀釋和裝瓶前，常見的做法是加入少量焦糖色以保持顏色一致，並稍微加甜。所以即使 Cognac 離開蒸餾器時是不甜的，喝起來仍可能略為圓潤。","young: freshness":"年輕：清新","old: depth":"老：深度","a little sugar":"少量的糖","Three label terms show the age, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. VS means at least 2 years, VSOP at least 4, XO at least 10. Picture a staircase with three steps: 2, 4 and 10. If a blend contains a 5-year-old and a 20-year-old spirit, the 5 counts: it can be a VSOP.":"三個酒標術語標示年份，而且一律指調和中最年輕的烈酒。VS 表示至少 2 年，VSOP 至少 4 年，XO 至少 10 年。想像一座三階的樓梯：2、4、10。如果一款調和包含 5 年和 20 年的烈酒，以 5 年為準：它可以是 VSOP。","5 yrs":"5 年","20 yrs":"20 年","youngest counts":"以最年輕的為準","Vodka is the freest spirit of all. It can be made in any country and from any plant raw material. There is no compulsory area of origin, as with Cognac, and no required ingredient, as agave is for Tequila. What makes a spirit vodka is neither the place nor the plant: it is the strength it is distilled to.":"伏特加是所有烈酒中最自由的。它可以在任何國家、用任何植物原料製作。它不像 Cognac 有規定的原產地，也不像 Tequila 必須使用龍舌蘭。讓一款烈酒成為伏特加的，既不是產地也不是植物，而是它被蒸餾到的濃度。","defined by strength":"由濃度定義","Premium raw materials":"高級原料","Although the choice is open, some raw materials are linked with premium vodka: cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes. After processing to create a sugary liquid, it is fermented just like any other spirit. The first two steps are the classic ones; vodka's real distinguishing feature arrives with the third, distillation.":"雖然選擇是開放的，但有些原料與高級伏特加聯想在一起：穀物，尤其是大麥、小麥和黑麥，以及馬鈴薯。經過處理產生含糖液體後，就和其他烈酒一樣進行發酵。前兩步是經典做法；伏特加真正的特點出現在第三步：蒸餾。","barley":"大麥","wheat":"小麥","rye":"黑麥","Vodka is a diluted neutral spirit. To count as neutral, the spirit must reach at least 95 or 96% abv, depending on the law of the producing country. Such a high strength needs a column still, although some producers use pot stills for part of the process. At that level almost no aroma remains.":"伏特加是稀釋過的中性烈酒。要算是中性，烈酒必須至少達到 95% 或 96% abv，視生產國的法律而定。這麼高的濃度需要柱式蒸餾器，不過有些生產者會在部分流程中使用壺式蒸餾器。在這個濃度下幾乎沒有香氣留下。","at least 95–96%":"至少 95–96%","column still":"柱式蒸餾器","Unaged, then diluted":"未陳年，再加以稀釋","After distillation, vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water to bottling strength, typically 40% abv. Think of a blank canvas: the producer's effort goes into taking away rather than adding, so the glass holds a clean spirit with almost no smell.":"蒸餾後，伏特加不會進桶：它保持未陳年、清澈透明。接著用純水稀釋到裝瓶濃度，通常是 40% abv。想像一張空白畫布：生產者的努力在於去除而不是增添，讓杯中是一款幾乎沒有氣味的潔淨烈酒。","no barrel":"不進桶","a blank canvas":"一張空白畫布","Made for mixing":"為調酒而生","Most vodka aims for the most complete neutrality possible. That lack of aroma is exactly what makes it so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails: it blends into juices, sodas and liqueurs without imposing its own taste. A bartender who wants a stronger drink without changing its flavour reaches for vodka first.":"大多數伏特加追求盡可能完全的中性。正是這種缺乏香氣的特質，讓它在混合飲料和調酒中如此受歡迎：它能融入果汁、汽水和利口酒，不會強加自己的味道。想讓飲品更有酒勁又不改變風味的調酒師，第一個就會拿伏特加。","liqueur":"利口酒","adds alcohol":"增加酒精","not its taste":"不改變味道","A hint of character":"一點個性","Some vodkas, however, keep a hint of character: faint touches of the raw material, such as a note of grain or potato, on the nose and palate. They stay very delicate, nowhere near a whisky or a brandy, and are still correctly described as neutral. It is like mineral water next to distilled water: subtle, but noticeable.":"不過，有些伏特加保留了一點個性：在香氣和口中有淡淡的原料氣息，例如穀物或馬鈴薯。這些氣息非常細緻，遠不及威士忌或白蘭地，仍可正確地描述為中性。這就像礦泉水與蒸餾水並列：細微，但察覺得到。","faint grain or potato":"淡淡的穀物或馬鈴薯","still neutral":"仍是中性","Grain: starch, not sugar":"穀物：是澱粉，不是糖","Whisky always starts with grain; you can picture it as beer that has been through a still. There is one obstacle, though: a barley grain is dry, hard and packed with starch rather than sugar. Yeast can do nothing with starch, so it has to be turned into sugar before fermentation can begin.":"威士忌一定從穀物開始；你可以把它想像成經過蒸餾器的啤酒。不過有一個障礙：大麥粒又乾又硬，充滿的是澱粉而不是糖。酵母對澱粉無能為力，所以必須先把澱粉轉化為糖，才能開始發酵。","starch":"澱粉","a distilled beer":"蒸餾過的啤酒","The first step is malting. The barley is allowed to start growing, and as it grows the grain makes enzymes, tiny chemical tools that can change starch. At the right moment hot air is blown through to stop the growth. From then on it is called malted barley: it carries everything it needs, but the sugar is not released yet.":"第一步是製麥。讓大麥開始生長，穀粒在生長時會產生酵素，這是能改變澱粉的微小化學工具。在適當的時刻吹入熱空氣以停止生長。從此就稱為麥芽大麥：它已具備一切所需，但糖還沒有被釋放出來。","sprouts":"發芽","makes enzymes":"產生酵素","hot air: stop":"熱空氣：停止","malted barley":"麥芽大麥","Crush, then add warm water":"碾碎，再加溫水","Next the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, sometimes with other grains, and mixed with warm water. In this bath the enzymes convert the starch into sugar, giving a sweet liquid ready for yeast. Each grain leaves its signature: barley brings cereal notes, corn sweetcorn, and rye a spicy, peppery edge.":"接著把麥芽大麥碾成粗粉，有時加入其他穀物，並與溫水混合。在這個水浴中，酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，得到一種等著酵母的甜液體。每種穀物都留下自己的印記：大麥帶來穀物氣息，玉米帶來甜玉米，黑麥則帶來辛香、胡椒般的鋒芒。","crushing":"碾碎","warm water":"溫水","cereal":"穀物","sweetcorn":"甜玉米","spicy":"辛香","The rules of Scotch":"Scotch 的規定","Scotch is whisky from Scotland, and the rules are precise. It must be distilled in Scotland and then aged in Scotland for at least three years. Both conditions matter: a Scottish spirit sent to mature across the border loses the right to the name, even if everything else about it is identical.":"Scotch 是蘇格蘭的威士忌，規定很精確。它必須在蘇格蘭蒸餾，然後在蘇格蘭陳年至少三年。兩個條件都很重要：一款蘇格蘭烈酒如果送到邊界另一邊熟成，即使其他一切都相同，也會失去使用這個名稱的權利。","distilled":"蒸餾","3+ years":"3 年以上","aged":"陳年","no longer Scotch":"不再是 Scotch","Two big families":"兩大家族","Time in oak is compulsory: the barrels give colour and aromas, and the whisky concentrates as some water and alcohol evaporate. Scotch then splits into two big families: Single Malt and Blended. The difference is not prestige or age but three questions: which grains, which kind of still, and how many distilleries.":"在橡木桶中陳年是強制的：酒桶帶來顏色和香氣，隨著部分水和酒精蒸發，威士忌也變得濃縮。Scotch 接著分成兩大家族：Single Malt 和 Blended。差別不在名氣或年份，而在三個問題：哪些穀物、哪一種蒸餾器、幾家蒸餾廠。","malted barley only":"只用麥芽大麥","malt + grain":"麥芽 + 穀物","pot still":"壺式蒸餾器","pot + column":"壺式 + 柱式","distilleries":"蒸餾廠","just one":"只有一家","several":"多家","A Single Malt Scotch meets three requirements: it is made only from malted barley, distilled in pot stills, and comes from a single distillery. 'Single' means one place of production, not one barrel. Pot stills give a characterful spirit: cereal, fruit, flowers and honey, then fruit cake and sweet spice after time in oak.":"Single Malt Scotch 符合三項要求：只用麥芽大麥製成、以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾，並來自單一蒸餾廠。「Single」表示單一生產地點，而不是單一酒桶。壺式蒸餾器帶來有個性的烈酒：穀物、水果、花香和蜂蜜，在橡木桶中陳年後還有水果蛋糕和甜香料。","one distillery":"單一蒸餾廠","flowers":"花香","sweet spice":"甜香料","Some Single Malts carry one extra aroma: smoke. It comes from peat, a natural fuel burned when the malted barley is heated at the end of malting. The smoke wraps around the grains and flavours them, and that flavour travels all the way to the glass. Only a few Single Malts are peaty, some of them very strongly.":"有些 Single Malt 多了一種香氣：煙燻。它來自泥煤，一種在製麥最後烘乾麥芽大麥時燃燒的天然燃料。煙霧包覆穀粒並為它們增添風味，這種風味會一路來到杯中。只有少數 Single Malt 帶有泥煤風味，其中有些非常濃烈。","peat":"泥煤","smoke in the malt":"麥芽中的煙燻","only a few":"只有少數","Scotland also makes grain whisky. It uses malted barley together with other grains and is distilled in a column still rather than a pot still. The result has a light aroma and a smooth texture. It rarely reaches the shelf on its own, because its real job is in the blend.":"蘇格蘭也生產穀物威士忌。它用麥芽大麥加上其他穀物製成，以柱式蒸餾器而不是壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。結果香氣清淡、口感柔順。它很少單獨上架，因為它真正的工作在調和中。","barley + other grains":"大麥 + 其他穀物","Blended Scotch":"Blended Scotch","Blended Scotch, the most widespread category, combines malt whiskies and grain whiskies from different distilleries, and of different ages. Think of an orchestra: the intense malts are the soloists, while the light grain whisky holds everything together. Blending gives consistency and complexity, and blends are usually smoother than Single Malts, from simple to complex.":"Blended Scotch 是最普遍的類別，結合了來自不同蒸餾廠、不同年份的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。想像一支管弦樂團：濃郁的麥芽威士忌是獨奏者，清淡的穀物威士忌則把一切串連起來。調和帶來一致性和複雜度，調和威士忌通常比 Single Malt 柔順，從簡單到複雜都有。","malts: soloists":"麥芽：獨奏者","grain: the base":"穀物：基底","smoother":"更柔順","Bourbon: three choices":"Bourbon：三個選擇","Bourbon is the best-known American whiskey. Many people link it to Kentucky, and that state does make the most, but the law allows Bourbon to be made anywhere in the United States. Its style comes down to three clear choices: the grain recipe, the way it is distilled and the type of barrel.":"Bourbon 是最知名的美國威士忌。許多人把它與肯塔基州聯想在一起，那個州的產量也確實最多，但法律允許 Bourbon 在美國任何地方生產。它的風格取決於三個明確的選擇：穀物配方、蒸餾方式和酒桶類型。","anywhere in the USA":"美國任何地方","grain":"穀物","barrel":"酒桶","51%+ corn, column at low strength":"51% 以上玉米，蒸餾柱、低濃度","First choice: at least 51% of the grain must be corn, usually topped up with barley and rye; corn brings sweetcorn notes. Second: Bourbon is normally distilled in a column still, but only to a low strength, so it keeps plenty of character. A column does not have to make a light spirit: it all depends on how high the strength goes.":"第一個選擇：至少 51% 的穀物必須是玉米，通常再補上大麥和黑麥；玉米帶來甜玉米氣息。第二：Bourbon 通常以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，但只到較低濃度，所以保留大量個性。蒸餾柱不一定會做出清淡的烈酒：一切取決於濃度拉到多高。","corn":"玉米","= character":"= 個性","New charred barrels":"炙燒過的新桶","new oak":"新橡木","charred inside":"內部炙燒","Seems sweet, but it is dry":"看似甜，其實不甜","A common trap: people often call Bourbon sweet. In fact it has no added sugar and is dry. The impression of sweetness comes from the vanilla, fruit and coconut aromas, which the nose links with desserts. In tasting language, sweet refers only to the taste of sugar, felt on the palate.":"一個常見陷阱：人們常說 Bourbon 很甜。事實上它沒有加糖，是不甜的。甜的印象來自香草、水果和椰子香氣，鼻子會把這些香氣與甜點聯想在一起。在品飲用語中，「甜」只指在口中感受到的糖的味道。","no added sugar":"沒有加糖","on the palate: dry":"口中：不甜","Tennessee: through the charcoal":"Tennessee：通過木炭","Tennessee whiskey is made like Bourbon, with the same corn majority, distillation and new charred barrels, but only in the state of Tennessee. It adds one step: the new spirit is filtered through maple charcoal before going into the barrel. This removes some impurities and makes it smoother, without adding any flavour: no maple, no smoke.":"Tennessee 威士忌的製法和 Bourbon 一樣，同樣以玉米為主、同樣的蒸餾方式和炙燒過的新桶，但只在田納西州生產。它多了一個步驟：新烈酒在入桶前會先經過楓木炭過濾。這能去除部分雜質，讓口感更柔順，卻不增添任何風味：沒有楓糖，也沒有煙燻。","maple charcoal":"楓木炭","only in Tennessee":"只在田納西州","Rye, and how to tell them apart":"Rye，以及如何分辨它們","American Rye whiskey is Bourbon's spicy twin: same column distillation, same new charred barrels, but at least 51% of the grain must be rye. That brings spicy, peppery aromas, with the vanilla sitting behind. To sort the three: mostly corn is Bourbon; corn plus maple charcoal in Tennessee is Tennessee whiskey; mostly rye is Rye.":"美國 Rye 威士忌是 Bourbon 的辛香雙胞胎：同樣以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾、同樣使用炙燒過的新桶，但至少 51% 的穀物必須是黑麥。這帶來辛香、胡椒般的香氣，香草則退居其後。要分辨三者：以玉米為主是 Bourbon；玉米加楓木炭、在田納西州生產是 Tennessee 威士忌；以黑麥為主是 Rye。","51%+ corn":"51% 以上玉米","corn + charcoal":"玉米 + 木炭","51%+ rye":"51% 以上黑麥","spicy, peppery":"辛香、胡椒味","In Ireland, most whiskeys combine pot-still and column-still spirits, and the typical style is light and smooth, easy to drink. Some Irish whiskeys are made only in pot stills, and some use an unusual ingredient: unmalted barley, which gives an oily texture and a nutty character.":"在愛爾蘭，大多數威士忌結合了壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒，典型風格清淡柔順，容易入口。有些愛爾蘭威士忌只用壺式蒸餾器製作，其中有些使用一種不尋常的原料：未發芽的大麥，它帶來油潤的質地和堅果般的個性。","column":"蒸餾柱","light and smooth":"清淡柔順","unmalted barley":"未發芽的大麥","oily texture":"油潤質地","nutty":"堅果","Canada uses many different grains and usually blends high-strength spirits, which are lighter, with low-strength spirits, which have more flavour. The result is balanced, versatile whisky. In the best Canadian whiskies, though, one thread runs through them all: rye, the signature flavour, spicy and peppery.":"加拿大使用許多不同的穀物，通常把較清淡的高濃度烈酒與風味較多的低濃度烈酒調和在一起。結果是均衡、用途廣泛的威士忌。不過，在最優秀的加拿大威士忌中有一條共同的主線：黑麥，辛香而帶胡椒味的招牌風味。","many grains":"多種穀物","signature: rye":"招牌：黑麥","Japan":"日本","Japan built its whisky industry using Scotland as the model, so you find both malt and blended whiskies there, just as with Scotch. The traditional style is elegant and refined, precise in every detail. In recent years, though, many Japanese producers have explored new styles and flavours, and the category keeps evolving.":"日本以蘇格蘭為範本建立了威士忌產業，所以那裡和 Scotch 一樣，同時有麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。傳統風格優雅而細緻，每個細節都很講究。不過近年來，許多日本生產者探索了新的風格和風味，這個類別也持續在演變。","Scottish model":"蘇格蘭模式","elegant":"優雅","refined":"細緻","new styles":"新風格","Sugar cane and the Caribbean":"甘蔗與加勒比海","Rum is made from sugar cane, a plant that loves heat, so production is centred on hot countries, and its historic heartland is the Caribbean. The region is a patchwork of small countries, each with its own traditions and rules. Sorting rum by colour or language works poorly: it is far more useful to follow the four stages of production.":"蘭姆酒用甘蔗製成，這是一種喜愛高溫的植物，所以生產集中在炎熱的國家，而它歷史上的核心地帶是加勒比海。這個地區由許多小國拼湊而成，各有自己的傳統和規定。依顏色或語言來分類蘭姆酒效果不佳：依循生產的四個階段要有用得多。","Caribbean":"加勒比海","stages, not colour":"看階段，不看顏色","Cane juice: grassy":"甘蔗汁：青草氣息","The first choice is the raw material. Freshly cut cane can be crushed and its sweet juice fermented straight away. Cane juice rums often have a very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour, like freshly mown grass. The best examples are rhum agricole, which in the Caribbean must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"第一個選擇是原料。新鮮砍下的甘蔗可以壓碎，甜甜的汁液立刻發酵。甘蔗汁蘭姆酒通常帶有非常明顯的青草、草本風味，就像剛割下的青草。最好的例子是 rhum agricole，在加勒比海必須來自馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普。","grassy":"青草氣息","Molasses: caramel":"糖蜜：焦糖","Most Caribbean distillers, however, use molasses: a black, sticky by-product of the industry that turns cane juice into sugar. It must be mixed with water before fermentation can start. Molasses rums have flavours of caramel and brown sugar, a rounder profile than the grassy freshness of cane juice.":"不過，大多數加勒比海蒸餾師使用糖蜜：一種黑色黏稠的物質，是把甘蔗汁製成糖的產業留下的副產品。發酵開始前必須先與水混合。糖蜜蘭姆酒帶有焦糖和紅糖風味，風味輪廓比甘蔗汁的草本清新更圓潤。","sugar factory":"製糖廠","brown sugar":"紅糖","Fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, but it also creates aromas, and in rum it can take centre stage. Managed in a certain way, it produces tropical fruit aromas such as banana or pineapple, sometimes very pronounced. Jamaican distillers are famous for this intensely fruity style, which comes from fermentation, not from added flavourings.":"發酵把糖轉化為酒精，但也會產生香氣，在蘭姆酒中它可能成為主角。以特定方式管理時，它會產生香蕉或鳳梨等熱帶水果香氣，有時非常明顯。牙買加的蒸餾師以這種果香濃郁的風格聞名，這種風格來自發酵，而不是添加的調味料。","Pot or column: intensity":"壺式或柱式：濃郁度","Caribbean distillers can choose their still, and that choice sets the intensity. A pot still gives a pronounced rum full of character. A short column with few sections also gives a flavourful spirit: this is how rhum agricole is made. Tall columns distilling to a high strength give light rums, as in Cuba and Puerto Rico. Many distilleries own both types.":"加勒比海的蒸餾師可以選擇自己的蒸餾器，而這個選擇決定了濃郁度。壺式蒸餾器能得到濃郁、充滿個性的蘭姆酒。層數少的矮蒸餾柱同樣能得到風味豐富的烈酒：rhum agricole 就是這樣製作的。蒸餾到高濃度的高蒸餾柱則得到清淡的蘭姆酒，例如古巴和波多黎各。許多蒸餾廠兩種都有。","Oak, steel and charcoal filters":"橡木桶、不鏽鋼與木炭過濾","A rum can be aged or not. Oak adds vanilla, sweet spice and colour, and some Caribbean countries require time in the barrel. Unaged rum rests in steel tanks and stays colourless. And if oak is required but the producer wants a white rum? Charcoal filtering removes the colour taken from the wood: a clear rum that has seen oak.":"蘭姆酒可以陳年，也可以不陳年。橡木桶增添香草、甜香料和顏色，有些加勒比海國家規定必須在桶中陳年一段時間。未陳年的蘭姆酒在鋼製桶槽中靜置，保持無色。如果規定要橡木桶陳年，但生產者想要白色蘭姆酒呢？木炭過濾能去除從木頭吸收的顏色：一款接觸過橡木的透明蘭姆酒。","vanilla, spice":"香草、香料","charcoal filter":"木炭過濾","aged white rum":"陳年的白色蘭姆酒","Blending, sugar and caramel":"調和、糖與焦糖色","Then comes blending: pot and column spirits, of different ages and even from different distilleries, build each style. Some rums are sweetened, a common practice in Central and South America, while some countries forbid it. Many get caramel for colour, sometimes almost all of it. Finally, pure water brings the rum down to bottling strength.":"接著是調和：壺式和柱式蒸餾的烈酒，不同年份，甚至來自不同的蒸餾廠，共同建立每一種風格。有些蘭姆酒會加甜，這在中南美洲很常見，而有些國家則禁止。許多蘭姆酒會加入焦糖色上色，有時幾乎所有顏色都來自焦糖色。最後，用純水把蘭姆酒降到裝瓶濃度。","Central/South America":"中南美洲","banned in some places":"某些地方禁止","Blue agave, only in Mexico":"藍色龍舌蘭，只在墨西哥","Tequila is a Mexican spirit with a clear identity: it can only be made in certain Mexican states named by law, and only from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico. It is not a cactus: long, spiky leaves fan out around a large, hard core. At harvest the leaves are cut away, leaving only the core the distiller wants.":"Tequila 是一種身分明確的墨西哥烈酒：它只能在法律指名的特定墨西哥州生產，而且只能用原產於墨西哥的藍色龍舌蘭製作。它不是仙人掌：長而帶刺的葉片圍繞著一個又大又硬的核心呈扇形展開。採收時會切除葉片，只留下蒸餾師想要的核心。","not a cactus":"不是仙人掌","the core":"龍舌蘭心","Mexican states":"墨西哥各州","Cooking and agave aromas":"烹煮與龍舌蘭香氣","Like grain, a fresh agave core has no sugar ready to ferment. The cores are cooked slowly in ovens until they turn soft and sugars form, a bit like a hard potato you can mash once cooked. Then they are crushed, releasing a sweet juice with the unmistakable aromas of blue agave: herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy and peppery.":"和穀物一樣，新鮮的龍舌蘭心沒有現成可發酵的糖。龍舌蘭心放在窯爐中慢慢烹煮，直到變軟並形成糖分，有點像一顆煮熟後就能壓成泥的硬馬鈴薯。接著將它壓碎，釋出甜甜的汁液，帶有藍色龍舌蘭獨特的香氣：草本、植物、橄欖、泥土和胡椒。","oven cooking":"窯爐烹煮","herbaceous":"草本","vegetal":"植物","earthy":"泥土","peppery":"胡椒","Tequila or 100% agave?":"Tequila 還是 100% agave？","The agave juice is mixed with water before fermentation, and the producer may add other sugars too. The law sets a floor: at least 51% of the sugars must come from blue agave. A label saying '100% agave' means no other sugars at all, and a more pronounced agave character. This is about sugars only: aged or unaged, any Tequila can be either.":"龍舌蘭汁在發酵前與水混合，生產者也可以加入其他糖。法律設下底線：至少 51% 的糖必須來自藍色龍舌蘭。酒標上寫著「100% agave」，表示完全沒有其他糖，龍舌蘭的個性也更鮮明。這只關乎糖：不論陳年與否，任何 Tequila 都可以是其中一種。","Tequila may be made in column stills, but the best ones are distilled twice in pot stills, stopping at a notably low strength. The lower the strength, the more of the agave's herbaceous, peppery aromas stay in the spirit. It is the exact opposite of vodka, pushed to a very high strength precisely to strip the aroma away.":"Tequila 可以用柱式蒸餾器製作，但最優秀的 Tequila 是在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，並停在明顯較低的濃度。濃度越低，留在烈酒中的龍舌蘭草本、胡椒香氣就越多。它正好與伏特加相反，伏特加被推到極高濃度，正是為了去除香氣。","twice":"兩次","less character":"個性較少","Blanco and Joven":"Blanco 與 Joven","After distillation the producer chooses whether to age the Tequila. There are two unaged versions. Blanco, also called Silver, is colourless and prized for showing agave at its purest. Joven, also called Oro or Gold, has a golden colour but has never seen a barrel: the colour comes from caramel, and other additives soften its texture.":"蒸餾後，生產者選擇是否讓 Tequila 陳年。有兩種未陳年的版本。Blanco，也稱為 Silver，無色，因為展現最純粹的龍舌蘭而備受推崇。Joven，也稱為 Oro 或 Gold，呈金黃色，但從未進過酒桶：顏色來自焦糖色，其他添加物則讓口感變得柔和。","pure agave":"純粹的龍舌蘭","colour: caramel":"顏色：焦糖色","Reposado and Añejo":"Reposado 與 Añejo","There are also two oak-aged versions. Reposado, meaning rested, spends between 2 and 12 months in oak: it is softer, but the wood rarely shows strongly and agave stays in the lead. Añejo, meaning aged, spends at least 12 months in barrel and combines agave with oak notes such as vanilla and spice.":"也有兩種經橡木桶陳年的版本。Reposado，意思是「靜置過的」，在橡木桶中待 2 到 12 個月：口感較柔和，但木頭的味道很少明顯，龍舌蘭仍居主導。Añejo，意思是「陳年的」，在桶中至少待 12 個月，結合了龍舌蘭和香草、香料等橡木氣息。","months in oak":"在橡木桶中的月數","agave leads":"龍舌蘭居主導","agave + oak":"龍舌蘭 + 橡木","Balancing agave and wood":"平衡龍舌蘭與木頭","Why do aged Tequilas spend fairly little time in barrel? Because the producer is looking for balance: some vanilla and spice, without burying the agave character that makes Tequila unique. Aged versions are then blended, may receive caramel to even out the colour, and are diluted with water before bottling.":"為什麼陳年 Tequila 在桶中的時間相對較短？因為生產者追求平衡：帶一些香草和香料，又不掩蓋讓 Tequila 獨一無二的龍舌蘭個性。陳年版本接著會經過調和，可能加入焦糖色讓顏色均勻，並在裝瓶前加水稀釋。","then caramel, water":"接著是焦糖色、水","A bought-in base and botanicals":"外購基底與植物性原料","Flavoured spirits start differently: the producer usually grows and ferments nothing, but buys in a ready-made spirit, most often the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka once diluted. Now and then the base is a rum, whisky or brandy. The best products then add natural ingredients, fruits, seeds, herbs and spices, known as botanicals.":"調味烈酒的起點不同：生產者通常什麼都不種植、也不發酵，而是外購現成的烈酒，最常見的是稀釋後成為伏特加的同一種中性烈酒。偶爾基底會是蘭姆酒、威士忌或白蘭地。最好的產品接著會加入天然原料：水果、種子、香草和香料，稱為植物性原料。","or rum, whisky, brandy":"或蘭姆酒、威士忌、白蘭地","fruits":"水果","seeds":"種子","spices":"香料","= botanicals":"= 植物性原料","Redistillation: flavoured, colourless":"再蒸餾：有風味、無色","The first method is redistillation. Diluted neutral spirit and botanicals go into a pot still together and are distilled. The vapour carries the aromas of the plants into the condenser, and what comes out is fragrant but colourless. It is the method usually behind the best gins.":"第一種方法是再蒸餾。稀釋過的中性烈酒和植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾。蒸氣把植物的香氣帶進冷凝器，流出的液體芳香但無色。最優秀的琴酒通常就是用這種方法製作的。","neutral + botanicals":"中性烈酒 + 植物性原料","fragrant":"芳香","Maceration: flavour and colour":"浸漬：風味與顏色","The second method is maceration: the botanicals steep in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, giving up both flavour and colour. It can last a few days or several months; the longer it goes on, the more flavour is drawn out, and gentle heating speeds things up.":"第二種方法是浸漬：植物性原料浸泡在烈酒中，就像冷泡花草茶，同時釋出風味和顏色。它可以持續幾天到幾個月；時間越長，萃取出的風味越多，溫和加熱則能加快速度。","flavour + colour":"風味 + 顏色","days → months":"幾天 → 幾個月","heat speeds it up":"加熱能加快速度","Bought-in flavourings":"外購調味料","The third method is the simplest: adding bought-in flavourings, natural or artificial. They are very concentrated, so only small amounts are needed. This route is usually chosen for cost reasons, instead of real botanicals. Many flavoured vodkas are made exactly this way.":"第三種方法最簡單：加入外購的天然或人工調味料。它們非常濃縮，只需少量使用。選擇這條路通常是出於成本考量，用它來取代真正的植物性原料。許多調味伏特加正是這樣製作的。","a few drops":"幾滴","natural or artificial":"天然或人工","very concentrated":"非常濃縮","lower cost":"成本較低","Flavoured vodka":"調味伏特加","Flavoured vodka is the most intuitive case: a neutral base given one clear flavour. The options are endless: vanilla, fruits such as apple or lemon, even spices like pepper. Most producers simply add bought-in flavourings, although some use redistillation. On the nose it is easy to spot: one flavour, clean and direct.":"調味伏特加是最直觀的例子：一個中性基底，加上一種明確的風味。選擇無窮無盡：香草、蘋果或檸檬等水果，甚至胡椒這類香料。大多數生產者只是加入外購調味料，不過也有些使用再蒸餾。在香氣上很容易辨認：一種風味，乾淨而直接。","one clean flavour":"一種乾淨的風味","Gin: juniper first":"琴酒：杜松子優先","Gin has one essential rule: juniper must be the leading flavour, with its resinous, piney notes. Alongside it you often find coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel. The base is usually neutral spirit, although other distilled spirits are allowed in the USA. A typical gin is colourless and unaged.":"琴酒有一條基本規定：杜松子必須是主導風味，帶有樹脂和松木般的氣息。除了杜松子，常見的還有芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根和柑橘皮。基底通常是中性烈酒，不過在美國也允許使用其他蒸餾烈酒。典型的琴酒無色、未經陳年。","juniper leads":"杜松子居主導","resinous, piney":"樹脂、松木","orris root":"鳶尾根","The best gins are usually redistilled with their botanicals, though some very delicate flavours are added afterwards; other producers simply add bought-in flavourings. On a label, London Dry Gin means the flavours were added during redistillation. Despite the name, it is not a place: a London Dry Gin can be made anywhere in the world.":"最優秀的琴酒通常是與植物性原料一起再蒸餾，不過有些非常細緻的風味是之後才加入的；其他生產者則直接加入外購調味料。在酒標上，London Dry Gin 表示風味是在再蒸餾時加入的。儘管名稱如此，它並不是地名：London Dry Gin 可以在世界任何地方製作。","anywhere":"任何地方","Bitter spirits and cocktail bitters":"苦味烈酒與調酒用苦精","Bitter spirits contain at least one bitter botanical, such as gentian, quinine or bitter orange. Bitterness shows only in the mouth: the nose cannot detect it. Cocktail bitters go further: highly concentrated and intensely bitter, they are never drunk alone but used by the dash, like salt and pepper in cooking, to add complexity.":"苦味烈酒至少含有一種苦味植物性原料，例如龍膽、奎寧或苦橙。苦味只在口中出現：鼻子無法察覺。調酒用苦精則更進一步：高度濃縮、極苦，從不單獨飲用，而是以滴數使用，就像烹飪中的鹽和胡椒，用來增添複雜度。","gentian":"龍膽","quinine":"奎寧","bitter orange":"苦橙","bitter only in mouth":"苦味只在口中","by the dash":"以滴數使用","Spiced rum is a very varied family. Many start from a light, unaged rum that is flavoured and coloured with caramel; only a handful use an oak-aged rum. Both real botanicals and other flavourings are used. So be careful: an amber spiced rum does not necessarily mean years in a barrel.":"香料蘭姆酒是一個非常多樣的家族。許多以清淡的未陳年蘭姆酒為起點，經過調味並以焦糖色上色；只有少數使用橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒。真正的植物性原料和其他調味料都會使用。所以要小心：琥珀色的香料蘭姆酒不一定代表在桶中多年。","light rum":"清淡的蘭姆酒","spices, flavourings":"香料、調味料","amber ≠ years":"琥珀色 ≠ 多年","A liqueur is a flavoured spirit that has also been sweetened, and the law sets a minimum sweetness. Most use neutral spirit, some brandy, rum or whisky. Any flavour is possible: citrus, coffee, herbs, hazelnut, even cream for a velvety texture. Many are coloured too, often artificially, because those colours are more stable and brighter.":"利口酒是經過調味、又加了甜的烈酒，法律規定了最低甜度。大多數使用中性烈酒，有些使用白蘭地、蘭姆酒或威士忌。任何風味都可以：柑橘、咖啡、香草、榛果，甚至用鮮奶油帶來絲滑的質地。許多利口酒也會上色，常常使用人工色素，因為這些顏色更穩定、更鮮豔。","minimum sweetness":"最低甜度","hazelnut":"榛果","coloured":"經過上色","Not spirits, but…":"不是烈酒，但是…","Aromatised wines are not spirits, yet every bar has them, because they are so useful in cocktails: a single ingredient brings sweetness, bitterness and acidity at once. The category is varied, but the basic recipe never changes, and it is built from four components.":"加味葡萄酒不是烈酒，但每個酒吧都有，因為它們在調酒中非常有用：一種材料就能同時帶來甜味、苦味和酸度。這個類別很多樣，但基本配方從不改變，由四個組成部分構成。","acidic":"帶酸度","in one ingredient":"在一種材料中","The four components":"四個組成部分","The four components are a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar, and a little spirit. Caramel is sometimes added too. Think of it as a recipe card: change the wine, the botanicals or the amount of sugar and you get a different product, but those four building blocks are always there.":"四個組成部分是基酒、一定包含某種苦味的調味料、糖，以及少量烈酒。有時也會加入焦糖色。把它想成一張食譜卡：改變葡萄酒、植物性原料或糖的份量，就會得到不同的產品，但這四個基本組成永遠都在。","bitter flavourings":"苦味調味料","+ caramel (optional)":"+ 焦糖色（可選）","The wine and the bitter flavourings":"葡萄酒與苦味調味料","The base wine is nearly always white and often fairly neutral, a blank canvas for the flavours; some producers use aromatic wines, or red or rosé. Flavourings go straight into the wine or are added as flavoured spirits. Recipes vary a lot, but all include bitter botanicals such as wormwood, gentian or quinine.":"基酒幾乎都是白葡萄酒，通常相當中性，是風味的空白畫布；有些生產者使用芳香型葡萄酒，或紅葡萄酒、粉紅酒。調味料直接加入葡萄酒中，或以調味烈酒的形式加入。配方差異很大，但都包含苦艾、龍膽或奎寧等苦味植物性原料。","white, neutral":"白葡萄酒、中性","sometimes red, rosé":"有時是紅酒、粉紅酒","Spirit, sugar, caramel":"烈酒、糖、焦糖色","A small amount of spirit, nearly always neutral, raises the alcohol and gives the product a longer life, especially once the bottle is open. Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry: sweetness comes from the wine itself or from added sugar. Caramel is optional, used for colour, and in red products made from white wine it can add caramel notes.":"少量的烈酒（幾乎都是中性的）能提高酒精濃度，讓產品保存更久，尤其是開瓶之後。幾乎沒有加味葡萄酒是完全不甜的：甜味來自葡萄酒本身或添加的糖。焦糖色是可選的，用來上色；在以白葡萄酒製成的紅色產品中，它還能增添焦糖氣息。","more alcohol":"更多酒精","lasts longer once open":"開瓶後保存更久","almost never dry":"幾乎從不是不甜的","caramel: colour":"焦糖色：顏色","Aromatised wines can be made anywhere, but two areas are especially famous: south-east France and north-west Italy. In both, the most widely made type is vermouth. Two rules define it: it is made from a white wine base, and it must be flavoured with wormwood, a botanical with a strongly bitter taste.":"加味葡萄酒可以在任何地方製作，但有兩個地區特別有名：法國東南部和義大利西北部。在這兩地，最普遍的類型是香艾酒。兩條規定定義了它：以白葡萄酒為基酒，而且必須用苦艾調味，這是一種苦味強烈的植物性原料。","white wine + wormwood":"白葡萄酒 + 苦艾","Dry and red":"Dry 與紅色","Watch the labels: a vermouth marked dry nearly always contains added sugar, just less of it. Red vermouths are usually heavily sweetened. And their colour? Since the base is a white wine, the red shade usually comes from caramel, which can also add a light caramel aroma.":"注意酒標：標示 dry 的香艾酒幾乎都含有添加的糖，只是比較少。紅香艾酒通常大量加甜。那它們的顏色呢？既然基酒是白葡萄酒，紅色通常來自焦糖色，焦糖色還能增添淡淡的焦糖香氣。","some sugar":"一些糖","very sweet":"非常甜","Vermouth behind the bar":"吧台後的香艾酒","Behind the bar, vermouth is a real all-rounder. A dry vermouth adds dryness and perfume to a gin-based drink, while a red one, sweet with a bitter edge, rounds out a whiskey cocktail. Either way it balances sweetness, bitterness and acidity in one pour, so it pays to know its style and sweetness before reaching for the bottle.":"在吧台後，香艾酒是真正的全能選手。不甜香艾酒為以琴酒為基底的飲品增添乾爽感和香氣，而甜中帶苦的紅香艾酒則讓威士忌調酒更圓潤。不論哪一種，它一次倒入就平衡了甜、苦和酸，所以在拿起酒瓶之前，值得先了解它的風格和甜度。","dryness, perfume":"乾爽感、香氣","whiskey + red":"威士忌 + 紅香艾酒","roundness":"圓潤","sweet · bitter · sour":"甜 · 苦 · 酸","Always the same method":"永遠用同一套方法","Tasting a spirit means looking at it closely, and doing that well needs a method you repeat the same way every time. If every sample is treated identically, the notes you write today can be compared with those you write next month. Before pouring anything, though, it pays to prepare the setting.":"品飲烈酒就是仔細地觀察它，而要做好這件事，需要一套每次都以相同方式重複的方法。如果每個樣品都以相同方式對待，你今天寫下的筆記就能和下個月寫的相互比較。不過在倒酒之前，值得先準備好環境。","next month":"下個月","today":"今天","same method":"同一套方法","Setting the scene":"布置環境","The room should be free of distracting smells: no strong perfume, cooking or scented candles. You need good natural light and a white surface, such as a sheet of paper, to judge colour without misleading reflections. The taster matters too: a clean palate, with no lingering toothpaste or coffee, and a well-hydrated body.":"房間裡不應有干擾的氣味：沒有濃烈的香水、烹飪味或香氛蠟燭。你需要良好的自然光和白色表面，例如一張紙，才能判斷顏色而不受誤導性反光影響。品飲者本身也很重要：味覺要乾淨，沒有殘留的牙膏或咖啡味，身體也要補充足夠的水分。","perfume":"香水","cooking":"烹飪","toothpaste":"牙膏","The right glass":"合適的酒杯","Then comes the glass. The ideal shape has a wide bowl that narrows towards the rim, a little like a tulip. The wide part gives the aromas room to rise, and the narrower opening gathers them and channels them to your nose. In a straight, open tumbler the scents drift away and the spirit seems less expressive.":"接著是酒杯。理想的杯形有寬大的杯肚，往杯口逐漸收窄，有點像鬱金香。寬的部分讓香氣有空間上升，較窄的開口則把香氣聚集起來，導向你的鼻子。在直筒開口的平底杯中，香氣會飄散，烈酒顯得較沒有表現力。","aromas gathered":"香氣聚集","aromas drift away":"香氣飄散","A small sample":"少量樣品","Even after dilution, a spirit is a very strong drink: at 40% abv the alcohol stings the nose and warms the mouth, hiding many details. So you work with a small sample of about 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon. It gives you everything you need without tiring your senses.":"即使經過稀釋，烈酒仍然是非常烈的飲料：在 40% abv 時，酒精會刺鼻並讓口中發熱，掩蓋許多細節。所以要使用大約 1.5 cL 的小樣品，大約一湯匙。它能提供你所需的一切，又不會讓感官疲乏。","alcohol stings":"酒精刺鼻","a tablespoon":"一湯匙","Look, smell, water, smell again":"看、聞、加水、再聞","The route is simple. First look at the sample and smell it neat. Then add the same amount of water, another 1.5 cL, which halves the strength. Smell again: aromas the alcohol was hiding often appear, like opening a window in a crowded room. Only then do you move on to tasting.":"流程很簡單。首先觀察樣品，並聞未稀釋的酒。然後加入等量的水，也就是另外 1.5 cL，讓濃度減半。再聞一次：被酒精掩蓋的香氣往往會出現，就像在擁擠的房間裡打開一扇窗。之後才進入品嚐。","same amount":"等量","new aromas":"新的香氣","Taste and spit":"品嚐並吐出","In the mouth, roll the liquid around for a few seconds, look for the flavours and then spit it out. Spitting is not rude: it lets you taste several samples while staying clear-headed, and judge the last one as carefully as the first. In short: small sample, eyes and nose, equal water, nose again, palate, spit.":"在口中，讓液體轉動幾秒鐘，尋找風味，然後吐出。吐出並不失禮：它讓你能品嚐多個樣品並保持頭腦清醒，對最後一個樣品的判斷也能和第一個一樣仔細。簡單來說：小樣品、看與聞、加等量的水、再聞、品嚐、吐出。","1.5 cL":"1.5 cL","eyes":"眼睛","spit":"吐出","stay clear-headed":"保持清醒","Appearance: colour":"外觀：顏色","Notes follow the order of the tasting: eyes, nose, palate. For appearance, colour is all you need. Many unaged spirits are colourless, while those aged in wood range from lemon to gold, amber and brown. Some flavoured products, especially liqueurs, can be vivid: pink, red, green, blue, even black. Colour is a first clue, not proof.":"筆記依照品飲的順序：眼睛、鼻子、口腔。外觀方面，只需要記錄顏色。許多未陳年的烈酒是無色的，而在木桶中陳年過的則從檸檬黃到金黃、琥珀和棕色都有。有些調味產品，尤其是利口酒，顏色可能很鮮豔：粉紅、紅、綠、藍，甚至黑色。顏色是第一條線索，而不是證據。","flavoured products":"調味產品","a clue, not proof":"是線索，不是證據","Nose: intensity and aromas":"香氣：強度與香氣","On the nose, first judge intensity: neutral, with almost no smell like many vodkas, then light, medium or pronounced. Then describe the aromas grouped by where they come from: the raw material, such as fruit or grain; the way it was made; and the oak and maturation, such as vanilla, spice or toasty notes.":"在香氣方面，首先判斷強度：中性，像許多伏特加一樣幾乎沒有氣味，再來是清淡、中等或濃郁。然後依來源分組描述香氣：原料，例如水果或穀物；製作方式；以及橡木桶和熟成，例如香草、香料或烘烤氣息。","fruit, grain":"水果、穀物","how it was made":"製作方式","fermentation…":"發酵…","oak and maturation":"橡木桶與熟成","where is it from?":"從哪裡來？","Palate, finish and complexity":"口中、餘韻與複雜度","On the palate you find the same groups of flavours, plus two observations: how much sugar you sense, and the texture, thin or richer. After spitting, measure the finish, how long the flavours linger: short, medium or long. Finally judge complexity, from neutral and simple up to very complex, when many flavours keep changing.":"在口中，你會找到同樣的風味分組，再加上兩項觀察：感受到多少糖，以及質地是稀薄還是較豐厚。吐出後，衡量餘韻，也就是風味停留多久：短、中等或長。最後判斷複雜度，從中性和簡單，一直到風味眾多且不斷變化時的非常複雜。","sugar?":"糖分？","simple":"簡單","some complexity":"有些複雜度","very complex":"非常複雜","Two scales, four elements":"兩座天平，四個元素","Good ingredients and tools help, but what makes a cocktail memorable is balance. Picture two sets of scales. The first weighs the strong part against the weak part; the second weighs sweet against bitter and sour. Together they give four points of balance, and every classic cocktail is built from these four elements.":"好的材料和工具有幫助，但讓一杯調酒令人難忘的是平衡。想像兩座天平。第一座秤的是強的部分對弱的部分；第二座秤的是甜對苦和酸。兩者加起來就是平衡的四個要點，每一款經典調酒都由這四個元素構成。","bitter/sour":"苦／酸","4 points of balance":"平衡的 4 個要點","The strong part":"強的部分","The strong part is the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more, and it is the heart of the flavour: rum in a Daiquiri, gin in a Martini. Change the spirit and you change the drink. Even another product from the same category alters the result, and replacing the base entirely creates a variation, such as an Old Fashioned made with rum.":"強的部分是基酒，通常是 40% abv 以上，它是風味的核心：Daiquiri 中的蘭姆酒、Martini 中的琴酒。換了烈酒，飲品也就變了。即使改用同一類別的另一款產品也會改變結果，而完全替換基酒則會產生變化版，例如用蘭姆酒製作的 Old Fashioned。","base: rum":"基酒：蘭姆酒","base: gin":"基酒：琴酒","whiskey → rum":"威士忌 → 蘭姆酒","= variation":"= 變化版","40% abv or more":"40% abv 以上","The weak part":"弱的部分","The weak part softens the power of the alcohol. One source is always there: ice, which melts a little as you stir or shake and adds water. Others are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, cream or milk, sodas, club soda and tonic. In a gin and tonic, gin is the strong part, while tonic and ice balance it.":"弱的部分讓酒精的力度變得柔和。有一個來源一定存在：冰塊，攪拌或搖盪時會融化一些並加入水分。其他來源是可選的，而且不含酒精：果汁、鮮奶油或牛奶、汽水、蘇打水和通寧水。在琴通寧中，琴酒是強的部分，通寧水和冰塊則平衡它。","ice: always":"冰塊：一定有","juices":"果汁","cream, milk":"鮮奶油、牛奶","soda, tonic":"汽水、通寧水","gin = strong":"琴酒 = 強","Many cocktails are first sweetened, then seasoned. Sweetness can come from sugar, from simple syrup, which is sugar dissolved in water, or from a liqueur. It rounds things off and binds them together, but on its own it tires the palate: a cocktail that is too sweet tastes cloying and heavy.":"許多調酒先加甜，再調味。甜味可以來自糖、簡易糖漿（溶於水中的糖）或利口酒。它讓味道圓潤、把各種元素結合在一起，但單獨存在時會讓味覺疲乏：太甜的調酒喝起來膩口又沉重。","simple syrup":"簡易糖漿","sugar + water":"糖 + 水","rounds, binds":"圓潤、融合","too much: cloying":"太多：膩口","Sour and bitter":"酸與苦","The counterweight is the modifier, which brings a sour note, a bitter note or both. Sourness comes mainly from citrus: a little lime or lemon juice makes the sip lively. Bitterness comes from cocktail bitters, used by the dash, or from bitter spirits. It works like cooking: a pinch of salt or a squeeze of lemon lifts a flat dish.":"平衡的砝碼是修飾材料，它帶來酸味、苦味或兩者兼具。酸味主要來自柑橘：一點萊姆或檸檬汁就能讓每一口變得活潑。苦味來自以滴數使用的調酒用苦精，或苦味烈酒。這就像烹飪：一撮鹽或擠一點檸檬汁，就能讓平淡的菜變得生動。","the modifier":"修飾材料","sour: citrus":"酸：柑橘","bitter: bitters":"苦：苦精","like salt and lemon":"就像鹽和檸檬","Ingredients with several roles":"身兼數職的材料","A single ingredient can play several roles. Aromatised wines such as vermouth bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity at once; a liqueur brings both alcohol and sweetness. The goal is a cohesive whole where no part dominates: if the drink tastes only of sugar, lemon or alcohol, it is not balanced yet.":"一種材料可以扮演多個角色。香艾酒等加味葡萄酒同時帶來甜味、苦味和酸度；利口酒則同時帶來酒精和甜味。目標是一個沒有任何部分壓過其他部分的融合整體：如果飲品喝起來只有糖、檸檬或酒精的味道，那就還沒有平衡。","vermouth":"香艾酒","sweetness":"甜味","nothing dominates":"沒有任何部分主導","One first split helps you find your way: short drinks and long drinks. Short drinks have few ingredients and a small volume; their weak part is almost only the water from ice during stirring or shaking. Spirit-forward cocktails and short sours belong here. Long drinks are lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy: highballs and long sours.":"先做一個區分就能找到方向：短飲和長飲。短飲的材料不多，份量也小；它們弱的部分幾乎只有攪拌或搖盪時冰塊帶來的水。烈酒主導型調酒和短酸酒屬於這一類。長飲則以汽水、果汁或乳製品延長：高球和長酸酒。","short sour":"短酸酒","ice only":"只有冰塊","long sour":"長酸酒","+ soda, juice":"+ 汽水、果汁","From short to long":"從短飲到長飲","An example shows the link. A short gin sour, shaken and served in a small glass, becomes a long drink if you pour it over ice and top it with club soda. The core ingredients stay the same; what changes is the amount of the weak part, and with it the strength, the volume and the moment you might enjoy it.":"一個例子能說明兩者的關聯。一杯搖盪後倒入小杯的短琴酒酸酒，如果倒在冰塊上並補滿蘇打水，就變成長飲。核心材料保持不變；改變的是弱的部分的份量，連帶改變了濃度、份量，以及適合享用的時機。","+ ice, club soda":"+ 冰塊、蘇打水","long drink":"長飲","Classic cocktails fall into four big families. Two are short: spirit-forward drinks, where the spirit leads, and short sours, which combine spirit, citrus and sweetness. Two are long: highballs, a spirit with a non-alcoholic mixer, and long sours, short sours lengthened with soda or sparkling wine. Let us meet them one by one.":"經典調酒分為四大家族。兩個是短飲：以烈酒為主角的烈酒主導型飲品，以及結合烈酒、柑橘和甜味的短酸酒。兩個是長飲：高球，也就是烈酒加無酒精調和飲料；以及長酸酒，也就是以蘇打水或氣泡酒延長的短酸酒。我們來逐一認識它們。","Short sour":"短酸酒","rgba(220,235,240,.6)":"rgba(220,235,240,.6)","Long sour":"長酸酒","short ↑ · long ↓":"短 ↑ · 長 ↓","Old Fashioned and Manhattan":"Old Fashioned 與 Manhattan","Spirit-forward cocktails are the strongest, putting the spirit on show; they are built in the glass or stirred, and the ice both chills and dilutes. The Old Fashioned is the template: American whiskey, a sugar cube and aromatic bitters. The Manhattan uses rye or Bourbon with the same bitters, swapping the sugar for sweet red vermouth.":"烈酒主導型調酒是最烈的，讓烈酒成為焦點；它們直接在杯中調製或攪拌，冰塊同時負責冰鎮和稀釋。Old Fashioned 是範本：美國威士忌、一顆方糖和芳香苦精。Manhattan 使用黑麥威士忌或 Bourbon 和同樣的苦精，但把糖換成甜紅香艾酒。","sugar cube":"方糖","aromatic bitters":"芳香苦精","rye or Bourbon":"黑麥威士忌或 Bourbon","sweet red vermouth":"甜紅香艾酒","built or stirred":"直調或攪拌","Sazerac and Rusty Nail":"Sazerac 與 Rusty Nail","The Sazerac starts from Cognac or rye, with sugar, a different style of bitters and a touch of absinthe. The Rusty Nail is the simplest of all: Scotch whisky with a Scotch-based liqueur, just two ingredients. Both follow the same idea: a spirit balanced by a little sweetness and, often, a little bitterness.":"Sazerac 以 Cognac 或黑麥威士忌為起點，加上糖、另一種風格的苦精和一點苦艾酒。Rusty Nail 是最簡單的：Scotch 威士忌加上以 Scotch 為基底的利口酒，只有兩種材料。兩者遵循同樣的概念：一種烈酒，以一點甜味、通常還有一點苦味來平衡。","Cognac or rye":"Cognac 或黑麥威士忌","touch of absinthe":"一點苦艾酒","Scotch liqueur":"Scotch 利口酒","just 2 ingredients":"只有 2 種材料","Gin gives two great classics. The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth, which alone provides both the sweet and the bitter note. The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and a red bitter spirit: three ingredients, three clear roles. Add cream to this kind of drink and you get the Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander.":"琴酒造就了兩款偉大的經典調酒。Martini 把琴酒與不甜香艾酒搭配在一起，香艾酒單獨就提供了甜味和苦味。Negroni 結合琴酒、甜紅香艾酒和一種紅色苦味烈酒：三種材料，三個明確的角色。在這類飲品中加入鮮奶油，就得到 Alexander 家族，例如 Brandy Alexander。","red bitter spirit":"紅色苦味烈酒","+ cream":"+ 鮮奶油","The short sour rests on a trio: strong, sour, sweet, shaken for a light, almost frothy texture. Daiquiri: rum, lime and simple syrup. Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye, lemon and syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. Pisco Sour: pisco, lime, syrup, egg white and a dash of bitters. Egg white makes a silky foam; aquafaba is the vegan alternative.":"短酸酒建立在三重奏上：強、酸、甜，搖盪後呈現輕盈、幾乎起泡的質地。Daiquiri：蘭姆酒、萊姆和簡易糖漿。Whiskey Sour：Bourbon 或黑麥威士忌、檸檬和糖漿，可選擇加蛋白和苦精。Pisco Sour：Pisco、萊姆、糖漿、蛋白和幾滴苦精。蛋白帶來絲滑的泡沫；鷹嘴豆水（aquafaba）是純素替代品。","syrup":"糖漿","Bourbon or rye":"Bourbon 或黑麥威士忌","egg white":"蛋白","vegan: aquafaba":"純素：鷹嘴豆水","Sour variations":"酸酒的變化版","Variations change the sweetener, the sour ingredient or both. In the Sidecar, Cognac meets lemon and triple sec, an orange liqueur that replaces the syrup. The Margarita uses tequila, lime and triple sec, with an optional salt rim. The Clover Club combines gin, lemon and raspberry syrup with egg white: same pattern, different colour.":"變化版會改變甜味劑、酸味材料，或兩者都改。在 Sidecar 中，Cognac 遇上檸檬和 triple sec，這種柳橙利口酒取代了糖漿。Margarita 使用 Tequila、萊姆和 triple sec，可選擇加鹽邊。Clover Club 結合了琴酒、檸檬、覆盆子糖漿和蛋白：同樣的模式，不同的顏色。","salt (optional)":"鹽（可選）","raspberry syrup":"覆盆子糖漿","The highball is the simplest mixed drink: a spirit and a non-alcoholic mixer, served long over cubed ice, like gin and tonic or whisky and soda. Some have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice, where the slightly bitter, sour juice acts as the modifier.":"高球是最簡單的混合飲料：一種烈酒加一種無酒精調和飲料，加入方塊冰做成長飲，例如琴通寧或威士忌蘇打。有些高球有自己的名字。Cuba Libre 是蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆。Greyhound 是伏特加和葡萄柚汁，微苦帶酸的果汁扮演修飾材料的角色。","spirit + mixer":"烈酒 + 調和飲料","grapefruit juice":"葡萄柚汁","grapefruit = modifier":"葡萄柚 = 修飾材料","Horse's Neck and Americano":"Horse's Neck 與 Americano","Other highballs add a detail. The Horse's Neck combines Cognac, ginger ale and bitters: a bitter accent on top of spirit and mixer. The Americano has a split base: sweet red vermouth and a red bitter spirit together, topped with club soda. Lighter than a Negroni, it is almost a lengthened Negroni without the gin.":"其他高球會多加一個細節。Horse's Neck 結合了 Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精：在烈酒和調和飲料之上再加一點苦味點綴。Americano 有分拆基底：甜紅香艾酒和一種紅色苦味烈酒合起來，再補滿蘇打水。它比 Negroni 清淡，幾乎就是去掉琴酒、延長版的 Negroni。","club soda":"蘇打水","long Negroni, no gin":"延長版 Negroni，不含琴酒","A long sour is a short sour made long. The Tom Collins is the model: gin, lemon and simple syrup over ice, topped with club soda. Swap the soda and the family grows: the Paloma pairs tequila and lime with a grapefruit soda, while the French 75 tops Cognac or gin, lemon and syrup with Champagne.":"長酸酒就是延長的短酸酒。Tom Collins 是範本：琴酒、檸檬和簡易糖漿倒在冰塊上，再補滿蘇打水。換掉蘇打水，這個家族就擴大了：Paloma 把 Tequila 和萊姆與葡萄柚汽水搭配，French 75 則在 Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬和糖漿上補上 Champagne。","+ club soda":"+ 蘇打水","+ grapefruit soda":"+ 葡萄柚汽水","Cognac or gin":"Cognac 或琴酒","Mojito and Singapore Sling":"Mojito 與 Singapore Sling","Some long sours are enriched with extra ingredients. The Mojito stays simple: rum, lime and sugar or syrup, with mint leaves that make it fresh and fragrant. The Singapore Sling is more complex: gin and lime, sweetened with a cherry liqueur and a herbal liqueur, with a dash of aromatic bitters and a final top of club soda.":"有些長酸酒會加入額外的材料。Mojito 保持簡單：蘭姆酒、萊姆和糖或糖漿，加上讓它清新芬芳的薄荷葉。Singapore Sling 則較複雜：琴酒和萊姆，以櫻桃利口酒和草本利口酒加甜，再加幾滴芳香苦精，最後補滿蘇打水。","sugar or syrup":"糖或糖漿","cherry liqueur":"櫻桃利口酒","herbal liqueur":"草本利口酒","bitters + soda":"苦精 + 蘇打水","Welcome to the first lesson of the course. Before we meet Cognac, whisky or rum, we need the map that explains them all. In this lesson we look at the four steps that every spirit goes through, at the difference between fermentation and distillation, and at the two kinds of still that distillers use: the pot still and the column still. Once these ideas are clear, almost every bottle on a bar shelf starts to make sense.":"歡迎來到課程的第一堂課。在認識 Cognac、威士忌或蘭姆酒之前，我們需要一張能解釋所有烈酒的地圖。這堂課我們要看每款烈酒都會經歷的四個步驟、發酵與蒸餾的差別，以及蒸餾師使用的兩種蒸餾器：壺式蒸餾器和柱式蒸餾器。一旦這些概念清楚了，酒吧架上幾乎每一瓶酒都會開始變得有道理。","So, what is a spirit? Put simply, it is an alcoholic drink whose strength has been raised by distillation. But distillation is only one part of the story. Every spirit, from the lightest vodka to the oldest brandy, follows the same four steps. First, the raw material is prepared. Second, it is fermented. Third, it is distilled. And fourth, the producer decides what happens after distillation. That fourth step has a lesson of its own, the next one. Today we focus on the first three.":"那麼，什麼是烈酒？簡單來說，它是經由蒸餾提高酒精濃度的酒精飲料。但蒸餾只是故事的一部分。每款烈酒，從最清淡的伏特加到最老的白蘭地，都遵循同樣的四個步驟。第一，準備原料。第二，發酵。第三，蒸餾。第四，由生產者決定蒸餾之後要做什麼。第四步有自己的一堂課，也就是下一堂。今天我們專注在前三步。","Step one: preparing the raw material. The goal is simple: to obtain a sugary liquid, because without sugar there can be no fermentation. The raw material must come from a plant. In theory any plant will do, but in practice only a handful are used, such as grapes, grains, sugar cane, agave and potatoes. Some, like grapes or sugar cane, already contain sugar that is easy to extract. Others, like grains, contain no sugar at all and must be processed to create it. And each raw material gives the spirit its own family of aromas.":"第一步：準備原料。目標很簡單：取得含糖液體，因為沒有糖就不可能發酵。原料必須來自植物。理論上任何植物都可以，但實際上只會用到少數幾種，例如葡萄、穀物、甘蔗、龍舌蘭和馬鈴薯。有些植物，像葡萄或甘蔗，本身就含有容易萃取的糖。其他植物，像穀物，完全不含糖，必須經過處理才能產生糖。而且每種原料都為烈酒帶來自己的香氣家族。","Step two: fermentation. Here a tiny living organism does the work: yeast. Yeast is added to the sugary liquid and feeds on the sugar. In return it produces two things: ethanol, the alcohol the distiller is after, and carbon dioxide, a gas that simply escapes as waste. When fermentation is over, the liquid usually contains between eight and ten percent alcohol by volume, roughly the strength of a strong beer. And yeast gives a bonus: it creates new aromas, especially fruity ones.":"第二步：發酵。在這裡，負責工作的是一種微小的生物：酵母。酵母被加入含糖液體中，以糖為食。作為回報，它產生兩樣東西：乙醇，也就是蒸餾師想要的酒精；以及二氧化碳，一種直接散逸的廢氣。發酵結束時，液體的酒精濃度通常在百分之八到十之間，大約是烈性啤酒的濃度。而且酵母還附贈一份禮物：它會產生新的香氣，尤其是果香。","A quick word on that expression, alcohol by volume. It tells you what share of a liquid is alcohol. If a spirit is forty percent alcohol by volume, then forty percent of what is in the glass is pure alcohol and the rest is mostly water. You will hear this measure throughout the course, so it is worth getting comfortable with it now.":"簡單說一下「酒精濃度」（alcohol by volume）這個說法。它告訴你液體中有多少比例是酒精。如果一款烈酒的酒精濃度是百分之四十，那麼杯中百分之四十是純酒精，其餘大部分是水。整個課程中你都會聽到這個單位，所以現在就值得先熟悉它。","Step three: distillation, the step that actually creates a spirit. Its aim is to concentrate the alcohol made during fermentation. The trick relies on one simple fact: alcohol boils at a lower temperature than water. So when the fermented liquid is heated to boiling, the vapours that rise contain a higher proportion of alcohol than the liquid left behind. These vapours are collected and cooled, and they turn back into a liquid that is stronger than the one we started with. Here is the key idea: fermentation makes the alcohol, distillation concentrates it.":"第三步：蒸餾，真正創造出烈酒的步驟。它的目的是濃縮發酵時產生的酒精。這個技巧依據的是一個簡單的事實：酒精的沸點比水低。所以把發酵液加熱到沸騰時，升起的蒸氣所含的酒精比例比留下的液體更高。這些蒸氣被收集並冷卻後，就會變回比原本更烈的液體。關鍵概念是：發酵產生酒精，蒸餾將它濃縮。","How strong is a spirit when it first comes off the still? Anywhere from about sixty to ninety-six percent. And this strength matters enormously for flavour. The lower the distillation strength, the more intense the aromas. The higher the strength, the fewer aromas survive. At ninety-six percent there is so little aroma left that the spirit is called neutral. Picture a radio playing in a noisy room: the louder the alcohol, the fainter the music of the aromas.":"烈酒剛離開蒸餾器時有多烈？大約從百分之六十到九十六都有可能。而這個濃度對風味影響極大。蒸餾濃度越低，香氣越濃郁。濃度越高，留下的香氣越少。到了百分之九十六，剩下的香氣少到這種烈酒被稱為中性。想像一台在嘈雜房間裡播放的收音機：酒精的音量越大，香氣的音樂就越微弱。","Now the stills. There are two types: pot stills and column stills. There are hundreds of designs, but each type has features in common. A pot still has three parts: a pot sitting on a heat source, a condenser that is kept cold, and a pipe linking the two. The liquid boils in the pot, the vapours climb up and pass into the condenser, often a coiled tube sitting in cold water, where they turn back into liquid. The stills used for Cognac are heated by gas burners; most modern pot stills use steam.":"接下來是蒸餾器。有兩種類型：壺式蒸餾器和柱式蒸餾器。設計有數百種，但每種類型都有共同的特徵。壺式蒸餾器有三個部分：放在熱源上的蒸餾鍋、保持冰冷的冷凝器，以及連接兩者的管子。液體在蒸餾鍋中沸騰，蒸氣往上爬並進入冷凝器，冷凝器通常是一段泡在冷水中的盤管，蒸氣在那裡變回液體。Cognac 使用的蒸餾器以瓦斯爐火加熱；大多數現代壺式蒸餾器則使用蒸汽。","The pot still works in batches. Think of a washing machine: you load it, run the cycle, then empty it and clean it before the next load. It cannot run continuously. And one pass is not enough to make a spirit, so most distillers who use pot stills distil twice. This is called double pot still distillation. The fermented liquid starts at about ten percent; after the first distillation it is about twenty-five percent; after the second, about seventy-five. The result is a fairly low-strength spirit, with medium to pronounced aromas and plenty of character and complexity.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作。想想洗衣機：裝入衣物、運轉一個循環，然後在下一批之前清空並清洗。它無法連續運轉。而且蒸餾一次不足以製成烈酒，所以大多數使用壺式蒸餾器的蒸餾師會蒸餾兩次。這稱為壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾。發酵液一開始大約是百分之十；第一次蒸餾後大約百分之二十五；第二次蒸餾後大約百分之七十五。成果是濃度相當低的烈酒，香氣中等至濃郁，充滿個性和複雜度。","The pot still has two limits: it works one batch at a time, and it can never make a very strong spirit, say ninety percent or more, however many times you distil. The answer to both problems was the column still. It is a tall, vertical structure divided into sections. Hot alcoholic vapour enters at the bottom and rises, while liquid runs down. In effect, many distillations are stacked on top of one another, all happening at once. The higher the vapour climbs, the stronger it becomes, and the spirit leaves near the top. Because it never has to be emptied, a column still runs continuously and quickly.":"壺式蒸餾器有兩個限制：它一次只能處理一批，而且不論蒸餾多少次，都永遠無法製作出非常烈的烈酒，例如百分之九十以上。這兩個問題的答案就是柱式蒸餾器。它是一種分成多層的高聳直立式結構。含酒精的熱蒸氣從底部進入並上升，液體則往下流。實際上，就是許多次蒸餾疊在一起，全部同時進行。蒸氣爬得越高就變得越烈，烈酒則從靠近頂部的地方流出。因為從不需要清空，柱式蒸餾器能連續而快速地運轉。","Not all columns give the same result, and this is a favourite exam trap. A short column with few sections makes a lower-strength spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, quite close to a pot still spirit. A tall column with many sections reaches high strengths and gives a light spirit. And the tallest columns, with the most sections, reach ninety-five or ninety-six percent and produce a neutral spirit. So remember: a column still does not automatically mean a light spirit. Its height, and the strength it reaches, decide.":"並非所有蒸餾柱都會得到相同的結果，這是考試中最愛出的陷阱之一。層數少的矮蒸餾柱製作出濃度較低、香氣中等或濃郁的烈酒，相當接近壺式蒸餾器的烈酒。層數多的高蒸餾柱能達到高濃度，得到清淡的烈酒。而層數最多的最高蒸餾柱能達到百分之九十五或九十六，產出中性烈酒。所以記住：柱式蒸餾器並不自動代表清淡的烈酒。決定結果的是它的高度，以及它達到的濃度。","Here is a memory tip. Think of the pot still as a lift and the column still as an escalator. The lift stops, opens, empties and starts again: that is batch distillation, slower, but it carries plenty of flavour. The escalator never stops: that is continuous distillation, and the higher it climbs, the lighter the spirit becomes.":"這裡有個記憶小訣竅。把壺式蒸餾器想成電梯，把柱式蒸餾器想成手扶梯。電梯會停下、開門、清空，然後再出發：這就是批次蒸餾，比較慢，但能載著大量風味。手扶梯從不停止：這就是連續蒸餾，而且爬得越高，烈酒就變得越清淡。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, every spirit follows four steps: prepare the raw material, ferment it, distil it, and finish it after distillation. Second, fermentation makes the alcohol, at around eight to ten percent, and distillation concentrates it: the lower the distillation strength, the more flavour remains. Third, the pot still works in batches and gives low-strength, flavourful spirits, while the column still runs continuously and, depending on its height, gives anything from flavourful to light or completely neutral spirits.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，每款烈酒都遵循四個步驟：準備原料、發酵、蒸餾，以及蒸餾後的收尾處理。第二，發酵產生酒精，大約百分之八到十，蒸餾則將它濃縮：蒸餾濃度越低，留下的風味越多。第三，壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，得到低濃度、風味豐富的烈酒；柱式蒸餾器則連續運轉，視高度而定，可以得到從風味豐富到清淡、甚至完全中性的烈酒。","In the last lesson we followed a spirit up to the moment it leaves the still. Now we look at what gives it its flavour, its sweetness and its colour. We will see where aromas come from, what oak does, why producers blend, how other flavours can be added, where sweetness and colour really come from, and why almost every spirit meets water before it is bottled. This fourth step is where two very similar spirits can end up worlds apart.":"上一堂課，我們跟著烈酒走到它離開蒸餾器的那一刻。現在我們來看是什麼賦予它風味、甜味和顏色。我們會看到香氣從哪裡來、橡木桶有什麼作用、生產者為什麼要調和、如何加入其他風味、甜味和顏色真正的來源，以及為什麼幾乎每款烈酒在裝瓶前都會遇到水。在這第四步，兩款非常相似的烈酒最後可能天差地遠。","First, flavour. It is built in layers. The raw material lays the foundation: grapes bring fruity and floral notes, barley brings cereal notes, agave brings herbal and peppery ones. Fermentation then adds more aromas, mostly fruity, created by the yeast. Finally, distillation decides how much of all this survives. Distil to a low strength and the aromas stay intense; distil to a very high strength and they almost disappear. Think of three sieves, one after the other, each letting more or less character through.":"首先是風味。它是一層一層建立起來的。原料打下基礎：葡萄帶來果香和花香，大麥帶來穀物氣息，龍舌蘭帶來草本和胡椒氣息。接著發酵增添更多香氣，主要是酵母產生的果香。最後由蒸餾決定這一切能留下多少。蒸餾到低濃度，香氣保持濃郁；蒸餾到極高濃度，香氣幾乎消失。想像三個前後相接的篩子，每一個都讓或多或少的個性通過。","Now a fact that surprises many people: every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry, meaning it contains no sugar at all. Whatever colour or sweetness you find later was added afterwards. So the aim of this fourth step is to adjust colour, aroma, sweetness and strength to suit the style being made. There are three broad paths: the spirit can stay unaged, it can be aged in oak, or it can be flavoured with something other than oak. Often the law makes the choice: Scotch whisky must be aged in oak, while Tequila may be aged or left unaged.":"接下來是一個讓許多人驚訝的事實：每款烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是無色、不甜的，也就是完全不含糖。你之後發現的任何顏色或甜味，都是後來才加入的。所以這第四步的目的，是依照要製作的風格調整顏色、香氣、甜度和濃度。大致有三條路：烈酒可以保持未陳年、可以在橡木桶中陳年，也可以用橡木以外的東西調味。法律經常替生產者做了選擇：Scotch 威士忌必須在橡木桶中陳年，而 Tequila 則可陳年也可不陳年。","Let's start with unaged spirits. To keep the clear look and the aromas that came off the still, the producer stores the spirit for a short time in stainless steel tanks. Steel is like a blank sheet of paper: it gives nothing and takes nothing. These spirits can still be sweetened or have their strength adjusted, and colour can even be added just before bottling, as we will see in a moment.":"我們從未陳年的烈酒開始。為了保留離開蒸餾器時的清澈外觀和香氣，生產者會把烈酒短暫存放在不鏽鋼桶槽中。不鏽鋼就像一張白紙：什麼都不給，也什麼都不拿。這些烈酒仍然可以加甜或調整濃度，甚至可以在裝瓶前加入顏色，我們等一下就會看到。","Oak ageing, also called maturation, is a very different story. The spirit rests in oak barrels, usually for years, and the wood adds both colour and aroma. The colour follows a set sequence: first lemon, then gold, then amber and, in very rare cases, brown. How much colour the spirit picks up depends on two things: the barrel and the time. A newer barrel and a longer stay give a deeper colour.":"橡木桶陳年，也稱為熟成，則是完全不同的故事。烈酒在橡木桶中靜置，通常長達數年，木頭會同時增添顏色和香氣。顏色依照固定的順序變化：先是檸檬黃，然後金黃，再來是琥珀色，極少數情況會變成棕色。烈酒吸收多少顏色取決於兩件事：酒桶和時間。桶越新、待得越久，顏色就越深。","Oak also brings aromas: vanilla, cinnamon, cloves and coconut. A new barrel, one that has never been used, gives the most. Once a barrel has been emptied and filled again, it is called an old barrel, and it gives less aroma. With every use it gives a little less again, just like a tea bag dipped in a second and then a third cup. So a producer who wants a bold oak imprint chooses new barrels, and one who wants a gentle touch chooses old ones.":"橡木桶也會帶來香氣：香草、肉桂、丁香和椰子。從未使用過的新桶帶來的最多。酒桶一旦被清空並重新裝填，就稱為舊桶，帶來的香氣會比較少。每使用一次就再少一點，就像一個茶包泡了第二杯、第三杯。所以想要大膽橡木印記的生產者會選擇新桶，想要溫和影響的則選擇舊桶。","Time adds something else. During maturation, some water and some alcohol slowly evaporate through the wood, so what remains in the barrel becomes more concentrated. And after a very long time, often decades, new aromas appear: fruit cake, dried fruit, leather and wood polish. These add layer upon layer of complexity, which is why a very old spirit seems to keep revealing something new.":"時間還會增添別的東西。熟成期間，部分水和酒精會慢慢透過木頭蒸發，所以留在桶中的部分會變得更濃縮。經過非常長的時間，通常是數十年，會出現新的香氣：水果蛋糕、果乾、皮革和木頭亮光蠟。這些香氣增添了一層又一層的複雜度，這就是為什麼非常老的烈酒似乎總能不斷展現新的面貌。","Next comes blending, a key stage for oak-aged spirits. No two barrels are exactly alike, even if they were filled with the same spirit on the same day. The blender's job is to combine the contents of many barrels into batches for a brand, and there are two aims. The first is consistency: people expect the same bottle to taste the same every time. The second is complexity: an extraordinary single barrel is rare, so the easiest way to build depth is to mix spirits with different characters. The more types of spirit a blender has to work with, the easier this becomes.":"接下來是調和，這是橡木桶陳年烈酒的關鍵階段。沒有兩個酒桶是完全相同的，即使它們在同一天裝入同一種烈酒。調和師的工作是把許多酒桶的內容物結合成一個品牌的批次，目的有兩個。第一是一致性：人們期待同一瓶酒每次喝起來都一樣。第二是複雜度：非凡的單一酒桶很少見，所以建立深度最簡單的方法，就是混合不同個性的烈酒。調和師可運用的烈酒種類越多，這件事就越容易。","Some spirits are flavoured with something other than oak, such as fruits, seeds, herbs and spices. There are three main techniques. Redistillation: the spirit is distilled again with these ingredients, giving a flavoured but colourless spirit. Maceration: the ingredients soak in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, and give it flavour and colour. Or ready-made flavourings are simply added. We will come back to all of this in the lesson on flavoured spirits.":"有些烈酒會用橡木以外的東西調味，例如水果、種子、香草和香料。主要有三種技術。再蒸餾：把烈酒與這些原料一起再蒸餾一次，得到有風味但無色的烈酒。浸漬：原料浸泡在烈酒中，就像冷泡花草茶，為它帶來風味和顏色。或者直接加入現成的調味料。我們會在調味烈酒那一堂課再回來談這些。","Now sweetness. Since every spirit leaves the still dry, any sweetness you taste was added later, and in most cases it is simply sugar. Be careful with the word: in this course, sweet means the taste of sugar on the palate, nothing else. A Bourbon, for example, has vanilla and fruity aromas that people often call sweet, yet it has no added sugar. It is dry. A sweet smell and a sweet taste are not the same thing.":"接下來是甜味。既然每款烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是不甜的，你嚐到的任何甜味都是之後加入的，大多數情況下就是糖。小心這個詞：在這門課中，「甜」指的是口中糖的味道，沒有別的意思。例如 Bourbon 有香草和果香，人們常說它很甜，但它沒有加糖。它是不甜的。聞起來甜美和嚐起來甜，不是同一回事。","And colour. Oak is the most obvious source. Then there is caramel colour. Because barrels give different shades, blenders sometimes add a very small amount of caramel so that every batch looks the same. Used correctly, caramel colour is not sweet and adds no aroma. Some spirits get all or nearly all of their colour from it, so even an unaged spirit can be deeply coloured. Finally, other natural or artificial colourings are used too, especially in liqueurs, sometimes in very bright shades.":"還有顏色。橡木桶是最明顯的來源。接著是焦糖色。因為不同的桶會帶來不同的色調，調和師有時會加入極少量的焦糖色，讓每一批看起來都一樣。正確使用時，焦糖色不甜，也不會增添香氣。有些烈酒的顏色全部或幾乎全部來自焦糖色，所以即使是未陳年的烈酒也可能顏色很深。最後，也會使用其他天然或人工色素，尤其是在利口酒中，有時是非常鮮豔的色調。","The very last step before bottling is dilution. The vast majority of spirits are brought down to forty percent alcohol by volume by adding completely pure water. Why? To make them drinkable: very high alcohol numbs the palate, so you could neither taste nor enjoy the spirit. This pure water adds no flavour; it only lowers the strength.":"裝瓶前的最後一步是稀釋。絕大多數烈酒會加入完全純淨的水，降到酒精濃度百分之四十。為什麼？為了讓它們適合飲用：極高的酒精會麻痺味覺，讓你既無法品嚐也無法享受烈酒。這些純水不會增添風味，只會降低濃度。","Here is the memorable tip for this lesson: colour is not proof of age, and a sweet smell is not proof of sugar. A dark spirit may owe its colour to caramel rather than to years in oak, and a dry spirit may smell of vanilla and fruit. When in doubt, ask how the spirit was made.":"這堂課的記憶小訣竅是：顏色不能證明年份，聞起來甜美也不能證明有糖。一款深色烈酒的顏色可能來自焦糖色，而不是在橡木桶中的歲月；一款不甜的烈酒也可能聞起來有香草和水果味。有疑問時，就問問這款烈酒是如何製作的。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, flavour comes from the raw material, from fermentation and from distillation strength, and every newly made spirit is colourless and dry. Second, after the still a spirit can stay unaged in steel, be aged in new or old oak, which adds colour and aromas, or be flavoured; blending brings consistency and complexity. Third, sweetness always comes from added sugar, colour comes from oak, caramel or other colourings, and most spirits are diluted with pure water to forty percent.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，風味來自原料、發酵和蒸餾濃度，而每一款剛製成的烈酒都是無色、不甜的。第二，離開蒸餾器之後，烈酒可以在不鏽鋼中保持未陳年、在新桶或舊桶中陳年以增添顏色和香氣，或經過調味；調和則帶來一致性和複雜度。第三，甜味一定來自添加的糖，顏色來自橡木桶、焦糖色或其他色素，而大多數烈酒會用純水稀釋到百分之四十。","Welcome to our first spirit family: grape brandy. A grape brandy is, quite simply, a wine that has been distilled, and the best known of all is Cognac, from south-west France. In this lesson we follow Cognac through the four steps we already know: where its grapes come from and how they become wine, why the law insists on pot stills, what oak and blending bring, and the three age terms you will find on the label.":"歡迎來到我們的第一個烈酒家族：葡萄白蘭地。葡萄白蘭地很簡單，就是經過蒸餾的葡萄酒，其中最知名的是來自法國西南部的 Cognac。這堂課我們要帶著 Cognac 走過已經熟悉的四個步驟：它的葡萄來自哪裡、如何變成葡萄酒、為什麼法律堅持使用壺式蒸餾器、橡木桶和調和帶來什麼，以及你會在酒標上看到的三個年份術語。","Step one, the raw material. Cognac must be made from grapes grown in a specific part of south-west France, north of the town of Bordeaux. Grapes from anywhere else cannot become Cognac, however carefully they are distilled. So the name is not a recipe that can be copied: it is an address. These grapes give Cognac its basic character, with fruity and floral aromas that you will still recognise in the glass years later.":"第一步，原料。Cognac 必須用種植在法國西南部、Bordeaux 市以北特定區域的葡萄製作。來自其他任何地方的葡萄都不能成為 Cognac，不論蒸餾得多麼用心。所以這個名稱不是可以複製的配方：它是一個地址。這些葡萄賦予 Cognac 基本的個性，帶有果香和花香，即使多年後你仍能在杯中認出它們。","Grapes are an easy raw material to work with, because their juice is already full of sugar. There is no need for complicated processing, as there is with grain. The grapes are simply pressed to release their juice. Picture a bunch of grapes on its way to becoming a bottle of wine: Cognac starts down exactly the same road.":"葡萄是很容易處理的原料，因為它的汁液本身就富含糖分。不需要像穀物那樣複雜的處理。只要壓榨葡萄釋出汁液就行了。想像一串正要變成一瓶葡萄酒的葡萄：Cognac 一開始走的正是同一條路。","Step two, fermentation. The sugary juice is fermented straight away, and the yeast turns its sugar into alcohol. The result is a wine. And this is the point to remember: what goes into the still is not grape juice and not grapes, but wine. Before it becomes Cognac, every drop of it has been wine. Halfway along the road, instead of heading for a glass, our bunch of grapes takes the turning towards the still.":"第二步，發酵。含糖的汁液立刻發酵，酵母把其中的糖轉化為酒精。結果就是葡萄酒。這是要記住的重點：進入蒸餾器的不是葡萄汁，也不是葡萄，而是葡萄酒。在成為 Cognac 之前，它的每一滴都曾經是葡萄酒。走到半路，我們這串葡萄沒有走向酒杯，而是轉向了蒸餾器。","Step three, distillation. For Cognac the law leaves no choice: the wine must be distilled twice in a pot still. Column stills are not allowed. As we saw earlier, the pot still works in batches: after each distillation it has to be emptied and cleaned before it can be filled again. It is slow and labour-intensive. The traditional Cognac still is heated by gas burners, and its condenser is a coiled tube sitting in cold water that is constantly refreshed.":"第三步，蒸餾。對 Cognac 來說，法律沒有留下選擇：葡萄酒必須在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次。不允許使用柱式蒸餾器。正如我們之前看到的，壺式蒸餾器以批次運作：每次蒸餾後都必須清空並清洗，才能再次裝填。這既緩慢又耗費人力。傳統的 Cognac 蒸餾器以瓦斯爐火加熱，冷凝器則是一段浸在持續更換的冷水中的盤管。","Why insist on so much effort? Because a pot still produces a spirit of relatively low strength, packed with flavour and character. That is exactly what Cognac needs: the fruity and floral aromas of the grapes carry through into the spirit instead of being stripped away. You could say that double distillation in a pot still protects the soul of the wine. It is the same reason pot stills are chosen for other characterful spirits too.":"為什麼堅持這麼費工？因為壺式蒸餾器產出的烈酒濃度相對較低，充滿風味和個性。這正是 Cognac 所需要的：葡萄的果香和花香延續到烈酒中，而不是被去除。可以說，壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾保護了葡萄酒的靈魂。其他有個性的烈酒選擇壺式蒸餾器，也是同樣的原因。","Step four, what happens after distillation. Fresh from the still, the spirit is colourless and cannot yet be called Cognac. The law says it must spend at least two years in oak barrels first. That time in wood gives Cognac its colour and adds aromas of vanilla and toast. Two years is only the minimum, though, and many Cognacs rest for much longer.":"第四步，蒸餾之後。剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒是無色的，還不能稱為 Cognac。法律規定它必須先在橡木桶中至少度過兩年。在木桶中的時間為 Cognac 帶來顏色，並增添香草和烘烤的香氣。不過兩年只是最低要求，許多 Cognac 會靜置得更久。","The finest Cognacs are aged for many years. As some water and alcohol evaporate through the wood, the spirit becomes very concentrated, and new aromas slowly develop: fruit cake, leather and wood polish. These are the signs of a long and patient maturation. If you ever smell a very old Cognac, try to find those three notes: they are the fingerprint of time. Then comes blending. Nearly all Cognacs are blends, made by combining spirits of different ages. Younger spirits bring freshness and fruit, older ones bring depth, and together they create extra complexity. The blender also aims for consistency, so that each bottle tastes like the last.":"最優秀的 Cognac 會陳年許多年。隨著部分水和酒精透過木頭蒸發，烈酒變得非常濃縮，新的香氣也慢慢發展出來：水果蛋糕、皮革和木頭亮光蠟。這些是長時間耐心熟成的標誌。如果你有機會聞到一款非常老的 Cognac，試著找出這三種氣息：它們是時間的指紋。接著是調和。幾乎所有 Cognac 都是調和的，結合了不同年份的烈酒。年輕的烈酒帶來清新感和果香，老的帶來深度，結合在一起則創造出額外的複雜度。調和師也追求一致性，讓每一瓶喝起來都和上一瓶一樣。","Before dilution and bottling, there are two more common touches. It is quite usual for producers to add a little caramel colour, to keep the shade the same from batch to batch, and to sweeten their Cognac slightly. Then, as with most spirits, it is diluted with pure water and bottled. So a Cognac can feel gently rounded on the palate, even though it left the still completely dry.":"在稀釋和裝瓶之前，還有兩個常見的處理。生產者加入少量焦糖色，讓每一批的色調保持一致，並為 Cognac 稍微加甜，這是相當普遍的做法。接著，和大多數烈酒一樣，用純水稀釋後裝瓶。所以即使 Cognac 離開蒸餾器時完全不甜，在口中仍可能感覺溫和圓潤。","Now the age terms, which are a favourite exam topic. Cognacs are grouped by age, and three labelling terms matter. Each one guarantees the age of the youngest spirit in the blend. VS means the youngest spirit is at least two years old. VSOP means at least four years. XO means at least ten years. Older spirits may be in the blend too, but the label always speaks for the youngest.":"接下來是年份術語，這是考試最愛的主題之一。Cognac 依年份分組，有三個重要的酒標術語。每一個都保證調和中最年輕烈酒的年份。VS 表示最年輕的烈酒至少兩年。VSOP 表示至少四年。XO 表示至少十年。調和中可能也有更老的烈酒，但酒標說的永遠是最年輕的那一個。","Here is the tip for this lesson. Think of a staircase with three steps: two, four and ten. And remember that the youngest spirit sets the step. Imagine a blend of a five-year-old spirit and a twenty-year-old spirit. The twenty-year-old does not count for the label: the youngest is five, so the blend can be called VSOP, but not XO.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：想像一座三階的樓梯：二、四、十。並記住，決定是哪一階的是最年輕的烈酒。想像一款由五年和二十年烈酒組成的調和。二十年的烈酒對酒標來說不算數：最年輕的是五年，所以這款調和可以稱為 VSOP，但不能稱為 XO。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Cognac is a grape brandy from a defined area north of Bordeaux; the grapes are pressed and the juice is fermented straight away into wine. Second, the law requires double distillation in a pot still, which gives a low-strength spirit full of flavour. Third, Cognac must spend at least two years in oak, most Cognacs are blends, often with a little caramel and sugar, and the age terms are VS for two years, VSOP for four and XO for ten, always counting the youngest spirit.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，Cognac 是一種葡萄白蘭地，來自 Bordeaux 以北的劃定產區；葡萄經壓榨，汁液立刻發酵成葡萄酒。第二，法律要求以壺式蒸餾器二次蒸餾，得到濃度低、風味飽滿的烈酒。第三，Cognac 必須在橡木桶中至少陳年兩年，大多數 Cognac 是調和的，常加入少量焦糖色和糖，年份術語則是 VS 兩年、VSOP 四年、XO 十年，一律以最年輕的烈酒計算。","In this lesson we meet vodka, the most widely mixed spirit behind any bar, and in many ways the opposite of the Cognac we have just studied. We will see what it can be made from, where it can be made, the one thing that really defines it, how it is finished after distillation, and the two styles you are likely to meet: the fully neutral vodka and the vodka that keeps a little character.":"這堂課我們要認識伏特加，任何酒吧中最常用來調酒的烈酒，而且在許多方面都與我們剛學過的 Cognac 相反。我們會看到它可以用什麼製作、可以在哪裡製作、真正定義它的那一件事、蒸餾後如何收尾，以及你可能會遇到的兩種風格：完全中性的伏特加，以及保留一點個性的伏特加。","Let's start with the big idea. With Cognac, almost everything is fixed: the place, the grape, the type of still. With vodka, almost nothing is. Vodka can be made anywhere in the world, and it can be made from any raw material. So what makes a spirit a vodka? Not the country, and not the plant. It is the strength to which it is distilled. Keep that in mind and the rest of the lesson falls into place.":"我們從大方向開始。Cognac 幾乎一切都是固定的：產地、葡萄、蒸餾器類型。伏特加則幾乎什麼都不固定。伏特加可以在世界任何地方製作，也可以用任何原料製作。那麼，是什麼讓一款烈酒成為伏特加？不是國家，也不是植物。而是它被蒸餾到的濃度。記住這一點，這堂課的其他內容就會水到渠成。","Step one, the raw material. Any plant-based raw material can be used, but some are traditionally linked with premium-quality vodka. These are grains, especially barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes. Whatever is chosen, it first has to be turned into a sugary liquid, because yeast needs sugar to work. Grains and potatoes are full of starch rather than sugar, so they must be processed first, much as we will see for whisky.":"第一步，原料。任何植物性原料都可以使用，但有些傳統上與高品質伏特加聯想在一起。這些是穀物，尤其是大麥、小麥和黑麥，以及馬鈴薯。不論選擇什麼，都必須先變成含糖液體，因為酵母需要糖才能工作。穀物和馬鈴薯充滿的是澱粉而不是糖，所以必須先經過處理，這部分我們在威士忌那一課也會看到。","Step two, fermentation. Once the sugary liquid is ready, yeast is added and fermentation takes place, exactly as for every other spirit. The yeast turns the sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide, and it creates some fruity aromas too. But for vodka, most of those aromas are not destined to last, because of what happens next.":"第二步，發酵。含糖液體準備好之後，加入酵母進行發酵，和其他所有烈酒完全一樣。酵母把糖轉化為酒精和二氧化碳，也會產生一些果香。但對伏特加來說，這些香氣大多注定不會留下，原因就在於接下來發生的事。","Step three, distillation, the heart of vodka. Vodka is a diluted neutral spirit. To count as neutral, a spirit must be distilled to at least ninety-five or ninety-six percent alcohol by volume. Which of the two depends on the law of the country where it is produced. Such a high strength can only be reached in a column still, the tall kind with many sections. Some producers do use pot stills for part of the process, but a pot still alone could never reach neutral strength.":"第三步，蒸餾，伏特加的核心。伏特加是稀釋過的中性烈酒。要算是中性，烈酒必須蒸餾到至少百分之九十五或九十六的酒精濃度。是哪一個數字，取決於生產國的法律。這麼高的濃度只能在柱式蒸餾器中達到，也就是層數很多的那種高蒸餾柱。有些生產者確實會在部分流程中使用壺式蒸餾器，但光靠壺式蒸餾器永遠無法達到中性的濃度。","Why the word neutral? Remember the rule from our first lessons: the higher the distillation strength, the fewer aromas survive. At ninety-five or ninety-six percent, a spirit has virtually no flavour left. The fruity notes of fermentation and most of the character of the raw material have been left behind in the still. That is not a fault: for vodka, it is the goal.":"為什麼叫「中性」？記住我們前幾堂課的規則：蒸餾濃度越高，留下的香氣越少。在百分之九十五或九十六時，烈酒幾乎沒有任何風味留下。發酵的果香和原料的大部分個性都留在了蒸餾器裡。這不是缺陷：對伏特加來說，這正是目標。","Step four, after distillation. Vodka is not aged in oak, so it gets no colour and no aromas from wood. It stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water down to bottling strength, typically forty percent alcohol by volume. That is why we call it a diluted neutral spirit: neutral when it leaves the still, diluted before it reaches the bottle.":"第四步，蒸餾之後。伏特加不在橡木桶中陳年，所以不會從木頭得到顏色或香氣。它保持未陳年、清澈透明。接著用純水稀釋到裝瓶濃度，通常是酒精濃度百分之四十。這就是為什麼我們稱它為稀釋過的中性烈酒：離開蒸餾器時是中性的，進入酒瓶前經過稀釋。","That same neutral spirit has another life, too. As we will see in the lesson on flavoured spirits, most gins, flavoured vodkas and liqueurs start from neutral spirit diluted with water, the very same base that becomes vodka. So understanding vodka also opens the door to a large part of the bar shelf.":"同樣的中性烈酒還有另一段人生。我們會在調味烈酒那一課看到，大多數琴酒、調味伏特加和利口酒，都是以加水稀釋的中性烈酒為起點，正是成為伏特加的同一個基底。所以理解伏特加，也就打開了通往酒架上一大部分烈酒的大門。","Now the styles. Most vodka is made to be as neutral as possible, and this neutrality is exactly what has made it so popular. In mixed drinks and cocktails it adds alcohol without imposing its own flavour, so juices, sodas and liqueurs stay centre stage. Think of it as a blank canvas: the bartender paints on it with other ingredients.":"接下來是風格。大多數伏特加的製作目標是盡可能中性，而正是這種中性讓它如此受歡迎。在混合飲料和調酒中，它增加酒精而不強加自己的風味，讓果汁、汽水和利口酒保持在舞台中央。把它想成一張空白畫布：調酒師用其他材料在上面作畫。","Some vodkas, however, keep a little character. On the nose and on the palate you may notice faint hints of the raw material, such as a touch of grain or of potato. These flavours remain very light compared with those of a whisky or a brandy, and these vodkas are still correctly described as neutral. The difference is subtle, a bit like the difference between two still mineral waters tasted side by side.":"不過，有些伏特加保留了一點個性。在香氣和口中，你可能會注意到淡淡的原料氣息，例如一絲穀物或馬鈴薯。與威士忌或白蘭地相比，這些風味仍然非常清淡，這些伏特加仍可正確地描述為中性。差別很細微，有點像並排品嚐兩款無氣泡礦泉水時的差異。","Watch out for a few classic exam traps. Vodka does not have to be made from potatoes, nor from grain: any raw material is allowed. It does not have to come from any particular country. It cannot be made to neutral strength in a pot still alone. And it is unaged, not matured in oak. Here is the tip for this lesson: for vodka, think strength, not place and not plant. If you remember that a vodka is defined by being distilled to neutral strength, ninety-five or ninety-six percent, you can answer almost any question about it.":"小心幾個經典的考試陷阱。伏特加不一定要用馬鈴薯製作，也不一定要用穀物：任何原料都可以。它不一定要來自特定國家。光靠壺式蒸餾器無法製作出中性濃度的伏特加。而且它是未陳年的，不在橡木桶中熟成。這堂課的小訣竅是：說到伏特加，想的是濃度，而不是產地或植物。只要記住伏特加的定義是蒸餾到百分之九十五或九十六的中性濃度，關於它的問題幾乎都能回答。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, vodka can be made anywhere, from any raw material, although grains such as barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes, are linked with premium vodka. Second, it is a neutral spirit distilled to at least ninety-five or ninety-six percent in a column still, then left unaged and diluted, typically to forty percent. Third, most vodka is as neutral as possible, which makes it so versatile in cocktails, while some keep faint hints of their raw material and are still called neutral.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，伏特加可以在任何地方、用任何原料製作，不過大麥、小麥和黑麥等穀物，以及馬鈴薯，與高級伏特加聯想在一起。第二，它是在柱式蒸餾器中蒸餾到至少百分之九十五或九十六的中性烈酒，之後保持未陳年並經過稀釋，通常到百分之四十。第三，大多數伏特加盡可能中性，這讓它在調酒中用途廣泛，而有些則保留淡淡的原料氣息，仍被稱為中性。","Welcome to the world of whisky, spelled with or without an e depending on where it comes from. In this lesson we focus on Scotland. We will see how hard, dry grain is turned into a sugary liquid, the rules that every Scotch whisky must follow, what makes a Single Malt, where the famous smoky flavour comes from, and how Blended Scotch is built from two very different kinds of whisky.":"歡迎來到威士忌的世界，依產地不同，英文拼法有時是 whisky，有時多一個 e。這堂課我們聚焦在蘇格蘭。我們會看到堅硬乾燥的穀物如何變成含糖液體、每款 Scotch 威士忌都必須遵守的規定、什麼造就了 Single Malt、著名的煙燻風味從哪裡來，以及 Blended Scotch 如何由兩種截然不同的威士忌組成。","First, what is a whisky? It is an oak-aged spirit that must be made from grains. A handy way to picture it is as distilled beer: grain, water and yeast make a kind of beer, and the still does the rest. Whisky is made all over the world, but the best-known examples come from Scotland, the United States, Ireland, Canada and Japan. Each grain leaves its own mark: barley gives cereal aromas, corn gives sweetcorn aromas, and rye gives spicy, peppery aromas.":"首先，什麼是威士忌？它是一種必須用穀物製作、經橡木桶陳年的烈酒。一個方便的想像方式是把它當作蒸餾過的啤酒：穀物、水和酵母做出一種啤酒，蒸餾器則完成其餘的工作。世界各地都生產威士忌，但最知名的來自蘇格蘭、美國、愛爾蘭、加拿大和日本。每種穀物都留下自己的印記：大麥帶來穀物香氣，玉米帶來甜玉米香氣，黑麥則帶來辛香、胡椒般的香氣。","Grains pose a problem, though. They are dry and hard, and they are full of starch rather than sugar. Yeast cannot ferment starch, so it has to be converted into sugar first. The classic method is clever, because it lets the barley do almost all of the work itself. It starts with a process called malting.":"不過穀物有個問題。它們又乾又硬，充滿的是澱粉而不是糖。酵母無法發酵澱粉，所以必須先把它轉化為糖。經典做法很聰明，因為它讓大麥自己完成幾乎所有的工作。一切從一個叫做製麥的過程開始。","In malting, the barley grains are allowed to start growing. As they grow, they create natural substances called enzymes, tiny tools that are able to turn starch into sugar. At just the right moment, hot air is used to stop the growth. From now on the grain is called malted barley. It carries its own tools, but it has not used them yet.":"在製麥時，讓大麥粒開始生長。它們在生長時會產生稱為酵素的天然物質，這是能把澱粉轉化為糖的微小工具。在恰到好處的時刻，用熱空氣停止生長。從此穀粒就稱為麥芽大麥。它帶著自己的工具，但還沒有使用。","Next, the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, and other crushed grains can be added at this point too. Everything is mixed with warm water, and in this bath the enzymes made by the barley get to work, converting the starch into sugar. The result is a sugary liquid, ready for the yeast. So remember the sequence: grain, malting, crushing, warm water, and the enzymes turn starch into sugar.":"接著，把麥芽大麥碾成粗粉，此時也可以加入其他碾碎的穀物。全部與溫水混合，在這個水浴中，大麥產生的酵素開始工作，把澱粉轉化為糖。結果就是準備好迎接酵母的含糖液體。所以記住這個順序：穀物、製麥、碾碎、溫水，然後酵素把澱粉轉化為糖。","From here the path is familiar. Yeast is added and fermentation begins. For distillation, whisky producers use both pot stills and column stills, although in some cases the law limits their choice. After distillation, whiskies are aged in oak. When maturation is complete they are blended and, where it is allowed and needed, coloured with caramel. Most are then diluted to forty percent alcohol by volume before bottling.":"從這裡開始，路就很熟悉了。加入酵母，開始發酵。蒸餾時，威士忌生產者會使用壺式蒸餾器和柱式蒸餾器，不過在某些情況下，法律會限制他們的選擇。蒸餾後，威士忌在橡木桶中陳年。熟成完成後，經過調和，並在允許和需要時以焦糖色上色。大多數接著會稀釋到酒精濃度百分之四十再裝瓶。","Now, Scotland. All Scotch whisky must be distilled in Scotland and then aged in Scotland for a minimum of three years. Both conditions matter: a spirit made in Scotland but matured somewhere else cannot be called Scotch. Within Scotch there are two important types to know: Single Malt Scotch Whisky and Blended Scotch Whisky.":"現在來看蘇格蘭。所有 Scotch 威士忌都必須在蘇格蘭蒸餾，然後在蘇格蘭陳年至少三年。兩個條件都很重要：在蘇格蘭製作、卻在其他地方熟成的烈酒，不能稱為 Scotch。在 Scotch 之中，有兩種重要的類型要認識：Single Malt Scotch Whisky 和 Blended Scotch Whisky。","A Single Malt must meet three conditions. It is made from one hundred percent malted barley, with no other grains. It is distilled in pot stills. And it comes from one distillery. That is what the word single means here: one distillery, not one barrel and not one year. Because they come from pot stills, Single Malts are characterful spirits. On the nose and palate you can find cereal, fruits, flowers and honey and, with time in oak, fruit cake and sweet spices. Two Single Malts from two different distilleries can taste remarkably different.":"Single Malt 必須符合三個條件。它用百分之百的麥芽大麥製作，沒有其他穀物。它以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。而且它來自單一蒸餾廠。這就是「single」在這裡的意思：單一蒸餾廠，不是單一酒桶，也不是單一年份。因為來自壺式蒸餾器，Single Malt 是有個性的烈酒。在香氣和口中，你會發現穀物、水果、花香和蜂蜜，在橡木桶中陳年後，還有水果蛋糕和甜香料。來自兩家不同蒸餾廠的兩款 Single Malt，味道可能非常不同。","There is one more flavour sometimes found in these whiskies: smoke. It comes from peat, a natural fuel that is burned when the grains are heated at the end of malting. The smoke from the burning peat flavours the grains, and that flavour travels all the way into the glass. But do not assume every Single Malt is smoky: only a few have peat flavours, although in some of them the smoke is very pronounced.":"這些威士忌中有時還會出現另一種風味：煙燻。它來自泥煤，一種在製麥最後烘乾穀粒時燃燒的天然燃料。燃燒泥煤產生的煙為穀粒增添風味，這種風味會一路來到杯中。但不要以為每款 Single Malt 都有煙燻味：只有少數帶有泥煤風味，不過其中有些煙燻味非常明顯。","Scotland also makes a second kind of whisky: grain whisky. It is made from a mix of malted barley and other grains, and it is distilled in a column still. The result has a light aroma intensity and a smooth texture. Grain whisky is hardly ever sold on its own. Its real job is to go into blends.":"蘇格蘭也生產第二種威士忌：穀物威士忌。它用麥芽大麥和其他穀物混合製成，並以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾。結果香氣強度清淡，口感柔順。穀物威士忌幾乎從不單獨販售。它真正的工作是進入調和威士忌。","A Blended Scotch Whisky is a blend of malt whiskies and grain whiskies from different distilleries. Picture an orchestra: the malts are the soloists, intense and full of character, while the light, smooth grain whisky is the string section that holds everything together. Blenders add extra variety by using whiskies of different ages. Blends vary a great deal: some are medium in intensity and fairly simple, others are pronounced and complex. Typically, they are smoother than malt whiskies.":"Blended Scotch Whisky 是來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌的調和。想像一支管弦樂團：麥芽威士忌是獨奏者，濃郁而充滿個性，而清淡柔順的穀物威士忌則是把一切串連起來的弦樂部。調和師使用不同年份的威士忌來增添更多變化。調和威士忌差異很大：有些強度中等、相當簡單，有些則濃郁而複雜。一般來說，它們比麥芽威士忌更柔順。","Here is the tip for this lesson. For a Single Malt, count three ones: one grain, malted barley; one kind of still, the pot still; and one distillery. Break any of these and you are no longer looking at a Single Malt. A Blended Scotch, by contrast, mixes malt and grain whiskies from several distilleries.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：說到 Single Malt，數三個「一」：一種穀物，麥芽大麥；一種蒸餾器，壺式蒸餾器；一家蒸餾廠。打破其中任何一個，你看到的就不再是 Single Malt。相反地，Blended Scotch 則混合了來自多家蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, grains hold starch, so barley is malted, crushed and mixed with warm water, and its enzymes turn the starch into sugar. Second, every Scotch is distilled and aged for at least three years in Scotland. Third, a Single Malt is one hundred percent malted barley, from pot stills, from one distillery, sometimes smoky from peat; a Blended Scotch mixes malt whiskies with light, column-distilled grain whisky from different distilleries, and is usually smoother.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，穀物含有澱粉，所以大麥要經過製麥、碾碎並與溫水混合，它的酵素才會把澱粉轉化為糖。第二，每款 Scotch 都在蘇格蘭蒸餾，並在當地陳年至少三年。第三，Single Malt 是百分之百麥芽大麥、以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾、來自單一蒸餾廠，有時因泥煤而帶煙燻味；Blended Scotch 則混合了麥芽威士忌與來自不同蒸餾廠、以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾的清淡穀物威士忌，通常更柔順。","In the last lesson we stayed in Scotland. Now we cross the Atlantic. In this lesson we meet the three great American whiskeys, Bourbon, Tennessee whiskey and Rye, and see what sets each one apart. Then we take a short tour of three more whisky countries: Ireland, Canada and Japan. You will see that a few simple choices, the grain, the still, the barrel and one unusual filter, explain almost everything.":"上一堂課我們待在蘇格蘭。現在我們橫越大西洋。這堂課我們要認識三大美國威士忌：Bourbon、Tennessee 威士忌和 Rye，看看它們各有什麼不同。接著我們會快速走訪另外三個威士忌國家：愛爾蘭、加拿大和日本。你會發現，幾個簡單的選擇，也就是穀物、蒸餾器、酒桶，以及一道不尋常的過濾，就能解釋幾乎一切。","Let's begin with Bourbon, the best-known American whiskey. Many people link it with Kentucky, and Kentucky is indeed the number one state for production. But Bourbon can be made anywhere in the United States. Its style depends on three factors: the recipe of grains, the way it is distilled, and the type of barrel it is aged in. First, the grains. At least fifty-one percent of the grain used for Bourbon must be corn. The rest is usually made up of barley and rye. Corn brings its typical sweetcorn aromas, and since it is the main grain, those aromas are at the heart of Bourbon's character.":"我們從 Bourbon 開始，最知名的美國威士忌。許多人把它與肯塔基州聯想在一起，肯塔基州也確實是產量第一的州。但 Bourbon 可以在美國任何地方生產。它的風格取決於三個因素：穀物配方、蒸餾方式，以及陳年用的酒桶類型。首先是穀物。Bourbon 使用的穀物中至少百分之五十一必須是玉米。其餘通常是大麥和黑麥。玉米帶來典型的甜玉米香氣，而既然它是主要穀物，這些香氣就是 Bourbon 個性的核心。","Second, distillation. Bourbon is typically distilled in a column still, but only to a low strength. This is a good reminder of an idea from our first lessons: a column still does not automatically make a light spirit. Stop the distillation at a low strength and plenty of flavour survives. So Bourbon comes out of its column full of character.":"第二，蒸餾。Bourbon 通常以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，但只蒸餾到較低濃度。這很好地提醒了我們前幾堂課的一個概念：柱式蒸餾器並不自動代表清淡的烈酒。在較低濃度時停止蒸餾，就能保留大量風味。所以 Bourbon 離開蒸餾柱時充滿個性。","Third, the barrel. Bourbon has to be aged in new charred oak barrels, meaning barrels that have never been used and whose insides have been burned. As we know, a new barrel gives the most colour and aroma. Put all three factors together, and Bourbon has pronounced and complex flavours of sweetcorn, cereal, fruit, vanilla and coconut.":"第三，酒桶。Bourbon 必須在炙燒過的新橡木桶中陳年，也就是從未使用過、內部經過燒烤的酒桶。我們知道，新桶帶來最多的顏色和香氣。把這三個因素加在一起，Bourbon 就有了甜玉米、穀物、水果、香草和椰子等濃郁而複雜的風味。","A word of warning about one word. People often describe Bourbon as sweet. But Bourbon has no added sugar: it is dry. The vanilla, fruit and coconut aromas make the nose think of desserts, and that is where the confusion comes from. In this course, remember, sweet only means the taste of sugar on the palate.":"關於一個詞要提醒一下。人們常形容 Bourbon 很甜。但 Bourbon 沒有加糖：它是不甜的。香草、水果和椰子香氣讓鼻子聯想到甜點，混淆就是從這裡來的。在這門課中，記住，「甜」只指口中糖的味道。","Now Tennessee whiskey. It can only be made in the state of Tennessee, and it is made in the same way as Bourbon, with one key exception. Before it goes into the barrel, the newly made spirit is passed through a filter of maple charcoal. This charcoal does not make a very fine filter, but it does remove some impurities and helps to give the spirit a smoother character. And note this carefully: the filtering adds no flavour. No maple taste, no smoke.":"接下來是 Tennessee 威士忌。它只能在田納西州生產，製作方式和 Bourbon 相同，只有一個關鍵的例外。在入桶之前，剛製成的烈酒會通過一道楓木炭過濾。這種木炭過濾不算非常精細，但確實能去除部分雜質，讓烈酒的個性更柔順。請仔細注意：過濾不會增添任何風味。沒有楓糖味，也沒有煙燻味。","A simple image helps. Tennessee whiskey is like a Bourbon that takes a shower before going into the barrel. The shower happens to the new, colourless spirit, not to the finished whiskey. After that, the story continues just as it does for Bourbon. Then there is Rye whiskey, Bourbon's spicy cousin. It is made in exactly the same way as Bourbon, except that at least fifty-one percent of the grains used must be rye rather than corn. That single change makes a big difference: rye gives the whiskey spicy and peppery aromas. Where Bourbon leans towards sweetcorn and coconut, Rye has a sharper, livelier edge.":"一個簡單的比喻會有幫助。Tennessee 威士忌就像一款在進桶前先沖了個澡的 Bourbon。沖澡的是無色的新烈酒，而不是成品威士忌。之後的故事就和 Bourbon 一樣。接著是 Rye 威士忌，Bourbon 的辛香表親。它的製作方式和 Bourbon 完全相同，只是使用的穀物中至少百分之五十一必須是黑麥而不是玉米。光是這一個改變就帶來很大的差異：黑麥讓威士忌帶有辛香、胡椒般的香氣。Bourbon 偏向甜玉米和椰子，Rye 則更鮮明、更活潑。","Let's leave America and travel to Ireland. Most Irish whiskeys are made from a blend of pot still and column still spirits, and they are typically light and smooth. There are also pot-distilled whiskeys in Ireland, and some of them use an unusual ingredient: unmalted barley, meaning barley that has not been through malting. It gives a distinctive nutty and oily character.":"我們離開美國，前往愛爾蘭。大多數愛爾蘭威士忌是由壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒調和而成，通常清淡柔順。愛爾蘭也有以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾的威士忌，其中有些使用一種不尋常的原料：未發芽的大麥，也就是沒有經過製麥的大麥。它帶來獨特的堅果和油潤個性。","In Canada, whiskies are made from many different grains, and they are typically a blend of high-strength and low-strength spirits: the high-strength ones are lighter, the low-strength ones bring more flavour. In the best Canadian whiskies, one flavour stands out as a signature: rye, with its spicy, peppery notes.":"在加拿大，威士忌用許多不同的穀物製作，通常是高濃度和低濃度烈酒的調和：高濃度的較清淡，低濃度的帶來更多風味。在最優秀的加拿大威士忌中，有一種風味作為招牌脫穎而出：黑麥，帶著辛香、胡椒般的氣息。","And Japan. Japanese whisky production was modelled on the industry in Scotland, so Japan makes both malt and blended whiskies. The traditional style is elegant and refined. But new products are increasingly exploring new styles and flavours, so this is a category on the move. Here is the tip for this lesson, a quick way to sort American whiskeys. Mostly corn: Bourbon. Mostly corn plus a maple charcoal shower, made only in Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Mostly rye: Rye. And all three share low-strength column distillation and new charred oak.":"還有日本。日本威士忌的生產以蘇格蘭的產業為範本，所以日本同時生產麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。傳統風格優雅而細緻。但新產品越來越多地在探索新的風格和風味，所以這是一個持續變動中的類別。這堂課的小訣竅，是一個快速分類美國威士忌的方法。以玉米為主：Bourbon。以玉米為主，再加上楓木炭淋浴，只在田納西州生產：Tennessee 威士忌。以黑麥為主：Rye。而這三者都以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度，並使用炙燒過的新橡木桶。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Bourbon is at least fifty-one percent corn, distilled in a column still to a low strength and aged in new charred oak; it can be made anywhere in the United States, though Kentucky leads, and it is dry. Second, Tennessee whiskey is made like Bourbon but only in Tennessee, with maple charcoal filtering before the barrel, which smooths but adds no flavour; Rye is at least fifty-one percent rye and tastes spicy and peppery. Third, Ireland blends pot and column spirits and sometimes uses unmalted barley, Canada uses many grains with rye as its signature, and Japan follows the Scottish model.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，Bourbon 至少含百分之五十一的玉米，以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到較低濃度，並在炙燒過的新橡木桶中陳年；它可以在美國任何地方生產，不過肯塔基州居首，而且它是不甜的。第二，Tennessee 威士忌的製法和 Bourbon 相同，但只在田納西州生產，並在入桶前以楓木炭過濾，讓口感柔順卻不增添風味；Rye 至少含百分之五十一的黑麥，喝起來辛香、帶胡椒味。第三，愛爾蘭調和壺式和柱式蒸餾的烈酒，有時使用未發芽的大麥；加拿大使用多種穀物，以黑麥為招牌；日本則依循蘇格蘭模式。","In this lesson we head to the Caribbean to meet rum. Rum is one of the most varied spirit families, from light and discreet to dark and intense, and at first it can seem impossible to sort out. But we have a tool that works every time: the four steps of production. We will look at the two possible raw materials, the fruity aromas that fermentation can build, the choice of still, and everything that can happen after distillation.":"這堂課我們前往加勒比海，認識蘭姆酒。蘭姆酒是最多樣的烈酒家族之一，從清淡低調到深色濃郁都有，一開始可能看起來根本無法分類。但我們有一個每次都管用的工具：生產的四個步驟。我們會看看兩種可能的原料、發酵能建立的果香、蒸餾器的選擇，以及蒸餾之後可能發生的一切。","The raw material for rum is sugar cane. Sugar cane grows in countries with a hot climate, so that is where rum production is centred, and its classic heartland is the Caribbean. The Caribbean is made up of many small countries, each with its own traditions, rules and regulations. People have tried to classify rum by colour, or by the language spoken where it is made, but neither approach works well. Following the four stages of production is far more useful.":"蘭姆酒的原料是甘蔗。甘蔗生長在氣候炎熱的國家，所以蘭姆酒的生產集中在那裡，而它的經典核心地帶是加勒比海。加勒比海由許多小國組成，各有自己的傳統、規定和法規。人們曾嘗試依顏色，或依產地使用的語言來分類蘭姆酒，但兩種方法效果都不好。依循生產的四個階段要有用得多。","Step one gives the distiller a choice between two raw materials. The first is fresh cane juice. The sugar cane is harvested and crushed to release a sweet juice that can be fermented straight away. Rums made from cane juice often have a very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour, a bit like freshly cut grass. The best examples are rhum agricole, which, in the Caribbean, must be made in Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"第一步讓蒸餾師在兩種原料之間做選擇。第一種是新鮮甘蔗汁。甘蔗採收後被壓碎，釋出可以立刻發酵的甜汁液。以甘蔗汁製作的蘭姆酒，通常帶有非常明顯的青草、草本風味，有點像剛割下的青草。最好的例子是 rhum agricole，在加勒比海必須在馬丁尼克或瓜地洛普製作。","However, most Caribbean distillers use the second option: molasses. Molasses is a black, sticky substance, the by-product of the industry that turns sugar cane juice into sugar. Before fermentation can start, it must be mixed with water. Rums made from molasses have flavours of caramel and brown sugar, rounder and darker than the fresh, green notes of cane juice. So, cane juice means grassy; molasses means caramel and brown sugar.":"不過，大多數加勒比海蒸餾師選擇第二個選項：糖蜜。糖蜜是一種黑色黏稠的物質，是把甘蔗汁製成糖的產業留下的副產品。發酵開始之前，必須先與水混合。以糖蜜製作的蘭姆酒帶有焦糖和紅糖風味，比甘蔗汁清新的青綠氣息更圓潤、更深沉。所以，甘蔗汁代表青草氣息；糖蜜代表焦糖和紅糖。","Step two, fermentation. As always, yeast turns sugar into alcohol, but in rum the fermentation can also be used to create tropical fruit aromas, and sometimes they are very pronounced. When distillers set out to maximise the flavour created during fermentation, the result can be a rum with an intensely fruity set of flavours. Jamaican distillers are well known for producing this style. So when a rum smells strongly of tropical fruit, think fermentation.":"第二步，發酵。和往常一樣，酵母把糖轉化為酒精，但在蘭姆酒中，發酵也能用來創造熱帶水果香氣，有時非常明顯。當蒸餾師刻意把發酵時產生的風味發揮到極致，就能得到一款果香極為濃郁的蘭姆酒。牙買加的蒸餾師以生產這種風格而聞名。所以當一款蘭姆酒聞起來有濃濃的熱帶水果味時，想想發酵。","Step three, distillation. Most Caribbean distillers can choose which still to use, and that choice decides how intense the rum will be. To create a pronounced, characterful spirit, they might use a pot still. Another option is a short column still, with few sections, which also gives a flavourful spirit; this is the case for rhum agricole.":"第三步，蒸餾。大多數加勒比海蒸餾師可以選擇使用哪一種蒸餾器，而這個選擇決定了蘭姆酒的濃郁程度。要製作濃郁、有個性的烈酒，他們可能使用壺式蒸餾器。另一個選擇是層數少的矮柱式蒸餾器，同樣能得到風味豐富的烈酒；rhum agricole 就是如此。","At the other end of the scale are rums with a light aroma intensity. These are made in tall column stills and distilled to a high strength, which strips away much of the aroma. Examples of this light style can be found in Cuba and Puerto Rico. And many Caribbean distillers own both pot stills and column stills, so they can make several different spirits with different intensities under one roof, like a painter with a full palette of colours.":"另一端則是香氣強度清淡的蘭姆酒。它們以高柱式蒸餾器製作，並蒸餾到高濃度，去除了大部分的香氣。這種清淡風格的例子可以在古巴和波多黎各找到。許多加勒比海蒸餾師同時擁有壺式蒸餾器和柱式蒸餾器，所以能在同一個屋簷下製作多種不同濃郁度的烈酒，就像擁有一整盤顏料的畫家。","Step four, after distillation, and here rum offers many paths. Some rums are aged in oak, which gives them colour and aromas of vanilla and sweet spice. In some Caribbean countries a period of oak maturation is even required by law. So how do you make a colourless rum in one of those countries? The distiller uses charcoal filtration, which removes the colour that the oak has given. The result is a white rum that has actually spent time in a barrel.":"第四步，蒸餾之後，蘭姆酒在這裡有許多條路。有些蘭姆酒在橡木桶中陳年，為它們帶來顏色以及香草和甜香料的香氣。在某些加勒比海國家，法律甚至規定必須經過一段橡木桶熟成。那麼在這些國家要怎麼製作無色的蘭姆酒？蒸餾師會使用木炭過濾，去除橡木桶帶來的顏色。結果就是一款確實在桶中待過的白色蘭姆酒。","The other way to make a colourless rum is simply not to use oak at all. The spirit is stored in steel vessels instead. These rums are unaged, and they keep the aromas of the newly made spirit. So a clear rum may be unaged, or it may be aged and then filtered: colour alone cannot tell you which.":"製作無色蘭姆酒的另一個方法，就是完全不使用橡木桶。烈酒改為存放在鋼製容器中。這些蘭姆酒未經陳年，保留了剛製成烈酒的香氣。所以一款透明的蘭姆酒可能未經陳年，也可能是陳年後再過濾：光看顏色無法分辨是哪一種。","When the spirits are ready, they are blended. This is where all that variety pays off: blenders can combine pot still and column still spirits, spirits of different ages, and even spirits from different distilleries, to build the style of each of their brands. Finally, a few last touches. Some rums are sweetened. This is common in Central and South America, but in some countries it is not permitted. Many rums also have their colour adjusted with caramel colour, and some get nearly all of their colour this way. Then, as with almost every spirit, the rum is diluted with water before bottling.":"烈酒準備好之後，就進行調和。這就是那些多樣性發揮作用的時候：調和師可以結合壺式和柱式蒸餾的烈酒、不同年份的烈酒，甚至來自不同蒸餾廠的烈酒，來建立旗下每個品牌的風格。最後還有幾個收尾處理。有些蘭姆酒會加甜。這在中南美洲很常見，但在某些國家是不被允許的。許多蘭姆酒也會用焦糖色調整顏色，有些幾乎所有的顏色都來自焦糖色。接著，和幾乎所有烈酒一樣，蘭姆酒在裝瓶前會加水稀釋。","Here is the tip for this lesson: never judge a rum by its colour. A white rum may have spent years in oak before charcoal filtering, and a dark rum may owe its colour mostly to caramel. Instead, walk back through the four steps: cane juice or molasses, how it was fermented, which still, and what happened afterwards.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：永遠不要以顏色判斷蘭姆酒。一款白色蘭姆酒可能在木炭過濾前已在橡木桶中待了多年，而一款深色蘭姆酒的顏色可能主要來自焦糖色。相反地，沿著四個步驟往回走：甘蔗汁還是糖蜜、如何發酵、用哪一種蒸餾器，以及之後發生了什麼。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, rum is made from sugar cane: cane juice gives grassy, herbaceous rums such as rhum agricole from Martinique and Guadeloupe, while molasses, the more common choice, gives caramel and brown sugar flavours. Second, fermentation can build intense tropical fruit, as in Jamaica, and the still decides intensity: pot stills and short columns for character, tall columns for light rums such as those of Cuba and Puerto Rico. Third, rum may be aged or unaged, charcoal-filtered to remove colour, blended, sometimes sweetened and often coloured with caramel.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，蘭姆酒用甘蔗製成：甘蔗汁帶來青草、草本風格的蘭姆酒，例如來自馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普的 rhum agricole；而較常見的糖蜜則帶來焦糖和紅糖風味。第二，發酵可以建立濃郁的熱帶水果香氣，例如牙買加，而蒸餾器決定濃郁度：壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱帶來個性，高蒸餾柱則做出清淡的蘭姆酒，例如古巴和波多黎各的蘭姆酒。第三，蘭姆酒可以陳年或不陳年、以木炭過濾去除顏色、經過調和，有時會加甜，也經常以焦糖色上色。","In this lesson we travel to Mexico to meet Tequila, a spirit with one of the most recognisable aromas on the bar shelf. We will see the plant it comes from and how that plant is turned into a sweet juice, what the words one hundred percent agave really mean, how the best Tequilas are distilled, and the four styles you will find on labels: blanco, joven, reposado and añejo.":"這堂課我們前往墨西哥，認識 Tequila，酒架上香氣最容易辨認的烈酒之一。我們會看看它來自哪一種植物、這種植物如何變成甜汁液、「100% agave」這幾個字真正的意思、最優秀的 Tequila 如何蒸餾，以及你會在酒標上看到的四種風格：blanco、joven、reposado 和 añejo。","Tequila has a very clear identity. It can only be made in certain states of Mexico, and it must be made from the blue agave plant, which is native to Mexico. Picture the plant: a large, hard core surrounded by long, spiky leaves, a little like a giant pineapple sitting in a crown of swords. It is the core that the distiller wants.":"Tequila 的身分非常明確。它只能在墨西哥的特定州生產，而且必須用原產於墨西哥的藍色龍舌蘭製作。想像這種植物：一個又大又硬的核心，被長而帶刺的葉片包圍，有點像坐在一圈刀劍中的巨大鳳梨。蒸餾師想要的就是這個核心。","Step one, processing the agave. When a plant is harvested, the leaves are cut away, leaving only the hard core. Just like grains, the freshly harvested core has no sugar ready to ferment, so it must be processed to create sugars. This is done by cooking the cores in ovens. Cooking makes them soft and creates sugars inside them. Think of a hard raw potato that becomes soft enough to mash once it has been cooked.":"第一步，處理龍舌蘭。採收時會切除葉片，只留下堅硬的核心。和穀物一樣，剛採收的龍舌蘭心沒有現成可發酵的糖，所以必須經過處理才能產生糖。做法是把龍舌蘭心放進窯爐烹煮。烹煮讓它們變軟，並在內部產生糖。想想一顆堅硬的生馬鈴薯，煮熟後就軟到可以壓成泥。","After cooking, the cores are crushed, releasing a sweet juice. And this juice carries the typical aromas of blue agave, a complex range of herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy and peppery notes. These are the aromas that make Tequila instantly recognisable, and the rest of the process is largely about deciding how much of them to keep.":"烹煮後，龍舌蘭心被壓碎，釋出甜汁液。這些汁液帶有藍色龍舌蘭的典型香氣，一系列複雜的草本、植物、橄欖、泥土和胡椒氣息。正是這些香氣讓 Tequila 一聞就認得出來，而之後的製程大部分都在決定要保留多少這些香氣。","Step two, fermentation. The agave juice is mixed with water to create a sugary liquid that can be fermented. At this point the producer has a choice: other sugars, not from agave, can be added to the liquid before fermentation. But there is a firm limit. At least fifty-one percent of the sugars must come from blue agave. In other words, agave must always provide more than half.":"第二步，發酵。龍舌蘭汁與水混合，製成可以發酵的含糖液體。此時生產者有一個選擇：可以在發酵前把不是來自龍舌蘭的其他糖加入液體中。但有一個嚴格的限制。至少百分之五十一的糖必須來自藍色龍舌蘭。換句話說，龍舌蘭一定要提供超過一半。","This is where an important label term comes in. When a Tequila says one hundred percent agave, it means that only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid, with no other sugars added. Spirits made only from agave sugars can have a more pronounced agave character. All other Tequilas are simply labelled Tequila. And note that this has nothing to do with age: any Tequila, unaged or aged, can be either Tequila or Tequila one hundred percent agave.":"一個重要的酒標術語就是在這裡出現的。當一款 Tequila 標示「100% agave」，表示製作含糖液體時只使用了藍色龍舌蘭，沒有加入其他糖。只用龍舌蘭糖分製作的烈酒，龍舌蘭個性可能更鮮明。其他所有 Tequila 就只標示為 Tequila。請注意，這與年份完全無關：任何 Tequila，不論未陳年或陳年，都可以是 Tequila 或 Tequila 100% agave。","Step three, distillation. Tequila can be made in column stills, but the best Tequilas are double distilled in pot stills, to a notably low strength. Remember our rule: the lower the distillation strength, the more of the raw material's aromas survive. The result is a very distinct and characterful spirit that shows off the herbaceous, peppery aromas of blue agave. It is the exact opposite of vodka, which is distilled to neutral strength precisely to remove aroma.":"第三步，蒸餾。Tequila 可以用柱式蒸餾器製作，但最優秀的 Tequila 是在壺式蒸餾器中二次蒸餾，到明顯較低的濃度。記住我們的規則：蒸餾濃度越低，留下的原料香氣就越多。結果是一款非常獨特、有個性的烈酒，展現出藍色龍舌蘭的草本、胡椒香氣。它正好與伏特加相反，伏特加被蒸餾到中性濃度，正是為了去除香氣。","Step four, after distillation. The distiller can choose whether to age the new spirit in oak or to leave it unaged. When Tequila is oak-aged, it is rarely matured for very long. The aim is balance: some oak aromas of vanilla and spice, without burying the agave character that makes Tequila unique. Oak-aged Tequilas are blended, and caramel colour may be used before they are diluted and bottled.":"第四步，蒸餾之後。蒸餾師可以選擇讓新烈酒在橡木桶中陳年，或保持未陳年。Tequila 經橡木桶陳年時，很少熟成很久。目標是平衡：帶一些香草和香料的橡木香氣，又不掩蓋讓 Tequila 獨一無二的龍舌蘭個性。經橡木桶陳年的 Tequila 會經過調和，並可能在稀釋和裝瓶前使用焦糖色。","Now the styles. There are two unaged styles. Blanco, also called silver, is noted for its pure expression of agave flavours: this is agave at its clearest. Then there is joven, also called oro or gold. Despite its golden colour, it is also unaged. Its colour comes from caramel, and its texture is softened with other additives. So a golden Tequila has not necessarily seen a barrel.":"接下來是風格。有兩種未陳年的風格。Blanco，也稱為 silver，以純粹展現龍舌蘭風味而著稱：這是最清晰的龍舌蘭。接著是 joven，也稱為 oro 或 gold。儘管呈金黃色，它同樣未經陳年。它的顏色來自焦糖色，口感則以其他添加物變得柔和。所以金黃色的 Tequila 不一定進過酒桶。","There are also two oak-aged styles. Reposado, which means rested, is aged in oak for between two and twelve months. This makes a softer spirit, but it rarely has prominent oak flavours, and it keeps its pronounced agave aromas. Añejo, which means aged, spends at least twelve months in oak barrels, and it shows both agave and oak flavours.":"也有兩種經橡木桶陳年的風格。Reposado，意思是「靜置過的」，在橡木桶中陳年兩到十二個月。這讓烈酒更柔和，但很少有明顯的橡木風味，並保留了鮮明的龍舌蘭香氣。Añejo，意思是「陳年的」，在橡木桶中至少度過十二個月，同時呈現龍舌蘭和橡木的風味。","Here is the tip for this lesson. When you read a Tequila label, ask two separate questions. First: how much agave? That is the difference between Tequila, with at least fifty-one percent agave sugars, and one hundred percent agave. Second: how long did it rest? Blanco and joven, none; reposado, two to twelve months; añejo, twelve months or more. The two questions never depend on each other.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：讀 Tequila 酒標時，問兩個獨立的問題。第一：用了多少龍舌蘭？這是 Tequila（至少百分之五十一的龍舌蘭糖分）和 100% agave 之間的差別。第二：它靜置了多久？Blanco 和 joven 沒有；reposado 兩到十二個月；añejo 十二個月以上。這兩個問題彼此從不相關。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, Tequila is made in certain Mexican states from blue agave, whose cores are cooked in ovens to create sugars and then crushed, giving herbaceous, vegetal and peppery aromas. Second, at least fifty-one percent of the sugars must come from blue agave, one hundred percent agave means agave only, and the best Tequilas are double distilled in pot stills to a low strength. Third, blanco or silver and joven or gold are unaged, the gold colour coming from caramel; reposado spends two to twelve months in oak, and añejo at least twelve months.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，Tequila 在墨西哥特定州以藍色龍舌蘭製作，龍舌蘭心在窯爐中烹煮以產生糖，然後壓碎，帶來草本、植物和胡椒香氣。第二，至少百分之五十一的糖必須來自藍色龍舌蘭，100% agave 表示只用龍舌蘭，而最優秀的 Tequila 是在壺式蒸餾器中二次蒸餾到較低濃度。第三，blanco（或 silver）和 joven（或 gold）都未經陳年，金黃色來自焦糖色；reposado 在橡木桶中待兩到十二個月，añejo 則至少十二個月。","In this lesson we explore flavoured spirits, a big and colourful family that includes flavoured vodka, gin, bitter spirits, cocktail bitters, spiced rum and liqueurs. We will see where these spirits start, the three main ways to add flavour, and what makes each type different. By the end, you will know why a London Dry Gin does not have to come from London, and what separates a liqueur from every other flavoured spirit.":"這堂課我們要探索調味烈酒，一個龐大又多彩的家族，包括調味伏特加、琴酒、苦味烈酒、調酒用苦精、香料蘭姆酒和利口酒。我們會看到這些烈酒從哪裡開始、增添風味的三種主要方法，以及每種類型的不同之處。到最後，你會知道為什麼 London Dry Gin 不一定來自倫敦，以及利口酒與其他所有調味烈酒的區別。","With flavoured spirits, the starting point is unusual. Producers do not have to begin with a raw material at all. In fact, most of them buy in a spirit that has already been made. The vast majority of flavoured spirits are made from the same neutral spirit that is diluted with water to make vodka. Occasionally, rum, whisky or brandy is used as the base instead. So the real craft here lies not in fermenting or distilling, but in adding flavour.":"調味烈酒的起點很不尋常。生產者根本不必從原料開始。事實上，大多數生產者是外購已經製作好的烈酒。絕大多數調味烈酒，用的是加水稀釋後成為伏特加的同一種中性烈酒。偶爾也會改用蘭姆酒、威士忌或白蘭地作為基底。所以這裡真正的功夫不在發酵或蒸餾，而在增添風味。","The best flavoured spirits get their flavour from natural ingredients such as fruits, seeds, herbs and spices. Together these are called botanicals. Other flavourings, referred to as artificial flavours, are also used. There are three common ways of adding flavour: redistillation, maceration, and adding ready-made flavourings, natural or artificial. Each method leaves a different mark on the finished spirit.":"最優秀的調味烈酒從水果、種子、香草和香料等天然原料取得風味。這些原料合稱為植物性原料。也會使用其他調味料，稱為人工香料。增添風味有三種常見方法：再蒸餾、浸漬，以及加入現成的天然或人工調味料。每種方法都會在成品烈酒上留下不同的印記。","In redistillation, a diluted neutral spirit is placed in a pot still together with the distiller's chosen botanicals, and the mixture is distilled. What comes out is a flavoured spirit that is colourless. In maceration, the botanicals are simply soaked in the spirit, a little like a cold herbal tea, and their flavours come out over time. This can take a few days or several months: the longer it lasts, the more flavour is extracted, and gently heating the spirit speeds things up. Maceration also gives the spirit colour.":"再蒸餾時，稀釋過的中性烈酒和蒸餾師選擇的植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器，然後蒸餾這個混合物。流出的是無色的調味烈酒。浸漬時，植物性原料只是浸泡在烈酒中，有點像冷泡花草茶，風味隨著時間釋出。這可能需要幾天到幾個月：時間越長，萃取出的風味越多，溫和加熱烈酒則能加快速度。浸漬也會為烈酒帶來顏色。","The third method is the simplest. Some producers, normally for reasons of cost, choose not to use botanicals and instead buy in natural or other flavourings. These are very concentrated, so only small quantities are mixed with the spirit to create the final product. To sum up the methods: redistillation gives flavour without colour, maceration gives flavour and colour, and bought-in flavourings give flavour quickly and cheaply.":"第三種方法最簡單。有些生產者通常出於成本考量，選擇不使用植物性原料，而是外購天然或其他調味料。這些調味料非常濃縮，所以只需少量與烈酒混合，就能製成最終產品。總結這些方法：再蒸餾帶來風味而不帶顏色，浸漬帶來風味和顏色，外購調味料則能快速、便宜地帶來風味。","Let's meet the types, starting with flavoured vodka. It comes in a wide range of flavours: vanilla, fruits such as apple and lemon, and spices such as pepper. Producers typically add bought-in flavourings to their neutral spirit, although some do use redistillation. The result is usually easy to recognise: one clear, direct flavour on a clean, neutral background.":"我們來認識各種類型，從調味伏特加開始。它有各式各樣的風味：香草、蘋果和檸檬等水果，以及胡椒等香料。生產者通常在中性烈酒中加入外購調味料，不過也有些使用再蒸餾。結果通常很容易辨認：在乾淨、中性的背景上，有一種清楚直接的風味。","Next, gin. Gin is a flavoured spirit that must have juniper as its predominant flavour. Other common botanicals include coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel. Gin is typically made from neutral spirit, although in the United States other distilled spirits can be used. Flavour can be added by redistillation, or producers can simply add bought-in flavourings. The best gins are usually redistilled, although some very delicate flavours are added after distillation. Gins are typically unaged and colourless.":"接下來是琴酒。琴酒是一種必須以杜松子為主要風味的調味烈酒。其他常見的植物性原料包括芫荽籽、歐白芷根、鳶尾根和柑橘皮。琴酒通常以中性烈酒製作，不過在美國可以使用其他蒸餾烈酒。風味可以透過再蒸餾加入，生產者也可以直接加入外購調味料。最優秀的琴酒通常是再蒸餾的，不過有些非常細緻的風味是在蒸餾後才加入。琴酒通常未經陳年、無色。","Now a classic exam point. The popular labelling term London Dry Gin indicates that the flavours were added during redistillation. It is a method, not a place: London Dry Gin can be made anywhere in the world. It does not have to be made in London. So when you see London Dry on a label, think of the method, not of the city: a London Dry Gin made on another continent is perfectly possible.":"接下來是一個經典考點。常見的酒標術語 London Dry Gin，表示風味是在再蒸餾時加入的。它是一種方法，而不是地點：London Dry Gin 可以在世界任何地方製作。它不一定要在倫敦製作。所以當你在酒標上看到 London Dry 時，想的是製法，而不是城市：在另一個大陸製作的 London Dry Gin 完全可能。","Bitter spirits are made with at least one bitter botanical, such as gentian, quinine or bitter orange. Here is an interesting detail: the bitterness can only be detected on the palate, not on the nose. The aroma comes from the bitter botanicals and from many others besides. Traditionally these spirits were drunk at the beginning or the end of a meal, but today they are mostly used in cocktails. Cocktail bitters are something different again: highly concentrated and intensely bitter spirits. Nobody drinks them on their own. Instead, they are used in tiny quantities, a dash or two, to give cocktails extra complexity, rather like salt and pepper in cooking.":"苦味烈酒至少使用一種苦味植物性原料製作，例如龍膽、奎寧或苦橙。這裡有個有趣的細節：苦味只能在口中察覺，鼻子聞不到。香氣來自苦味植物性原料，也來自許多其他原料。傳統上這些烈酒在用餐開始或結束時飲用，但如今大多用在調酒中。調酒用苦精又是另一回事：高度濃縮、極苦的烈酒。沒有人會單獨飲用它們。它們以極少量使用，一兩滴就能為調酒增添額外的複雜度，有點像烹飪中的鹽和胡椒。","Spiced rum is a very varied category, both in the base rum and in the flavourings added. Some are made from a light, unaged rum that is flavoured and coloured with caramel. Only a handful are based on oak-aged rums. Both botanicals and other flavourings are used. So, once again, an amber colour does not prove years in a barrel.":"香料蘭姆酒是一個非常多樣的類別，不論是基底蘭姆酒還是加入的調味料都是如此。有些以清淡的未陳年蘭姆酒製作，經過調味並以焦糖色上色。只有少數以橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒為基底。植物性原料和其他調味料都會使用。所以，再說一次，琥珀色不能證明在桶中多年。","Finally, liqueurs. A liqueur is a flavoured spirit that has also been sweetened. Most are made from neutral spirit, but some start from characterful spirits such as brandy, rum or whisky. There is no limit to the flavours that can be used, or to the methods of adding them, and one notable ingredient found in some liqueurs is cream. Sugar is added after flavouring, and by law a liqueur must reach a minimum level of sweetness. Many are also coloured: natural colour from maceration can fade quickly, so artificial colours are widely used to keep the colour stable and to offer a broader, often vivid, range of shades.":"最後是利口酒。利口酒是經過調味、又加了甜的烈酒。大多數以中性烈酒製作，但有些以白蘭地、蘭姆酒或威士忌等有個性的烈酒為起點。可以使用的風味沒有限制，添加的方法也沒有限制，某些利口酒中一個值得注意的原料是鮮奶油。糖是在調味之後加入的，依法利口酒必須達到最低甜度。許多利口酒也會上色：來自浸漬的天然顏色可能很快褪色，所以廣泛使用人工色素，讓顏色保持穩定，並提供更廣泛、常常很鮮豔的色調。","Here is the tip for this lesson: a liqueur is flavour plus sugar. Gin, flavoured vodka and bitter spirits are flavoured too, but only a liqueur must, by law, be sweet. And for gin, remember that London Dry describes how it is made, not where. A quick check: if a spirit is flavoured but not sweet, it is not a liqueur.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：利口酒就是風味加糖。琴酒、調味伏特加和苦味烈酒也有風味，但只有利口酒依法必須是甜的。至於琴酒，記住 London Dry 描述的是製法，而不是產地。一個快速檢查法：如果一款烈酒有風味但不甜，它就不是利口酒。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, most flavoured spirits start from a bought-in neutral spirit, and flavour is added by redistillation, which keeps the spirit colourless, by maceration, which adds colour, or with bought-in flavourings. Second, gin must taste mainly of juniper, and London Dry means flavours added by redistillation, anywhere in the world; bitter spirits have at least one bitter botanical, cocktail bitters are used in tiny amounts, and spiced rum is often a light rum plus flavourings and caramel. Third, a liqueur is a flavoured spirit sweetened to a legal minimum, in any flavour, even cream, and is often coloured.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，大多數調味烈酒以外購的中性烈酒為起點，風味透過再蒸餾（讓烈酒保持無色）、浸漬（增添顏色）或外購調味料加入。第二，琴酒必須以杜松子味為主，London Dry 表示風味以再蒸餾加入，可在世界任何地方製作；苦味烈酒至少有一種苦味植物性原料，調酒用苦精以極少量使用，香料蘭姆酒則常是清淡的蘭姆酒加上調味料和焦糖色。第三，利口酒是加甜到法定最低甜度的調味烈酒，可以是任何風味，甚至鮮奶油，而且常經過上色。","In this lesson we look at a family that is not, strictly speaking, made of spirits at all: aromatised wines. So why do they belong in a spirits course? Because you will find them on almost every bar, and they are some of the most useful ingredients in cocktails. We will see the four components that every aromatised wine shares, what each one does, where these wines are best known, and the rules that define the most famous of them: vermouth.":"這堂課我們要看一個嚴格來說根本不是由烈酒組成的家族：加味葡萄酒。那為什麼它們會出現在烈酒課程中？因為幾乎每個酒吧都有它們，而且它們是調酒中最有用的材料之一。我們會看到所有加味葡萄酒共有的四個組成部分、每個部分的作用、這類酒最知名的產區，以及定義其中最有名的一種，也就是香艾酒的規定。","Aromatised wines are a diverse category, with many recipes and styles. Yet they are all built from the same four components: a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar, and a spirit. A fifth ingredient, caramel colour, is sometimes used as well. Think of a stool with four legs: wine, bitterness, sweetness and spirit. Take one away, and the whole thing wobbles.":"加味葡萄酒是一個多樣的類別，有許多配方和風格。但它們都由同樣的四個組成部分構成：基酒、一定包含某種苦味的調味料、糖，以及烈酒。有時也會使用第五種原料：焦糖色。想像一張有四隻腳的凳子：葡萄酒、苦味、甜味和烈酒。拿掉一隻，整張凳子就會搖晃。","Let's start with the base wine. Most aromatised wines are made from a white wine. Most producers choose a relatively neutral wine, which works as a blank canvas to show off the added flavours. Others prefer aromatic wines, and then balance the wine's own aromas with their choice of flavourings. There are also aromatised wines made from red or rosé wine, but white is by far the most common base.":"我們從基酒開始。大多數加味葡萄酒以白葡萄酒製作。大多數生產者選擇相對中性的葡萄酒，作為展現添加風味的空白畫布。有些則偏好芳香型葡萄酒，再用選擇的調味料平衡葡萄酒本身的香氣。也有以紅葡萄酒或粉紅酒製作的加味葡萄酒，但白葡萄酒是目前最常見的基酒。","Second component: the spirit. A small quantity of spirit must be added to every aromatised wine. There are two reasons. It raises the level of alcohol, and it gives the product a longer shelf life, especially once the bottle has been opened. The spirit chosen is nearly always neutral, so that it adds strength without getting in the way of the flavours.":"第二個組成部分：烈酒。每款加味葡萄酒都必須加入少量烈酒。原因有兩個。它能提高酒精濃度，也能讓產品保存更久，尤其是開瓶之後。選用的烈酒幾乎都是中性的，這樣它能增加濃度，又不會干擾風味。","Third component: the flavourings. They can be added directly to the wine, or in the form of flavoured spirits. The recipes are extremely varied, but they all have one feature in common: they use bitter botanicals. The classic examples are wormwood, gentian and quinine. You may recognise gentian and quinine from our lesson on bitter spirits: the same bitter family turns up again here.":"第三個組成部分：調味料。它們可以直接加入葡萄酒中，或以調味烈酒的形式加入。配方極為多樣，但都有一個共同特點：使用苦味植物性原料。經典的例子是苦艾、龍膽和奎寧。你可能還記得苦味烈酒那一課的龍膽和奎寧：同一個苦味家族在這裡又出現了。","Fourth component: sugar. Almost no aromatised wines are completely dry. The sweetness can come from the wine itself or from sugar added by the producer. This sweetness is what balances the bitterness of the botanicals, and together they give aromatised wines their characteristic bittersweet taste. Bitter without sweet would be harsh; sweet without bitter would be dull.":"第四個組成部分：糖。幾乎沒有加味葡萄酒是完全不甜的。甜味可能來自葡萄酒本身，也可能來自生產者添加的糖。正是這份甜味平衡了植物性原料的苦味，兩者結合，賦予加味葡萄酒獨特的甜中帶苦滋味。只有苦沒有甜會太刺激；只有甜沒有苦又會太平淡。","And the optional extra: caramel colour. It is not always used, but it plays an important role in red vermouths. These are made from a white wine base, so their red or brown colour does not come from the grapes: it is given by caramel. In this case, caramel can also add aromas of caramel to the drink. So a red vermouth is not, as many people assume, a red wine with herbs.":"還有一個可選的額外原料：焦糖色。它不一定會使用，但在紅香艾酒中扮演重要角色。紅香艾酒以白葡萄酒為基酒，所以它的紅色或棕色不是來自葡萄，而是由焦糖色賦予的。在這種情況下，焦糖色也能為飲品增添焦糖香氣。所以紅香艾酒並不像許多人以為的，是加了香草的紅葡萄酒。","Where are aromatised wines made? They can be made anywhere in the world, but the best-known areas of production are south-east France and north-west Italy. In both countries, the most widely made type of aromatised wine is vermouth. Vermouth follows two rules. It is made from a white wine base, and it must be flavoured with wormwood, a strongly bitter botanical. Wormwood is the botanical that defines every vermouth. Beyond that, each producer builds their own recipe of herbs, spices and other botanicals.":"加味葡萄酒在哪裡製作？它們可以在世界任何地方製作，但最知名的產區是法國東南部和義大利西北部。在這兩個國家，最普遍的加味葡萄酒類型是香艾酒。香艾酒遵循兩條規定。它以白葡萄酒為基酒，而且必須用苦艾調味，這是一種苦味強烈的植物性原料。苦艾是定義每一款香艾酒的植物性原料。除此之外，每位生產者都會建立自己的香草、香料和其他植物性原料配方。","Now, a couple of label traps. A vermouth labelled dry is almost never truly dry: it nearly always has some added sugar, just less than other styles. Red vermouths, on the other hand, are typically heavily sweetened. So in vermouth, the word dry means less sweet, not without sugar. Read the style on the label, and expect some sweetness in every bottle.":"接下來是幾個酒標陷阱。標示 dry 的香艾酒幾乎從不是真正不甜的：它幾乎都加了一些糖，只是比其他風格少。相反地，紅香艾酒通常大量加甜。所以在香艾酒中，dry 這個詞的意思是「比較不甜」，而不是「沒有糖」。讀酒標上的風格，並預期每一瓶都帶有一些甜味。","Why do bartenders love aromatised wines? Because a single ingredient can bring three things to a cocktail at once: sweetness, bitterness and acidity. Acidity comes from the wine, bitterness from the botanicals, sweetness from the sugar. That is why you will meet vermouth again in some of the great classics we will study in the cocktail lessons, from the Manhattan to the Martini and the Negroni.":"為什麼調酒師喜愛加味葡萄酒？因為一種材料就能同時為調酒帶來三樣東西：甜味、苦味和酸度。酸度來自葡萄酒，苦味來自植物性原料，甜味來自糖。這就是為什麼你會在調酒課程中再次遇到香艾酒，出現在我們要學習的一些偉大經典調酒中，從 Manhattan 到 Martini 和 Negroni。","Here is the tip for this lesson: vermouth equals white wine plus wormwood, and even a dry vermouth carries a little sugar. If you also remember the four-legged stool, wine, bitterness, sugar and spirit, you can describe any aromatised wine. And remember that a red vermouth owes its colour to caramel, not to red wine.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：香艾酒等於白葡萄酒加苦艾，而且即使是不甜香艾酒也帶有一點糖。如果你也記得那張四腳凳：葡萄酒、苦味、糖和烈酒，你就能描述任何一款加味葡萄酒。還要記住，紅香艾酒的顏色來自焦糖色，而不是紅葡萄酒。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, aromatised wines are not spirits, but every one is built from a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar and a small amount of usually neutral spirit, with caramel as an option. Second, the base is usually a fairly neutral white wine, the spirit raises alcohol and lengthens shelf life, and almost none are fully dry. Third, the best-known areas are south-east France and north-west Italy, where the main type is vermouth: a white wine base with wormwood, where even dry has sugar and red is heavily sweetened and coloured with caramel.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，加味葡萄酒不是烈酒，但每一款都由基酒、一定包含某種苦味的調味料、糖，以及少量通常是中性的烈酒構成，焦糖色則可選擇使用。第二，基酒通常是相當中性的白葡萄酒，烈酒能提高酒精濃度並延長保存期限，而且幾乎沒有一款是完全不甜的。第三，最知名的產區是法國東南部和義大利西北部，那裡的主要類型是香艾酒：以白葡萄酒為基酒並加入苦艾，即使是 dry 也有糖，紅香艾酒則大量加甜，並以焦糖色上色。","In this lesson we learn how to taste a spirit properly. Not how to enjoy a glass with friends, but how to look at a spirit closely, describe it accurately and write notes you can trust. We will see how to prepare the room, the glass and yourself, the step-by-step method for tasting, and what to write down for appearance, nose, palate and finish.":"這堂課我們要學習如何正確地品飲烈酒。不是如何和朋友享受一杯酒，而是如何仔細觀察一款烈酒、準確地描述它，並寫下值得信賴的筆記。我們會看到如何準備房間、酒杯和你自己，逐步的品飲方法，以及在外觀、香氣、口中和餘韻方面要記錄什麼。","The key word is consistency. If you take exactly the same approach with every sample, your notes will describe each spirit accurately, and you will be able to compare them, even months later. A note written today should mean the same thing as a note written next year. So the method matters as much as the spirit in the glass.":"關鍵詞是一致性。如果你對每個樣品都採取完全相同的方法，你的筆記就能準確描述每一款烈酒，你也能相互比較它們，即使是幾個月後。今天寫下的筆記，應該和明年寫下的筆記代表同樣的意思。所以方法和杯中的烈酒一樣重要。","Start with the setting. There should be no distracting smells in the room: no perfume, no cooking, no scented candles. You need a good source of natural light, and a white surface, such as a sheet of paper or a white tablecloth, to help you judge the colour of the spirit without misleading reflections.":"從環境開始。房間裡不應有干擾的氣味：沒有香水、沒有烹飪味、沒有香氛蠟燭。你需要良好的自然光源，以及白色表面，例如一張紙或白色桌布，幫助你判斷烈酒的顏色，而不受誤導性反光影響。","Then the glass. Choose one with a wide bowl that narrows towards the top, a little like a tulip. The wide bowl gives the aromas room to gather, and the narrower opening concentrates them and channels them towards your nose, which makes the nose much easier to assess. In a straight, open glass, the aromas simply drift away.":"接著是酒杯。選擇杯肚寬大、往上收窄的杯子，有點像鬱金香。寬大的杯肚讓香氣有空間聚集，較窄的開口則把香氣集中並導向你的鼻子，讓香氣更容易評估。在直筒開口的杯子裡，香氣就這樣飄散了。","And finally, the taster. Your palate should be clean, with no lingering flavours, so no toothpaste or coffee just before a tasting. And you should be well hydrated. Treat it like preparing an instrument before a concert: if the instrument is not ready, even the best music sounds wrong.":"最後是品飲者。你的味覺應該是乾淨的，沒有殘留的味道，所以品飲前不要刷牙或喝咖啡。而且你應該補充足夠的水分。把它當成音樂會前調整樂器：如果樂器沒有準備好，即使最好的音樂聽起來也會走調。","Now the method. Remember that spirits, even after the distiller has diluted them, are still very strong drinks. At forty percent alcohol by volume, it is not easy to make a fully accurate assessment: the alcohol stings the nose and can numb the palate. So the recommended approach uses a small sample and some water.":"接下來是方法。記住，烈酒即使經過蒸餾師稀釋，仍然是非常烈的飲料。在酒精濃度百分之四十時，要做出完全準確的評估並不容易：酒精會刺鼻，還可能麻痺味覺。所以建議的方法是使用少量樣品並加一些水。","Pour a small sample of one and a half centilitres, that is about half a US fluid ounce, roughly a tablespoon. First, look at it and assess its appearance. Then smell it and assess the nose, while it is still neat. Only after that do you add water: the same amount again, one and a half centilitres. This halves the strength of the sample.":"倒出一點五公分升（1.5 cL）的少量樣品，大約是半個美制液量盎司，大約一湯匙。首先觀察它，評估外觀。然後聞它，在仍未稀釋時評估香氣。之後才加水：再加同樣的量，一點五公分升。這會讓樣品的濃度減半。","Now smell the spirit again. With less alcohol in the way, aromas that were hidden often appear, like opening a window in a crowded room. Next, assess the palate: take a small sip, let it move around your mouth and look for the flavours. Then spit. Spitting is completely normal in a tasting: it keeps your head clear, so you can judge the last sample as carefully as the first.":"現在再聞一次烈酒。少了酒精的阻擋，原本隱藏的香氣往往會出現，就像在擁擠的房間裡打開一扇窗。接著評估口中：喝一小口，讓它在口中轉動，尋找風味。然後吐出。在品飲中吐出完全正常：它讓你保持頭腦清醒，對最後一個樣品的判斷也能和第一個一樣仔細。","So, what do you write down? The notes follow the same order: appearance, nose, palate. For appearance, you only need the colour. The main scale goes from colourless to lemon, gold, amber and brown. Unaged spirits are usually colourless, while oak-aged ones move along that scale. Some spirits, especially flavoured spirits and liqueurs, can show other colours: pink, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple, even black.":"那麼，要記錄什麼？筆記遵循同樣的順序：外觀、香氣、口中。外觀方面，只需要記錄顏色。主要的色階從無色到檸檬黃、金黃、琥珀和棕色。未陳年的烈酒通常是無色的，而經橡木桶陳年的則沿著這個色階移動。有些烈酒，尤其是調味烈酒和利口酒，可能呈現其他顏色：粉紅、紅、橙、黃、綠、藍、紫，甚至黑色。","On the nose, first judge the intensity: neutral, light, medium or pronounced. A neutral vodka sits at one end, an intense rum or a peaty whisky at the other. Then describe the aromas, and it helps to group them by where they come from: the raw material, such as grape, grain, cane or agave; the processing, such as fruity notes from fermentation; and oak and maturation, such as vanilla, spice or dried fruit.":"在香氣方面，首先判斷強度：中性、清淡、中等或濃郁。中性的伏特加在一端，濃郁的蘭姆酒或泥煤威士忌在另一端。然後描述香氣，依來源分組會很有幫助：原料，例如葡萄、穀物、甘蔗或龍舌蘭；加工，例如發酵帶來的果香；以及橡木桶和熟成，例如香草、香料或果乾。","On the palate, you look for the same groups of flavours: raw material, processing, oak and maturation. You also note other observations, in particular the sugar level, whether the spirit is dry or sweet, and the texture, for example light and smooth or richer and oily. Finally, the finish: what stays after you have spat. Judge its length, short, medium or long, and its character: neutral, simple, some complexity or very complex. A very complex finish keeps offering new flavours, one after another, long after the sip has gone.":"在口中，你要尋找同樣的風味分組：原料、加工、橡木桶和熟成。你也要記錄其他觀察，尤其是含糖量，也就是烈酒是不甜還是甜，以及質地，例如輕盈柔順或較豐厚油潤。最後是餘韻：吐出後留下的東西。判斷它的長度，短、中等或長，以及它的特質：中性、簡單、有些複雜度或非常複雜。非常複雜的餘韻會在那一口消失很久之後，仍不斷呈現一個接一個的新風味。","Here is the tip for this lesson, a little rhyme for the method: pour a little, look and sniff, add the same in water, sniff again, then taste and spit. And remember: the same amount of water as spirit, every time, so that every note you write is comparable. Write your notes as you go, while each impression is still fresh.":"這堂課的小訣竅，是一段關於方法的小口訣：倒一點，看一看、聞一聞，加等量的水，再聞一次，然後品嚐並吐出。還要記住：每次加入與烈酒等量的水，讓你寫下的每則筆記都能相互比較。邊品飲邊寫筆記，趁每個印象還新鮮的時候。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, prepare the conditions: no distracting smells, natural light, a white surface, a glass with a wide bowl that narrows at the top, a clean palate and good hydration. Second, follow the method: a small sample of about one and a half centilitres, look and smell, add the same amount of water, smell again, taste, then spit. Third, write down the colour, the nose intensity from neutral to pronounced, the aromas grouped by source, the palate with sugar and texture, and the finish with its length and complexity.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，準備好條件：沒有干擾的氣味、自然光、白色表面、杯肚寬大且往上收窄的酒杯、乾淨的味覺和充足的水分。第二，遵循方法：大約 1.5 cL 的少量樣品，觀察並聞香，加入等量的水，再聞一次，品嚐，然後吐出。第三，記錄顏色、從中性到濃郁的香氣強度、依來源分組的香氣、口中的含糖量和質地，以及餘韻的長度和複雜度。","In this lesson we step behind the bar. Before we learn any recipes, we need the principle that sits underneath all of them: balance. We will look at the two sets of scales that every cocktail is built on, strong against weak, and sweet against bitter or sour, and then at the first big division of the cocktail world: short drinks and long drinks. With these ideas, hundreds of recipes suddenly become much easier to understand.":"這堂課我們走到吧台後面。在學習任何酒譜之前，我們需要了解隱藏在所有酒譜之下的原則：平衡。我們會看看每一款調酒都建立在其上的兩座天平：強對弱，以及甜對苦或酸；接著看調酒世界的第一個大分類：短飲和長飲。有了這些概念，數百個酒譜會突然變得容易理解得多。","What makes a great cocktail? Good-quality ingredients and the right tools certainly help. But what really separates a good cocktail from a great one is balance, and a balanced cocktail shares many of the qualities we look for in a fine spirit. Generally speaking, two sets of scales are used to achieve it. The first weighs strong against weak. The second weighs sweet against bitter, sour, or both.":"什麼造就了一杯好調酒？高品質的材料和合適的工具當然有幫助。但真正區分一杯不錯和一杯出色調酒的，是平衡，而一杯平衡的調酒，具備許多我們在優秀烈酒中追求的特質。一般來說，要達到平衡會使用兩座天平。第一座秤的是強對弱。第二座秤的是甜對苦、酸，或兩者。","Let's start with the strong side. The strong element of a cocktail is the base spirit. It is generally forty percent alcohol by volume or higher, and it is the centrepiece of the flavour: the rum in a Daiquiri, the gin in a Martini, the whiskey in an Old Fashioned. The rest of the drink is built around it.":"我們從強的一方開始。調酒的強元素是基酒。它一般是酒精濃度百分之四十以上，也是風味的核心：Daiquiri 中的蘭姆酒、Martini 中的琴酒、Old Fashioned 中的威士忌。飲品的其餘部分都圍繞著它建立。","The weak side softens that strength. One source of weakness is always there: ice. When a cocktail is stirred or shaken with ice, some of it melts and dilutes the drink. Other weak ingredients are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, dairy products such as cream, sodas, club soda and tonic. Think of a gin and tonic: the gin is the strong part, while the tonic and the ice bring the weak part.":"弱的一方讓這份強度變得柔和。有一個弱的來源一定存在：冰塊。調酒與冰塊一起攪拌或搖盪時，部分冰塊會融化並稀釋飲品。其他弱的材料是可選的，而且不含酒精：果汁、鮮奶油等乳製品、汽水、蘇打水和通寧水。想想琴通寧：琴酒是強的部分，通寧水和冰塊則帶來弱的部分。","Change the strong element and you change the drink. Even using a different brand of spirit from the same category can alter a cocktail. A more radical change is to replace the strong component with a completely different spirit. For example, make an Old Fashioned with rum instead of whiskey, and you have a rum Old Fashioned: same structure, new character.":"換了強元素，飲品也就變了。即使使用同一類別中不同品牌的烈酒，也可能改變一杯調酒。更大的改變是用完全不同的烈酒替換強的組成部分。例如用蘭姆酒取代威士忌製作 Old Fashioned，就得到蘭姆酒 Old Fashioned：同樣的結構，新的個性。","Now the second set of scales. It is very common for a cocktail to be sweetened, and then seasoned with another ingredient, called a modifier, which provides a bitter or sour counterpoint, or both. Sweetness can come in many forms: plain sugar, simple syrup, which is just sugar dissolved in water, or liqueurs. But beware: if a cocktail is too sweet, it becomes cloying and unpleasant.":"接下來是第二座天平。調酒常常先加甜，再用另一種材料調味，這種材料稱為修飾材料，它提供苦或酸的對比，或兩者兼具。甜味可以有多種形式：一般的糖、簡易糖漿（就是溶於水中的糖），或利口酒。但要小心：如果調酒太甜，就會變得膩口又令人不快。","So the sweetness has to be balanced. On one side there are sour ingredients, which means acidic ones, above all citrus juices such as lemon and lime. On the other side there are bitter ingredients, most obviously cocktail bitters, added by the dash. It works just like cooking: a squeeze of lemon or a pinch of salt can lift a dish that tasted flat and heavy.":"所以甜味必須被平衡。一邊是酸的材料，也就是帶酸度的材料，最主要的是檸檬和萊姆等柑橘汁。另一邊是苦的材料，最明顯的就是以滴數加入的調酒用苦精。這就像烹飪一樣：擠一點檸檬汁或撒一撮鹽，就能讓一道平淡沉重的菜變得生動。","Remember too that a single ingredient can provide several of these elements at once. Aromatised wines such as vermouth are the perfect example: they bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity in one pour. The key to success is to balance strong against weak, and sweet against bitter and sour, so that the result is a cohesive whole where no single component dominates the others.":"也要記住，一種材料可以同時提供好幾個元素。香艾酒等加味葡萄酒就是完美的例子：一次倒入就帶來甜味、苦味和酸度。成功的關鍵是平衡強與弱、甜與苦和酸，讓結果成為一個融為一體、沒有任何單一部分壓過其他部分的整體。","Put the two scales together and you get the four points of balance: strong, weak, sweet, and bitter or sour. Every cocktail is built from these four. Once you understand them, a bartender can adjust any recipe as needed, adding a little more citrus to a drink that is too sweet, or a little more dilution to a drink that is too strong.":"把兩座天平放在一起，就得到平衡的四個要點：強、弱、甜，以及苦或酸。每一款調酒都由這四個元素構成。一旦理解了它們，調酒師就能依需要調整任何酒譜：太甜的飲品多加一點柑橘，太烈的飲品多一點稀釋。","Now the first big division: short drinks and long drinks. Short drinks usually have a limited number of ingredients, and they rely on dilution from shaking or stirring with ice to provide the weak component. They are small and concentrated. Within this category there are two families: the spirit-forward cocktail, where the spirit takes centre stage, and the short sour, built on spirit, citrus and sweetness.":"接下來是第一個大分類：短飲和長飲。短飲通常材料數量有限，依靠搖盪或攪拌時冰塊帶來的稀釋提供弱的部分。它們份量小而濃縮。在這個類別中有兩個家族：以烈酒為主角的烈酒主導型調酒，以及建立在烈酒、柑橘和甜味上的短酸酒。","Long drinks are typically larger, with a higher volume. Their weak component is often provided by sodas, juices, dairy products or other non-alcoholic drinks. Within this category there are two families: the highball, the simplest of all mixed drinks, and the long sour. We will meet all four families, with their classic recipes, in the next lesson.":"長飲通常較大，份量較多。它們弱的部分常由汽水、果汁、乳製品或其他無酒精飲料提供。在這個類別中有兩個家族：高球，所有混合飲料中最簡單的；以及長酸酒。下一堂課我們會認識全部四個家族和它們的經典酒譜。","Short and long drinks are closely related. Take a short sour of gin, lemon juice and simple syrup. Pour it over ice and top it with club soda, and it becomes a long drink, a Tom Collins. The core ingredients stay the same; what changes is the amount of the weak part, and with it the volume and the strength.":"短飲和長飲密切相關。以一杯由琴酒、檸檬汁和簡易糖漿組成的短酸酒為例。把它倒在冰塊上並補滿蘇打水，它就變成長飲，也就是 Tom Collins。核心材料保持不變；改變的是弱的部分的份量，連帶改變了份量和濃度。","Here is the tip for this lesson: think of a cocktail as a dish to season. The spirit is the main ingredient, ice and mixers are the water in the pot, sugar is the sweetness, and citrus and bitters are the salt and lemon that bring it to life. If one flavour shouts louder than the others, the dish is not balanced yet.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：把調酒想成一道需要調味的菜。烈酒是主要食材，冰塊和調和飲料是鍋裡的水，糖是甜味，柑橘和苦精則是讓它活起來的鹽和檸檬。如果有一種味道比其他味道喊得更大聲，這道菜就還沒有平衡。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, balance uses two sets of scales: strong against weak, and sweet against bitter, sour or both. Second, the strong part is the base spirit, usually forty percent or more; the weak part is dilution from ice, plus juices, dairy, sodas or tonic; sweetness comes from sugar, simple syrup or liqueurs, and is balanced by citrus or bitters, while aromatised wines can bring all three at once. Third, short drinks rely on ice dilution and include spirit-forward cocktails and short sours; long drinks are lengthened with mixers and include highballs and long sours.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，平衡使用兩座天平：強對弱，以及甜對苦、酸或兩者。第二，強的部分是基酒，通常百分之四十以上；弱的部分是冰塊帶來的稀釋，加上果汁、乳製品、汽水或通寧水；甜味來自糖、簡易糖漿或利口酒，並由柑橘或苦精平衡，而加味葡萄酒能同時帶來三者。第三，短飲依靠冰塊稀釋，包括烈酒主導型調酒和短酸酒；長飲以調和飲料延長，包括高球和長酸酒。","In this last lesson we meet the classic cocktail families. There are hundreds of classic cocktails, and new ones are invented all the time, so the cocktail world can look overwhelming. In fact, it is not. Most classics belong to one of four families: the spirit-forward cocktail and the short sour, which are short drinks, and the highball and the long sour, which are long drinks. Let's see how each family works, and which famous drinks belong to it.":"在這最後一堂課，我們要認識經典調酒家族。經典調酒有數百款，新的調酒也不斷被發明，所以調酒世界看起來可能令人不知所措。其實不然。大多數經典調酒屬於四個家族之一：烈酒主導型調酒和短酸酒，屬於短飲；高球和長酸酒，屬於長飲。我們來看看每個家族如何運作，以及哪些知名飲品屬於它。","First, the spirit-forward cocktail. These drinks are higher in alcohol than the others, and they celebrate their strong ingredient. In their simplest form they combine a spirit with sugar and bitters, or a spirit with a liqueur. In more complex versions, sweetness and bitterness are balanced with various combinations of sugar, aromatised wines and bitters. They are generally built in the glass or stirred, and the ice provides both dilution and chilling.":"首先是烈酒主導型調酒。這些飲品的酒精濃度比其他飲品高，它們頌揚的是強的材料。最簡單的形式是烈酒加糖和苦精，或烈酒加利口酒。較複雜的版本中，甜味和苦味以糖、加味葡萄酒和苦精的各種組合來平衡。它們一般直接在杯中調製或攪拌，冰塊同時提供稀釋和冰鎮。","The Old Fashioned is the model: Bourbon, a sugar cube and aromatic bitters. The Manhattan uses rye whiskey or Bourbon with the same kind of aromatic bitters, but the sweetness comes from sweet vermouth, whose complexity makes it quite distinct from the Old Fashioned. The Sazerac takes Cognac or rye whiskey, sugar, a different style of cocktail bitters and a touch of absinthe. And the Rusty Nail is the simplest of all: Scotch whisky with a whisky-based honey liqueur.":"Old Fashioned 是範本：Bourbon、一顆方糖和芳香苦精。Manhattan 使用黑麥威士忌或 Bourbon 和同類的芳香苦精，但甜味來自甜香艾酒，它的複雜度讓 Manhattan 與 Old Fashioned 大不相同。Sazerac 使用 Cognac 或黑麥威士忌、糖、另一種風格的調酒用苦精和一點苦艾酒。而 Rusty Nail 是最簡單的：Scotch 威士忌加上以威士忌為基底的蜂蜜利口酒。","Gin gives two more great classics. The Martini combines gin with dry vermouth, which on its own brings both the bitter and the sweet element. The Negroni combines gin, sweet vermouth and a red bitter spirit: three ingredients, three clear roles. One more modification is worth knowing: adding cream creates the Alexander family of cocktails, such as the Brandy Alexander.":"琴酒又帶來兩款偉大的經典調酒。Martini 結合琴酒與不甜香艾酒，香艾酒單獨就帶來苦味和甜味兩個元素。Negroni 結合琴酒、甜香艾酒和一種紅色苦味烈酒：三種材料，三個明確的角色。還有一個值得認識的變化：加入鮮奶油，就產生了 Alexander 調酒家族，例如 Brandy Alexander。","Second family: the short sour. It is built on a classic balance of strong, sour and sweet. A classic sour uses a spirit, a citrus juice, and an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup. These drinks are shaken: shaking chills and mixes the ingredients, adds some dilution, and creates a light, airy texture. Some recipes also call for egg white, which gives a foam head and a silky texture. Many bars now use vegan alternatives such as aquafaba, the water chickpeas are cooked in.":"第二個家族：短酸酒。它建立在強、酸、甜的經典平衡上。經典酸酒使用一種烈酒、一種柑橘汁，以及簡易糖漿這類無調味甜味劑。這些飲品以搖盪製作：搖盪能冰鎮並混合材料、增加一些稀釋，並創造輕盈、充滿空氣的質地。有些酒譜還要求加蛋白，它帶來泡沫層和絲滑的質地。如今許多酒吧使用純素替代品，例如鷹嘴豆水（aquafaba，煮鷹嘴豆的水）。","Three classics show the pure formula. The Daiquiri: rum, lime juice and simple syrup. The Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye whiskey, lemon juice and simple syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. And the Pisco Sour, made with pisco, a grape brandy: pisco, lime juice and simple syrup, plus one egg white and a dash of bitters. In the Pisco Sour, the egg white is essential.":"三款經典調酒展現了純粹的公式。Daiquiri：蘭姆酒、萊姆汁和簡易糖漿。Whiskey Sour：Bourbon 或黑麥威士忌、檸檬汁和簡易糖漿，可選擇加蛋白和苦精。以及 Pisco Sour，用葡萄白蘭地 Pisco 製作：Pisco、萊姆汁和簡易糖漿，再加一顆蛋白和幾滴苦精。在 Pisco Sour 中，蛋白不可或缺。","More complex sours change the formula by using a flavoured sweetener, a different sour ingredient, or both. The Sidecar: Cognac, lemon juice and triple sec, an orange liqueur, in place of the syrup. The Margarita: Tequila, lime juice and triple sec, with an optional salt rim. And the Clover Club: gin, lemon juice and raspberry syrup, with egg white and an optional touch of vermouth.":"較複雜的酸酒會改變公式，使用有風味的甜味劑、不同的酸味材料，或兩者都改。Sidecar：Cognac、檸檬汁和柳橙利口酒 triple sec，取代糖漿。Margarita：Tequila、萊姆汁和 triple sec，可選擇加鹽邊。以及 Clover Club：琴酒、檸檬汁和覆盆子糖漿，加上蛋白，並可選擇加一點香艾酒。","Third family: the highball, the simplest of all mixed drinks. It is a long drink, a spirit with a non-alcoholic mixer, served over cubed ice. Gin and tonic, vodka and tonic, and whisky and soda are obvious examples. Some highballs have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice.":"第三個家族：高球，所有混合飲料中最簡單的。它是一種長飲，烈酒加無酒精調和飲料，倒在方塊冰上供應。琴通寧、伏特加通寧和威士忌蘇打都是明顯的例子。有些高球有自己的名字。Cuba Libre 是蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆。Greyhound 是伏特加和葡萄柚汁。","Some highballs go a little further. The Horse's Neck adds bitters to a spirit and a mixer: Cognac, ginger ale and bitters. Others use a split base for the strong element. The Americano is the classic example: its strong part is shared between a red bitter spirit and sweet vermouth, topped with club soda.":"有些高球更進一步。Horse's Neck 在烈酒和調和飲料之外加入苦精：Cognac、薑汁汽水和苦精。其他高球則在強元素上使用分拆基底。Americano 是經典例子：它強的部分由一種紅色苦味烈酒和甜香艾酒分擔，再補滿蘇打水。","Fourth family: the long sour, which includes several sub-categories: the Collins, the Sling and the sparkling sour. In their simplest form, they are just short sours turned into long drinks by adding club soda. The Tom Collins is the perfect example: gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, topped with club soda.":"第四個家族：長酸酒，包括幾個子類別：Collins、Sling 和氣泡酸酒。最簡單的形式，就是加入蘇打水變成長飲的短酸酒。Tom Collins 是完美的例子：琴酒、檸檬汁和簡易糖漿，再補滿蘇打水。","The club soda can be swapped for something else. In a Paloma, it becomes a flavoured soda: Tequila and lime juice with a Mexican grapefruit soda, or alternatively grapefruit juice mixed with soda. In a French 75, it becomes Champagne: Cognac or gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, topped with Champagne. That is a sparkling sour.":"蘇打水可以換成別的東西。在 Paloma 中，它變成有風味的汽水：Tequila 和萊姆汁，加上墨西哥葡萄柚汽水，或改用葡萄柚汁混合蘇打水。在 French 75 中，它變成 Champagne：Cognac 或琴酒、檸檬汁和簡易糖漿，再補上 Champagne。這就是氣泡酸酒。","Other long sours are enhanced with extra ingredients. Sometimes it is simple, as in the Mojito: rum, lime juice, sugar or simple syrup and mint leaves, topped with soda water. Sometimes it is more complex, as in the Singapore Sling: gin and lime juice, sweetened with a cherry liqueur and a herbal liqueur, with a dash of aromatic bitters and a top of club soda.":"其他長酸酒會加入額外的材料來提升。有時很簡單，例如 Mojito：蘭姆酒、萊姆汁、糖或簡易糖漿和薄荷葉，再補滿蘇打水。有時則較複雜，例如 Singapore Sling：琴酒和萊姆汁，以櫻桃利口酒和草本利口酒加甜，再加幾滴芳香苦精，最後補滿蘇打水。","Here is the tip for this lesson. To place any cocktail, ask two questions. Is it short or long? And is it built around the spirit, or around citrus? Short and spirit-led: spirit-forward. Short with citrus: short sour. Long with just a mixer: highball. Long with citrus: long sour. Then remember the four points of balance: strong, weak, sweet, and bitter or sour.":"這堂課的小訣竅是：要為任何一款調酒定位，問兩個問題。它是短飲還是長飲？它是圍繞烈酒，還是圍繞柑橘建立的？短飲、以烈酒為主：烈酒主導型。短飲、有柑橘：短酸酒。長飲、只有調和飲料：高球。長飲、有柑橘：長酸酒。然後記住平衡的四個要點：強、弱、甜，以及苦或酸。","Before the quiz, remember three things. First, spirit-forward cocktails are the strongest, built or stirred: Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Sazerac, Rusty Nail, Martini and Negroni, with cream giving the Alexander family. Second, short sours are spirit, citrus and sweetener, shaken: Daiquiri, Whiskey Sour and Pisco Sour, with egg white essential in the Pisco Sour, and variations such as the Sidecar, Margarita and Clover Club. Third, highballs are a spirit and a mixer over ice, such as the Cuba Libre, Greyhound, Horse's Neck and Americano, while long sours are lengthened sours, such as the Tom Collins, Paloma, French 75, Mojito and Singapore Sling.":"做測驗之前，記住三件事。第一，烈酒主導型調酒是最烈的，以直調或攪拌製作：Old Fashioned、Manhattan、Sazerac、Rusty Nail、Martini 和 Negroni，加入鮮奶油則產生 Alexander 家族。第二，短酸酒是烈酒、柑橘和甜味劑，搖盪而成：Daiquiri、Whiskey Sour 和 Pisco Sour，Pisco Sour 中蛋白不可或缺，變化版則有 Sidecar、Margarita 和 Clover Club。第三，高球是烈酒加調和飲料倒在冰塊上，例如 Cuba Libre、Greyhound、Horse's Neck 和 Americano；長酸酒則是延長的酸酒，例如 Tom Collins、Paloma、French 75、Mojito 和 Singapore Sling。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/s1"]=1;
